{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998318-ic-promethean-the-created-2e-muddy-waters","id":998318,"title":"[IC] (Promethean: The Created 2E) Muddy Waters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play","Play by Post"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-04T11:06:18-07:00","id":998318,"title":"[IC] (Promethean: The Created 2E) Muddy Waters","content":"<b><u>Muddy Waters</u></b><br /> <br /> <i>Winnipeg the ruin, Winnipeg of the haunted past, </i><br /> <i>Winnipeg of murder and flames. </i><br /> <i>Winnipeg of cold and death, </i><br /> <i>Winnipeg of the hopeless, </i><br /> <i>Winnipeg the doomed.</i> <br /> \u2013Jonathan Ball, Preface to The Shadow Over Portage and Main<br /> <br /> Once upon a time, it was marked \u2018Chicago of the North\u2019 and it was supposed to be the first city in North America to hit a population of a million, but it was eaten out by corruption, and then crippled by the following strikes. It\u2019s a patchwork city, cobbled together from the corpses of several others, and assembled around the beating heart of three mighty rivers. It\u2019s the Heart of the Continent, born in bloody revolution, and steeped in fire and blood ever since.<br /> <br /> It is a city of extremes.<br /> <br /> Extremes in temperature, extremes in relationships, extremes in arts.<br /> <br /> It has been called the most generous city in Canada, and also its most racist.<br /> It is home to fatalistic visionary artists who never get their careers off the prairie ground.<br /> Locals can\u2019t wait to get out of here, and visitors don\u2019t want to leave.<br /> <br /> You can make one thing into another in Winnipeg, and that\u2019s true alchemy.<br /> <br /> <b>Current Player Characters</b><br /> <b>1. </b>@Caladiru : Earth Crisis/Earth-Dies-Screaming/Earth, Recovering Centimanus<br /> <b>2. </b>@Wormwood : Mark 5, Hero with an \u2018F\u2019 in good<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> <i>Thursday, November 3<sup>rd</sup>, 2016<br /> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/iO0aqlP.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Winnipeg, Manitoba</a></i><br /> <br /> Something strange is afoot in the city of Muddy Waters- a thick fog hangs over the entire city, thicker than much of the population has ever seen in their lifetime. As the day waxes on, the locals expect it to dissipate, but it doesn't. For the first time in living memory, the fog holds, it <i>persists</i>. There's a Thing That Must Not Be, so we must be in Winnipeg. The people continue on with their day- they are a people of sweltering heat and freezing cold, a little mist isn't going to keep them from their lives. Terracotta edifices disappear into low-lying clouds as pale streetlights cast small bubbles of incandescence out into the concealing fog.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/manitoba/university-manitoba-strike-picket-march-1.3836215\" target=\"_blank\">Faculty protest corruption on the campus of the University of Manitoba.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/manitoba/health-sciences-centre-locked-down-after-shots-fired-nearby-1.3828759\" target=\"_blank\">The Health Sciences Centre closes after a shoot out at Starbucks.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/manitoba/henderson-shoppers-window-crash-1.3834472\" target=\"_blank\">A car smashed through the storefront of a Shopper's Drug Mart.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.vogue.com/13498484/saskatoon-winnipeg-canada-prairie-travel-guide\" target=\"_blank\">Vogue just released an article praising the city for eclectic, exotic beauty </a><br /> <br /> All in all, a normal day.<br /> <br /> A hundred year journey begins with a single step- where does your Pilgrimage begin?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 11-05-2016, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T11:54:18-07:00","id":998352,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: </b>OOOOOOOOOO | <b>Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 6/12 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b><br /> </div> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/bQqlJpj.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Cold and shame don't really get to her, so she's just wearing boots and jeans and a black racerback top that shows off her Inscription and her hideous countenance. Her rugged backpack full of books and tapes and living supplies is slung over her shoulders, and her hair hangs low and untamed.<br /> <br /> As long as she has the fog on her side, she's headed into the Exchange District today. Hopefully Mark 5 is coming along, too. In her experience, this body of hers gets hassled less by Winnipeg humans when it has a man accompanying it, and picking fights isn't her plan today. Instead, she's hoping to do a close investigation of the alleys and cobblestones for Pilgrim marks and other signs of Created passing through.<br /> <br /> <i>Intelligence or Wits + Investigation, I roll a chance die either way. <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/453363\" target=\"_blank\">First roll of the campaign, Intelligence+Investigation</a>: <u>1d10h10</u> <b>0</b><br /> <br /> Let's start this off right by making that a dramatic failure for a Beat.</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T20:11:14-07:00","id":998585,"title":"","content":"<b>Earth</b><br /> <br /> Market Square is surprisingly quiet at this time of day. No one in the nearby offices or college campus have gone on break, and no one has gone to get lunch at the various restaurants and coffee shops that surround you. The air smells like used cigarettes and mouldering leaves, and a strange undercurrent of floral perfume as the fog lies heavy across the streets, occluding the normally welcoming architecture that had aged so carefully into a gandfatherly air, but now the wrought iron fire escapes and balcony railings jut out like teeth from stone edifices. It's limestone, ocean stone, so different from the gorgeous red sandstone of your birthplace... so much colder. You darken the doorway of <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/maps/@49.8975361,-97.1402791,3a,75y,85.65h,86.61t/data=!3m6!1e1!3m4!1slLPF_azKUEQMlTX-RsgWTw!2e0!7i13312!8i6656!6m1!1e1\" target=\"_blank\">92 Albert Street</a>, catching a glimpse of some graffiti. A lone woman walks by across the street, looking at something on her phone, oblivious to all the world.<br /> <br /> You can read the alchemical symbolism clearly. The warped, multi-faceted face with the heavy brows and judgemental eyes is a Hekatonkheir, a Hundred-Handed One, a Centimanus. The hourglass is a symbol of heaven joining with earth, obviously intended to stand in for the airy nature of the sanguine Dead Girl and the heavy stone of Earth's own melancholic humour. The 'Fuck Off!' was likely there before, but the stencil below... that was put down at the same time. Ominous words- &quot;YOUR END WILL COME&quot; -in bold letters. There was a finality to that statement. The vaguely American Southwestern iconography that surrounded it offered dangerous hints.<br /> <br /> It seemed that even amongst her own people, Earth was an outcast. She couldn't run from what she'd done at the Grand Canyon.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Earth gains a Beat from the Dramatic Failure and gains the Alienated Condition. Her reading of what is purely mortal graffiti with a veneer of her own past is giving the illusion that the local Created know who she is, and want her out of here. Or, worse, that someone has followed her from Arizona.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 11-05-2016, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T22:21:01-07:00","id":998619,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Alienated<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: </b>OOOOOOOOOO | <b>Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 6/12 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div><br /> <br /> <br /> What in the world was so interesting about those phones? What were they looking at all the time? She hadn't actually held one in her hands before, so it was a complete mystery to her.<br /> <br /> Alchemical graffiti, <i>that </i>she understood. Her face darkened as she recognized the obvious message. Her Repute preceded her, as always. She thought about defacing the tag, finding a broken bottle or a chunk of brick and tearing up the painted surface- but no, not yet. That could wait. It's better to let revenge cook for a while, until you find someone to take it out on.<br /> <br /> Instead, she growled and climbed onto a dumpster to get a handhold on the bottom rung of an access ladder. At least she knew she was in an area with recent Created traffic. She continued the search for other Pilgrim Marks in the area, this time climbing onto rooftops and into out of the way urban crevices humans couldn't easily reach. AC units, fire escapes, spots that could only be seen from a certain angle in a certain light.<br /> <br /> <i><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/453518\" target=\"_blank\">Strength+Athletics</a>: <u>8d10h8</u> <b>2 </b>[should have been 7 dice, ignore that last die]</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 11-05-2016, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T03:51:59-07:00","id":998684,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> As usually, Mark 5 was atop of things, running over the roofs towards the point Earth had wanted to meet up. He was late because he beat up a mugger or something like a mugger. Wearing just a black shirt, jogging pants and some old running sneakers, he wasn't fashionable, but practically dressed. He wasn't wearing his mask, so he didn't go as Rockbreaker at the moment.<br /> Running around on rooftops was also a nice opportunity to improve on his Parkour, so when he noticed someone 'intruding' in his realm, he slid down a water pipe to meet up.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=894a13fe\" target=\"_blank\">Dexterity+Athletics: 2 sux</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T20:41:40-07:00","id":999043,"title":"","content":"<b>Earth &amp; Mark 5</b><br /> <br /> The youthful-looking Titan sailed across the rooftops, the sound of heavy footsteps perplexing the humans who lived in the apartments and artisan's lofts that were being leased above the storefronts. The fog swirled around him, parting before his vigorous motion. Even without the active application of alchemy, Mark 5 was an image of natural physical prowess and grace. There aren't manyregions in Winnipeg where you could get away with leaping between rooftops. Most would-be parkour practitioners in the city either ran through either side of the Exchange District, or they found themselves a forest and leapt through the trees.<br /> <br /> From up on the rooftops you can see the occasional car pass by, looping lazily around the intersecting streets. A moving van pulls up to the Winnipeg Film Group theatre, Cinemathique, and begins unloading pallets of soda and boxes of chocolate bars. An East Indian couple sidesteps some of the workmen on their way to a children's furniture store. The woman is carrying a baby in a cloth wrap, the little homunculus bouncing in time to their mother's stride, gazing in wonder at the world around them with uncomprehending, fuzzy vision.<br /> <br /> Mark is familiar with the area himself. The Exchange is, along with a centre of arts and culture, a nightlife hub in Winnipeg. It's also close enough to the North End that every once in a while, something unsavoury goes down. <a href=\"http://www.metronews.ca/news/winnipeg/2016/11/01/winnipeg-halloween-fight-video-goes-viral.html\" target=\"_blank\">Halloween night he was walking up Main Street when a woman was clotheslined by some passing brute who'd started fighting with a man nearby</a>. One of the men valiantly threw himself at the assailant, hurtling him into the street. They were sloppy, unskilled, graceless. Mark 5 had ended the battle easily, even without alchemy, handily flattening both of them in quick succession. He's still not quite sure what he did to frighten the nearby crowd of humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T23:50:28-07:00","id":999091,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Alienated<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: </b>OOOOOOOOOO | <b>Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 6/12 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div><br /> She was still shook from the ominous graffiti when Mark 5 caught up to her, sitting on a fire escape, looking for more weirdness in the alley. She just grunted to acknowledge him, no eye contact.<br /> <br /> &quot;There's more of us in the neighborhood. They know I'm here, and they don't want me. Left a message to scare me off.&quot;<br /> <br /> She waved in the direction of the offending mural.<br /> <br /> &quot;Whatever. If they want me, they'll feel my radiance and come get me. But there's supposed to be older pilgrim marks around here, too. If we can find some, maybe there's treasure. Or trouble. Better than hanging around being hungry, anyway.&quot;<br /> <br /> She still hadn't looked him in the eye, but she relaxed a little as she sniffed the air. &quot;Weird fog today. Think it's haunted?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T05:21:07-08:00","id":999175,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 5/10 <br /> Beats: 0/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b><br /> </div> <br /> Not for the first or last time, Adonis shakes his head at what a strange city Winnipeg is. The humans seem to claw at each other here out of anger and desperation. Don't they realize that won't help them? He keeps his head down as he walks, relying on the power of Assimilate to mask his movement through the crowds. This way, he's just another person to them. <br /> <br /> His thoughts wander to Lily. He wonders what she's up to. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>Has she moved on? Has she found someone new? </i></span>He didn't ask her to stay loyal to him, nor him to her, but he still remembers her smiling down on him when he pleased her in some way. The touch of her skin on his... He shakes himself. <i><span style=\"color:#00ff00\">\u200bDon't stay stuck in place. You're still friends. That's better for you now. </span></i>Lily hadn't been upset with him when he told her he needed to move on. She had just given him a kiss on the cheek and told him to come to her if he needed anything. And it was true- but he didn't need Lily to guide him and train him anymore. He needed somebody to call a companion. Lilly couldn't be that to him... could she?<br /> <br /> The fog is thick tonight, thicker than usual. Is it somehow different tonight? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T09:07:46-08:00","id":999246,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> Mark 5 greeted Earth with a nod, then silently watched her before he turned his gaze towards the mural and the surrounding area. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;They want a fight, they get it.&quot; </span>He looked down, at the streets, then he shook his head and added <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Don't know about the fog. Definitely not normal. But don't know about haunted. Be right back.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> With this, he went to investigate the mural and it's supposed message.<br /> <br /> <br /> __________________________________________________ __________________________________________________<br /> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=5deba802\" target=\"_blank\">Wits+investigation 0 sux</a><br /> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=73302df4\" target=\"_blank\">going with intelligence wouldn't have made a difference, either.</a><br /> welp. Let's turn that into a dramatic failure, too, just so we have two dangerous Prometheans acting on complete misconceptions ^^&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T11:42:51-08:00","id":999350,"title":"","content":"<b>Adonis</b><br /> <br /> A walk down <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/maps/place/Portage+Place+Shopping+Centre/@49.8930025,-97.1497778,16z/data=!4m5!3m4!1s0x52ea73e2a02afa61:0x48c9bdc8c2a4d306!8m2!3d49.8929887!4d-97.1477179\" target=\"_blank\">Portage Avenue</a> was benefitted by the quiet, subtle alchemy of the Alembics at work in the Muse's body, but even without the Azoth-aided instinct to step where no one would be standing, it became fairly clear to Adonis that no one would have hassled him along the way. People went out of their way to avoid eye contact with one another, keenly aware that for all the polite veneer of storefronts and office buildings, downtown Winnipeg was something of a hollowed out husk, with a few oases of life, like the Exchange District, or Broadway. Along either side of Portage Avenue, unkempt beggars sit in ragged parkas with cardboard signs. The seasons are harsh on the homeless in Winnipeg. The man you just stepped past, as invisible to the crowds as you would be if you charged your Alembic, stretches out two completely fingerless hands. One side of his face is a mess of pale skin, an ear completely missing, his hair fallen out in clumps, eyebrows and eyelashes gone. He might have appeared to be Native American, at one point.<br /> <br /> Eventually, Adonis takes a turn up <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/maps/place/Oxford+Hotel+(Man)+Ltd/@49.8954112,-97.1429092,17z/data=!3m1!4b1!4m5!3m4!1s0x52ea715bea9943ff:0xfe8f762026e02b39!8m2!3d49.8954112!4d-97.1407205\" target=\"_blank\">Notre Dame, passing the Solid Gold strip club in the Oxford Hotel</a> he'd heard about every so often from Lily or her friends before taking another sharp right and wandering up Albert Street into Market Square. The fog is doing fascinating things to the cobblestone streets and terracotta tenements, making them damp with condensed dew. You can hear twenties swing music playing at half speed, emanating from one of the upper windows in a decaying apartment block. A small shack of a diner called White Star slumps next to it, the red paint on its walls valiantly trying to keep up appearances.<br /> <br /> He comes into Market Square to enjoy the solitude and quiet of the park, away from the stifling presence of human crowds.<br /> <br /> <b>Earth &amp; Mark 5</b><br /> <br /> Primed, perhaps, by Earth's own conviction, Mark 5 follows their translation of the alchemical symbolism present in the graffiti. This presents an opportunity to the Titan and the Fury, a chance to direct their martial prowess upon a potentially worthy foe. However, a thought crosses his mind. If this Promethean followed Earth all the way from Arizona, surely they had been wronged, perhaps even lost loved ones, to the horror that was Earth-Dies-Screaming. He likes Earth, and finds their efforts to be good fascinating, but don't their victims deserve justice as well? Who does the Soldier fight for? Who does the Martyr die for? It's an... unsettling question to be sure, one that will likely plague his strongly polarized moral compass for quite some time.<br /> <br /> However, the two Prometheans can feel something at their edge of their awareness. <br /> <br /> Something is coming. Something heavy with the Flame Immortal. <br /> <br /> Poor, foolish Created- you've fallen into a trap.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Mark 5 takes a Beat and gains the Alienated Condition. Everyone rolls Wits + Azoth to detect Azothic Radiance, including Adonis. Realistically, Adonis should have sensed Earth from several blocks away, but they're close enough now that they can <b>all </b>sense one another. Unless, of course, Adonis decided to store his Azoth in his Hovel (wherever that may be) in which case he isn't giving off Radiance of any kind right now.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T12:45:46-08:00","id":999375,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 5/10 <br /> Beats: 0/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> Quiet. As much as he wants to be around people, people don't give quiet enough credit. The solitude reminds him of his trip here from Ontario, weeks and months of wandering the roads, hitchhiking with strangers as far as Disquiet would permit them. <br /> <br /> He's about to settle in for some sullen contemplation when something draws his attention. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>Azoth? </i></span><br /> <br /> [Adonis attempts to detect Azothic Radiance. Wits 2 + Azoth 2 = 4 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/453970\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>.[/spoiler]<br /> <br /> Yes, two other Created. His mood perks up. He rarely encounters other Created in person. He'll follow the Radiance to its source and speak to them. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>Hopefully they're in a talking mood. </i></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T13:08:39-08:00","id":999388,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Alienated<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Titan made a face. A rather ugly face. This... conflict was uncomfortable. He avoided to look Earth in the eyes.<span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Looks like you were right.&quot; </span>He gave the city a long, hard lookand mumbled something under his breath. Conceivably, it was a challenge to the world at large.<br /> He was never one to wait long for a challenge to appear. Before long, he was going to seek it out.<br /> Then, he noticed another Azothic Radiance. Looks like the locals didn't waste much time at least. Less time to contemplate, more time to just act.<br /> <br /> He reached out his hand to Earth, to help her get up. She didn't need the help, yeah sure. Still, it was a gesture of... of what, actually? <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;You coming?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> __________________________________________________ __________________________________________________<br /> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=3a4b3205\" target=\"_blank\">Wits+Azoth- 1 sux</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T13:47:09-08:00","id":999412,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Alienated<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: </b>OOOOOOOOOO | <b>Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 6/12 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <i><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/453996\" target=\"_blank\">Wits+Azoth</a>: <u>6d10h8</u> <b>4</b></i><br /> <br /> In the mood she was in, she didn't take his hand. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I'm coming.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She hoisted herself up and soon felt her Fire roar. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;You feel that too? Bet that's our guy.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> It was hard to say whether the Titan would stand by her if it came to blows. They hadn't known each other that long, and there were many reasons to hate and fear her, many of which she repeated to herself in her sleep. She wasn't sure whether she could take him in a fight, either. But hopefully they could at least close ranks against a stranger.<br /> <br /> When Adonis came into sight, she looked him dead in the eye and slammed one fist against the offending graffiti. She pointed fingers at him that crackled with electricity. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;That's the one. Get over here, pretty boy. You painted this, huh?&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T14:45:34-08:00","id":999442,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 5/10<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;That's the one. Get over here, pretty boy. You painted this, huh?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> It's a Created alright. Two, actually. One he knows: Mach 5. The other one...<br /> <br /> His heart drops into his feet. <i><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">It's </span></i><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">her. </span>Earth, the Tammuz. The former Centimanus. Her name has been whispered among the Created. The dead drops they usually use to communicate with each other have told of her coming, and the rumors have been swirling about what she did as a Hundred-Handed One. <br /> <br /> He looks at the graffiti Earth was referring to.<br /> <br /> [Wits 2 + Investigation 0 = chance dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/454006\" target=\"_blank\">how is this possible</a>?[/spoiler]<br /> <br /> Then he looks back at the angry Tammuz, eyes spooked and his hands up. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Um... no? Look, um- Earth, right? I'm not sure this thing has anything to do with you. This is... just graffiti.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> He looks over at Mach 5 and spreads his arms, pleading for backup. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Come on, Mach 5. Back me up. Am I smart enough to come up with something like this?&quot; </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T18:50:36-08:00","id":999521,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Alienated<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: </b>OOOOOOOOOO | <b>Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 6/12 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Um... no? Look, um- Earth, right?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;In the flesh.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;I'm not sure this thing has anything to do with you. This is... just graffiti.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Not the reaction she expected. She let the lightning dissipate. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;No. Look.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She spread the gnarled and warty fingers of her right hand across the tagged wall, channeling her inner art critic.<br /> <br /> The face looking in multiple directions at once: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Hundred faces, hundred hands. Centimani.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The hourglass with the bottom filled up. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Sand and sky. Earth and air. Me and- <span style=\"font-size:9px\">you know, Her.</span>&quot;</span><br /> <br /> A stick figure that vaguely resembled a kokopelli. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Arizona. Where I came from.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Her fingers curled around a rogue <i>'fuck off' </i>and moved on to the more recent-looking <b>'YOUR END WILL COME.' </b><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I <i>know</i> a threat when I see one. I <i>know</i> the stories they tell about me.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Come on, Mach 5. Back me up. Am I smart enough to come up with something like this?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She narrowed her eyes at her fellow Tammuz. The whole world allayed against her. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;You <i>know</i> this one?&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T21:31:29-08:00","id":999565,"title":"","content":"Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Alienated<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> <br /> <br /> Brown eyes narrowed as the offering hand was ignored. His help being rejected by humans was something he was used to. It still hurt, but it's bearable. But having another created's back and being treated the same? That was bitter. He just nodded when Earth noticed the other Azothic Radiance. Something to take out these feelings on would be nice. He still wasn't sure whether he'd help Earth or her former victims. Maybe neither?<br /> With these thoughts clouding his mind, he silently came along. When Adonis came into view, his expression changed from sour to confusion.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;You <i>know</i> this one?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Kind of. It's the pretty boy. Didn't know he's from Arizona.&quot;</span> He looked at Adonis, pointing at the mural. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;I know <u>this</u> certainly wasn't smart.&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 11-07-2016, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T08:07:00-08:00","id":999746,"title":"","content":"<b>Earth, Mark 5, and Adonis</b><br /> <br /> Tensions are rising in Old Market Square. The Muse seems to be on the receiving end of hostility from both Tammuz, but how long before the two Named turn against each other? The fog swirls dangerously, static electricity crackling in the air in that holds the tension of an impending thunderclap. It wouldn't take a lot of Divine Fire for this to turn ugly. All it needs is for Earth to be willing to vent her wrath in a manner befitting the king of Olympus. Adonis is unsteady in the face of Earth. Her Radiance is... cleaner than it has been, but still crackling with her Torment and hate, and the acrid taste of Flux still boils just beneath the surface, and as one of the Created, he can see her right hand for what it is, a gnarled talon grotesquely bound with cords of muscle; the last of Earth-Dies-Screaming's hundred hands.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Everyone can roll Wits + Empathy to judge if anyone is lying... and what else they may be feeling. Earth and Mark 5 make this roll at a -2 penalty because of the Alienated Condition.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 11-07-2016, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T08:12:57-08:00","id":999751,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Alienated<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <a href=\"http://http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=2542ee18\" target=\"_blank\">Oh oh.... 0 sux =D (3-1-2)</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T09:25:09-08:00","id":999785,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Alienated<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: </b>OOOOOOOOOO | <b>Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 6/12 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <i>Resolving Alienated to auto-fail the Wits+Empathy roll and take a Beat.</i><br /> <br /> So they <i>do </i>know each other. Figures it was all a trick. When you're a Fury, it doesn't take much of a spark to assume the worst in people. She shrugs her backpack off and hurls it a ways down the alley to keep her books and tools safe. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;This whole city's full of liars and tricksters. Winnipeg <i>weaklings.</i> Here's what I think of your <i>art.</i>&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <i>Spending 2 Pyros to charge Arc, flaring Disfigurements. Then activating Spark with the Shock effect to hit everything within 3 yards, especially including the graffiti on the wall. Dexterity+Athletics+Azoth+3 willpower, 10 dice:</i> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/454240\" target=\"_blank\"><i>failure.</i></a> <i>Maybe that's for the best.</i><br /> <br /> Lightning arcs and sizzles around her body, the charge builds, and...nothing happens. The charge shorts out in a puff of acrid smoke. Earth brutally self-owns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 11-07-2016, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T10:20:49-08:00","id":999800,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Alienated<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;So that's your true face, huh?&quot;</span> he spit at Earth when the lightning sizzled, his voice thick with boiling anger.<br /> <br /> You can try to play Mark 5. You can attack him, shoot at him, stab him in the leg, and he won't take offense to it.<br /> But calling him a weakling is a horrible mistake. Even more so if all <i>you </i>are is a horribly evil monster. Sure, Earth said she tried to &quot;atone for her sins&quot;, but those are just words. Words are nothing.<br /> Actions speak loudest, and her attempt to attack him speaks a VERY clear message. He was going to reply in kind.<br /> And after Earth was down, he'd have a talk with the pretty kid. A non-verbal, punchy talk.<br /> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=2bff21dd\" target=\"_blank\">Brawl+Strength 3 Sux</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T10:27:22-08:00","id":999802,"title":"","content":"<b>Earth, Mark 5, and Adonis</b><br /> <br /> Lightning flares about Earth before vanishing in an acrid cloud; sound and fury signifying nothing except that she's willing to fight for her right to exist in peace. Her initial lash may have been ineffectual, but it was a warning shot- the lightning is there to answer her if only she stretches out her hand. The yelling and the arguments, even the physical blows, aren't any worse than what the local shopkeepers are used to hearing and seeing from the vagrants who occasionally use Market Square as a place to smoke up and howl obscenities at their unfair existence, it's even downright civil as far as they can tell. No 'bitch' this, no 'fuck you' that... the thunderclap that caused a brown-out around the block is new.<br /> <br /> Some store owners are coming to the windows or half-stepping out their doors, trying to see if the peculiar fog has transformed into a thunderstorm. People tend to mind their own business in downtown Winnipeg, but if things escalate any further turning a blind eye won't make them feel any safer- the police from their headquarters two blocks away will.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: If you're going to escalate this into a Brawl you should roll Initiative. Earth takes 3 Bashing Damage, which, thanks to the Imperatus Alembic, will have healed up in about 22 minutes.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 11-07-2016, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T12:48:53-08:00","id":999896,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker, Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 5/10<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Kind of. It's the pretty boy. Didn't know he's from Arizona.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Adonis gets even more confused- and that's a rare thing. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Um... I came here from Ontario.' </span><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000080\">I know <u>this</u> certainly wasn't smart.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> Adonis looks from one Named to the other, his eyes growing wider with fear. What the hell is going on here? Do they just want to bash on the cute guy, or did he miss something in what looked like normal graffiti? <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis attempts to determine if Earth and Mark 5 are being honest, and if Earth's anger is faked to justify her antagonism or if she really thinks he did it. I would argue that his Specialty in Emotions should count here. Wits 2 + Empathy 3 + Specialty 1 = 6 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/454293\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He becomes more frantic as he sees Earth throw her backpack aside. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;This whole city's full of liars and tricksters. Winnipeg </span><i>weaklings.</i><span style=\"color:#DAA520\"> Here's what I think of your </span><i>art.</i><span style=\"color:#daa520\">&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Look. Earth. I get that you're upset, but this wasn't me. And I'm not even sure what this-&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He visibly flinches as she charges her Alembic, but blinks when it fails- and causes a brown-out around the block. He winces. If he's learned anything about humans, it's that they don't like unexpected changes in their situation, and act quickly and violently against the source of that interruption. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;So that's your true face, huh?&quot; </span>Mark 5 didn't take well to Earth's outburst, and slugs her. <br /> <br /> Adonis gives a bereaved sigh. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Aw, fuck me.&quot; </span>He walks up to the two Tammuz, and throws an arm around each of them. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Come on, you two! Let's get you sobered up!&quot; </span>He saids it loudly, for the benefit of any people who may be watching, and then he lowers his voice to an angry hiss.<span style=\"color:#00ff00\"> &quot;We <i>so </i>do not have time for this shit! Police HQ is right down the street, how do you think they would react to seeing three Created throwing down? They would start reenacting <i>Frankenstein, </i>but with SWAT cars and shotguns instead of torches and pitchforks. Let's go somewhere so that we can talk about this.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis is going to try and make Mark 5 and Earth calm down. Manipulation 3 + Persuasion 3 = 6 dice-&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/454300\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>. Crisis averted- for now.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T13:30:05-08:00","id":999921,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged<br /> Alembics: Arc (2), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: </b>BBBOOOOOOO | <b>Willpower: 4/5 | Pyros: 4/12 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> Mark 5 sends her stumbling and crashing into the wall. The dude can <i>hit</i>. That's Vitality for you. She growls and readies another charge, when Adonis steps in:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;We <i>so </i>do not have time for this shit! Police HQ is right down the street, how do you think they would react to seeing three Created throwing down? They would start reenacting <i>Frankenstein, </i>but with SWAT cars and shotguns instead of torches and pitchforks. Let's go somewhere so that we can talk about this.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Stupid Muses, always trying to break up a fight before it gets good. She looks from Adonis to Mark 5, then holds up her empty palms in surrender. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Fine. Where?&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T21:46:10-08:00","id":1000141,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Alienated<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;We <i>so </i>do not have time for this shit! Police HQ is right down the street, how do you think they would react to seeing three Created throwing down? They would start reenacting <i>Frankenstein, </i>but with SWAT cars and shotguns instead of torches and pitchforks. Let's go somewhere so that we can talk about this.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ugh. The boy had a point. He threw Earth a dark look, and grumbled something about snakes. Then he sighed and nodded.<span style=\"color:#000080\"> &quot;Fine. Lead the way.&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 11-08-2016, 04:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T04:58:10-08:00","id":1000222,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 5/10<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis gives a small sigh of relief. He really didn't expect that to work. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;This way.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> He leads them with some speed away from Old Market Square, to a vacant lot with no windows or doors looking down into it, and illuminated by the faint glow of a streetlight. In the murk of the corner furthest from the light, he turns to face the Tammuz. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Okay. So. I guess you two have already met each other.&quot; </span>He puts a spread hand on his chest. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">\u200b&quot;I had <i>nothing </i>to do with that graffiti. I honestly didn't see anything that specifically pointed to you, Earth. But I may not have been looking at find something.&quot; </span>He tries to keep his ideas nice and neutral. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Or maybe this fog has something to do with it. Maybe it screws with how you see things. Because you're both pretty sure about what you saw, and <i>I'm </i>pretty </span><span style=\"color:#00ff00\">sure about what I saw. We can't both be right, yeah?&quot;</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T05:46:26-08:00","id":1000236,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Mark 5</span><br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Alienated<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Noticed I hadn't included a picture yet. This is approximately how you can envision Mark 5:<br /> <img src=\"http://images.tapology.com/headshot_images/4752/large/Mike-Bronzoulis-hs.jpg?1389585800\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div></b></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Okay. So. I guess you two have already met each other.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Met - yes. But do we know each other? Not sure anymore&quot; </span>the Soldier said with more than a hint of reproach.<br /> <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Or maybe this fog has something to do with it. Maybe it screws with how you see things. Because you're both pretty sure about what you saw, and <i>I'm </i>pretty sure about what I saw. We can't both be right, yeah?&quot;</span><br /> This caused some very wide eyes. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;You think the fog... changes <b>thoughts</b>? How?&quot;</span> This idea was more than just a little unsettling. For as long as he could remember, his body was the tool of his will. He could steel his body to deal with physical threats, no problem. However, the mere idea of something being able to attack his thoughts, lead his actions, was horrifying.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  Copied the Name-Speech colour idea from Adonis 11-08-2016, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T07:23:08-08:00","id":1000261,"title":"","content":"<b>Earth, Mark 5, and Adonis</b><br /> <br /> The three Created quickly move up Bannatyne, out of Market Square, and round the corner up Princess street, <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/maps/@49.8982631,-97.1423533,19.4z\" target=\"_blank\">ending up in the darkened loading bay of a children's furniture store</a>, behind a semi trailer awaiting attention from the skeleton crew of the store's staff. They can hear the distant music of indie pop from a restaurant up the street. Despite the close quarters of the Exchange, round a block and you can almost disappear into a different world. For all the facts that the distance is fairly short, it <i>feels </i>significantly longer, and people act accordingly. Headlights from passing cars cast bright spots and long shadows along the wall, highlighting additional graffiti.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: If anyone wants, you can roll to try and find Pilgrim Marks of one kind or another. Wits + Composure - 2 due to darkness and fog, or Wits + Investigation -2 for the same.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T07:34:09-08:00","id":1000265,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Mark 5</span><br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Alienated<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b><br /> </div> <br /> His mind on other matters, Mark 5 did not notice any Pilgrim Marks. Maybe that's for the best...?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=f32a3530\" target=\"_blank\">0 sux</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 11-08-2016, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T09:11:04-08:00","id":1000292,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged<br /> Alembics: Arc (2), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: BBBOOOOOOO | Willpower: 4/5 | Pyros: 4/12 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">wits+composure-2, <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/454552\" target=\"_blank\">fail</a><br /> edit: I rolled 3 dice and I should have rolled 4, here's the extra die: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/454580\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a><br /> The trip wasn't a total bust after all!</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Backpack retrieved, Earth follows them to the neutral ground behind the loading dock, keeping an eye out for Pilgrim Marks on the way.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Told you the fog was haunted.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She turns the matter over on her tongue, like a persistent jawbreaker. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Azoth calls to Azoth. You knew I was volatile, but we still decided to stick together a couple weeks ago when I blew into town. No grudge. I've taken a lot of hits.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Maybe you didn't paint it, pretty boy. You're not acting like you would if you did. Maybe it was someone else in town, or an angel. Point is: I know the Created here heard all the stories, and they don't want me around. But I ain't like that no more. I just wanna pay my dues and stick around folks who get that I'm just Earth now.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 11-08-2016, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T12:23:18-08:00","id":1000379,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 5/10<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><br /> </div> <span style=\"color:#daa520\">&quot;Maybe you didn't paint it, pretty boy. You're not acting like you would if you did. Maybe it was someone else in town, or an angel. Point is: I know the Created here heard all the stories, and they don't want me around. But I ain't like that no more. I just wanna pay my dues and stick around folks who get that I'm just Earth now.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> \u200bAdonis spreads his arms again. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Hey, I get that. I mean, I've heard the rumors about what went down. But if you say you're on the level now...&quot; He shrugs. &quot;I believe you. For what it's worth.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Adonis takes a moment to look around at the walls of the loading bay, looking for Pilgrim Marks. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Wits 2 + Composure 2 - Fog 2 = 2 dice -&gt; 0 successes. Let's go ahead and make that a Dramatic Failure for a Beat.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Hey, what's this?...&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T12:34:59-08:00","id":1000381,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Mark 5</span><br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Alienated<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Told you the fog was haunted.&quot;</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Haunted is one thing. This? This is way worse!&quot; </span>Mark 5 tried to hide the fact how much this was unsettling him.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Azoth calls to Azoth. You knew I was volatile, but we still decided to stick together a couple weeks ago when I blew into town. No grudge. I've taken a lot of hits.&quot; </span><br /> Mark 5 didn't like it, but it was true. He made a decision, and he always went through with what he decided on. No matter if the way there was steep. In fact, that's how he liked them.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;True enough. As promised, I'll stick around and help you become less volatile. No grudges.&quot; </span><i>But I'll keep an eye on you.</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Hey, what's this?...&quot; </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Huh? What did you find?&quot;</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T07:52:01-08:00","id":1000786,"title":"","content":"<b>Earth, Mark 5, &amp; Adonis</b><br /> <br /> The Muse notices a <a href=\"http://www.feelnumb.com/wp-content/uploads/2011/02/amalgamation.gif\" target=\"_blank\">symbol</a> on the side of the trailer that they're standing beside, painted in a sharp black and outlined in a beautiful gold paint that might actually be mixed with gold dust or shredded gold leaf. There are no other distinguishing features on the trailer, and the rest of the loading bay is suspiciously clear of any kind of graffiti or markings. This isn't a Pilgrim Mark, you're certain of that, but there's a feeling, echoing somewhere in Azothic Memory, that you <i>know </i>what this symbol means.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Alright, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> you get a Beat and the Spooked Condition, which can be Resolved by pursuing this avenue of investigation. Anyone who wants to can roll Wits + Occult to identify the symbol, if they want to.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T08:57:53-08:00","id":1000822,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Mark 5</span><br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Alienated<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b><br /> </div> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=a455b041\" target=\"_blank\">Nope</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T10:05:52-08:00","id":1000860,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/454818\" target=\"_blank\">wits 3+occult 3</a>: <u>6d10h8</u> <b>1</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T10:28:28-08:00","id":1000871,"title":"","content":"<b>Earth</b><br /> <br /> The symbol painted on the semi trailer is the alchemical sign for amalgamation. In metallurgy, an amalgam is Mercury mixed with any other metal into a solid, and the Refinement Mercurius is the Refinement of Pyros. The symbol would suggest that whoever owns this semi trailer is involved in using alchemy in some way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T11:24:17-08:00","id":1000907,"title":"","content":"Earth explains this information to Mark 5 and Adonis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T17:02:29-08:00","id":1001079,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Spooked<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 5/10<br /> Beats: 1/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b><br /> </div> <br /> The revelation of the sign rattles Adonis. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Shit. Alchemists?&quot; </span>He looks around. He's never had the displeasure of dealing with an alchemist, but he knows them by reputation: mad bastards who try to mess with Pyros and get messed up in the head by it. Some of them are supposed to be decent, but the majority like to cut open Created to try and steal the Vitriol they contain.<br /> <br /> His eyes narrow and he looks at the others. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">\u200b&quot;Do you think we should warn the others?&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T01:21:16-08:00","id":1001245,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Alienated<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> &quot;Do you think we should warn the others?&quot;*<br /> <br /> The Soldier looked grim. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot; What we SHOULD do is take care of him.&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  Colour 11-10-2016, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T04:57:13-08:00","id":1001313,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Spooked<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 5/10<br /> Beats: 1/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> Mark 5's suggestion makes Adonis' face twist in displeasure. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Um, I'm a Mimic. I'm not exactly sure going around and killing humans is a good move for me.&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T10:11:26-08:00","id":1001395,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Alienated<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> &quot; Um, I'm a Mimic. I'm not exactly sure going around and killing humans is a good move for me.&quot;*<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Ugh. Of course. But listen, you do not have to do it, you can just help us FIND him. We'll take care of the rest&quot;</span> he tried to persuade Adonis.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I would opt to auto fail that roll to Resolve Alienated, if that's okay. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Right, Earth?&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  colour 11-10-2016, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T12:05:21-08:00","id":1001418,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged<br /> Alembics: Arc (2), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: BBBOOOOOOO | Willpower: 4/5 | Pyros: 4/12 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> A lightbulb goes on over her head (metaphorically, you have to specify with Electrification.) This is a great opportunity to be a Vigilante!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Mark's got it figured out. Warn the rest if you want. You two are about the only Created I know around here, even if my reputation got here first.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She pounds her fists together, and sparks fly. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Either way, we're taking care of it. Let's see what we got in here.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <i>Strength 4+Larceny 1 to forcefully break into the trailer, finding a brick or something to help if needed. 5 dice: </i><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/455082\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T12:32:32-08:00","id":1001429,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Spooked<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 5/10<br /> Beats: 1/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis breathes a sigh of relief. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Alright. I'll help you find him. If we need to ask any questions, just leave it to me.&quot; </span>He flashes a charming smile, but not before his eyes dart around, fearing the sudden appearance of an alchemist- or worse, multiple alchemists- in their midst. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T13:51:04-08:00","id":1001474,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Alienated<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)</b><br /> </div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Either way, we're taking care of it. Let's see what we got in here.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Atta girl!&quot;</span> he said, looking forward to the simplicity of the task. Find evil bastard, do him in - lot's of people saved (even if they'd never know). The end. And the best part: He could do it through fighting. Fighting to protect the peace - if this wasn't what being a Soldier meant, he had no clue about it at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T09:51:20-08:00","id":1001818,"title":"","content":"<b>Earth, Mark 5, &amp; Adonis</b><br /> <br /> The trailer opens easily- it's a semi trailer, not a safe -and the door rolls up dramatically. Headlights from passing cars flood into the room at periodic intervals, reminding the Created within that this space is visible to those outside, even if they <i>are </i>on the opposite side of the room from the door. What they find inside is... not what they expected. The trailer is refrigerated, for the most part, and filled with pallets and pallets of little vials that are marked in a tidy mixture of medical terminology and alchemical symbolism.<br /> <br /> Some of the liquids in the vials are simply clear, others are red, others are greenish-black, others are blue, and some are the colour of dried blood. There are containers full of capsules and powders, assorted glassware, and some seriously heavy-duty containers marked, in no uncertain terms, as a biohazard.<br /> <br /> The scientific terminology isn't terribly clear to this group of Created, but the alchemical symbolism... that's another story. One of the larger containers marked as a biohazard, a long, low rectangle, like a casket, has a red light that started blinking on the side of it.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Mark 5 gets a Beat from resolving Alienated. So far, everyone has two Beats, so we're moving forwards nicely. Roll Wits + Science or Wits + Occult to decipher the symbolism on the different vials and packages. Using different Skills will get you different information. Everyone roll Wits + Composure.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T14:05:30-08:00","id":1001926,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged<br /> Alembics: Arc (2), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: BBBOOOOOOO | Willpower: 4/5 | Pyros: 4/12 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> It's so <i>clean </i>in here. It's weird. Alchemy is an act of flesh and soul and bubbling Vitriol, not glass and refrigeration. It feels to her like the three of them are under a microscope.<br /> <br /> Seeing the heavy box with a biohazard sign and ominous blinking light makes her skin crawl. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Pandoran in there,&quot;</span> she warns. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Maybe. Don't drop your guard. Maybe lower that door, too.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Some of these symbols look familiar. She examines them closely, keeping an eye on the blinking box. Especially interested in finding any books or written material lying around.<br /> <br /> <i><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/455326\" target=\"_blank\">Wits+Composure</a>: <u>6d10h8</u> <b>4</b><br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/455328\" target=\"_blank\">Wits+Occult</a>: <u>6d10h8</u> <b>2</b><br /> Also just making sure that we're the only sources of Azothic Radiance in this trailer. <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/455330\" target=\"_blank\">Wits+Azoth</a>: <u>6d10h8</u> <b>2</b></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T16:32:25-08:00","id":1001972,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Spooked<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 5/10<br /> Beats: 1/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> Adonis looks about the van. The lights from the road spook him something fierce- as does the clinical nature of the van. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;I thought alchemists were supposed all fumes and bubbling cauldrons. This looks something out of a sci-fi movie.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Pandoran in there. </span><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Maybe.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> Adonis' eyes flick over to the casket and he jerks away from it with a hiss. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Shit. Okay, anybody have any ideas how to deal with that? Torch the van?&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis is going to try and glean information from the van.<br /> <br /> Wits 2 + Composure 2 = 4 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/455355\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>.<br /> <br /> Wits 2 + Occult 1 = 3 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/455356\" target=\"_blank\">1 successes</a>.<br /> <br /> I assume that us investigating the van counts as resolving Spooked?</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 11-12-2016, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T17:16:12-08:00","id":1001992,"title":"","content":"<b><div align=\"center\">Earth</div></b><br /> In response, Earth just holds up two fingers while examining a test tube. Lightning arcs between them like a Tesla coil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T01:38:52-08:00","id":1002155,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Mark 5</span><br /> Conditions: Tenacious<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div><br /> <br /> <br /> Mark 5 looked very carefully around. If there was danger afoot, he'd have to protect the other two (especially the boy), after all.<br /> This whole situation felt wonky. Something about the colors was offputting.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Pandoran in there. </span><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Maybe.&quot; </span><br /> The Tammuz narrowed his eyes. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;If it moves, kill it as fast as you can. No holding back.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> Carefully observing the symbols, he tried to remember if he knew their meaning.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\"><a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=8f0fc99d\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#000080\">4 sux on Wits+Composure = Exceptional Success due to Heart of Clay</span></a><br /> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=29f274c4\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#000080\">1 sux on Wits+ Occult</span></a></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 11-12-2016, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T20:48:39-08:00","id":1002454,"title":"","content":"<b>Earth, Mark 5, &amp; Adonis</b><br /> <br /> The symbols are all immediately recognizable to you, the most well-known alchemical signs for different metals. The different colours correspond to different symbols- blue for cobalt, red for mercury and phosphorus, greenish-black for copper and tin, the one resembling dried blood for iron. You know a little bit about human alchemy, so maybe these are potions? Liquified Distillations of Pyros, Transmutations held in stasis until they're imbibed. That hardly explains all the nonsensical medical jargon though. It's the clear vials that are the biggest shock. They're marked with the symbol for Vitriol.<br /> <br /> Earth's suspicions are confirmed when they find the symbol for Flux etched into each and every biohazard container. More of the containers have begun to flash with cyclopean red eyes, blinking with curiosity at the Created standing about them. They can hear the faint sounds of laboured breathing rising into excited gasps through the thick metal containers, the scrabbling sound of sharpened nails and... other things ...against slick steel. The containers are sealed tight, so the Pandorans within aren't at risk of getting out anytime soon.<br /> <br /> Adonis notices a small lab centre off to one side, complete with gloves, goggles, centrifuge, and protective clothing. It is kept meticulously clean, and appears to be used solely for taking samples and running tests on the inventory. For the first time, you notice a slight chill to the trailer, as if it is moderately refrigerated. Earth manages to find a thick spiral notebook hanging off a hook on one of the walls; it appears to be part inventory, part lab report, part journal, and part thesis. Whoever was responsible for these writings, they've been cooped up here in the trailer for a while, taking orders from someone else. Every page of the notebook is topped with a tidy letterhead marked with the same symbol painted on the trailer, and with a name in bold lettering, Amalgama LTD.<br /> <br /> Mark 5, on the other hand, is alert and aware, and he can hear someone coming up the street, complaining loudly on a phone &quot;... yeah, yeah, there'll be a new truck here in an hour or so. Some furniture store was nice enough to store the trailer for me. Look, I'm not sure about these new compounds we're testing out, they're too reactive, too volatile. What? No- I got the material straight from Tucson, been with the truck the whole way, taking random samples, running tests. They. Don't. Work. Yeah? Tell that to corporate. We're losing contracts to LDI and Cheiron because even if our product is better, the side effects are too unpredictable to make them safe. Fine, whatever. We'll talk when I get this load to the office.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Adonis gets a Beat, having Resolved the Spooked Condition by investigating further. Mark 5 gains the Steadfast Condition. Someone is coming back for the trailer, roll Dexterity + Stealth to conceal yourselves, if that's what you plan on doing.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 01-02-2017, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T04:48:54-08:00","id":1002500,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Mark 5</span><br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Steadfast<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> The unclear noises and imagesfrom the biohazard containers made his stomach feel weird. Sick.<br /> These things were not meant to be, and yet here they were. But what got his blood boiling was the Vitriol. There was only one way to get the real thing, and the implications meant Prometheans in the area had been unsafe, despite his work.<br /> <br /> He was considering how to trash the place when he heard the phonecall outside.<br /> Hearing the approaching Alchemist, (that was him, he was sure of it), he quickly went through their options. He could probably chase him down without trouble, but they'd be seen. And from the sounds of it, he wasn't alone.<br /> There was bigger fish to catch.<br /> The others heard a hissing <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Someone coming. Hide!&quot; </span>as he picked a place where he wouldn't be visible, bent on ambushing the target.<br /> He had questions, and he was going to get some answers.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=9b271d1e\" target=\"_blank\">1 sux on Dext+Stealth</a><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T07:49:26-08:00","id":1002527,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 5/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis tilts his head. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#00ff00\">Amalgama LTD...&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Someone coming. Hide!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Adonis' head whips up towards the back of the van. He gets ready to hide, but then he gets another idea. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;You guys wait here.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> He quickly jumps out of the van and feigns a buzzed swagger, and walks right up to the alchemist. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Oh hey there. You lost too?&quot; </span>He leans in close to the alchemist, his face friendly and showing extreme interest. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Hey, you're pretty cute. You doing anything right now?&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis is going to try and distract the alchemist with a Seduction roll. The Eros Persistent Condition grants him the ability to get an exceptional success and impose the Swooning Condition on the subject at 3 successes on Persuasion rolls. Manipulation 3 + Persuasion 3 + Seduction 1 = 7 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/455785\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T08:25:07-08:00","id":1002536,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Mark 5</span><br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Steadfast<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;You guys wait here.&quot; </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\"><i>&quot;WHAT THE HELL IS THAT IDIOT DOING!&quot;</i> </span>went furiously through Mark 5's head, but he was in place already: getting out now would only increase the chances of the rashly acting Mimic being hurt and/or taken hostage. Despite not knowing him that well, he didn't want to endanger him; this was not what he was trying to achieve here.<br /> <br /> Frustrated, Mark 5 waited for a sign of aggression to swoop in (hopefully, in time).<br /> He could only hope the Mimic knew what he was doing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Hey, you're pretty cute. You doing anything right now?&quot; </span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;What... What's that supposed to achieve!?&quot;</span></i><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T11:13:59-08:00","id":1002565,"title":"","content":"<b>Earth</b><br /> <br /> She gave Mark 5 her most human expression yet, a completely bewildered <i>&quot;i have no idea what's going on???&quot;</i><br /> <br /> But hide she did, leaving aside the journal and vials for now to find a good spot she could actually squeeze her misshapen body into. At least she was compact.<br /> <br /> <i><br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/455865\" target=\"_blank\">Dex+Stealth+WP</a>: <u>5d10h8</u> <b>5</b><br /> Wow, lucky. Maybe she stumbled on something interesting in her search for a hiding spot?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T14:59:01-08:00","id":1002648,"title":"","content":"<b>Earth, Mark 5, and Adonis</b><br /> <br /> The <a href=\"http://vignette1.wikia.nocookie.net/bones/images/9/96/Clark_Edison.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20090312054925\" target=\"_blank\">supposed Alchemist</a> rounds the corner, fresh off the phone, and almost runs face first into the supernaturally charming Galateid. The benefits of his sanguine humour and finely tuned Azoth sets a fire in the young man, a blush unconsciously rising to his cheeks as he backpedals and tries to get around Adonis towards the trailer. He seems barely coherent at this point, just stringing words together &quot;Wh- wait, lost? I was just, and you... uh...&quot; He gestures back over his shoulder with a thumb &quot;Work. I, uh, I need to get this trailer full of medical supplies back to the office, <i>my</i>, office. Truck will be here soon- an hour maybe? Really, really can't. Need the job to pay off student loans, you know?&quot; He looks horrified with himself, realizing that he's babbling to an extremely compelling total stranger who just came completely out of nowhere. He turns on his heel and starts towards the trailer, hunched over as though trying to disappear from view.<br /> <br /> Earth manages to squeeze her way under the lab centre, bumping up against a door on one of the cabinets in her haste to escape. The door opens, and an old book, apparently handwritten, falls out. Notes and sketches on loose pieces of paper slip out from between the pages, covered in spidery writing and all-too familiar symbols that wake something deep in Azothic Memory. One of the loose illustrations floats its way over to her, and when it brushes her skin it's like the brush of a hand against her Azothic Radiance. This book is more than it appears, and it calls to the Torment inside her, urging her to find an outlet.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: The Amalgama LTD employee has only a single Door left for Social Maneuvering. Adonis' Impression is Perfect, so he can roll again immediately. Earth finds an Athanor, but what, exactly, is written within it and what secrets it contains will remain to be seen. You know, instinctively, that the Athanor is attuned to Stannum.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T21:03:21-08:00","id":1002760,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged<br /> Alembics: Arc (2), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: BBBOOOOOOO | Willpower: 3/5 | Pyros: 4/12 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> Hunched under the lab center, not hearing anyone step inside the trailer just yet, Earth furtively grabs the book and flips through it. What is it, exactly? If possible she'd like to figure out what type of Athanor it is, but if that will take more time, she can wait and consult her Library for help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T14:38:47-08:00","id":1003078,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 5/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis claps a hand on the presumed alchemist's shoulder and spins him around. He then moves in close and places his other hand on the alchemist's chest, and his gaze turns nakedly lustful. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Oh come on. You have a minute. Maybe even fifteen.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis is going to make another attempt to seal the deal with the alchemist to buy the others time to sneak away. Manipulation 3 + Persuasion 3 + Area of Expertise 2 = 8 -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/456137\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T10:54:32-08:00","id":1003484,"title":"","content":"<b>Adonis</b><br /> <br /> The alchemist is visibly sweating, knees on the verge of buckling, before impulsively throwing himself at Adonis. The sudden kiss breaks off as the alchemist takes a step, breathes, and gestures out of the loading dock. &quot;Coffee first? Clementine Cafe is up the street. We'll talk and... see how things go.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T17:45:07-08:00","id":1003708,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Informed (Athanor)<br /> Alembics: Arc (2), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: BBBOOOOOOO | Willpower: 3/5 | Pyros: 4/12 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> Earth realizes that no one's coming.<br /> <br /> Earth tells Mark 5:<span style=\"color:#DAA520\"> &quot;No one's coming.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She squeezes out from under the lab equipment, dimly aware that her body is chilled. She stuffs the Athanor in her backpack, and steals the spiral notebook journal as well. The Pandorans continue to scrabble and claw against their imprisonment, but she ignores them. She walks back to the vials and <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/aivisura/steven-universe-gem-shards\" target=\"_blank\">stares at them</a>.<br /> <br /> She runs a horrid finger along the clear vials of stolen Vitriol. Memories are rushing back: Dead Girl straddling a fallen man-thing who spoke in tongues and bled shadows. Her hands are deep inside his eviscerated chest cavity, gripping his guts. She's stealing from him. There's no glint of humanity in her eyes, they're wide and flat and reflective as mirrors. Earth-Dies-Screaming is hunched nearby, telling her what to listen for and where to squeeze to draw it out best.<br /> <br /> Standing here in the refrigerated clean trailer, Earth realizes that Dead Girl didn't want to do that. But she did it anyway, because they were tog\u035de\u0341\u034f\u035et\u0338\u035dh\u0489\u0321e\u0334\u0336\u0340r\u0358\u0321<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;This is <i>us,</i>&quot;</span> she whispers to Mark 5. Her voice isn't rough, it's confused and quiet. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;The ones who made this Vitriol, they didn't ask to be used this way. She didn't want this.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Her fists clench. She tries to justify why this little vial bothers her so much: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;It isn't right. It <i>isn't alchemy!</i>&quot;</span><br /> <br /> What Milestones these came from, she can't imagine. She pictures herself crushing them in her hands, denying the alchemists their prize- and all that bottled enlightenment wasted in a puddle on the floor of a semi-trailer, lapped up by hungry Pandorans in boxes.<br /> <br /> She looks over at Mark 5, angry and lost. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;We can't...use this, can we? We couldn't. We <i>could</i>- you <i>can</i> use it this way- but- it's...it's <i>stolen, </i>but not the way a TV is stolen. I don't know another word.&quot;</span> Language fails the Named. She's stuttering and tripping over her tongue.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;But if we just break it- then what was the point? That whole stupid useless Pilgrimage that cooked it just ends in- in- a puddle! But if we took it, it would be like- fuckin'- spraypainting a soul in a paper bag and huffing it!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Earth throws up her hands. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Just- say something any time, Hero. I'm not good at this <i>doing the right thing </i>gig.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T18:09:21-08:00","id":1003719,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 5/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis accepts the kiss willingly. This is different, it's <i>new. </i>The man is different from Sharon, different from Lily: smell, taste, touch, sound, feel. It's over before he would like. The man isn't the most attractive one he's seen, but he's been wanting to try this, see if a human's sex makes a difference in the experience. It does, but it's a pleasant one. Not a change of quality, but a change of characteristics.<br /> <br /> Part of him wants to show this man what he can do right here and now, throw the man up against the wall and blow his mind. But that's not the idea- he needs to stay on target. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">\u200b&quot;That's fine. I won't keep you all night. Let's just get coffee. If it's a work thing, you can just say you got stuck in traffic or something.&quot; </span>He says it in a conversational tone, but hopefully the two Tammuz in the van can hear him and get the hint to grab what they want/need and get out. He gestures up the alley, his smile now less hungry and more friendly. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Shall we?&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T22:22:20-08:00","id":1003781,"title":"","content":"Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Steadfast<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> <br /> Mark 5 heard a faint &quot;Shall we?&quot; outside. Apparently Adonis placed the Alchemist under some sort of Mind control. Not bad. He actually came in handy. After they could not be heard anymore, Mark 5 came out of his Hiding spot, to see Earth Watch the Vitriol. He listened carefully, at one point stroking a vial, sadly. A pilgrim like him, reduced to this. He expected rage. There was none. Just one word in his mind:<br /> Why?<br /> <br /> &quot;Just- say something any time, Hero. I'm not good at this*doing the right thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mark 5 contemplated the problem. Taking it was out of the question. Leaving it here, behind... &quot;Defiling. Is what this is. It won't Stay here.&quot; Destroying it? Unthinkable.<br /> Taking it with them wouldn't solve the problem.<br /> How do you show respect to those who won't notice? A memory bubbled up. Men in fancy clothes, looking alike, shooting and making noise as a Box is carried and put in a hole.<br /> How strangely appropriate.<br /> &quot;Humans do this thing were they put a body back in the Earth. Then talk about the person. They show respect to fallen warriors like that. We could do that- to be dealt with like real humans, even if it is in death, they'd probably have liked that.&quot;<br /> Something wet on his face. Strange. He was sure there had not been any rain.<br /> &quot;And then, Earth, we will avenge them. We find who is responsible for this, and we will put them to JUSTICE!&quot;<br /> He smashed his fist on the Wall of the trailer at that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T00:32:47-08:00","id":1003804,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Informed (Athanor)<br /> Alembics: Arc (2), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: BBBOOOOOOO | Willpower: 3/5 | Pyros: 4/12 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> She raises her fist in sympathy. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Hell yeah, brother.&quot;</span> Her mind isn't quite made up about the burial idea, and she can't actually articulate what<i> 'put them to justice' </i>means in her own words, but it seems to fit the moment.<br /> <br /> She grabs the Vitriol vials and puts them in her backpack, and also swipes a couple of randomly selected potions for later examination.<br /> <br /> The imprisoned Pandorans continue scratching and slobbering. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Hey- if we wreck the joint too bad, they might get loose. That's bad for us: I can't make 'em listen anymore.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> There's got to be a power source in here to keep the trailer refrigerated and the fancier equipment running. She hunts for an outlet along the floor or next to the equipment. If she finds one, she unplugs as needed to expose the outlet, slobbers on her fingers, and rather lewdly jams them into the socket.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'm assuming that if there's an outlet to be found, I can let it ride from my earlier perception-related successes to find it. I'll roll anew if you prefer.<br /> <br /> If there's an outlet, Earth spends 2 turns jacked into it before breaking off, which should clear her damage and (more to the point) restore 2+1 Pyros with Efficient Conductor.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T09:03:59-08:00","id":1003971,"title":"","content":"<b>Adonis</b><br /> <br /> You keep reminding yourself that there's a totally practical reason for having ambushed this guy and dragged him off to coffee. Solely to protect fellow Created, just to keep this alchemist from finding you out, but you can feel your sanguine humour surge nonetheless. He's shy, he's unsure, there's a tension in his shoulders that suggests discomfort but he's smiling nonetheless. The coffee shop is a cozy, cave-like place, full of reclaimed wood surfaces and exposed brickwork, you had to descend a narrow staircase to get down into it, but the space is warm, inviting, and intimate, full of incandescent light, and well-loved brass coffee presses and other brewing implements. You were expecting a coffee shop, but what you <i>weren't </i>expecting was a rather extensive and tempting <a href=\"http://clementinewinnipeg.com\" target=\"_blank\">menu</a>.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Roll Wits + Empathy to read his emotional state</i><br /> <br /> <b>Earth and Mark 5</b><br /> <br /> Divine Fire surges into Earth's flesh, healing, repairing, rejuvenating. Her Azoth flares in response, the alchemical reaction sending her humours surging. For a brief moment, the mask presented by her Azoth fades, and the twisted, Flux-scarred claw that is her right hand is wreathed in electricity. With the sudden loud snap of blown fuses, the lights in the trailer flicker and fade, and any digital screens that may have been active, but sleeping, suddenly flare into snow and then immediately die. The only light left in the trailer are the blinking lights of the containment caskets of the Pandorans. In response to the flare of Azoth they collectively fall silent, and then begin to yowl. You can even hear <i><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=T_y1AjUGGX8\" target=\"_blank\">words</a> </i>amidst the empty, hungry cries.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Earth heals all Bashing Damage, and gains three points of Pyros</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T11:50:59-08:00","id":1004034,"title":"","content":"Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Steadfast<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> <br /> <br /> Mark 5 met the raised fist for a fistbump, then started taking random stuff he could easily carry, preferably written stuff, as Earth blew out the fuse. He did not know yet how they would exact justice, but he knew he needed Information for that. <br /> <br /> The yowling gave him goosebumps, and he Frantically looked to Earth. &quot;Dont want to leave these things here. Too dangerous, could get loose. Gasoline and fire works on these, yes?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T13:53:50-08:00","id":1004106,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 5/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b><br /> <br /> <br /> </div> Adonis keeps having to remind himself that this man isn't just someone he wants to be with. This is an <i>alchemist, </i>with Pandorans and Vitriol in the back of a truck. But he just can't be cold and methodical about it like a Tammuz or Osirian could. His veins don't flow with the cold ooze of Phlegm or the inky syrup of Melancholy, but the warm, scarlet water of Blood. He hasn't seen this man do anything bad. He seems fine. He can't be all bad, right? <br /> <br /> He settles down at the table across from the alchemist. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;I'm Mark, by the way.&quot; </span>He puts out a hand. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">\u200b&quot;Don't worry, I won't keep you long. Who do you work for, exactly?&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Wits 2 + Empathy 3 + Emotions Specialty 1 = 6 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/456726\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T14:30:00-08:00","id":1004115,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Informed (Athanor)<br /> Alembics: Arc (2), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 3/5 | Pyros: 7/12 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Yeah, they sound hangry. Lemme see what I can do.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Earth sets her bag down, rubs her hands together to get a charge going, and tags one of the containment boxes with a lightning bolt. Her skeleton flickers like an x-ray in the darkness.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Using Spark as a 2L weapon, Dex 1+Athletics 3+Azoth 3+Willpower 3, 10 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/456738\" target=\"_blank\">1 success.</a> I'm having awful luck with this power. 3 lethal damage to the contents of that nice metal box, maybe?</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T19:20:05-08:00","id":1004202,"title":"","content":"<b>Earth and Mark 5</b><br /> <br /> There's a sudden, very loud, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=87_NrF3n_zk\" target=\"_blank\">scream</a> that emerges from the case as the Pandoran within shudders and jerks- steel casing affords it no protection from lightning fuelled by the Divine Fire. Pandorans in the nearby cases twist and jerk, and you can hear them suddenly hear the sound of something dragging heavily on steel. One of them has managed to twist far enough around in its casket that it found a weak point in the seal, and is prying at the edge. It screeches in triumph, and suddenly you can hear others, with claws and teeth and tentacles and far stranger appendages, starting to tear at their bindings. The caskets you hit suddenly rings like a gong, with the sudden snap of giving joints echoing in the room. It heaves upwards with the sudden violent motion of the Unborn within, and the hungry gasps, awful sucking sounds like an open wound, worm their way into your ears.<br /> <br /> Music drifts lazily down the street from the restaurant less than a hundred feet away from where you're standing.<br /> <br /> Human laughter, the sound of friends and families sharing meals, is carried along with it.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: This particular Pandoran is almost out, but you already dealt it a decent amount of damage. It's worth remembering that the second Distillation of Arc enables you to make an AoE attacks, letting you handle more Pandorans at once... but in that case Mark 5 should probably get out of the way.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Adonis</b><br /> <br /> The alchemist smiles shyly, taking the offered hand, seeming ready to burst into laughter at the absurdity of a handshake coming <i>after </i>a kiss. You can see all the typical signs of attraction... and of submission. Lowered head, partially covered eyes, rubbing the back of his neck. He faces you, leans in across the table. &quot;My name's Erwin. I work for Amalgama LTD you've... probably never heard of it. It's a chemical company that specializes in advanced pharmaceuticals and biotech, head office is in London, but British companies have always had good relationships with Canadian ones. They do a lot of work with the National Research Council of Canada.&quot; He pauses, but keeps babbling into the long silence.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm not very high up in the company, just a chemical analyst. They basically have me chained to a truck full of different compounds- some medicinal, some performance enhancing, all sorts of stuff. Only thing about Amalgama is... they headhunt. Persuasively. Persistently. Find down on their luck medical students with particularly eclectic talents, and make offers that are hard to refuse. I couldn't afford to pay through the nose for the products they sold in order to pay off my student loans, so now I work for them instead.&quot; He shakes his head &quot;Can you believe that? I wanted to be a <i>doctor</i> before all that.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Manipulation (or Presence) + Persuasion to get him to open up in more detail. Choose the rabbit hole you want to go down.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T00:21:18-08:00","id":1004280,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Mark 5</span><br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Steadfast<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 4/11 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;<b><i>SHIT!</i></b>&quot; </span>Reality could be surreal. This situation certainly was. The sounds of the people outside quickly gave way to the Pandorans fighting their restraints. <i>&quot;This might have been a mistake&quot; </i>went through Mark 5's head, as they awoke the dormant beasts. In response to the urgency of the situation, he fired up his Motus Alembic, gathering Pyros inside to strengthen his body.<br /> They had to take care of these things, or the people outside were in danger, and they'd be to be blamed. He wanted to be in peak condition to make sure everyone stayed safe.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Hit as hard as you can! No holding back shots on my account, are we clear?!&quot; </span>he shouted to Earth.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Mark 5 gathers 2 Pyros (6-2=4) this scene to be spent with another Pyros next scene to activate Exemplary Athleticism.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T00:29:21-08:00","id":1004282,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Informed (Athanor)<br /> Alembics: Arc (2), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 2/5 | Pyros: 7/12 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Instinctively, she tries to command the Pandorans to obey her and fall in line with her Azothic mantle of lordship. It's like trying to flex a muscle she doesn't have anymore. After everything she did for power over Flux, it's gone now. Ha. Haha.<br /> <br /> She turns up the dial on her Alembic, and her whole body crackles with electricity. The sound of human laughter (beautiful, carefree, maddening) registers with her, but it twists in her mind. There's no positive desire to protect innocent people. She just wants to hurt the Pandorans. Not to give them a quick death, but to fill their last moments with suffering, to punish them for the crime of existing and hungering and reminding her.<br /> <br /> She raises a fist at Mark 5. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;We're clear!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> And then she lights up. Words spill out: <b><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;DIE! DIE FOR MASTER!&quot;</span></b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">spending 1 pyros to charge Arc further with Divine Lightning. Spark+Shock+Divine Lightning is Dexterity 1, Athletics 3, area of expertise+interdisciplinary specialty (Creatures of Flux) 2, Azoth 3. 9 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/456861\" target=\"_blank\">6 successes!</a><br /> <br /> If the fallout from this counts as causing a setback or trouble due to anger or cruelty, Earth takes a Beat from Enraged.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 11-17-2016, 03:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T05:04:50-08:00","id":1004340,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 5/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis nods along, like he's seen humans do to show that they are listening to what another person is saying. And he is- intently. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Really? That's pretty interesting! So you're working on some pretty high-end stuff, right? Stuff that most people haven't even heard of, I bet.&quot; </span>He smiles. This is what he needs to be asking, but what he really wants to ask is more interesting things: <i><span style=\"color:#00ff00\">\u200bIs this the first time you've ever been interested in a man? You're not a bad person, are you? Do you know what exactly those vials and tubes you're protecting contain?</span></i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis is going to ask about the compounds. He knows it's Vitriol, but he wants to see if the alchemist knows or suspects that, too. <br /> <br /> Manipulation 3 + Persuasion 3 = 6 dice -&gt;<a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/456878\" target=\"_blank\"> 4 successes</a>. With the Eros Persistent Condition, that's an Exceptional Success, and the alchemist should already have Swooning.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T13:56:56-08:00","id":1004611,"title":"","content":"<b>Earth and Mark 5</b><br /> <br /> The Fury stretches forth her hand, and a bolt of divine retribution answers her. In the enclosed space of the trailer, a clap of thunder like the splitting of the world deafens the two Created as sheets of lightning roll off of Earth's flesh and into everything surrounding her. Holes are burned through solid steel as lightning arcs from casket to casket, the twisted forms of Pandorans twisting indistinctly as dark, vague shapes against a background of blinding white before bursting into flames, spasming as electricity empowered by Torment rips its way through their alchemical flesh, leaving nothing behind but charred flesh. The entire trailer smells of burned pork. You can see daylight through the trailer, holes have been burned through it by the sheer intensity of the blast, molten metal cooling rapidly as it drips down onto ruined pallets of vials and capsules. The entire place has gone from neat and austere to ground zero of a horrific blast.<br /> <br /> Not even the Titan Mark 5 could stand against it. He raises a hand to shield his eyes and lightning smites his arm, charring it from the inside out, rendering it useless. He can feel the lightning rippling its way through his flesh, and against his skin he can see the blackened remnants of his nerves standing out against his skin. In some areas, it's simply irritated to red, and in others it has gone pale and dead, or ashen and is flaking off entirely. He can still feel the bolts twisting in his innards, and knows that it will leave him on the brink of death if he allows it to continue. He needs to find a source of electricity. Now. Before the explosion attracts nearby humans.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Earth manages to fry the Pandorans. All of them. At once. To the point of death. This resolves her Aspiration to use lightning as a weapon, and grants a Beat. And, as the fallout of the blast severely injured a throngmate, she takes another Beat from Enraged. Earth also gains the Inspired Condition due to the Exceptional Success, feeling like an instrument of divine wrath after a blow like that. Mark 5, on the other hand, takes 3 Aggravated Damage and 6 Lethal Damage, and will take another point of Lethal Damage once per turn for the next six turns. You can no longer perform any further investigations of the trailer, as it is well and truly trashed.<br /> <br /> Mark also takes the Arm Wrack Tilt, and gains a Beat due to getting damage in one of his three rightmost Health boxes.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Adonis</b><br /> <br /> He nods humbly, but there's an edge of a smug smile- like he's proud to be on the cutting edge of medicine &quot;Oh no, it's some pretty serious stuff. We're making efforts into treating just about every major degenerative disease you can think of, things no one should ever have to suffer through. The chemical process involved makes absolutely no sense from a purely scientific process, but they've got some kind of solvent, I have no idea what, that lets them rework chemical bonds and set off chain reaction in highly unexpected ways. Only problem is, to produce drugs with more lasting effects on their subjects, we need an absurdly rare stabilizing agent. I have no idea where they get it from, they just send me to pick it up and use it, and they'll expend no end of resources to acquire more or protect what they have. My job is to mess around with the recognized compounds.&quot; He takes a sip of his coffee.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm a little bit of a savant when it comes to chemical reactions. You'd be surprised what the right reagents in the right order in the right proportion can do.&quot; Suddenly, the lights in the building flicker, and you can hear an explosion in the distance. Erwin leaps to his feet, tearing a cellphone from his side, ready to dial. Screams and panicked voices fill the restaurant with a cacophonous din.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: He doesn't know what he's guarding, and probably isn't aware that he's performing alchemy at all. All he knows is that he can produce scientifically unusual results with chemical compounds, but he hasn't had the time or the inclination to expound much on its philosophical or metaphysical implications. You get the sense that he's happier without asking the big questions, even as you get the sense that they're gnawing at him. You gain the Connected (Erwin) Persistent Condition- you've really managed to bond on this &quot;date&quot;.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 11-17-2016, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T14:35:01-08:00","id":1004634,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Mark 5</span><br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Steadfast<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (2), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: AAALLLLLLO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 4/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Mark 5 blinked, to adjust his eyes after the lightning. He took a quick look around to assess the damage Earth dealth, and gave the Vigilante an awestruck look. He hadn't ever seen anything like this. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;<i><b>Dude.</b></i>&quot; </span>His left arm dangled uselessly to his side, but he paid it no attention. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Wow!&quot; </span>was about all he could get out. Which was more praise than anyone else ever had gotten from him.<br /> Then he shook his head. <i>Admire later, get out now.</i> He needed to patch himself up a bit. The Pyros he gathered for the fight was channeled into Hygeius instead, to allow him to move without having to consider his broken arm and injuries. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Let's head back!&quot; </span>he said as he got out, gathering what pieces of paper he had with him that might be still readable.<br /> <br /> Outside, he considered flipping the trailer, but decided against it. The first punishment had been exacted. This war had only just begun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  forgot to mark down dmg 11-20-2016, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T14:48:09-08:00","id":1004647,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 5/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis raises from his seat, looking around. It could be a coincidence, but after seeing Earth cause a brownout with Arc, he suspects it isn't. He looks over at Erwin. It's clear that Erwin isn't really aware of what he is doing. He thinks he's just working with regular chemicals. He has no understanding- or, in his book, great culpability- in whatever Amalgama LTD is working on. He leans over a gives him a quick peck. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">\u200b&quot;I'm sorry, do you need to leave? This is just bad timing.&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T15:52:47-08:00","id":1004683,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Informed (Athanor), Inspired<br /> Alembics: Arc (3), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 2/5 | Pyros: 6/12 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> Earth is floating. She doesn't feel <i>happy </i>exactly, but lifted up, set apart, empowered, mighty. She echoed the Titan: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Wow.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Smell of charred flesh and burning hair. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Yeah, let's- uh- let's get the fuck outta here.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She grabs her backpack, stowed near the outer edge of the trailer, and vaults out into the alley. Seeing Mark 5 move so smoothly with his wrecked and shocked body is oddly inspiring- a human would be dead by now. But he'll be even worse off if she doesn't do something. So she channels Pyros from DC to AC, so to speak, and lets her disfigurements flare as she rejuvenates him with silver lightning.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;That's a start. We need to go, anywhere. Adonis will find us.&quot;</span> And she tries to disappear from the scene, through a back door or down a side street.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">1 pyros to charge Imperatus, 2 pyros to heal 6 lethal damage on Mark 5 with Lightning Therapy.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T08:09:31-08:00","id":1004945,"title":"","content":"<b>Earth and Mark 5</b><br /> <br /> Silver lightning flows into the Titan, wrapping around ruined limbs and suffusing into the skin like water into dry, cracked earth. His body dramatically improves in the space of seconds, the creative prowess of the Divine Fire regenerating flesh and bone, miraculously healing what would have taken a human <i>weeks </i>to recover from. Earth is keenly aware of the devastating power at her disposal; that self-same blow would have been the death of a human, no ands, ifs, or buts. The raw power of Divine Lightning would have twisted through their flesh, and they would have died twisting and screaming in torment. As the greatest part of Mark 5's injuries subside, Earth cannot help but notice the effects Corporeum has on his body. He looks... human. Even his Disfigurements fall away as the Divine Fire suffuses his flesh, and all that remains is the human mask made into truth. His veins still stand out as blackened rivers along his skin, and his hair and flesh still smokes, but he looks<i> alive</i>.<br /> <br /> Mark 5 can feel sudden vitality flowing back into him, but he knows that for all that his body is sustained with alchemy, he still hasn't exceeded the limits of what humanity can achieve in terms of raw physical prowess and skill. Humans are tougher than you thought, tougher than you ever gave them credit for. Even with Pyros forcing your limbs to work properly and concealing your alchemical nature, you know that, had this been ordinary lightning, a human would have lived. More than that, they would have been able to get back up and keep moving. This is what the human body is capable of- enduring whatever the world throws at them, gritting their teeth, and moving forwards. It's a lesson that you learned well once before. Another twist of electricity fires in your gut as residual lightning dances. You aren't entirely out of the woods yet.<br /> <br /> The two Created flee the scene, <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/maps/dir/87+Princess+Street,+Winnipeg,+MB+R3B+1K2/309+McDermot+Avenue,+Winnipeg,+MB+R3A/@49.8979691,-97.1433103,19z/data=!3m1!4b1!4m13!4m12!1m5!1m1!1s0x52ea715c21e09871:0xaafeec7cefdff2f9!2m2!1d-97.1423416!2d49.8981336!1m5!1m1!1s0x52ea715e9e551233:0xa4f44b1624eeada1!2m2!1d-97.1431202!2d49.8980165\" target=\"_blank\">rounding the block into a deep alley filled with fire escapes </a>even as people race past them and towards the source of the explosion. A few turn and let out cries of surprise as Mark 5, still smoking, burns still visible on his skin, runs past them. It would be easy enough to scale a fire escape and hide out on a rooftop for a while, wait for this to all blow over, but Mark is still suffering from the glancing blow of Divine Lightning he received. They'll need to find an electrical generator, and soon, or simply wait for the lightning to subside and use Earth's alchemy to patch him up as best they can.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Mark 5 is down to just 3 Aggravated Damage and, as of this turn, 1 Lethal Damage. The damage will accrue for five more turns before the effect runs out. Wits + Streetwise to figure out where to find an electrical generator in order to patch up Mark 5.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Adonis </b><br /> <br /> Erwin stiffens in surprise at the peck on the cheek. He doesn't seem to be used to touch as a sign of affection. Either that or it's been a very long time since anyone's kissed him. He glances over nervously, and flashes a sheepish, apologetic smile &quot;You know, I think I might need to. Today has been... strange. Good strange, I think, but still strange.&quot; He looks mortified for a second, raising hands in apology &quot;Not that I meant <i>you're </i>strange, just that the day is in general and...&quot; He suddenly closes his mouth, as though realizing that he's just digging himself deeper into his hole, and wordlessly withdraws a business card. He leans in, cautiously. There are two false starts, as if he's a deer in the headlights, and he also gives Adonis a peck on the cheek.<br /> <br /> &quot;Call me. It was nice meeting you, Mark.&quot; And with that, he's gone. You look at the card- it's a depersonalized, corporate business card. You think the gold on the logo for Amalgama LTD might actually be gold leaf, or maybe it's just high quality paint. You're absolutely certain that apart from his name, every other low-level employee of the company with enough pull to have a desk of their own has a card just like this, but it still <i>means </i>something. It's a sign of trust.<br /> <br /> Humanity has so many little rules, so many little rituals. Why was skipping ahead in line an unforgivable sin? Who judged what was appropriate progression for a conversation, or a suitable length of eye contact? Sometimes, the vast web of unspoken connections, unspoken rules, implicit threats, and punishable sins, felt like a vast, storm-tossed ocean. What, then, was this that you just shared with this erstwhile enemy?<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Adonis has experienced a Milestone here about social conventions, social rituals, and relationships. This one is Minor. Adonis is a Galateid, he's made for love, to give it and to receive it. He's also trying to understand the Role of Companion, and so far his understanding of Aurum Roles, and the relationships they build, are translated through the lens of D/s relationships and the Follower Role. How you process this experience will help guide your Pilgrimage forwards, at least on Aurum. I'm not going to award the Vitriol Beats just yet, because I want to see how Adonis interprets it, and Milestones are all about the learning experience.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 11-18-2016, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T21:36:39-08:00","id":1005236,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Informed (Athanor), Inspired<br /> Alembics: Arc (3), Imperatus (1), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 2/5 | Pyros: 3/12 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> Ignore the humans gawping, just keep moving. She flinches when she thinks she sees her name written on a wall at the alley's edge, but it just says EARN. Street art is really tripping her up today. Generators, generators, if she were electricity (which she sort of is) where would she be?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Wits 3, Streetwise 0, 2 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/457363\" target=\"_blank\">failure</a><br /> <br /> Let's use this as a chance to get dejected and fulfill the Alienated Torment.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But all she can think about is how badly she wrecked Mark 5's body without meaning to, and all the fallout that's gonna come from detonating the trailer, and right then someone points at the two of them and <i>screams.</i> Despite her pathetic attempts to stop being a monster, everything she ever touches breaks. That's all she'll ever be, she's just holding Mark 5 and Adonis back from their stupid fake Pilgrimage.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I can't help you with this,&quot;</span> she blurts out. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Find it yourself!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She abandons the search for help and hustles up a fire escape, opting for that &quot;lay low on a rooftop&quot; plan instead.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T06:24:29-08:00","id":1005326,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 5/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis waits a few seconds for Erwin to leave, and then follows. His minds swirls at the events that have just transpired, and he senses that he has achieved a Milestone he wasn't even searching for. <br /> <br /> Up until now, his understanding of human interactions has been through the lens of domination and submission: one party party takes control over another. Done poorly, the dominant party seizes control from the submissive party by force, without consent; that was how Sharon did things. Done well, the submissive party offers up control willingly, and the dominant party accepts it as an offering; that was how Lily did things. This is neither. Erwin is clearly smitten with him- Divine Fire fire within him made sure of that- but he didn't really surrender himself to Adonis, or demand that Adonis surrender to him. This was a compromise. Erwin had requested they see each other again, but he had made no demand of time or place. It was up to him to accept or decline. Erwin had extended his hand, and Adonis was free to accept it or not. Accepting it meant they could build something together. Refusing it meant whatever they could have ended tonight. Was this what being a Companion meant? Meeting somebody halfway, not fully giving or taking control, but sharing it? <i><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">I need to see him again. I need to learn more... </span></i><br /> <br /> He walks out of the cafe and sees the commotion. People are running in the direction of the van. He looks around, trying to get a read on what has happened, though part of him already suspects. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>What the hell did they do, and where are they? </i></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis tries to get a handle on what happened based on the reactions of the crowd. Wits 2 + Composure 2 = 4 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/457427\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>.<br /> <br /> He's also going to try and sense where Mark 5 and Earth are, assuming they are close enough that their Azothic Radiance would be detectable. Azoth 2 = 2 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/457428\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T11:42:28-08:00","id":1005418,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Mark 5</span><br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Steadfast<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (2), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: AAALOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 4/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Energy went through his body, and Mark 5 could feel the Pyros flowing from Earth restoring his mangled body.<span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Thanks!&quot; </span>He was aware that he was still badly hurt, but he had been through worse. Humans are resilient, and so was he. Still, he was gathering a lot of attention the way he looked. That was not good. And he needed to get patched up.<br /> So he was surprised when Earth split:<span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I can't help you with this,&quot;</span> she blurts out. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Find it yourself!&quot;</span><br /> His first instinct was to feel left alone, but then he thought about the divine wrath he had just been witness to. Causing this much destruction must have taken quite a toll. He now understood better than ever why other Created talked of her (of Earth-Dies-Screaming, he corrected) the way they did. It was more important than ever to him to help Earth along on her Pilgrimage. This much power must be used for good. Because it would make a horrible foe. Considering that Earth even patched him up quite a bit, it was possible she was totally out of juice. To split up makes even more sense if she wants to recharge.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;We'll meet up at the usual place. Whoever finds the pretty boy brings him along!&quot; </span>he shouted, then turned another way.<br /> If his mental map was right, and it usually was, he knew where a source of electricity was nearby. He was incredibly focused; situations where his existance was threatened where scarce, and he took them very seriously.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=8b525970\" target=\"_blank\">Wits+Streetwise+1WP</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  forgot to mark dmg 11-20-2016, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T20:13:03-08:00","id":1005557,"title":"","content":"<b>Adonis</b><br /> <br /> The Muse can see cellphones raised high to film the carnage, the flashing lights of a police car, and the siren of a fire truck blares in the distance. You can see sparks periodically flying from and obliterated fuse box inside the loading bay, and smoke rising from the wreckage of the trailer. Erwin is talking to the police, looking utterly crushed. He needed that job, and now it's at risk. Adonis can pick up snippets of conversation &quot;I heard there was a power surge&quot; &quot;Some kind of medical trailer, sensitive chemicals&quot; &quot;All went up in smoke, bad reaction to a shock&quot; &quot;It's a wonder the store didn't light on fire&quot; &quot;Heard the initial charge might have come from the building.&quot; &quot;Saw a <i>huge </i>flash of light, and then two people fled the scene. One looked pretty badly burned- you don't think anyone was <i>in there</i> when it happened, do you?&quot;<br /> <br /> The alchemist spots you in the crowd and walks over. He doesn't have anyone else to talk to, and he looks shell-shocked, cellphone in hand. &quot;That trailer was tens of thousands of dollars of company money and resources. Hundreds of paid work hours. Years in research and altered formulas. I am so screwed. Something <i>must </i>have made it through that, right?&quot; He looks pleadingly, hopefully, at his only fixed point in a storm. A drowning man snagging onto a nearby, friendly plank. Even as you process your revelation, even as you see the sudden connection on his face, the tentative, trusting outreach, and feel your internal crucible surge in response... Azoth calls. Earth and Mark 5 didn't go far.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Adonis gets two Vitriol Beats from the Minor Milestone. I'm starting to get a better idea of how he's processing relationships, and that helps enormously. He also senses that Mark 5 and Earth are only a block and a bit away- not out of range of their Azothic Radiance (or Adonis' for that matter) by a large margin.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Earth and Mark 5</b><br /> <br /> The Fury struggles to contain her own anguish, riding out the wave of Torment within her, trying <i>not </i>to do what comes naturally and vent her rage at everything within striking distance of her divine lightning. The Alembic is still blazing with Pyros- she only needs to reach out and touch it, and she can vent her pain, vent her rage, let the Divine Fire blaze until it smoulders its way back down to a more manageable intensity. She's abandoned Mark 5 after nearly killing him in an overzealous attempt to destroy living reminders of her own monstrous past. She's standing on the precipice of an abyss, but she doesn't believe anything lies back from the edge. There is only the cliff, and the abyss.<br /> <br /> Earth sees a small flock of butterflies near the edge of the building, and she sees a familiar scene. She sees the wreckage of her wrath, gazing down from above, and she sees a frightened horde of humanity surrounding it. She can hear the wailing of people and sirens, and knows she's done this tothem. But there's something different about this than about the paper mill. Perhaps it's the glimmer of Azoth she can see down below, the warm flame of Adonis, as he speaks, comfortable, intimate, with an alchemist. But in this moment- she <i>feels </i>something that manages to pierce her even through the haze of her Torment. She needs only to recognize it for what it is.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Earth regains all Willpower, and must roll Resolve + Composure - Azoth to avoid gaining the Tormented Condition. However, she's also experiencing a Minor Milestone. This whole situation reminds her of the paper mill, but there's something different about it. What Earth takes away from this is likely going to be very different depending on whether she succumbs to Torment or not, and how she chooses to interpret the scene.</i><br /> <br /> The Titan, meanwhile, finds himself a streetlight. It isn't much, but there's enough electricity coursing through it that he needn't risk blowing it out before it can heal him. He stretches out a ruined hand towards the smooth, green-painted metal of its side, and electricity coils up his arm, invigorating his flesh and causing his Azoth to surge in sympathy. He can already feel himself healing, but he also can't shake his resolution that Earth must be helped along her Pilgrimage. He is a Soldier- and Soldiers have missions, don't they? But what is his mission regarding Earth? And who is giving it to him? He pauses for a moment, twinging as the healing power of electricity channeling Pyros meets the Torment-laden lightning Earth had struck him with.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: So, as it so happens your average streetlamp pumps out enough electricity to be comparable to an electric fence, so it's releasing 6 Bashing Damage per turn. You have three turns before it risks shorting out. This turn, he heals a point of Lethal Damage and a point of Aggravated Damage. This saves a point of Bashing Damage that will roll over next turn. He suffers another point of Lethal Damage, leaving him with a total of Two Aggravated Damage and one Lethal. He also gains a point of Pyros. Mark 5 is also experiencing a Minor Milestone.</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T10:54:02-08:00","id":1005762,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Mark 5</span><br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Steadfast<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (2), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: AALOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 5/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> The streetlight gave out enough current to aleviate his damage a bit, and Mark 5 decided to hang around a bit longer. He didn't want to short it out, but taking as much as was save seemed like a good idea at the moment.<br /> It also gave him a little bit of time to think.<br /> <br /> His idle thoughts had stumbled on something. From the beginning, he had <i>thought </i>his mission was involving Earth in some way, shape or form, but up until now their cooperation was more a curiosity-driven experiment than a mission, because he had no objective. He had simply been intrigued by her, by her past and how she wanted to turn into a good person. However, he kind of doubted that it was possible and wanted to be close, in case she gave in to her dark desires. He thought she nearly did, once, today.<br /> But now, he <i>knew </i>the truth. She had thwarted an Alchemist's work, and resisted the temptation (was even horrified!) of taking someone else's Vitriol. Evil does not do that. Evil takes power when it can. It hurts, it doesn't save, never protects. And yet, when he had been wounded and weakened, she healed him.<br /> <i>&quot;Who you are is who you build, step by step, through your actions and decisions.&quot;</i><br /> Earth has truly advanced on her way to Good.<br /> And now, it was clear why the Angel had sent him to this city:<u> Earth must proceed on the Pilgrimage. And others must learn of her Progress.</u><br /> He decided to accept the mission.<br /> He will see to it, will make sure she does not stray. She may have to face her past, but she will not have to do so alone.<br /> Redeeming a Villain.<br /> A daunting task, truly.<br /> Worthy of a Titan. Truly.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: To Mark 5's rather simple black-and-white-view, the ever-grey Earth is straight-up white now. His Martyr-insight had been how your choices to take a certain action (or not) are what builds up into your character. Her actions speak a clear language to him: vanquished Evil and healed a friend ('abandonment' rationalized through thinking she's out of juice and 'one streetlight per person').<br /> Which means, obviously, that helping her turn firmly to the Light Side, so to speak, is his Angel-sent mission. He, on the other hand, decides to answer the divine call. The Principle can hand out tasks, but it is up to the Created to chose to do them. He is no one's minion, after all.<br /> Earth is also sort of a Living MacGuffin to him, now. As in, her progression on the Pilgrimage is more than just &quot;for her own sake&quot;, it also speaks a very clear language to other Prometheans: You might fuck up badly, but do not give up; there is still hope for you! Even the infamous Centimanus Earth-Dies-Screaming managed to come back and progress, after all. This is not about her, society, or Mark 5, this is about Prometheans all over the world!<br /> Kind of like taking a vital target in war, this will boost the troop's morale. Through this, he will enable others to fight against the frustration and desperation so common on the Pilgrimage.<br /> <br /> He also uses the remaining 2 turns to suck up as much Energy as he can without blowing it. </i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 11-20-2016, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T16:50:31-08:00","id":1005903,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Informed (Athanor), Inspired<br /> Alembics: Arc (3), Imperatus (1), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 6/12 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <i>Butterflies. </i>Dusty laugh. The Principle is showing her something, here of all places. But is it real, or the beginnings of an Elpis vision, or her Vivid Dreams leaking into reality? An angel, or just a bunch of pretty bugs?<br /> <br /> Earth is hunched on the edge of the building, watching the crowd gathered and the sirens blaring. <i>Here we are again. </i>She holds out her twisted sinewy claw and lets herself desperately hope that a butterfly will alight on it. It's alright, no one can see her.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">+3 Willpower and +3 Pyros from Enraged.<br /> <br /> Resist Torment: Resolve+Composure-Azoth, 2 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/457803\" target=\"_blank\">failure</a><br /> <br /> Taking the Tormented Condition, and a Beat for risking Torment. 5 Beats become 1 Experience, hooray.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Black bile rises in her throat. The Winnipeg mist thickens and settles and darkens. The sirens get loud and harsh. She coughs and sputters and feels the crushing weight of failure, the futility of hope. The butterflies circle, and she cackles at them, slumped to the ground.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I see how you do it now,&quot; </span>she taunts. Her words are already stunted and failing her. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;You come to us </span><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b><i>af\u0489t\u034fe\u0341r\u035c</i></b></span><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">we're worthless. You wait, until</span><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><i><b>a\u0340f\u0489te\u0338r</b></i></span><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">we've lost!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She rolls over and stares at the dark sky. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;B\u0336eca\u0358use\u0361 w\u031bhe\u0341n\u0338 y\u0360ou're\u0489 at \u0322t\u031bh\u0358e\u034f bott\u0358o\u0360m...y\u0338ou'\u0315ll\u0322 b\u0337e\u0328l\u0341i\u0341e\u0489v\u0362e \u0321</span><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><i><b>a\u0303\u0364\u034c\u0315n\u030f\u030c\u0340y\u033d\u0311\u036b\u030c\u0366t\u0350\u0368\u0301\u0313\u0328h\u036d\u034a\u036f\u0302\u0367\u0334i\u035b\u0346\u0357\u0314n\u036a\u0303\u0308\u030f\u0308\u0341g\u030a\u0313\u0367</b></i></span><span style=\"color:#DAA520\"> t\u0362o\u0322 \u0361fee\u0358l l\u0341ik\u0336e the\u035fre'\u035es\u0358 still \u0321</span><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><i><b>h\u033c\u031e\u0333\u0330o\u0362\u032b\u033a\u0330\u0347\u032bp\u0347\u0354e\u034e\u035a\u0353\u0329.\u0316\u0326&quot;\u0358\u0348\u0354\u0347\u0345\u0354\u0331\u0356&quot;\u0340</b></i></span><br /> <br /> Earth swipes her claw at them, and pounds it into the rooftop, but only crunches her bones instead of causing an awful earthquake. Can't even wreck shit right. She stumbles to her feet and accuses the butterflies: <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>&quot;\u0364\u0368\u0307\u034b\u0368\u0311\u0338\u0326Y\u0367\u036c\u0368\u0365\u0311\u0489\u0348O\u0367\u0311\u0351U\u033e\u033f\u036a\u0346\u0362\u0355\u033b\u0320 \u0367\u0312\u0351\u0301\u0368\u0335\u0349\u032c\u033cC\u030a\u030e\u0367\u0352\u031d\u0331\u033b\u0316\u032e\u032bA\u031e\u0333\u0329\u0332\u0331\u0348N\u031a\u0344\u0309\u0353\u0345\u032f'\u0369\u030b\u0301\u030c\u0321\u033a\u032e\u0326\u0326\u0347T\u036a\u030d\u0369\u0315 \u0324\u0325\u031f\u0355\u0349\u032a \u032b\u032d\u032c\u032f\u0330\u031e\u032dM\u0357\u0365\u036c\u0313\u0342\u0308\u036aA\u036a\u033f\u0366\u034c\u0357\u0301\u0350\u035fN\u0350\u0302\u036e\u036c\u034c\u036e\u0340\u0326\u031e\u033cI\u036d\u036f\u0331\u032f\u0355\u0333P\u0304\u0313\u030f\u0352\u0318\u032dU \u0356\u032a\u0330\u0345\u032aL\u0363\u0350\u0356\u031c\u033a\u032b\u0319\u033bA\u0312\u0367\u0307\u0310\u0346\u0363T\u0343\u0335\u0329\u033b\u032b\u0356\u0319\u0347\u032fE\u0365\u0302\u0352\u0311\u0367\u032e\u0320\u0348\u032e\u0348\u0323\u0359 \u033e\u036d\u036d\u0351\u0367\u034a\u035e\u0320\u032f\u033c\u0332\u031fM\u0369\u033e\u036d\u032c\u0319\u0349E\u036c\u030c\u0314\u0313\u0364\u0305\u0321\u0323\u0359\u031d\u0331\u0333,\u0351\u0364\u0315\u0349\u0353 \u0352\u0366\u0314\u0306\u034a\u0366\u0367\u0345\u034e\u031fA\u0367\u0307\u0312\u030c\u030fN\u0367\u0308\u0321\u0354\u0329\u033a\u0353\u0331\u0331G\u0308\u0329\u0349\u032b\u0345\u0349\u0317E\u0346\u0301\u0321\u035aL\u0314\u0313\u036f\u0305\u0300\u0337\u0330\u031f\u0348\u033c \u0326!\u034c\u030f\u030d\u0362&quot;\u030f\u0352\u0312\u034f</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> She can't manage anything else. The words just aren't coming out.<br /> <br /> Instead, she glowers down at the people below. One lesson of the Savage: you can go pretty deep down the rabbit hole before you stop being human and become a monster, and that final line is a heavy one. She's trying hard to cling to that lesson right now, convincing herself that sinking is something totally different from stepping off the path entirely. Another lesson: fear of the Other brings a community together. You become the object of their fascination and fear. That rage and its consequence has a place in the community it hurts, in a way that a tsunami on the other side of the world doesn't.<br /> <br /> She followed that lesson and thought the Vigilante was about a community too, a kind of Savage that attacked outsiders, turning that fury and fear into a force that defended the right people.<br /> <br /> How could she have been so <i>stupid?<br /> <br /> What are you, a Mimic? You <b>idiot. </b>You can't become part of a human community, not by breaking and destroying, or <b>ever.</b> You can't even protect other freaks like you. Mark 5 is probably <b>dead</b> by now, because of <b>you!</b> And Adonis has joined up with the <b>alchemist!</b> Typical Galateid, thinking with their <b>blood,</b> <b>hurting </b>and <b>betraying </b>you like they always do-</i><br /> <br /> She shuts her eyes tight and grabs her hair, mouthing the words <i>I know, I know, <b>I know, </b>just <b>stop saying it, </b>think about something else-</i><br /> <br /> Look at how afraid those people are. They don't understand what she did, and they never will. If she stops lying to herself for once, she can admit that she didn't go full God of Thunder to protect those pretty laughing voices in the cafe- she did it to hurt the Pandorans, because that was what she Had To Do. It doesn't matter whether the humans are afraid of her, because it isn't about them, even if it seems like it. It's all personal, because she's Alienated from everyone else on this miserable planet. Embodying the Vigilante is about channeling her Torment into a code, something that <i>she </i>knows is right, and damn the world if it stands against her. Earth is the only one who will ever know what's right for Earth- not Mark 5, not Adonis, not Heartsblood, not Dead Girl, not the Principle- and Earth will define herself by spitting her fury at the entire world. This is humanity: furious, zealous certainty of who you are- or if not that, then at least what you stand for and what you will <i>never </i>accept.<br /> <br /> She hefts her backpack and disappears into the fog, seeking out some isolated junkyard or construction site or crackhouse, or maybe a foggy Scottish highland to brood on.<br /> <br /> No- a garden, or a park, or some earthy green space. She needs to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 11-20-2016, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T06:13:48-08:00","id":1006160,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 5/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis stands tongue-tied for a second. He knows, on a certain level, that destroying the van was probably the best move Earth and Mark 5 could have made. But the van was Erwin's responsibility, and failing in your responsibilities to your superiors is a Bad Thing in human society. Erwin may be an alchemist, but he doesn't know what it is that he's doing. He's not a cackling madman ripping the Vitriol out of Created. He's not a bad person. And he needs to tell Mark 5 and Earth- especially Earth- before they try to kill him. He gives the man a hug. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;You're not going to lose your job. I'm sure of it.&quot; <i>Even if I have to use Eros to make them give it back to you. </i>&quot;Do you... want me to walk you home?&quot; </span>He's going to be fuck-all help against a Titan and a Savage, but humans seem to appreciate it when others make them promises they know probably won't be kept. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T08:49:45-08:00","id":1006215,"title":"","content":"<i>Evening, November 3<sup>rd</sup> 2016</i><br /> <br /> <b>Adonis</b><br /> <br /> It's a bit of a walk to Erwin's apartment, almost half an hour, given traffic lights and a willingness to keep talking. You end up at a <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/maps/@49.8862749,-97.1365478,3a,75y,66.46h,122.3t/data=!3m7!1e1!3m5!1sqAoe5x-KKmWz-zFPS6-w5g!2e0!6s%2F%2Fgeo3.ggpht.com%2Fcbk%3Fpanoid%3DqAoe5x-KKmWz-zFPS6-w5g%26output%3Dthumbnail%26cb_client%3Dmaps_sv.tactile.gps%26thumb%3D2%26w%3D203%26h%3D100%26yaw%3D87.55172%26pitch%3D0%26thumbfov%3D100!7i13312!8i6656\" target=\"_blank\">building</a> that evokes Neoclassical beauty, with limestone statues of nubile youths holding up the lower, older, ledges covering windows. There's a touch of Gothic elegance to the design, just like the opulent hotel you passed as you walked down the street. The alchemist babbles most of the way, talking about his upbringing on the east coast of America, the college experience, his parents, his sister. You find yourself silent for most of it, listening. No alchemy brought this about, no Transmutations encouraged this wellspring of information- it was only words, simple physical contact. Adonis understands that, even if he doesn't understand the experiences and emotions that Erwin is describing, he nods along supportively regardless. He ends up inviting you up to dinner, and he looks so... piteous. Pleading.<br /> <br /> This would be the &quot;give&quot; portion of the &quot;give and take&quot; that you've heard of, you imagine.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: If Adonis stays, he'll gain a Beat from the Connected (Erwin) Condition. Blowing off the pissed off Fury and the very black-and-white Titan is probably a bad idea, especially when they know you're with an alchemist, but is the burgeoning relationship with Erwin more important than shared struggles with the two Created?</i><br /> <br /> <b>Earth</b><br /> <br /> Driven silent with anguish and rage, Earth leaves without another word, leaving Adonis and Mark 5 alone with their futile journey. In her Tormented agony, she can barely sense her internal alchemy changing, the small still voice of Vitriol dripping into her flesh, whispering that she's growing, that she's making progress. It's possible that she might not even notice it at this time. She wants to vent her rage, lay waste to something, but the Alembic has exhausted itself- even the Divine Fire cannot sustain something forever. She wanders idly up Main Street, crossing past the Exchange District and into the North End, a dreadful wasteland of purely human design. You can see the shift immediately, crumbling edifices and ramshackle homes, yards full of discarded refuse and broken toys, the disenfranchised, the dispossessed, all milling about. Earth is left alone.<br /> <br /> She wanders idly, looking for a place she can vent or brood, eyeing up a train yard and an industrial park, before coming across something extraordinary. <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/maps/dir/309+McDermot+Avenue,+Winnipeg,+MB+R3A/Urban+Eatin&#39;+Landscapes,+100,+765+Main+Street,+Winnipeg,+MB+R2W+3N5/@49.9018992,-97.1468283,15z/data=!3m1!4b1!4m14!4m13!1m5!1m1!1s0x52ea715e9e551233:0xa4f44b1624eeada1!2m2!1d-97.1431202!2d49.8980165!1m5!1m1!1s0x52ea715c64f0d501:0x69fc71ff0e56eb20!2m2!1d-97.1329625!2d49.9061928!3e2\" target=\"_blank\">A patch of green in the midst of decay.</a> It appears to be deserted at this time, but it is without a doubt a human place. If she desires work, this is the place for her.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: All of your Alembics have ground out (so they are without charge) due to the fact we have now changed scenes. For your personal edification, this is the <a href=\"http://urbaneatin.com\" target=\"_blank\">website</a> of the place in question. The North End of Winnipeg is a massive food desert, and is home to pretty close to 90% of the crime in the city. It's a run down neighbourhood the tons of people write off, but a rare few groups try and bring some vitality back into the area in a grassroots movement. They're fighting, but it's an uphill battle. She gains two Vitriol Beats.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Mark 5</b><br /> <br /> Though charging the Alembic proved to be only incidentally useful, healing proved more fruitful. He actually <i>gained </i>Pyros in addition to healing totally and completely. The only question is, what now? He could track down Earth, but she likely wants to be left alone right now, and she can handle herself. What will the Titan find for himself to do? It would be easy enough to follow after her, but perhaps there are other things he could busy himself with.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Unlike the others, Mark 5 doesn't have a clear &quot;next step&quot; for this scene, so it's entirely up to you what happens next. Perhaps he can find some criminals to go all superhero on. Perhaps he can find a martial arts gym to join. Or perhaps he can just follow after Earth. Either way, it will almost certainly lead to complications. If you want to track down criminal action or find a martial arts gym roll Wits + Streetwise. He's healed of all damage, and gains two Vitriol Beats and two points of Pyros.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 11-21-2016, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T04:31:34-08:00","id":1006652,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 5/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis bites his lip with indecision. Part of him wants to go inside with Erwin, to comfort him, to feel their skin touch and explore his body. But the others will start to wonder where he has gone, and he can't imagine Earth- or Mark 5 for that matter- being very happy with him sleeping with an alchemist. He looks at Erwin. The look on his face is so obvious, but what good is a night of passion going to be if he's dead the next day? Don't humans sometimes disappoint people to do something better for them later? He takes Erwin's face in his hands and gives him a long, slow kiss. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;I know this probably isn't what you want, but I promise you that I'll be back. Tomorrow, even. It's just that I have something I need to take care of tonight.&quot; </span>He waits for any response Erwin gives, and then turns around and walks down the street, looking over his shoulder a couple times at Erwin. Once Erwin heads inside, Adonis breaks into a quick jog, back in the direction of where he sensed Earth's and Mark 5's Azoth. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T21:50:05-08:00","id":1007028,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Informed (Athanor), Inspired, Tormented<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 6/12 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> The golem labors. There's an entrenching tool in her backpack; she draws it and hops the fence. She gets down on her hands and knees, digging up weeds. Getting rid of things that don't belong, like her.<br /> <br /> Time passes, cars go by. As long as she works, she doesn't think. But thoughts of the stolen Vitriol in her pack still bubble up.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Wits+Crafts to be semi-productive and avoid damaging the urban garden: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/458634\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a><br /> <br /> Also a question: Would Pandorans be able to detect and dig up the stolen Vitriol if she buried it? Intelligence+Occult (Creatures of Flux): <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/458635\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T07:20:17-08:00","id":1007225,"title":"","content":"<b>Adonis </b><br /> <br /> Erwin doesn't say much, he's a little busy blushing dramatically, so instead he just thanks you for the walk home and sets a date for dinner tomorrow. You're supposed to meet him back at the apartment and you'll discuss what to do then. The jog back is a good deal quicker than the walk out, especially seeing as there's no one to walk with or talk to. The plume of smoke rising off the street is noticeably dulled, and a plain white truck, almost like an armoured van, is out in front of the loading bay as humans in bulky yellow suits and helmets, with duct tape around every possible open seam, picking their way through the smoking debris as some members of the fire department look on. The police have made their way over and are questioning people a little off to one side, and yellow tape, marked in bold black letters, surrounds the loading bay, hanging off of street lamps and the edges of the hazmat van itself.<br /> <br /> It's easy enough to find Mark 5, who hasn't yet left the area, slumped near a lamppost around the block from the devastated trailer, taking a breather. He certainly looks a lot better than what he heard from the crowd would suggest, but maybe he wasn't hurt as badly as they thought. Human memory is a notoriously unreliable thing. You can feel your own Azoth glowing magnificently. It danced in sympathy to the close proximity of Erwin's soul, magnifying itself. However, Azoth is an intense flame, and it has a propensity for scorching those who get too close.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Regain a point of Pyros from close contact with humans. Roll Azoth to see if Erwin is afflicted with Disquiet, as it is now a new scene and he's going to be a significant character for Adonis in the future, I imagine. <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=228915c1\" target=\"_blank\">Erwin got a Success,</a> so you'll need two or more to inflict Disquiet.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Earth</b><br /> <br /> The community garden is right across from a rather friendly looking work yard that is full of stacks of wood and bags of soil from making planters of all kinds. On the one side of the street is evidence of decaying industry, and on the other is a vibrantly green park, with a small inset amphitheatre, and a little ways up on a hill, this garden and a heritage house that doubles as a museum in the summer. There isn't really a fence, unless you count the faded planks at waist height a 'fence'. The garden itself is surprisingly full, even discounting the weeds. This autumn has been unusually warm, and anything that was planted for the next season has already sprouted and had an extra three weeks of growing it really shouldn't have. There's lettuce, rhubarb, mint, and dill all ready to harvest. She carefully works her way around the plants, taking care only to remove the weeds, leaving the beautiful, young plants alone. It has been said that gardening is a deeply meditative and calming hobby. What use does the Fury see in it? Is she simply taking her Inscription to heart, or is it something more?<br /> <br /> Distracting herself from the worst of her Torment, she still manages to ponder the question of the Vitriol. She remembers, in her days as a Freak, that her pack could <i>smell </i>it in the organs of Created, and more than once they helped her track down a Vitriol Fount. Only problem is, a glass bottle is <i>significantly </i>less secure than either the flesh of a Promethean or an Athanor, but, so far, it doesn't appear as though there are any Unborn wandering the streets of this city. Perhaps it would be safe.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Explaining why gardening is significant to Earth will result in establishing how it is a self-affirming action for her, rewarding Pyros.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T09:18:16-08:00","id":1007283,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 6/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b><br /> </div> <br /> Adonis rushes over to Mark 5 and gives him a look over. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Earth got a little zap-happy, I guess.&quot; </span>He kneels down and attempts to repair what damage he can. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;I'm sorry I took off like that. I figured it would be better if I led the alchemist away, so that you guys could keep searching and maybe wreck what you could. Which you, uh, did.&quot; </span>He finds himself talking about Erwin as his fingers roam over Mark's body- not in the way he wants to do to Erwin, but in the gentle, probing way Lily taught him. &quot;First aid,&quot; she called it. She also called it &quot;aftercare&quot; when they were done one of their sessions, but this was definitely first aid. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">\u200b&quot;The alchemist doesn't know squat about all this. He's not even an alchemist, really. He didn't make any of it, he was just guarding it. He thinks it was just cutting edge chemical stuff.&quot; </span>He pauses. He stops paying attention to Mark. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;His name's Erwin. He's scared he's going to lose his job. It sounds like he really needed it.&quot; </span>He looks Mark in the eye. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;I know you guys probably won't buy this, but he's not a bad person. Don't hurt him.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Azoth 2 = 2 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/458761\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>. Erwin's still smitten with Adonis in a completely healthy, non-obsessive way.<br /> <br /> Adonis attempts to undo some of Mark 5's damage. Intelligence 1 + Medicine 2 = 3 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/458762\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T11:55:41-08:00","id":1007358,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Mark 5</span><br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Steadfast<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Earth got a little zap-happy, I guess.&quot; </span><br /> <i>Zap-happy?! </i>Did this Mimic really think he had <b>any</b> idea of what Earth did? Who she is? <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;She did not get zap-happy, she called down thunder and lightning like a freakin' Quashmalim! And thank the Principle she did, because she immolated several pandorans with it. With <b>one </b>strike. Who knows what would have happened to the people in the caf\u00e9 if she hadn't.&quot;</span> He shook his head, disgusted by the idea.<br /> Being touched by Adonis was weird. Uncomfortable. Extremely uncomfortable. Mark 5 knew about first aid, he knew this was supposed to help him. Adonis had good intentions. But he wasn't used to it being applied on him. Or feeling gentle touches, in general. He was <i>fine</i>, anyway. With the intention of shoving the Mimic gently away, Mark 5 swiped Adonis' hands away. A bit too quickly, too strongly. Maybe it was just his strength. Maybe he was more uncomfortable with this than he thought. Or maybe he'd gotten more angry than he realized. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Thanks, but I'm fine. Earth patched me up&quot;</span> he said quickly.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">\u200b&quot;The alchemist doesn't know squat about all this. He's not even an alchemist, really. He didn't make any of it, he was just guarding it. He thinks it was just cutting edge chemical stuff. </span><span style=\"color:#00ff00\">His name's Erwin. He's scared he's going to lose his job. It sounds like he really needed it. </span><span style=\"color:#00ff00\">I know you guys probably won't buy this, but he's not a bad person. Don't hurt him.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> Now that was suspicious, wasn't it? <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;You're damn right I don't buy this. But how the hell can <i>you </i>believe that?! He does NOT know what he's working with? Keeps Pandorans in tanks and has no clue what it is? That doesn't make sense!&quot; </span>Even if this were true, he was part of a criminal organization exploiting their fellow Created. Destryoing hopes of the Great Work fullfilled. Unknowingly killing someone is still killing someone. He was responsible. Evil.<br /> <br /> Mark 5 knew Galateids sometimes got weird about people. He looked Adonis in the eye. &quot;<span style=\"color:#000080\">Sure it's not just your blood clouding your mind, pretty boy?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 11-23-2016, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T13:35:48-08:00","id":1007401,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 6/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Keeps Pandorans in tanks and has no clue what it is? That doesn't make sense!&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;He wasn't lying, I could tell! When Pandorans run out of Pyros, they go dormant until they detect Azoth. The lights only started blinking when we went into the van. He... he must've thought they were deadly chemicals or something. His bosses probably told him he had to keep those caskets closed.&quot; </span>But doubt starts to creep into his borrowed heart.<span style=\"color:#00ff00\"> <i>He didn't lie. He didn't know. ... Did he? </i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000080\">Sure it's not just your blood clouding your mind, pretty boy?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Adonis stiffens. And there it is. <i>Don't trust the Galateids, they're just sluts for humans. </i>He's heard that one plenty of times. The fact that he was <i>made</i> to love just draws even more derision from those who found that out. His lip rises in a sneer. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">\u200b&quot;And having tar clog up your brains is so much better?&quot; </span>He stands. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Where the hell is Earth?&quot; </span></div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T13:41:26-08:00","id":1007407,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Informed (Athanor), Inspired, Tormented<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 6/12 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> The labor continues.<br /> <br /> Her affinity for gardening comes from <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C4Wv5M9JPao\" target=\"_blank\">somewhere before words</a>. It's not something she could express to someone else yet. She can't really articulate it herself outside of the safety of dreams. It's a tangle of feelings around her Lineage element, the words of her Inscription, memories of her first encounter with humans in a house in Phoenix with a beautiful garden. The urge is something like: work to help a living thing grow and be healthy and vibrant, instead of twisting and corrupting it. Believing that the plant will have a good future, despite the fact that she touched it and cultivated it- <i>because </i>she cultivated it, even.<br /> <br /> Right now though, she's cut off from her Elpis and the work is directionless. &quot;Meditative and calming&quot; isn't where she's at. She can't reach that feeling of purpose and Faith, but she works to keep the anxiety at bay. The gardening doesn't feel right, but not doing it feels worse.<br /> <br /> She's carrying some heavy bags of planting soil while pondering the Vitriol issue when suddenly she stops, drops the bags, sits on the ground. Why bother? Without her Elpis, she can't see any point in burying the bottles as Mark 5 suggested. Stupid, useless gesture, even more nonsensical than burying a human corpse. She was never really going to honor the Created they were stolen from. That just isn't who she is. She's alone, Alienated, hopeless, and the only path for her in this miserable world is the one she makes for herself.<br /> <br /> Earth digs out the phials of Vitriol from her pack, contemplates, and consumes all of it. Some of it spills onto the soil and plants she was working with, but it doesn't matter now, does it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T19:44:58-08:00","id":1007527,"title":"","content":"<b>Earth</b><br /> <br /> The distilled Vitriol drips down her throat, slowly seeping into her alchemical flesh. This isn't the visceral predation and violation of the lacuna, it isn't the warm, self-assured refinement process of a Milestone, pointing in the right direction. It's cold, emotionless. Vitriol built up in her, but that was all. There was an emptiness to it that even in her days as a Freak she hadn't experienced. The glass bottles fell, hollow, pointless, into overturned soil. The alienated Promethean heard footsteps behind her, and someone giving a relieved sigh.<br /> <br /> &quot;Thanks for doing the weeding, eh? I was going to be stuck her all afternoon, crazy weather, huh?&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a woman, with the lilting voice Earth has come to associate with the First Nations people of Manitoba. The woman comes around one side, clearly planning to sit herself down and help Earth finish off her work in the garden. She sits down, and offers Earth a <a href=\"http://media.istockphoto.com/photos/woman-in-autumn-picture-id184660191\" target=\"_blank\">friendly smile</a>, before it fades as she gives her a quick up and down. Something in her face shifts, and Earth gets the terribly uncomfortable sensation that this woman is <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=5442e33e\" target=\"_blank\">seeing right through her</a>. She glances down to the empty glass bottles, and gives Earth a stony stare.<br /> <br /> &quot;Look- I'm happy to work with you, and I can tell something is eating you, but crawling into a bottle isn't going to fly with me. My mom and dad did that, and they never came back out, and I'm not going to watch anyone do that to themselves again. We work, you want to talk, you talk, you don't, you don't. Either way works for me.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: She got two successes on a roll to <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=9a36b7e3\" target=\"_blank\">resist Disquiet.</a> Roll Azoth to see if you'll exceed that and inflict Disquiet. Just so we're clear, this woman is under the impression that the vials that formerly held Vitriol are actually individual alcohol servings. Earth gains three Vitriol Beats, and should roll 7 dice to avoid Stepping Backwards.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Adonis and Mark 5</b><br /> <br /> There's a tension in the street, in the knowledge of the fading sirens in the background, of the quiet hum of humanity. Of insults fuelled by clashing viewpoints flashing between two Created beings. But the pressing question is where the Fury who just unleashed the wrath of the gods has ran off to. Wherever she is, she's far off enough that her Azothic Radiance no longer butts up against theirs, meaning that she's not an insignificant distance away from them. Several city blocks, at least.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's more than one way to track Earth down. Azoth is almost a certainty, but ordinary, human skill is another means of tracking her down. Staying near Earth, keeping an eye on her, protecting her, getting her to stay the course, that's Mark 5's goal now. That's his mission. He might be pissed at the Muse, but right now, Earth could be anywhere, doing anything, and just about <i>anyone </i>could get to her before they can.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: You can use Wits + Streetwise to figure out where Earth would end up</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T22:09:14-08:00","id":1007562,"title":"","content":"Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Steadfast<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5<br /> <br /> *\u200b&quot;And having tar clog up your brains is so much better? Where the hell is Earth?&quot;<br /> <br /> Mark 5 was taken aback. Why was the Mimic so angry? He had simply asked a question. Not really getting it, he shook his head. &quot;No. Impaired judgement is never good.&quot;<br /> Adonis was right in regards to Earth, though. They had to find her. It was important, they needed to talk. Maybe She could put some Sense into.<br /> They could not feel her Azothic Radiance, so they'd have to track her down the old - fashioned way. <br /> He had found her once, already. He could do so again. The Titan rose, confident, with a determination he gathered from his new purpose, and proclaimed &quot;I have an idea. Follow me.&quot;<br /> <br /> (<a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=298a1a47\" target=\"_blank\">http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/Wik...?hash=298a1a47</a>) 4sux on wits+Streetwise","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T22:29:31-08:00","id":1007573,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Informed (Athanor), Inspired, Tormented<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 6/12 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Stepping Backwards: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/458960\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>, Earth gets 1 Vitriol Beat and takes Disconnected. -2 on Social rolls with humans for a while.<br /> <br /> Disquiet: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/458962\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes</a>. Yay!</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The bottles tumble onto the dirt. The only thing Earth feels is regret. But that's a good sign; if she weren't on the road, she wouldn't feel <i>anything</i>.<br /> <br /> &quot;Thanks for doing the weeding, eh? I was going to be stuck here all afternoon, crazy weather, huh?&quot;<br /> <br /> A human is talking to her. Alarm bells go off: someone looking for her? She's looking right at her. She <i>knows, </i>somehow.<br /> <br /> &quot;Look- I'm happy to work with you, and I can tell something is eating you, but crawling into a bottle isn't going to fly with me. My mom and dad did that, and they never came back out, and I'm not going to watch anyone do that to themselves again. We work, you want to talk, you talk, you don't, you don't. Either way works for me.&quot;<br /> <br /> Her dead flesh doesn't have the capacity to cry (yet?), but she feels the urge. Earth looks up at the human, brushes dirty hair out of her own eyes, and makes a sort of affirmative humming sound.<br /> <br /> She hesitates, picks up the empty bottles, and pushes herself to her feet. Holds up the bottles and looks at the human for direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T06:51:46-08:00","id":1008057,"title":"","content":"<b>Mark 5 and Adonis</b><br /> <br /> It's easy enough to find some people on the street to get talking- Earth cut a pretty distinctive figure, and storming off with such an obvious desire to be left alone more or less projected a vibe of simmering anger and pure 'Screw off'. The people Mark 5 chats up; the homeless, the disenfranchised, informants and information brokers with fading prison tats, all point him in the same direction. Mark 5 isn't exactly the most <i>sociable </i>Promethean Adonis has ever seen, so where did he meet all these people, exactly?<br /> <br /> Mark's own knowledge of Earth gives him a pretty good place to start after getting pointed in the right direction. Parks and gardens stick out like sore thumbs in the crumbling industrial vistas of the North End of Winnipeg. They end up at the Joe Zuken Heritage Park, the first green space that Mark 5 and Adonis stumble across, and see the unexpected sight of Earth, former terror Earth-Dies-Screaming, gardening with a human woman.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: I'm leaving the details of the people Mark 5 ends up talking to open-ended so that</i> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> <i>has the opportunity to detail some of Mark 5's exploits as a vigilante. What little acts did he perform to get these people to open up to him? Is he actively making the streets a better place, or are his misunderstandings of right, wrong, violence, physical contact, and motivation simply making people too afraid to <b>not </b>talk to him?</i><br /> <br /> <b>Earth</b><br /> <br /> The woman sighs, no talking works, but she'd hoped that Earth would open up. Then again, how could she possibly know what Torment does to her? She gestures off-handedly towards a large blue plastic bin, pulls out her own tools, and settles down into the garden. In silence they weed and harvest lettuce and rhubarb, they trim cuttings off of mint and dill, and transplant them into pots for indoor growing. No point in letting perfectly good herbs go to waste over the winter.<br /> <br /> There's a kind of silent communication between Earth and the woman that stumbled across her- something that goes beyond words. It's a kind of language she can understand; there's tension and discomfort communicated with a particular curl of the shoulders that spreads across the upper back, but there's comprehension and shared sorrow in the lines of her face, and practiced skill in the sudden deft movements of fingers.<br /> <br /> Earth can see, coming across the field, as she picks up a bag of soil to follow the wordless direction of her fellow gardener, Adonis and Mark 5. They came after her.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: So Earth now has the Disconnected Condition, an Experience, a Vitriol Experience, and a whole smattering of other Conditions. Wow, is she ever an Experience generator. In either case, Mark 5 and Adonis have caught up with you, so I'll leave the floor open for you guys to interact with characters. If anyone makes rolls, or I feel the need to mention something, I will, but for now go nuts with character interactions.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere's a few potential plot points here,</i> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> <i>still needs to bring up Erwin with Earth, </i><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> <i>still has the Athanor, and she also has a few surviving potions from the Amalgama trailer, which were <b>not </b>pure Vitriol.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T13:52:35-08:00","id":1008257,"title":"","content":"Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Steadfast<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5<br /> <br /> It felt good being appreciated by the people. His past works obviously left an Impression. The old man with the cane remembered his lesson- he hadn't been in need of a cane before he met Mark 5. A better man now, helpful and forthcoming.<br /> The Tattoo guys were still Thankful. As far as the Titan could gather, they were some sort of family, all brothers, who had to Defend themselves against some armed Bastards few weeks ago. They were losing, so the Tammuz Stepped in. A few he had saved from muggings, a few he had stopped from mugging. When he was around, people seemed to get along. He was a good influence.<br /> <br /> Once Earth was in sight, Mark 5 waved at her. Things had gone smoothly, so obviously he had been on the right path so far.<br /> <br /> OOC:<br /> Most of the people were afraid of Mark 5, he has threatened to or actually beaten them up ( or someone they know). To them, he is a crazy guy who could crush you today and protect your sorry ass tomorrow. Completely mental. No Rhyme or reason To his actions.<br /> Some resent him: they fought against oppressors Or bullies, and had been Winning For The First time when this asshole came around and beat them up.<br /> The Tattoo wearing guys belonging to a Gang had been losing a fight, and since the other side was 'obviously' attacking them (they actually were striking back) he stepped in. Now their area of influence was twice it's size.<br /> The now-cane guy was once again beating his daughter (for taking drugs) when Mark 5 could See him. As punishment his leg was broken. His daughter was horrified, and took to caring for her father, who was in a curious Position now: she stopped taking drugs, which was all he wanted, but he was in constantly pain now. He hated Mark 5 (who he thought of as some sort of ex-boyfriend/dealer), but was too afraid to do anything.<br /> However, there were still quite a few people genuinly happy to see him- mainly the homeless who often found themselves the victims of more privileged people with a temper, aggressive mobsters and overly protective neighbours. Someone that actually seemed to care about their wellbeing, to the point he took the fight to their Tormentors, was a godsent. That he was obviously mental was a minor point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T22:00:25-08:00","id":1008413,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Informed (Athanor), Inspired, Tormented, Disconnected<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 6/12 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 1/5</b></div> <br /> This is weird. (this isn't weird.) This is <i>so weird. </i><br /> <br /> She's working alongside a human, and it feels like she's sleepwalking. She's too numb to really appreciate it. Her own body language isn't instinctively human- she can recognize feelings and motives in the human's movements, but it feels like she can't reflect them back. She just labors and stays silent, keeping her self-pitying melancholy to herself.<br /> <br /> But they're sharing the work. Whatever else is in the deeper waters of their minds, their conscious focus is the exact same thing. It's nice!<br /> <br /> The others are here, to her great surprise. No alchemist in sight. Earth frets about it as she carries the bag, and finally sets it down where it's needed. She exposes her palms and raises her eyebrows to the human, trying to convey calm and pause.<br /> <br /> With her hands and clothes covered in dirt, she lumbers over to the other Created. It's tense. Her Azothic radiance is simmering with Torment. She puts a hand over her mouth and drags it sharply sideways, leaving a black smear around her lips. <i>Speechless.</i><br /> <br /> She averts her eyes from Mark 5, her face showing shame. Instead she scowls at Adonis, demanding explanation. <i>Well?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T08:10:44-08:00","id":1008541,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 6/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis hesitates. Mark 5 didn't really by his story, and he doubts Earth will, either. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Uh... well. I led the alchemist away so that you could take a look around the van. And, uh... destroy it, I guess. Nice work. I don't think he knows what was in those tubes and stuff. He thinks he's just working for a chemical company. He wasn't talking about Vitriol or Pandorans. He wasn't making anything. He just guarded the van. The van was his responsibility, so... he might lose his job. He might not, but what do you think is better? I mean, we could let that happen. But he has a thing for me. If you think he could be useful, we could keep him alive. Maybe help him keep his job.&quot;</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T13:02:02-08:00","id":1008651,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Mark 5</span><br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Steadfast<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Even though the Tammuz was basically brimming with joy upon seeing Earth, he did not miss her ashamed look. This whole business must have brought up some rather unhappy memories. He took notice of the torment, and something within him stirred. Memories of a similar state. He had to help her. But how? This was unknown territory, however, he had seen humans cheer each other up in times like this, so he tried to do the same. Trying his best at smiling sympatheticly, it came out passable... barely. Better than anyone could have expected, though, really. It was a smile, at least. The titan's hand reached out to awkwardly pat Earth on the arm twice, then he immediately stopped the gesture. This was weird. How was this supposed make someone feel better?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;If you think he could be useful, we could keep him alive.&quot;</span><br /> Now, Adonis was speaking his language. Useful. He might actually be that, since his bosses are the ones they...<br /> Everything <i>clicked</i>.<br /> A Titan, tasked with keeping a former Centimanus on the path. A Fury, former Centimanus, on the Path of the Vigilante.<br /> Apparently, an entire Corporation of Alchemists, guilty of the most horrible crimes against the Created. All three in the same city. How very clear. How very obvious what is meant to happen.<br /> <i>&quot;Punish those responsible of the same crimes as you once committed, and find absolvation in distancing yourself from Earth-Dies-Screaming through that&quot;.</i> Who better to help with a task like this than a Soldier?<br /> And finally, the Mimic. The wonderful Mimic, distracted and curious, defending a potential Alchemist. A potential Alchemist the Tammuz would have probably just... <b>handled</b> rather than listened to. Pretty Boy must have been sent by the Principle, to ensure that this crucial piece of Earth's redemption is not broken before its time.<br /> Mark 5 facepalmed and exclaimed <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Yes, of course!&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <i>OOC: So basically Mark sees Earth looking away due to shame, smiles and pats her arm. What she makes of that... we'll see about that =D</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 11-26-2016, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T21:57:49-08:00","id":1009177,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Informed (Athanor), Inspired, Tormented, Disconnected<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 6/12 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 1/5</b></div> <br /> Earth stares at Mark 5 like something from another planet after his reassuring gesture. An attack? She shoves him back in a locker-room way, but doesn't say a word.<br /> <br /> She doesn't have the energy to object to Mark 5's explanation, she just wearily shrugs and waves it off. What does it matter? She'll be leaving them behind soon, anyway.<br /> <br /> Another attack- oh, Mark is hitting himself. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Yes, of course!&quot; </span><br /> <br /> Earth looks baffled. She'd really like to just dig a hole down to the Underworld and disappear from all human and inhuman contact, but for one last time she opens her palms to Mark. <i>Out with it, then.</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T05:39:12-08:00","id":1009736,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 6/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis looks over at Mark 5, slightly confused. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Um... what's 'of course'?&quot;</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T07:21:09-08:00","id":1009763,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Mark 5</span><br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Steadfast<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If Mark hadn't felt uncomfortable patting Earth in the first place, this might have hurt. In addition, he had kind of been in Earth's place earlier, with Adonis trying to help, making him feel uncomfortable. So instead, he felt reinforced in his understanding that this type of contact was not meant for him.<br /> <br /> Incredulous at their question, Mark 5 pointed at them <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Don't you see? This was meant to be!&quot; </span><br /> He waved at all of the city.<span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Alchemists out there, perfect for a Vigilante! And the Pretty Boy knows one of them. With the Non-Alchemist, we can find them. We can take them out, make the city save for other Created.&quot; </span><br /> Mark 5 smiled.<span style=\"color:#000080\"> &quot;With this, we can prove once and for all that Earth is a good person!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <i>OOC: So yeah, that Adonis might have different interests or goals doesn't really cross his mind. Why would he? After all, Mark 5 has a Mission now. Everything else is secondary. Yes, even the fact that other people have their own life. Good old-fashioned 'Everything for the Mission!'</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T01:00:23-08:00","id":1010099,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Informed (Athanor), Inspired, Tormented, Disconnected<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 6/12 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 1/5</b></div> <br /> She's not into it. This fake alchemist would never work with them. The only thing in this awful world that's &quot;meant to be&quot; is her returning to the cold mud of the grave. Woe is me, alienation and dejection, doomed to walk the world alone, shrouded in Torment, etc etc, you get the picture-<br /> <br /> Wait, &quot;Earth is a good person?&quot; She stumbles over that part. She points to her chest, dumbfounded. Maybe she misheard him. Why? Why say that against all evidence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 12-01-2016, 01:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T04:41:57-08:00","id":1010150,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 6/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis doesn't really get why Mark 5 is now so willing to let Erwin live, but he's happy. He didn't want Erwin's death on his conscience. He notices that Mark 5 perked up when he mentioned &quot;useful,&quot; so if that's how he needs to keep Erwin safe, so be it. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;He's head over heels for me. I'm sure if I ask him, he'll be willing to give me whatever information I want.&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T10:22:13-08:00","id":1010251,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Mark 5</span><br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Steadfast<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;He's head over heels for me. I'm sure if I ask him, he'll be willing to give me whatever information I want.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> What a truly strange phrase. While aware that it meant something like feeling strongly for someone to the point one has clouded judgement, the Titan was unsure what exactly that meant.<br /> The Non-Alchemist still had to be punished for his crimes, of course, but for now, they needed him. Adonis seemed really on board with the Mission, though. Wasn't that forthcoming earlier. &quot;<i>Good!&quot; </i>Mark 5 thought. He didn't know what exactly changed his mind, but if it meant he'd help them out with his mind control, so be it.<br /> <br /> The confused look on Earth's face was unexpected, though. He had expected joy or something like it. Decisiveness. Determination. What was confusing her though?<br /> Well, it couldn't all be easy, could it? Mark 5 pointed at her. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Erm, yes, you. This is all about you. Or did you want to ask something else?&quot; </span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T00:26:02-08:00","id":1010963,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Informed (Athanor), Inspired, Tormented, Disconnected<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 6/12 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 1/5</b></div> <br /> Well, she can't be <i>that</i> alienated if their master plan is All About Her, can she? Mark 5 and Adonis came after her, and not to drive her away. A little bit of fire lights up behind her eyes. Her insides churn, and she coughs up black bile into the dirt. Removing the blockage loosens her tongue a little. She croaks at them: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;you think i'm good?&quot;</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T06:34:08-08:00","id":1011041,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Mark 5</span><br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Steadfast<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;you think i'm good?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> This was a unforseen question. Wasn't that what her journey was all about - become good? <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Yes, of course. Actions speak for themselves. We've been together for a while now, so I can tell by yours. And I know what Good is.&quot; </span>Then, with a smile and pointing a thumb at himself, he added the Nickname she'd given him: <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Hero talking, remember?&quot;</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T15:26:04-08:00","id":1011246,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 6/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> <span style=\"color:#daa520\">&quot;You think I'm good?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Adonis looks over at Earth, surprised. This is- was- Earth-Dies-Screaming, the stories of whose horror reached as far north from Arizona as the Canadian Plains. Her words and actions tonight have made her seem every bit as tough as the stories have said; not as scary, of course, since she has given up the Refinement of Flux. But now she seems downright vulnerable. This surprises him, and he starts thinking back to the human interaction he has had. A memory of Lily giving words of encouragement when he doubted his worth wells up, and he decides that something like that would be right- just not as personal as he had tried with Mark 5. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Well, I mean, Mark 5 told me about how you used lightning to destroy those Pandorans. If those things got out, they would've killed a lot of people. Destroying them was Good, Earth. A Really Good thing.&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T00:03:52-08:00","id":1011395,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Informed (Athanor), Inspired, Tormented, Disconnected<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 6/12 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 1/5</b></div> <br /> Her humours are balancing. The storm clouds start to clear.<br /> <br /> Earth looks from Mark 5 to Adonis, wary- and then suddenly the lurching monster pulls them both in for a tight, breath-stealing hug. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;thanks.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Resolving Tormented, +1 Beat.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> She pulls away, and walks back over to the human gardener. She can't quite make eye contact, but she clears her throat and croaks: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;i gotta go. but i'll come back.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> When she returns to the throng, her usual bored-teenager expression is back, but she's standing up a little straighter. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Alright, I'm in. Your plan sounds decent, Hero. Now let's blow this place, it sucks.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T06:38:32-08:00","id":1012548,"title":"","content":"<i>Night, November 3<sup>rd</sup>, 2016</i><br /> <b>Adonis' Apartment- Earth, Mark 5, and Adonis</b><br /> <br /> Before leaving the community garden, the woman Earth was gardening with- and how strange it was, that she didn't seem to care to ask for a name or offer one herself -gave a relieved smile at seeing the obvious affection Earth held for the people who came to get and when the Promethean approached she laid a reassuring hand on her arm- the arm knotted with corded muscle and curled talons for fingers. &quot;I'll be here when you do.&quot;<br /> <br /> The three Created make their way back through the city, led by the Muse to a run-down tenement not too far off from where they began. There's plenty of them around the university where the youthful looking Galateid would fit right in, and most people are too busy with their own issues to notice any strange comings and goings. The fog has lifted, and there's a bit of a chill to the night air. Even with the streetlights, and the quieter, but still present, bustle of Ellice and Portage Avenue, the city has gone quiet, but the building has not. It hums with human voices of all description at all levels of volume. Some shout, some whisper, some speak in English, some in French, and some in far more distant languages besides.<br /> <br /> The spoils of their impromptu raid against Amalgama LTD are spread out on the floor. A series of potions in thick tempered glass, marked with a series of alchemical symbolism and medical jargon, and a rough journal with a weatherbeaten cover, a patchwork mixture between diary, manifesto, day planner, and alchemical diagram. An Athanor. But where to start?<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Intelligence + Occult or Intelligence + Science to decipher the labels on the potions. Intelligence + Occult or Intelligence + Empathy to decipher the text within the Athanor. Earth has the Informed (Athanor) Condition, and as it is a Stannum Athanor, she gets a +2 bonus to understanding it. She could also conceivably use her Library at this point.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T08:20:35-08:00","id":1012591,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Mark 5</span><br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Steadfast<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div><br /> A genuine hideout. Impressive! Even more, it was in the midst of humans! Adonis earned quite a lot of respect from bum-dweller Mark 5 with this.<br /> Sure, the Titan didn't strictly need to sleep, so he didnt need a home like this; but that doesnt mean he didnt desire one. His attempts so far were limited, though.<br /> He'd have to ask the Mimic how he got it at some point. But now, there was hero-ing to do!<br /> <br /> The Potpourri of voices was oddly comforting. Since he didnt get what about half of them meant, they turned into a peaceful Background noise.<br /> With this, he turned his attention to the labels: &quot;What have they Stolen from you?&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=4268a0c9\" target=\"_blank\">1 sux on Int+Occ: Decipher labels</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  Couldn't sit down to write yesterday. 12-06-2016, 01:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T13:20:19-08:00","id":1012748,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 6/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> When they get to his apartment, Adonis take a moment to close his eyes and take a deep breath, a content look on his face. The sound of so many people around... it's comforting. The English he understands, the French he doesn't, the other languages he is only slightly aware of. It's a confused jumble of voices that keeps him aware of the humanity he so longs to attain, even when he sleeps. <br /> <br /> He looks at the potions and sees the alchemical symbols. His stomach churns a little. Erwin said he just watched the van, but if he was a scientist, wouldn't he know alchemical symbols weren't used in science? <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>Wait, are they? </i></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis attempts to understand the labels of the potions and the text. Intelligence 1 + Occult 1 = 2 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/462973\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>. Intelligence 1 + Empathy = 4 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/462974\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T13:55:45-08:00","id":1012761,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Informed (Athanor), Inspired, Disconnected<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 6/12 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 1/5</b></div> <br /> Earth is a little starstruck that Adonis has an <i>apartment(!) </i>instead of some condemned building or crevice under a bridge. Hell of a place to make your lair.<br /> <br /> She focuses on the Athanor, and draws out some of Dead Girl's collected journals and observations from a deep and safe place in her backpack. Her Library is a patchwork thing, something like the journal itself. It's a mix of direct observation and secondhand rumor, filtered through stained envelopes and notebooks of poetry and Polaroids and semi-scientific taxonomy, most of it in the Muse's elegant handwriting. There's useful and concrete information in there, but immersing herself into Dead Girl's mindset and their time on the road brings strange feelings.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Gonna resolve Informed. Intelligence 1 + Occult 3 + Stannum 2 + Library 1: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/462977\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>, exceptional success with Informed.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T07:15:16-08:00","id":1013142,"title":"","content":"<b>Mark 5</b><br /> <br /> You pick up a bottle containing a rust red potion. You can see that the colour mostly stems from a granular, rough powder. As you look closer, you can see that there are flecks of yellow, what might be copper, mixed in with the rest. The first symbol is a downwards facing triangle with an arrow pointing upwards from the base of the triangle, two lines crossing through the middle of the arrow's shaft. This is contained within two Vs, framing it within a diamond that extends upwards and downwards diagonally off of the two side corners of the diamond. A third, and last, symbol sits off to the side of the extended diamond, a gentle upwards swoop and a sharp downwards angle.<br /> <br /> Crocus of Iron, Alembic, Distillation. A potion that bestows a Distillation of a Ferrum Alembic?<br /> <br /> <b>Adonis</b><br /> <br /> The Muse takes up an elegant looking bottle, something like a perfume spritzer that is filled with a dark blue liquid. There's a word in elegant script scrawled across it; 'Indulgence'. It's contained within a heavily stylized version of the alchemical symbol for cobalt, and etched down near the barcode is the same extended diamond and elegant angled swop that is on the far more utilitarian potion in Mark 5's hands. Cobalt, Alembic, Distillation. A potion that bestows a Distillation of a Cobalus Alembic?<br /> <br /> You set it down and read some of the first few pages of the Athanor. For your entire life, your attitude has been that of Aurum. You are a Mimic. You have been a mirror and a follower to the humans around you, trying to cater to them, learn their ways, slide seamlessly into their lives. But there's pain, hatred, and a self-loathing to these words that genuinely shocks you. A page or two of seemingly rational journal, with mad scribbles on the margins suggesting either later reflection, or the crushing depths of Torment. You come to a <a href=\"https://images.coplusk.net/project_images/104265/image/full_Mental_Illness_1315269787.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">page</a> that was created with some care. <br /> <br /> Perhaps you need to take a step away from it right now.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Adonis gains the Shaken Condition. Empathizing with someone who had been in the depths of Torment is not a gentle experience.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Earth</b><br /> <br /> The pretty boy seems a little overwhelmed, but maybe a fellow Fury can internalize it more. Earth reads quickly, turning from one patchwork journal to another. She can easily track the author of the Athanor's frustrations, the constant looming threat of Disquiet, the eternal outsider status. Like wielding lightning and smashing buildings, writing this was a form of release for the author, a kind of catharsis. She could track when they were <i>in </i>Torment, and when they slipped <i>out </i>of it, just through the writing. They wrote more, and much less coherently, when they were Tormented. The author couldn't stand the way humans rejected their own over minuscule differences, it disgusted them, and they endeavoured to make a home for the night creatures, the unloved, the broken things. They would be the eye of a hurricane, a shelter in a hostile world.<br /> <br /> The Named leaps back and forth from one book to the other. She understands rejection. Dead Girl was an expert at demonstrating it. When she was particularly deep in her Torment she'd string others along and then crush them, body and soul, to prove her devotion to Earth-Dies-Screaming. She sees those words, sees the places where the tip of the pen dug deeply into paper with the intensity of emotion in the writing. Dead Girl understood obsession and rejection intimately, and she professed to love the unloveable, but did she really? You compare the collections of her writings with that of the Athanor, and it's like two warring philosophies- one that seeks to meet rejection with acceptance, and another that seeks to reject the world that rejected them. You compare simple, rough-hewn transmutation equations, and illustrations of a humanoid form full of storm clouds letting them loose into the world around them, with Polaroids from Dead Girl's collections. Images of Wastelands and candid shots of Earth-Dies-Screaming with their pack.<br /> <br /> You can hardly recognize yourself in that twisted flesh.<br /> <br /> Eventually, Dead Girl's final gift to you gets put away, and only the Athanor remains. You know what it has to teach you.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Earth gains the Informed (Stannum) Condition. You can use it on any roll that conceivably fits the Stannum philosophy, or more directly, on Transmutations.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T16:03:02-08:00","id":1014035,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent), Shaken<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 6/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis reads the journal with growing horror, and he almost feels ill. Hatred, disgust, loneliness, contempt: every sentence of the journal that isn't alchemical jargon oozes these emotions. It rattles him, because he's suddenly confronted with a fact he would rather ignore: these are human emotions. Sooner or later, he's going to feel them, too. This is Torment. He's never had to face it, and he has no idea what he will be like when he finally does. He finally comes to the page covered with scribblings and blood, the one dominated by the drawing of the hanged girl. His stomach lurches and he quickly slams the Athanor shut, and shoves it away from himself. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Shit. This is... bad. What made them like... this?&quot; </span><br /> <br /> He looks away from the Athanor and over at the potion he studied, which he picks up again. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">\u200b&quot;Cobalus Distillation in this one.&quot; </span>Cobalus. Impurity. The Cathars. In a lot of ways, it's the opposite of Aurum: Mimics study what makes humans beautiful and good and perfect, Cathars study what makes humans ugly and bad and imperfect. He shudders at the thought, because it reminds him that humans really can be ugly. He's seen it first hand. He stands and takes a couple steps away from the others. This shit is scary.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T22:07:18-08:00","id":1014162,"title":"","content":"Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Steadfast<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5<br /> <br /> <br /> Heat welled up inside. A Ferrum distillation. <br /> A Created went through hardships, took on challenges, improved himself, just like him.<br /> And now, someone else could use the fruits of that labour as easily as the Chips they reach for from the comfort of their sofa.<br /> Someone's hard work, taken away, just like that.<br /> &quot;They cheat. They steal. They miss the point!&quot; went through his head, in a loop that got faster and faster.<br /> He Suddenly let go of the flask, letting it tumble on the table. His Grip had gone hard. He didnt want to break it.<br /> His breathing closer to angry snorting Than anything.<br /> Bastards.<br /> <br /> Mark 5 took a step back, Only To notice Adonis in the corner. The shaken face of his was oddly calming. Lile the people he saved looked like before he appeared. The Titan closed his eyes, trying to remember first meeting Adonis. He still couldn't recall his name. But he was sure the Mimic hadn't looked shaken then. &quot;Guess he just realized what he was in for&quot; He thought grimly.<br /> Then, all attention was turned to Earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T11:18:40-08:00","id":1017723,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Informed (Stannum), Inspired, Disconnected<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 6/12 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 1/5</b></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Shit. This is... bad. What made them like... this?&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Blame their creator, or the Principle. This is who we are. Torment is real, more real than pretending to be human. Embracing it is better than running away.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She's staring at a photo. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;If you knew how bad it could get, you'd see this is better. This is the floor, but there's...an infinity of mud under that floor. You get lost down there. At least they're being honest about how fucked it is.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She puts it away. That's all she says on the subject for right now.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;It's not good when I take the lead. What do we do with this?&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T11:43:48-08:00","id":1017731,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent), Shaken<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 6/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;It's not good when I take the lead. What do we do with this?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Adonis turns around and shrugs, still troubled by the journal and the turn the conversation took. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Figure out how they got their hands on this stuff, maybe. Find out who they... destroyed to get this stuff from. What if the potions came from their Refinements? Maybe if we got in touch with the other Created in the city, ask about someone who was following Ferrum and Cobalus, that could be a lead.&quot; </span>He walks back over to the others and squats down, looking from the journal to the potions with a dour expression. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">\u200b&quot;In the meantime, we should hold on to these. I could keep this stuff here, if you guys want. Or we could split it up. I'm meeting Er... the not-alchemist tomorrow night again. Maybe I could try to get some information out of him about this.&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T06:45:21-08:00","id":1018439,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Steadfast<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;You get lost down there. At least they're being honest about how fucked it is.&quot;</span><br /> <i>Which is why it's so important to show others that there is a way out, </i>Mark 5 thought. He said <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;I appreciate honesty. Even if I don't understand.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Maybe if we got in touch with the other Created in the city, ask about someone who was following Ferrum and Cobalus, that could be a lead.&quot;</span><br /> Actually, that sounded like a decent idea. The Tammuz nodded. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Sounds good. I'll be on to that.&quot;</span> He gave Earth an questioning look: <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Wanna tag along?&quot; </span>It would make things harder, sure. But he was not one to back out of a challenge. Plus this could send a message, too.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">\u200b&quot;In the meantime, we should hold on to these. I could keep this stuff here, if you guys want.&quot; </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Sounds good to me. Not gonna carry that around. It'd feel... wrong&quot; </span> he said, pointing to the Ferrum cannister.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;I'm meeting Er... the not-alchemist tomorrow night again. Maybe I could try to get some information out of him about this.&quot; </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Be careful. Cover of Night would be perfect for him to try something, so it could get dangerous. Try to arrange a meeting out in the open, among people and during the day, next time.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T11:18:06-08:00","id":1019341,"title":"","content":"<b>Friday November 4<sup>th</sup> 2016</b><br /> <br /> The day is unnaturally hot. The city should be buried in snow at this point, but outside temperatures are reaching 14<sup>0</sup>C and people are milling about in t-shirts and shorts. It will soon be a Friday night in Winnipeg, and the city will, briefly, come alive. How do you spend your day?<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Alright guys, how are you going to spend your day? We're making a bit of a jump to the next evening, so if you want to get in Extended Actions this would be the time. Intelligence + Occult or Intelligence + Streetwise could help you track down known supernatural elements or whispers on the underground. Manipulation + Socialize could help you track down whatever social events are going down. It's really up to you. What does the Throng do next?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T10:48:16-08:00","id":1020494,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Informed (Stannum), Inspired, Disconnected<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 6/12 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 1/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> In the late dark dead of last night, Earth went back to the community garden, dug a shallow grave, and buried herself in it.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Azoth 3 + Composure 3 + Vivid Dreams 1. <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/468849\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes.</a> 3 Pyros regained, and 1 more for the sun rising on Friday morning.<br /> <br /> I'll do a bit of flashback now. Here's two pictures of Dead Girl.<br /> <a href=\"http://68.media.tumblr.com/3b73aece6b4461da8e5668b05d3e11e2/tumblr_inline_ns308bWGId1t3nzp0_500.png\" target=\"_blank\">More human</a> (same artist who did the pic I'm using for Earth)<br /> <a href=\"http://cmro.travis-starnes.com/images/characters/deadgirl.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Less human</a> (the Marvel character I'm borrowing the name from)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Her undead fist breaks through the dirt just before dawn. She sees the sun rise while walking back to Adonis' place, and it sparks a little hope as always. In his bathroom, she takes a cold shower for the first time in too long.<br /> <br /> Plan for today: revised version of the plan from yesterday. Earth consults her handy mobile Library to help look for pilgrimage markers, Wasteland scars, and other supernatural signs of Promethean activity. There's some good stuff in there about hunting the Created.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I don't know how exactly we want to handle the extended action as far as target numbers and time per roll. I'll assume it's one roll per hour maybe? And I'll just make the 4 rolls I'm allowed and see where it gets me. Intelligence 1 + Occult 3 + Library 1<br /> <br /> First roll: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/468852\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a><br /> <br /> Second roll: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/468853\" target=\"_blank\">4 successes</a><br /> <br /> Third roll: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/468854\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a><br /> <br /> Fourth roll: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/468855\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a><br /> <br /> 10 successes after 4 hours of searching Winnipeg on foot.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Once she's found some things, she links up with Mark 5 and Adonis to share her info.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 12-21-2016, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T11:06:13-08:00","id":1020504,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent), Shaken<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 6/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> That night, Adonis lies on his mattress, and lets the sound of human voices wash over him and lull him to sleep. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis will have a Pyros-restoring dream. Azoth 2 + Composure 2 = 4 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/468864\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>, so 2 Pyros plus 1 from the dawn to bring him up to 9 Pyros.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <hr /><br /> Adonis looks around the street. The presence of so many humans around is exciting, but they don't have time to mingle. There's a murder they need to investigate, and finding their fellow Created will help that along. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Whoever these Amalgama people really are, they could be keeping tabs on all of us. We need to find the others and find out what they now, or at least warn them.&quot; </span>He's blabbing, trying to control the fear that has been roiling in his stomach since last night and all day. He looks at the others for guidance. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Any ideas on where to start?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis will attempt to get a feel for what is happening on the streets. Manipulation 3 + Socialize 2 = 5 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/468858\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes</a>, but I'm going to go ahead and make it a failure to resolve Shaken</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T01:34:52-08:00","id":1021191,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Steadfast<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 7/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> As most nights, Mark 5 didn't go to sleep. He hardly ever felt a real need to, anyway. Instead, he was out, 'keeping the city save' and putting an ear to the ground, in case he could gather any information on disappearing 'hobos' or 'weirdos'.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Any ideas on where to start?&quot;</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;We could start with whether any of us could dig something up. Earth?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">\u200b<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> 1 Pyros due to sunrise. <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=6974e5bf\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#00ff00\">0 sux.</span></a><span style=\"color:#00ff00\"> Resolving Steadfast to get 1 sux.</span></div></div> </div> </div></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T12:51:16-08:00","id":1021371,"title":"","content":"<i>Friday November 4<sup>th </sup>2016</i> <b>- Evening</b><br /> <br /> <b>Earth</b><br /> <br /> Pyros surges through your veins, recharging in the chilled embrace of the soil. Things <i>whisper </i>to you through the ground, memories that aren't your own, fingers brushing along your skin. Nostalgic, desperate, frustrated, resentful. You aren't sure how much is dream, and how much reality. As usual, your dreamscape is... difficult to describe. It's from a place before language, a place that is all vibration and sensation and endless fields of flame. Your Azoth surges in sympathy, opening to the very source of the Flame Immortal. You get the idea that it is trying, desperately, to communicate with you, but it can't quite reach you.<br /> <br /> You spend most of your morning, and a good part of the afternoon, wandering from the community garden, to the Exchange, to the West End, and back downtown towards Adonis' apartment. Pilgrim Marks are such a varied form of communication, a mixture of simplistic ideograms and complex alchemical ciphers. They're a patchwork of language, English blended with Church Latin, street maps from above blended with transmutation equations. It's base lead and refined gold all in one.<br /> <br /> You pick your way through delayed conversations, Created sharing progress, breakthroughs, triumphs, and sorrows- words that might be taken for crude graffiti tags serving as key and identifier for the equations that comprised the conversation. However, every Pilgrim Mark you find makes reference to the same thing, a weekly Friday night meeting at the <a href=\"http://www.theforks.com/attractions/at-the-forks/oodena-celebration-circle\" target=\"_blank\">Oodena</a> <a href=\"http://www.theforks.com/uploads/ck/files/AboutOodena.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Celebration</a> <a href=\"http://www.theforks.com/uploads/ck/files/OodenaConstellations.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Circle</a>.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Earth gains four points of Pyros and a point of Willpower. This extra Willpower will fade at the end of the scene if it isn't used</i><br /> <br /> <b>Adonis</b><br /> <br /> The Muse wanders the streets, almost aimlessly. He's still shaken from reading the Athanor the night before; what will Torment be like for him, when he finally falls into it? He doesn't really connect with anyone in his social circle, or through polite conversation on the street. He ducks into a coffee shop and looms over a mug and a pastry. Eventually, he passes the <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/maps/place/National+Research+Council+Canada/@49.8939687,-97.1514931,19.08z/data=!4m5!3m4!1s0x0:0xea243044383677d0!8m2!3d49.8937933!4d-97.1505996\" target=\"_blank\">National Research Council of Canada</a> and the <b>Amalgama LTD </b>office beside it, the gilt-edged black symbol gleaming in the sunlight on the side of a lilac metal building. <br /> <br /> Is Erwin in at the office today? Could he go in and just... see him? Humans do that, don't they? Visit boyfriends at work? He wonders what he might do to Erwin, if he came across him in Torment?<br /> <br /> The Galataeid is thrown off his game, wasting the rest of his morning, needing a bit of time to himself. He meets up with Earth and Mark 5 after lunch.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Adonis gains a Beat, a point of Willpower, and three points of Pyros</i><br /> <br /> <b>Mark 5</b><br /> <br /> Nervous humans speak to the Titan, telling him about strange vagrants who loiter around the Forks and in St. Boniface. They seem eager for him to go after them, maybe they're dangerous? Who knows what the local Created are like. Perhaps they are amassing to figure out what to do with Earth. Perhaps they are terrorizing the humans around them. People speak in hushed whispers, thinking that these scarred and somewhat fearsome wanderers might be some kind of new gang, what, with their distinctive looks and peculiar tags.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Mark 5 gains a Beat and a point of Pyros</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T03:08:25-08:00","id":1023644,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 8/11 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> Mark 5 started with sharing his information. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There are apparently some strange faces, somewhere around the Forks and St. Boniface. Could be a group of Created. Not sure if it's safe to go there, humans are not very helpful in that regard. We could check out the area, looks like they tagged it, so there might be Pilgrim Marks. Maybe that's the right trace, who knows?&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  copy-pasted Steadfast, though that Condition has been resolved 01-01-2017, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T07:17:35-08:00","id":1023746,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 9/10<br /> Beats: 3/5 I Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis rubs the back of his head, feeling sheepish. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;I... haven't done anything today. I get a little skittish around the others, sometimes. You never know if they're in a good mood or not. I would like it if we went as a group. That's not a problem, is it guys?&quot;</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T13:10:29-08:00","id":1023908,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Informed (Stannum), Inspired, Disconnected<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: <i>6</i>/5 | Pyros: 10/12 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 1/5</b></div> <br /> The image that stays with her from her Pyros dreams is a sense that some angelic thing is trying to Descend to the Earth from another plane of existence, but it keeps &quot;missing&quot; the right frequency of reality, and the near-miss causes waves and earthquakes instead of divine visitation.<br /> <br /> Productive day. She's getting a sense of the local language of signs. It probably helps that she's been on the road longer than the others, as far as she knows- she has a better sense of what to look for. And she actually has things to tell the others!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;The Forks is what they call that spot where the Red River splits in two, right? A little south of Downtown? There's this place on the shoreline called Oodena with a bunch of standing stones and mystical stuff- pretty sure that's what the signs are talking about. There's this group Ramble there every Friday, that's gotta be what the humans are talking about.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She bops Adonis on the arm, which she's seen people do. Usually people stronger than Adonis. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;We'll cover you. I don't wanna go alone, either.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T02:07:45-08:00","id":1024161,"title":"","content":"Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 8/11 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Titan watched the friendly attack with interest. He had seen people do that to each other, but apparently missed some integral part of how to do it or when it is appropriate. He had liked hanging around that gym.<br /> He Openly watched the Mimic's reaction with curiousity.<br /> <br /> &quot;We'll cover you. I don't wanna go alone, either.&quot;<br /> &quot;Sure, I prefer that, too. Being together is better than seperating. They always get you one by one when you are seperated.&quot;<br /> He had seen that in a movie about some sort of serial killer. As far as he was concerned, that was what they were dealing with.<br /> He took notice of Earth preferring company. That was good.... right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":"01-01-2017, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T06:14:43-08:00","id":1024261,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 9/10<br /> Beats: 3/5 I Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis gives an &quot;ooph&quot; of surprise as Earth hits his arm, but her tone is friendly, and he knows that if she wanted to truly hurt him, she could- probably without even touching him. He rubs his shoulder a little, but smiles back at Earth. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Alright then. Let's head to the Forks. Might be better if you let me do the talking, Earth. They'll know me, I can prove that you turned over a new leaf.&quot;</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T13:16:12-08:00","id":1025142,"title":"","content":"<u>The Forks</u><br /> <br /> <b>Evening-</b> Friday November 4<sup>th</sup><br /> <br /> You spend most of your afternoon wandering the Forks, walking along the pathways that border the mighty Red River. At a <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/maps/@49.8891738,-97.1274812,3a,75y,101.06h,82.15t/data=!3m7!1e1!3m5!1svVD1yjQebgCQx7G1ULNNhg!2e0!3e2!7i13312!8i6656\" target=\"_blank\">viewpoint</a> gazing across to the other side, flanked by worn stone bison, you can see the weather-beaten edifice of the St. Boniface Cathedral, the only thing left standing of the original building after a catastrophic fire in 1968, the second such fire to destroy the place. In the summer, the river rises up to cover the walkways that are supposed to allow safe travel at the water's edge, submerging the works of men, indifferent to the passage of humanity. You saw a <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/maps/@49.8870986,-97.1304089,3a,75y,180.2h,87.66t/data=!3m8!1e1!3m6!1s-dCMtCX3uHiE%2FVdpVMl1BZjI%2FAAAAAAACRH0%2F0soG9ZskLQQZ5-H_jYm2lSWhrl1_I5-gQCJkC!2e4!3e11!6s%2F%2Flh4.googleusercontent.com%2F-dCMtCX3uHiE%2FVdpVMl1BZjI%2FAAAAAAACRH0%2F0soG9ZskLQQZ5-H_jYm2lSWhrl1_I5-gQCJkC%2Fw203-h100-k-no-pi-0-ya50.58404-ro-0-fo100%2F!7i10240!8i5120\" target=\"_blank\">marker</a>, under a permanent tent, outside the Market, that shows where the water rose in a massive flood in the 50s. The Red River brought people to Winnipeg, and it could rise up and take them away. It was a sleeping giant the people in the city were keenly aware of. All too often, the Red would give up bodies. Red ribbons with bleeding black ink are tied to bridge railings, torn at by the wind, commemorating the forgotten, the invisible.<br /> <br /> As night begins to fall, humanity begins to clear out. You find the <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/maps/@49.8868,-97.1290862,3a,75y,194.02h,83.4t/data=!3m8!1e1!3m6!1s-9rir6eNONAg%2FWBn6yZHqvYI%2FAAAAAAAAV_g%2Fs_TrKcVlRxESnXb1ll4bmVFUFfRQEAlTwCLIB!2e4!3e11!6s%2F%2Flh6.googleusercontent.com%2F-9rir6eNONAg%2FWBn6yZHqvYI%2FAAAAAAAAV_g%2Fs_TrKcVlRxESnXb1ll4bmVFUFfRQEAlTwCLIB%2Fw203-h100-k-no-pi-0-ya39.47028-ro-0-fo100%2F!7i5376!8i2688\" target=\"_blank\">Oodena Celebration Circle</a>... and you wait.<br /> <br /> The constant clicking of the weathervane pays witness to the wind as the lamplight glows in the twilight. You sit on the grassy hillside, gazing down at an ancient horizon that was elevated over millennia by the silt that gave the city its name. Winnipeg. Muddy Waters. The giant metal armatures are empty, their tiny peepholes and summoning circles void of the stars that will, in time, fill them. As the wind picks up, the aeolian harp built into the Northeast armature begins to moan and sing. The light fades, the tuneless song increases in volume.<br /> <br /> The sound speaks to something deep within both Adonis and Earth, a thing from before words, a Divine Breath.<br /> <br /> Like a lighthouse calling ships home, the light of the winter fire pit and the tuneless harp call to the Created.<br /> <br /> They come.<br /> <br /> They come in tattered rags and patchwork finery, they come at their best, they come as they are, and are those things altogether different? There are more Created gathered here at once than you have ever even <i>heard </i>of. Almost two dozen come strolling down the shallow steps and shambling across the rolling hills. Sturdy folk with clay in their hair and tattoos on their skin feel the stones carved with an outline of a Mesopotamian lion, the herald of the Harvest, and of Tammuz. Gaunt people with missing features and complexions of grey, black, green, and blue gather by the carving of Aset while a group of almost jaundiced individuals, their skins a riot of colours and textures, stand by the outline of Orion, tension like a thunderhead hanging over them. The beautiful, fitting every possible description of the word, lounge on the grass, while strange, damaged people leaking shadow and smoke, their faces and bodies a whirlwind of symbols, sit beneath the lyre.<br /> <br /> They seem to gather by Lineage out of habit, more than anything, as if they come to their shared symbols through Memory instead of conscious thought. The crowd slowly mixes, as the patchwork, premature people seek out those they recognize, avoid those they dislike, and ramble about the group. The fire pit down at the lowest point, in the centre of an Azothic compass, is conspicuously empty. There is no tradition, no law, for gatherings such as this. The Created must build it like they do everything else.<br /> <br /> When someone is ready, they will go down and speak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T14:05:37-08:00","id":1025156,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 8/11 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> The landscape was like it was MADE to be used by Created in their gatherings. But this couldn't be, could it? Anyway, it was an inspiring sight, all these Created coming to Ramble. Mark 5 seldomly thought about how he was small, how he might be part of something bigger - usually, he was too concerned with other things. But what he saw here made him realize once again that he wasn't alone, and that what he did was neither a seperate experience nor all that extraordinary: he was but a keg in a larger machine. Somehow, this was comforting.<br /> <br /> It was a sight to see, indeed. The thought of all these Created hearing about Earth's Change, imagining how this would give them new strength for their Pilgrimage made Mark 5's heart leap. Prematurely? Maybe. But this was a taste of what the Milestone, once fulfilled, would feel like, he was sure of it.<br /> He looked at the others. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;You know your way around here better than me, Pretty Boy. You lead, we follow, right behind you. Someone tries something funny with you, I'll take care of it.&quot; </span><br /> His voice was resolute, his posture determined. The Mimic could be sure he could rely on the Titan. To highlight this, he smiled, and clapped Adonis carefully on the back. After all, the gesture seems to have worked with Earth.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 01-01-2017, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T17:02:51-08:00","id":1025202,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Informed (Stannum), Inspired, Disconnected<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: <i>6</i>/5 | Pyros: 10/12 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 1/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> The harp echoes, she sits and listens. There's got to be some kind of ley line or fairy ring at a place like this, but she doesn't have the tools to sense it. Or does she? While there's still enough light to read, she skims her notes and looks for any familiar signs in the Circle.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Just throwing this out in case it gets me anywhere. Is there any evidence that the Celebration Circle is a place of supernatural energy and power based on the ones Earth has seen before, or just a highly symbolic mortal place? Intelligence 1 + Occult 3 + Library 1, 5 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/471444\" target=\"_blank\">1 success.</a> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Earth lurked behind the others. She didn't hide her Flux scars and twisted claw in front of the gathered pilgrims, but she was more aware of them than usual. She shunned the beautiful ones lounging on the grass, and stared with longing at the fluid and shadowy Riven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T08:06:16-08:00","id":1025440,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 9/10<br /> Beats: 3/5 I Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> Adonis takes a deep breath and blows it out again. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Well, here goes nothing,&quot; </span>he whispers, more to himself than to the others. He walks down to the fire pit. He stands for a moment, turning on the spot and taking in the Created around him: his fellow Muses, doomed to both attract and repel humans; the Tammuz, strong and dour like Mark 5 and Earth; the spiteful Frankensteins, the impassive Osirians, the ominous Ulgans.<br /> <br /> After he completes his turn, he begins. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Hello, everybody. Those of you who haven't met me before, my name is Adonis. I'm a Muse following the Refinement of Aurum. I would like to introduce two Tammuz who are new to Winnipeg. The first one is Mark 5, a Titan. The other is...&quot; </span>he braces himself. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Earth, a Fury who was once the Centimanus called Earth-Dies-Screaming.&quot; </span>He puts up his hands at the outburst. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Please! I know we've all heard stories about what Earth-Dies-Screaming did. But I promise you, that's not who Earth is anymore. She's better. Which brings me to my second point.&quot;</span> He recaps the events of the previous night, leaving out his brief fight with Mark 5 and Earth, and his &quot;date&quot; with Erwin.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;The man I talked to- and I guess humans in general- think that Amalgama is just a cutting-edge drug and make-up company. But what we found inside doesn't line up with that. At least some people working for the company are alchemists, who are killing Created to use our Alembics and Vitriol to make potions for their own profit. We stole a journal that belonged to one of our own, and two potions, one of a Ferrum Alembic and the other of a Cobalus Alembic. Does anybody here know of somebody who was following either or both of those Refinements and disappeared at some point?&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Adonis is going to try and convince the Created to accept Earth, and to ask if anybody knows a missing Promethean who was following one or both of the Refinements used in the potions. I'll treat those as two separate rolls, since the Create might not by his claim that Earth has turned a leaf, but would be willing to share what they know. I'll be using Presence since, to me, that feels like the &quot;group&quot; social Attribute, which means that my Unearthly Mien will apply here.<br /> <br /> Convincing: Presence 3 + Persuasion 3 = 6 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/471583\" target=\"_blank\">2 success</a>. Assuming we're going with the &quot; E.S. on 3's stack&quot;, that's an exceptional success, and the assembled Prometheans have the Swooning Condition towards Adonis.<br /> <br /> Getting Information: Presence 3 + Persuasion 3 = 6 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/471584\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>.<br /> <br /> I'm okay with rerolling these with Manipulation instead of Presence if you think that's more appropriate.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 01-02-2017, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T09:18:51-08:00","id":1025471,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> Scout looked over the other proto-people and was amazed. So many of his kind- like nothing he'd ever seen. The knowledge of humanity here would be staggering. If only they all could plumb the depths of the azothic memory collectively as one and share the experience! How many steps along the path it would take them all? It was incredible. Every detail, Scout inscribed into his mind. This ramble would be legendary as far as he was concerned, and he would not let it's memory fade.<br /> <br /> Scout kept his ears open, and his eyes up as he did his best to take in the features of each of his fellow Created, starting with other Nepri, and listening for their names and paths. Anyone speaking would find him listening, though he himself spoke rarely. He found his own mission, the search for the supposed Centimanus, taking a secondary seat. At least, until he found himself walking right towards the center where Adonis spoke.<br /> <br /> Scout didn't bother to hide his inquisitive heterochromatic gaze. And one hand moved to stroke his goatee as he'd seen someone in a movie do once. Reformed. Both fortunate and otherwise. The story of this... Amalgama however. That was horrifying. The very word Alchemist sent a tingle up and down his spine. He was too new in town, or so he was certain. He looked around, hopeful to see what others might have to say. He would approach these three when the immediate questions were answered. If nothing else, perhaps he could use the Azothic memory to search for signs of the missing. If they had alembics, he might could use them as an aid. He'd never exactly tried using Azothic memory in that fashion, but it might provide a clue, if no others had anything.<br /> <br /> Scout waited, and let his blue and green eyes settle on Earth, studying the flux scars. Fascinating indeed.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> Would you like a roll for Scout's passively gathering of information as he drifts through the Ramble? And could Wisdom of Ages be used the manner Scout is thinking of?</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8122,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","user":"ArchonAres","date":". 01-02-2017, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T13:14:52-08:00","id":1025538,"title":"","content":"<b>Evening-</b> Friday November 4<sup>th</sup><br /> <br /> <b>Adonis</b><br /> <br /> The group Ramble rumbles discontentedly while looking at the reformed Freak, but they can hardly say no to such a persuasive young man. There are quiet whispers of welcome across the gathering, and some grumbles. A few members of the other Lineages look at Adonis longingly, and the Muses delightedly clap and gesture their welcome. When it comes to vanished members of the Refinements, they shake their heads. Someone from the group of Riven, arms adorned with tight ribbon wraps that held all sorts of antique keys- you never know what a key will open -steps forwards. Half their head is shaved and the other half is long and dyed in a riot of colours, woven into one long braid. As they move, you can see the ribbons slip and slide, showing punctures and tears from teeth and talons, leaking mists into the night air that billows like smoke about their face.<br /> <br /> &quot;You said that the human was talking about where the truck came from when he found you, right? He mentioned... Tucson, I think? That's in Arizona. You hear things, about Arizona; most everyone knows a Pilgrim who went through Arizona, because there's a lot of alchemy to be found in Sedona and Tempe. Old Athanors, out there in the red sands.&quot;<br /> <br /> They're speaking to more than you now, you can tell, they're speaking to the Ramble as a whole, telling them a story.<br /> <br /> &quot;Only problem is, we have a tendency not to come <i>out </i>of Arizona. Phoenix is a waypoint, you see. Biggest city there, easiest place to stop. And there, the humans are as troublesome as they come. The police <i>know </i>things there, things they shouldn't. They're dirty too; rounding us up, and they share what they know all the way down to Mexico. No one went missing <i>here</i>, but I'd bet you anything that somebody is missing down <i>there</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: The Ramble collectively is resolving the Swooning Condition to accept Earth and to share what they know. Roll Wits + Empathy to get a feel for the crowd.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Earth</b><br /> <br /> Your journals suggest that this isn't like the Loci, Verges, or Hallows you've seen before. Things would be just plain <i>weirder </i>if they were, and the Riven would probably be on edge. They're sensitive to that sort of thing. But, that doesn't mean that it wasn't built by somebody who knew what they were doing. Azoth is strange- it's the Flame Immortal, the Furnace of Creation, the existence of the Created, the Unborn, and the Dominions suggests that it is itself alive, that it possesses a consciousness, a Principle. What does Pyros know? What does Pyros remember? How does it communicate at all? You've heard of Demiurges, humans that are conduits for the Divine Fire. Alchemists <i>steal </i>Pyros, but Demiurges have it just <i>flow </i>through them. But does a Demiurge have to make a Promethean?<br /> <br /> You notice that the Riven with the ribbons is looking at you know. They seem... intrigued. They've heard the stories, who hasn't. Wait- they said something about Arizona, didn't they? That's where you were made. Surely, they can't be expecting <i>you </i>to speak up now? It certainly doesn't help you can see the other Golems checking you out. Is it possible that you have 'siblings' here?<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Powerful symbolism, but it isn't a Locus, Verge, Hallow, or other such place of power. You could make a Presence + Expression roll here to try and tell a suitable story and contribute to the Ramble, or make some other kind of Social roll.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Scout</b><br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Pilgrim's Landmarks <b>could </b>help, but the Created the Athanor and potions were from aren't from around here. It wouldn't help all that much. Wisdom of Ages couldn't, but if you want to pass your Humours around Glimpsing the Crasis could. Roll Wits + Occult to gather useful information from the crowd.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 01-02-2017, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T16:37:51-08:00","id":1025622,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Informed (Stannum), Inspired, Disconnected<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: <i>6</i>/5 | Pyros: 10/12 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 1/5</b></div> <br /> Earth isn't really a deep, complex, theoretical thinker by nature. Contemplating the workings of Pyros for too long makes her head hurt. But maybe there was a spark of the Everything Fire behind the construction of this place. It would explain why it draws other Created here. She's naturally drawn to fire, even though it bites her just as hard as anyone- &quot;like a moth to the flame,&quot; her creator said. Maybe this little corner of cold, doomed Winnipeg is attracting their kind to its Flame as well, despite the danger of gathering all at once. How the place hasn't become a Wasteland is a mystery to her. Maybe you're supposed to conserve your Pyros here, as a sign of respect. Or it's a trick to keep the moths weak if the Fire decides to swallow them.<br /> <br /> She leans over to Mark 5 and whispers: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;You ever been around so many of us? Wild, right?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> It's weird and humbling. If there's an etiquette for this, she doesn't know it. She keeps imagining Pandorans crawling out of the ground to feast on them, or an awful Firestorm, but nothing happens. Well- as soon as Adonis speaks, it'll get ugly. Her Torment tells her she's not welcome here.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;...But I promise you, that's not who Earth is anymore.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> It isn't? She <i>does</i> feel different now that she's back on the road. More focused. And her body isn't roiling and bubbling with Flux anymore. Is she someone else now? The same entity that Earth Crisis was when she clawed out of the Arizona desert, or someone different?<br /> <br /> Some scrawny Nepri with a goatee and different eyes is obviously staring at her. Weird, he looks kinda like she does. She makes eye contact, squatting at the edge of the circle, and flips him the bird with her Flux-twisted claw. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;See something you like, nerd?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Oh- it looks like Adonis' speech went...really well. They're not even raising their pitchforks. She's visibly dumbstruck. When the Muse comes back, she mumbles something to him: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Hey, uh...I thought that wouldn't go so good. You really went out on a limb for me. I won't forget you did that.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The Riven with the ribbons and keys and wild hair is absolutely fascinating to her. Earth can't take her eyes off them, except when she occasionally gets self-conscious and stares at her feet. Many eyes are on her, and her tattoo itches: 'A MAN OF WORDS AND NOT OF DEEDS IS LIKE A GARDEN FULL OF WEEDS.' After yesterday, she can think of worse things to be than a garden full of weeds. She takes a breath and strides forward into the circle.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Uh...hey. I'm Earth.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> A flash of memory from her stolen body: people sitting on folding chairs at an AA meeting, repeating <i>&quot;hi, earth.&quot; </i>The memory makes her laugh a little. She has a surprisingly nice laugh, like a hiccup. It breaks the ice. As she speaks, her Inscription glows bright on her bare bicep and sparks with Pyros.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;That's all true. I come from Phoenix, and my creator always told me to stay out of the city. The cops know what to look for, and they try to kill us if they see us. The one who made me- she's called Heartsblood, eight foot tall, hard as granite, devil with a hammer- she'd lurch around in the desert looking for fights, and even she stayed out of Phoenix. See, she was looking for a worthy challenge, or some Titan crap like that...<br /> <br /> ...there's an Unfleshed called Waking Cloud who runs vision quests out in the desert for rich humans from the tech industry, Burning Man types. I think he's looking for someone with the expertise to help him program his progeny...<br /> <br /> ...weird stuff out in Tucson. I guess the old mission there is haunted, and there's a secret cabal of magicians doing rituals with the bells. Heartsblood always said to watch my back around there, they're as dangerous as alchemists...<br /> <br /> ...you need to watch out for this Pandoran, the Calavera. It looks like a fancy skull when it's dormant and shows up in traveling shows in the Southwest and Mexico- stupid humans- and it always wakes up on the Days of the Dead. I can tell you all about Pandorans...&quot;</span><br /> <br /> That kind of stuff. Traveler's tips for the Southwest, people she met down there, places to see or avoid. It feels good to be useful to the crowd, hoping that someone might derive some use out of her experiences. She doesn't talk much about being Centimani, only in passing. As the glow from her Inscription fades, she adds one more thing:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I got a question. Earth-Dies-Screaming used to travel with Dead Girl. She's a Galateid, traveled all over the place, used to follow Gold and Bronze and have a throng on the East Coast...a lot of the time, she had these big beautiful wings. Knew a secret Flux way to call down Firestorms. Liked to get inside peoples' heads. Twist them.<br /> <br /> Do any of you know that name?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Making a good impression, practicing her storytelling, and seeking information about Dead Girl. Especially want to impress the Ulgan with the ribbons and keys. Presence 3 + Expression 1, Willpower 3, spending 1 Pyros to add +3 Expression from Inscription. 10 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/471720\" target=\"_blank\">6 successes!</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T19:26:47-08:00","id":1025684,"title":"","content":"Regret<br /> Conditions: Introspective (Refinement)<br /> Alembics: Externalize, Plumb the Fathoms, Prime the Vessel<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO<br /> Willpower: 4/4<br /> Pyros: 5/10<br /> Beats: 0/5<br /> Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> <br /> <br /> Centimani...Centimani, Pandoran, Flux, Pyros, Azoth, Qashmal, Elpis, Vitriol, Alchemy, the Great Work, words, words, words that Regret has heard over and over again but had very little context for. Prime drilled them into his head when he was created. Frank explained them in a way he could better understand as they traveled to Winnipeg, but like any word describing what they represent is very different from knowing what they represent. And while Regret certainly didn't know what those words truly represented, some part of him DID...and that was both a comforting and terrifying feeling. <br /> <br /> Amongst the other patchwork people like himself, Prime &amp; Frank called them the Frankenstein Lineage, he listened to stories of comings and goings. Of lessons learned and lost. Of the Great Work. Of the world. Of Prometheans and Humetheans...no wait, that was wrong...of human-theans...of the ones who have homes. Yes. That was it. People made of those who could never go home, who had no home of their own trying to become people who have homes. People like himself, trying to become people like the ones who make up his body. &quot;Atta boy Regy, language is a filthy whore anyway&quot;, he remembered Frank saying as he helped him practice speaking. His hands, mouth, and tongue was the artist who died in battle, and while they often remembered how best to say any given thing Regret himself was still trying to master their intricacies. <br /> <br /> It was nice to be around people like himself and Prime, who didn't act like Prime. It was also nice to listen to their stories too. It was also nice to listen to people who were only sort of like himself and Prime, and for now it was nice to be around them too. He wondered what he would do after the gathering was over though. He came to Winnipeg to learn more about what being a Promethean meant, and while listening to the others did help him greatly he knew this many of his kind couldn't stay in one place for longer than an evening at best. He knew this partly because Frank had warned him about this, and partly because The Fire knew this. He needed to find another Frank, someone who he could learn from but wasn't like Prime. He needed someone who could see their own mistakes. Someone who knew sorrow. Someone who knew beyond themselves what it was like to loose something.<br /> <br /> Centimani...former-Centimani...someone who was once the Enemy, but is no longer the Enemy. That's a start.<br /> <br /> <br /> *OOC: Regret, a muscular Frankenstein in a dirty camo-jacket with a large gym bag hanging on a lopsided shoulder, is staring at Earth not to dissimilar to how Scout is, albeit he makes no gestures and his stare might be misconstrued as angry. In truth, it's a mixture of determination and hope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T03:38:02-08:00","id":1025819,"title":"","content":"Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 8/11 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5<br /> <br /> &quot;You ever been around so many of us? Wild, right?&quot;<br /> &quot;No, never. It's humbling.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Mark 5 carefully observed the crowd during The early part of Adonis speech, and made out two guys focusing on Earth, which Flipped on of them, an Osirian, off. Where they a threat? Did they hold a grudge? The Titan Marked them as dangerous and Glared at them, first at the Wretched, then the creep. He wanted them to know that Earth was under his protection.<br /> <br /> Then, he was taken by surprise: the pretty boy's speech was good. Really, really good. Great, even.<br /> Up until now, he had considered him, well, nothing really. Useful at getting to Amalgam, maybe. But the Mimic just proved that he had hidden depths, and even more importantly, that he was good at something the Titan wasn't. He smiled. The Principle seemed really intent on lending Earth a Hand in keeping on good path.<br /> Then Earth went up, and did a great job herself at talking To the masses.<br /> <br /> All in all, things went better than he had expected.<br /> He hoped he would not mess up when it was his turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T08:05:40-08:00","id":1026527,"title":"","content":"<b>Evening-</b> Friday November 4<sup>th</sup><br /> <br /> <b>Earth</b><br /> <br /> The Named surprises everyone by being astonishingly eloquent. She speaks, and the words pour out of her. It's a kind of fluid poetry, sharing her experiences, sharing the lore that she's accumulated. Earth doesn't even need Dead Girl's journals for this, it's all <i>her</i>. She can hear the Ramble whispering and muttering and interjecting in her stories. A few people pipe up about the Unfleshed, how there's more of them in Korea and Japan than anywhere else, or talk about a friend of a friend who went to Phoenix and didn't come out. They talk about a city out in California where mages have gotten <i>ideas </i>about the Divine Fire, and where Pandorans haunt a subway station that is absolutely coated in Pilgrim Marks and written Rambles of all description. A couple curse loudly when it comes to the Calavera, especially fellow Golems. It's a cautionary tale passed around the Lineage about what goes wrong when you put a body down in the ground and expect a person to come climbing back out. There's better ways to do it, if you just have the <i>words</i>.<br /> <br /> A blue skinned Nepri in worn canvas robes and a thick trench coat shakes their head. Their chest is bound tight, like a mummy, and you aren't sure you want to know why. They shake their head and stroke a long, curly square beard and laugh. &quot;What is it about Golems and words?&quot; You can feel the Galataeids behind you staring into your back and you don't know what <i>they </i>are thinking. They thinking the Freak dragged a fellow Muse down with her? Thinking that a fellow Pilgrim is dead because of her? Someone speaks up.<br /> <br /> &quot;Haven't heard anything about anyone calling themselves Dead Girl, but it's hard to keep track of the stories, sometimes. You said she likes wings, messing with people's heads and making Firestorms? Would be easy enough to get her confused with the nasty sort of Messenger...or get a Messenger confused with her, but we'll keep an ear to the ground sister. You keep walking your trail until you figure out where it ends.&quot; There are murmurs of agreement throughout the Ramble.<br /> <br /> Somebody else steps forwards, a Wretched with loose stitches and peeling skin, to start talking. &quot;Well you know what they say about the Messengers, lightning never strikes the same place twice. 'Course that's straight up bullshit, or else we wouldn't all be here!&quot; There's a lopsided smile with a drooping cheek and a ripple of laughter. &quot;I've heard of a place where the angels are thick on the ground, where even <i>humans </i>go to get a look at 'em. Met this Pilgrim on my way through Oregon and <i>they </i>said-&quot; And the story goes on.<br /> <br /> Earth isn't paying too much attention, because the Riven with mist in their wake, ribbons on their arms, and keys on their wrists is heading towards her. They don't seem wholly...real. Like they're stepping on different ground as they head towards her and seat themselves on the ground. They extend a hand, worn and cracked with work, ink and blood and dirt caught under fingernails, and offer a small, crooked smile. &quot;They call me Satin. How long you been in town, Earth-Who-Lives-Again?&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Earth gains the Connected (Winnipeg Ramble) Persistent Condition. This gives her a +2 to all rolls with the local Created, and can be resolved for an instant Exceptional Success regarding them. The Condition awards a Beat when you go out of your way to do a favour for the group you're Connected to.<br /> <br /> <b>Adonis</b> also gains a Beat for his Exceptional Successes in getting the Ramble to accept Earth and help out.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T08:30:08-08:00","id":1026540,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div><br /> Scout ignored getting flipped off. Not by a long shot the worst that had happened to him. The glare from the titan got a little smile back from him. That was how you disarmed angry people wasn't it? He was mostly certain about that. Yes, smiling was good. Should he introduce himself? He could never remember these things.<br /> <br /> Scout stopped musing at his facial hair and listened to the prometheans around him, collecting the Ramble's information as best as he could. He kept himself carefully away from the personal space of others, and this time remembered to smile and nod to people as he listened to their stories. Listen now, speak later. Perhaps he could even learn something useful to them. Yes. Perhaps then they'd let him study them.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Gathering information- Wits+Occult: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/471683\" target=\"_blank\">3 success.</a>.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T11:09:43-08:00","id":1026617,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 7/11 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> Getting a smile in response made Mark 5 suspicious. This guy didn't take him seriously?! Sounded dangerous.<br /> His first instinct was to step into the Riven's way as Satin approached, but he had noticed how Earth had watched Satin: fascination., and something else. Hope? Since the Riven seemed friendly, he decided to instead go talk to the Ramble.<br /> The Titan went up. Driven by his purpose, he didn't care about how he speaks knowing he was bad with words, instead he fired up his Pyros so they saw the outline of his built and resilient body, and spoke clearly and loudly. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;I am Mark 5, by way of Mudbreaker. I'm with Earth and the prett... with Adonis. We're out to <i>break</i> some Amalgam. Any sort of help is welcome. You want to tag along? Welcome. Know anything about them, no matter what? Welcome. Got anything we can use? Welcome.&quot; </span><br /> He went on to talk about a few other things: about his journey, the Vampire attack he witnessed, about Mudbreaker, who suddenly left him alone. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;If you know her, or know where she might be, I'd be thankful if you told me.&quot;</span><br /> He supported what Adonis said about Earth as a first-hand witness to him taking care of the Pandorans. He left out that he was hurt in the process, non-Titans wouldn't understand that Earth just acted on what he told her to do, anyway, in his opinion. Finally, he told them how they could get into contact with him as long as he was in the city. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;If there is something I can do for you while we are here, let me know. I try to help where I can.&quot;</span> A hero had to be there for the people, after all. Even if they weren't actually people.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=49e78f2a\" target=\"_blank\">2 Pres + 1 Pyros + Willpower 3 - Unskilled 1</a>= 2 sux </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T12:00:30-08:00","id":1026639,"title":"","content":"<b>Evening-</b> Friday November 4<sup>th</sup><br /> <br /> <b>Scout</b><br /> <br /> The Nepri wandered through the crowd, picking up the latest rumours of the strange and the macabre. Some of the local Pilgrims told stories about the tunnels under the Exchange district- not the walkways, those everyone knows about, no, the old tunnels, the ways people moved stock, mail, and bodies from building to building in the days before air conditioning and the internet when they had absolutely no desire to brave the horrendous weather outside. They're mostly abandoned, these days. Kept under lock and key, abandoned, forgotten, but what's any of that to the Night People? They say vampires rest in those tunnels the way they use catacombs, like they use the Prohibition smuggling tunnels in Moosejaw. They also say there are Pilgrim Marks and Athanors... if you want to brave the licks and the Unborn.<br /> <br /> They're talking about the old cathedral, the one across the river. It burned down <i>twice </i>in less than a century, and Winnipeg has always had a thing for alchemy. There are rumours that it did (might still) have Athanors inscribed into the walls, alchemical secrets in the masonry. There are rumours that at least one of the fires was a Firestorm. Whatever <i>really </i>happened, the city isn't likely to <a href=\"http://bonifacecathedral.weebly.com/uploads/2/1/9/5/21959016/1662309.jpg?251\" target=\"_blank\">forget it</a> any time soon.<br /> <br /> \u200bEveryone knows that the Red River and the Assiniboine are the lifeblood of the city. Their meeting at the Forks is the reason the city was a centre of trade amongst the First Nations people for hundreds of years. What most people <i>don't </i>know is that the Rivers have serious <b>weight</b>. Some say that Underworld Rivers follow the real ones, and that if you swim deep enough in the Red River you'll start swimming towards the surface of the Underworld. They also say it isn't the only Invisible Realm to have a River in the same place.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Scout gets Story Hooks equal to successes. These are things to pursue if you want to, or not. It's urban legends and tall tales, with various degrees of truth.</i> <br /> <br /> <b>Mark 5</b><br /> <br /> He speaks well enough, for a Titan. The stories about <i>qashmallim </i>and Firestorms were getting old, anyways. No telling what either of those things was liable to do, so why waste time trying to figure it out? Besides, Firestorms were more like natural consequences of alchemical buildup, and the Created were careful not to create Wastelands in Winnipeg. The weather was volatile enough without adding the Divine Fire to the mix. Someone over in the group of Golems called out &quot;Mudbreaker? She's long gone son- went north, chasing the Aurora. Everyone goes chasing the Aurora once or twice in their Pilgrimage, but she's wild for it. Getting too dangerous up north these days, though. Lots of skin-changers gathering with some kind of mad moon spirit.&quot; There were nods and murmurs of agreement. A couple of the Created here had met a death under the teeth and talons of werewolves.<br /> <br /> The blue-skinned Osirian in the trenchcoat points at Mark 5 and shakes his head &quot;Don't you go messing with alchemists kid, they'll suck your humours dry to get what they want. Pyros works miracles for them same as us. They don't know we're here, and if they do, they're leaving us alone, which is just fine with me. Lead with your head, not with your fists. Start asking yourself <i>why </i>they're doing what they're doing, instead of focusing on <i>what </i>they're doing.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T15:42:33-08:00","id":1026722,"title":"","content":"Regret<br /> Conditions: Introspective (Refinement)<br /> Alembics: Externalize (0), Plumb the Fathoms (0), Prime the Vessel (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO<br /> Willpower: 4/4<br /> Pyros: 5/10<br /> Beats: 0/5<br /> Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> <br /> <br /> This feeling...muscles tightening, fists clenching, teeth clenching, vision focusing, this feeling is something Regret knows all too well. This is the Storm inside that sends the dead soldier to battle against anything they can. Anything to stop the Torment. A mission that ends in pain, sweat, anger, and...<br /> <br /> Regret tries to steady himself, he didn't think the one who glared back next to Earth would affect him this way. The only other one who did was Prime, and that was because they wouldn't listen to him. They couldn't understand what it was like to acknowledge their mistakes. They could only blame others for their own Torment. Regret didn't want to become like that, that's why he listened to Frank and joined his Refinement. He wanted to understand. So that is what he must do now. He must understand. The problem was the...other one besides Earth, Mark 5 is what he calls himself, were they like Prime? Did he not care to understand?<br /> <br /> A brief hesitation, before a brief memory as gentle as the flicker of a candle crossed his mind. &quot;One step at a time brother. One step at a time.&quot; He missed Frank, who Bleeds Shadows, but this was something he had to do by himself. The Fire knew it. Frank knew it. He knew it. Then, taking one step forward before taking another, he approached Mark 5. <br /> <br /> Regret: &quot;Hi&quot;<br /> <br /> Good start, try to make him understand why you've come up to him. Why you were staring at Earth.<br /> <br /> Regret: &quot;I'm Regret, and I want to understand what it means to be one of the Created.&quot;<br /> <br /> There, was that so hard? There is no need to do something that you'll regret later. Now, to draw your line. You cannot take a step back down the Long March, the soldiers are counting on you to bring them and yourself Home. <br /> <br /> Regret: &quot;But I will not go to war.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> *OOC: The Frankenstein has openly approached Mark 5 without fully noticing that others have also started talking to him. He seems more agitated than before, but again this is purely miscommunication. One very strange thing about this Wretch, this Regret, is that they have an surprisingly soft voice compared to the very muscular body it belongs too. There is almost a hint of sophistication there, but it's buried under his curtness and awkward way he structures his words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 01-04-2017, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T01:48:29-08:00","id":1026925,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 7/11 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> When Mark 5 finished his &quot;speech&quot;, for lack of a better word, The Wretched from before approached the Titan, looking very angry. Was he going to attack him infront of the whole Ramble? Mark 5 prepared himself mentally for a confrontation, when Regret opened his mouth: &quot;Hi&quot;<br /> <i>&quot;...what?&quot;</i> the Titan thought.<br /> &quot;I'm Regret, and I want to understand what it means to be one of the Created.&quot;<br /> <i>&quot;What's there to understand? Humiliation and Trauma Conga is what we are. You ought to try to understand humans.&quot;</i><br /> &quot;But I will not go to war.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">&quot;Erm...okay? Then don't?&quot; </span>What a weird guy. He must be fairly young for a Promethean. Mark 5 remembered his early days, and suddenly felt sympathy for the Wretched who called himself Regret.<br /> Then someone said something about Mudbreaker and his mind went to a different place. She <b>had </b>been here!Crazy for something dangerous, that indeed sounded like her. She was still around! The feeling inside his chest surprised him. He was happy? But he was still angry with her! The thrill of anticipation, the knowledge he can repay her for what she did to him - with a beating, that is - that must be what he felt. Surely!<br /> Wolves that attacked the Created, huh? Sounds like there is plenty of work for the Righteous here to do. Maybe he could talk the others in taking a detour...<br /> <br /> &quot;Don't you go messing with alchemists kid, they'll suck your humours dry to get what they want. Pyros works miracles for them same as us. They don't know we're here, and if they do, they're leaving us alone, which is just fine with me. Lead with your head, not with your fists. Start asking yourself <i>why </i>they're doing what they're doing, instead of focusing on <i>what </i>they're doing.&quot;<br /> What does it matter why they do it, if what they do is so wrong? How can it be okay to let others suffer, as long as you are not bothered? He shook his head. This must be why he was a hero, and the blue Osirian wasn't.<br /> All he said was something that had been brewing inside his heart ever since he saw the bottle:<span style=\"color:#0000FF\"> &quot;It may be fine with you, but not with me. Someone, somewhere, ends one Pilgrim after the other. Titan, Mimic, Fury, no matter who, and puts all their hopes and dreams, all they were and could become, in little bottles. This must not be.&quot;</span> He got progressively sadder, as he said this, which left Mark 5 confused. This was not an emotion he was very familiar with. He left the stage for someone else to Ramble and returned to his group.<br /> <i>...<br /> ...<br /> ...<br /> His </i>group. Strange that he would think of them like that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T02:21:51-08:00","id":1026936,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Informed (Stannum), Inspired, Disconnected, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble)<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 9/12 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 1/5</b></div><br /> Weird new experience: bonding with other Tammuz about the Calavera and what a wretched bastard it is. Others know this stuff too? It feels like sharing a tribal tradition with people she's never met. She never thought about the thing having any spiritual significance, just something not to get killed by. But it makes sense when they talk about it. Maybe Heartsblood taught her more than she realized.<br /> <br /> Infuriating to go to all this trouble and not hear any news about Her. She's never thought about it before, but...she does sound like one of the dark angels. That parches her throat. Is that what she wanted? Some kind of ascension into the Pyros? She snaps back: &quot;No! Not a Messenger. She's just like us, and always will be. Flux never took anybody up to heaven or hell.&quot;<br /> <br /> Earth-Dies-Screaming dug deep into Flux and only ended up with a bigger hole to crawl out of, and now she's got nothing left of her awful knowledge. The only way she can make sense of her experience is if it was all pointless to begin with. She never had a chance at the transformative revelation that the Sages of Dissolution chattered about, the anti-alchemy of achieving true emptiness, as far from humanity as Lucifer was from God. The image of Dead Girl becoming a Messenger without Earth to hold her back makes her...<br /> Jealous.<br /> <br /> Oh, the Riven is here. Earth shakes it off and sits down, grabs their hand. It feels like meeting a ghost.<br /> <br /> &quot;Satin? Like the guy who lives in hell?&quot;<br /> <br /> She throws up the horns, awestruck. &quot;That's badass! My creator gave me a weird name at first: 'Earth Crisis.' I think she saw it on a poster. I been trying to make it mine.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I been here like 2 weeks. Came down from this dead factory town called Powerview-Pine Falls where I got back onto Tin. I really wrecked their shit!&quot;<br /> <br /> Mark 5 is talking to the group, she points him out to Satin. &quot;We've been running together since I got here. He heard the stories about me, we fought, we figured it out. Now we've been breaking bad guys. Adonis started tagging along the other day. They ain't so bad. Wouldn't have come here without 'em. I guess my reputation precedes me, and I kinda...flipped my shit a little when I first looked around for Pilgrim signs. Thought everybody had their eyes on me. Even Mark. Stupid. He's on my side, and I'm on his. They wouldn't have gotten me out of Torment if they weren't.&quot;<br /> <br /> Earth suddenly realizes that she hasn't been stuttering since she addressed the Ramble. That stops once she's conscious of it.<br /> <br /> &quot;sorry. i, uh- never talk this much.&quot;<br /> <br /> She scratches her hair. Bugs in it. &quot;so- can you see ghosts? are there any hanging around me? i always wondered.&quot;<br /> <br /> Earth is very obviously into Satin's whole look, but that's being ignored for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T03:11:34-08:00","id":1026945,"title":"","content":"Regret<br /> Conditions: Introspective (Refinement)<br /> Alembics: Externalize (0), Plumb the Fathoms (0), Prime the Vessel (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO<br /> Willpower: 4/4<br /> Pyros: 5/10<br /> Beats: 0/5<br /> Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> <br /> <br /> Mark 5: &quot;Erm...okey? Then don't?&quot;<br /> <br /> Regret lets out a sigh of relief. This is a good start. Maybe he is like Frank. Maybe he misunderstood what he meant when he wanted help &quot;dealing with Amalgam.&quot; This wouldn't have been the first time Regret himself has misunderstood someone's words and their intentions. This is why he follows...Plumbum, why he follows Plumbum. So he can understand Prometheans better, the world better, himself better. <br /> <br /> Others speak up, others like and not like Mark 5. Regret understands their words but not their meaning, but Mark 5 does. He even responds to the blue skinned Promethean that's not like Regret, Frank, and Mark 5.<br /> <br /> Mark 5: &quot;It may be fine with you, but not with me. Someone, somewhere, ends one Pilgrimage after the other. Titan, Mimic, Fury, no matter who, and puts all their hopes and dreams, all they were and could become, in little bottles...&quot;<br /> <br /> Fear, panic, can this happen to himself? Could this happen to Frank or Prime? Why would anyone with a Home want to do that to another being? Regret was at a loss for words, feelings that were his own welled up inside right next to the Fire, as the Dead Soldiers quaked each in panicked memory of their agonizing demise. But that was not all Mark 5 said...<br /> <br /> Mark 5: &quot;...This must not be.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Dead Soldiers stopped. Ears recognized words, muscles remembered pitch, eyes remembered images. Images of an aging man standing in front of a line of people. All humans. All dressed in army cloths. All humans in the line before the old man, including the dead soldier, spoke in perfect unison. &quot;Sir, yes sir!&quot; They had heard this speech before. It made them angry. It made them hate.<br /> <br /> Still battling with his own emotions at the revelations of the danger Amalgam presented, but reeling from the building anger that fills the cold dead flesh of the Soldiers and Regret, he levels his head with what Frank called a &quot;deep breath&quot; and then words flowed out of Regret, either articulated by the Artist who died in war or the Fire within. But words Regret knew to be true.<br /> <br /> Regret: &quot;Is Amalgam the Enemy? Frank once told me Ignorance is the Enemy. He said all the world's suffering could be traced back to the fact people just don't understand each other sometimes. Or, just don't want to bother understanding each other. That's why we follow the Refinements. They allow us to understand the world right? So we can find a Home. It makes sense when you think of it like that doesn't it? But the Enemy can only be the Enemy when it actively wants to destroy you, doesn't it? That's why Prime said the Enemy was Flux. The part of the Fire that breaks things down, that twists and dissolves, that dehumanizes. The part the Centimani study, the part that fuels the things that bite and claw and sleep unseen until the Fire wakes them. That sounds more like the Enemy, since it can destroy you. But like Ignorance, Flux doesn't specifically target any one thing. Prime even said it'll rip itself apart in time, that's why it hasn't destroyed everything already right? How can a force of nature be the Enemy? And if those who use Flux are the Enemy then how can a Centimani be redeemable? The Enemy is the Enemy isn't it? The Enemy cannot be the Enemy until it isn't can it? Is Amalgam the Enemy?&quot;<br /> <br /> Regret didn't realize it, but he had given his first Ramble. The part of him that knew the words gave form to his doubts and fears, his pain and concerns. His hopes that war could be avoided before it's begun...<br /> <br /> <br /> *OOC: Regret's Ramble finally shows the eloquence he's capable of, but also shows his nativity to the gathering. Despite his physique and size the way he speaks is reminiscent of a child trying to make sense of a cruel world, but beyond that desperate search for understanding lies an undertone of pain, sorrow, and a desire to question and challenge more established viewpoints. Especially those that espouse violence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 01-05-2017, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T07:48:52-08:00","id":1027022,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> Scout took his time listening to each person ramble, and the various things he'd learned. So many athanors... he'd need to get close and attempt to locate them at some point.<br /> <br /> When Regret had stood and done his ramble, Scout was nodding. What he said made both lots of sense and no sense. Flux was the enemy, but it was also a piece of all of them- a part of the Divine Fire. Ignorance was an enemy, true.<br /> <br /> He found himself walking to the center stage, all three foot ten inches of him, and cleared his throat to make sure he was known before he spoke up. If it was one thing he hated, it was being talked over just because he was small. He waited to make sure he had the Ramble's attention before he spoke, his nearly-monotone voice loud, if a little squeaky. He hated talking to groups because of that.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I am Scout, Knowledge Seeker and Originist. I am from New Mexico, and have traveled broadly once with my Genitor, until he was destroyed. I mapped the Athanors we found where we traveled- from New Mexico, to Old Mexico, and down into the Yuctan peninsula. I give this knowledge freely to you, my brothers and sisters, so that it may be shared with others.</span>&quot; he paused to let that sink in, then looked to Regret, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I came here in search of the Earth-dies-screaming, to watch her and find out more about her, as a known Centimani. But found Earth-Who-Lives-Again in her stead, walking the path once more. This is a proof- even Centimani are not always our enemy, for they can be Redeemed. Protect yourself, but know- the centimani, those fallen to Flux, they are our brothers and sisters, as much as you are mine. They may walk the path again one day, as Earth Who Lives Again does. They need only guidance to find the way. Guidance, like Earth has had</span>,&quot; he waved his hand towards Mark 5 and Adonis, and let that sink in for a moment as well.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Amalgama, they are not our brothers and sisters. But they are humans- those who we would have for brothers and sisters after our New Dawn. I myself am afraid of Alchemists. To have my vitriol taken and be dissected like a government project. But we must not let fear rule us- we should not hurt these people. Only their company, and the true Alchemists within,</span>&quot; He looked to Mark 5 again, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">And with that, you have my full support.</span>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8122,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","user":"ArchonAres","date":". 01-11-2017, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T08:15:08-08:00","id":1027038,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 7/11 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> &quot;Frank once told me Ignorance is the Enemy. He said all the world's suffering could be traced back to the fact people just don't understand each other sometimes. Or, just don't want to bother understanding each other.&quot;<br /> Why was everyone so hung up on <i>intention</i>? The blue Osirian, this Regret, and that Scout... was there something he was missing here? He WAS trying to understand everyone. But no matter why you do something, if it is Evil, so are you, if it is good, so are you...right?<br /> Mark 5 was brooding. There was something to take away here... But what was it?<br /> <br /> &quot;This is a proof- even Centimani are not always our enemy, for they can be Redeemed. Protect yourself, but know- the centimani, those fallen to Flux, they are our brothers and sisters, as much as you are mine. They may walk the path again one day, as Earth Who Lives Again does. They need only guidance to find the way. Guidance, like Earth has had&quot;<br /> Why did Scout wave at him, Mark 5 wondered. He didn't guide Earth - the Principle did. He was just lending a hand. Then, something hit him: If Earth could be redeemed, all Centimani potentially could... which was his hope, in a way. So far, so good. But how could he judge them, then? How could he end them, if they carried the potential to change? Was he truly Good if he destroyed Evil which could be made Good? Which could become good by itself?<br /> ... was this something about Intention?<br /> Mark 5's head hurt. This was <i>so </i>confusing.<br /> <br /> &quot;Amalgama, they are not our brothers and sisters. But they are humans- those who we would have for brothers and sisters after our New Dawn. I myself am afraid of Alchemists. To have my vitriol taken and be dissected like a government project. But we must not let fear rule us- we should not hurt these people. Only their company, and the true Alchemists within. And with that, you have my full support.&quot;<br /> Mark 5 felt like he missed something important here, again. Was it intention, again? Why not fight back against injustice?<br /> Thankfully, the Scout was less averse to his mindset than Regret: he said there is an acceptable target. Why is one part acceptable, the other isn't, though?<br /> His head starting hurting again.<br /> In either case, he was relieved: not only did someone offer his help, this someone apparently understood something about this confusing topic of Intention. Maybe he could learn something himself. He nodded at Scout as a sign of thanks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T18:11:56-08:00","id":1027369,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 9/10<br /> Beats: 4/5 I Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> Scout's words about Amalgama make Adonis feel much better. He remembers how Mark 5 initially refused to show Erwin any mercy until he portrayed him as a potential tool. He smiles and nods. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">\u200b&quot;That's what I was trying to tell Mark 5 last night!&quot; </span>He turns back to Mark 5. The Titan has shown a major black/white worldview. But that's not really his fault. Mark 5 is a Titan, Adonis is a Mimic. Human nature is supposed to be his strong suit. Maybe he should try to help Mark 5 understand. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;How do I explain this? ... Sometimes, people do bad things without meaning to. Nobody ever sees themselves as being evil, even if they are. But a lot of times, people don't even know that what they are doing is helping others to do good. If they knew what they were really doing, they would probably stop. So you need to see if people realize what they are doing. And if they don't, you need to show them what's really going on. But you need to be... subtle about it. You can't just shove their nose in it.&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T00:20:40-08:00","id":1027479,"title":"","content":"Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 7/11 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5<br /> <br /> <br /> *&quot;How do I explain this? ... Sometimes, people do bad things without meaning to. Nobody ever sees themselves as being evil, even if they are. But a lot of times, people don't even know that what they are doing is helping others to do good. If they knew what they were really doing, they would probably stop. So you need to see if people realize what they are doing. And if they don't, you need to show them what's really going on. But you need to be... subtle about it. You can't just shove their nose in it.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Titan was surprised. Adonis knew about this? He carefully listened, but it was so complicated. &quot;But how can you not see you are evil? Why can you not Show them openly?&quot; You do evil, but feel good, and you do not want to be evil and if you knew you are evil you would stop, but you must be subtily told? So confusing.<br /> And.... scary.<br /> &quot;I... did I do something wrong?...evil?&quot; Mark 5 asked Adonis tentatively. He looked ... vulnerable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T21:25:15-08:00","id":1028424,"title":"","content":"<b>Evening-</b> Friday November 4<sup>th</sup><br /> <br /> <b>Earth</b><br /> <br /> Satin laughs, and it isn't what you expected. It's husky and hoarse, they croak like a crow, but it sounds <i>right</i>, it sounds <i>lived in</i>. They shake their head and lift up and arm, showing off the multi-coloured ribbons. &quot;I have been called that once or twice, but Satin,&quot; you hear the careful stressing of syllables here, <b>sat-in</b> not <b>sat-an</b> &quot;is a kind of fabric, sort of like silk. I used to think it was all frilly and delicate and didn't suit me at all, I love it now. Know why?&quot; They grin, and lines spring up in their face, adding a little bit of depth to the ethereal figure &quot;Because satin is made from silk, and silk is strong as all hell. It's beautiful to look at, sure, but it's strong as anything. Strong as steel. Spiders make it, and butterflies make it too. Can you guess which one I am?&quot; There's a dare to the smile, a vivacity and a scream to the world that invites it to judge, to condemn. You get the sense that Satin has carved a place for themselves, wedged between two or more worlds, a spider in the centre of a web, a butterfly afloat on the wind, and they'll be damned if anyone moves them from that spot unless they choose to go.<br /> <br /> They twine a hand around their braid, playing with it as Earth falls self-consciously silent. &quot;You know, you're nothing like the stories said you would be. Everyone who's heard them gets the impression that you're a jagged cliff to crash into, an unthinking force of nature that smashes anything that gets too close, but that's not you, is it? You're a lot more than that.&quot; They pause for a moment, eyes looking around you, through you, instead of at you &quot;And no ghosts either, so if you're feeling haunted that's just your own mind talking.&quot; Satin takes a deep breath and looks off to one side, thinking very carefully about if they should risk what they say next &quot;Stories got another thing right, didn't they? Dead Girl. She was a hell of a lot more to you than someone to be lonely together with, huh? You're looking for her. Sure you want to find her?&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Earth does indeed resolve the Aspiration about meeting someone who knows her through Repute, and can choose another.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Adonis, Scout, Regret, Mark 5</b><br /> <br /> The blue Nepri looks over at Mark 5 with furrowed brow and pursed lips, and he slowly marches himself over there, eyes downcast and hands in pockets. He sits himself on the hillside and pats the ground beside him, inviting the Titan to sit. He sighs heavily, and shakes his head &quot;Look, kid, you're obviously new at this, but let's get one thing straight. If you've been in Torment, I mean <i>really </i>been in Torment, you've done some things that most humans would probably call evil. Hell, you might have unintentionally done some things they call evil even without Torment, I don't know you, but I know a bit about Mudbreaker and she wasn't exactly the motherly type. Here's the thing- nobody can tell you what 'good' or 'evil' is, you have to figure that crap out for yourself, but I'll tell you one thing I know for sure. When you start talking about evil and sin, it really all starts with treating people like <i>things</i>.&quot; He looks... uncomfortable being so touchy-feely and tries to distract himself immediately by focusing on Scout.<br /> <br /> &quot;Who was your Genitor, Eagle Scout? There's probably some people who'll want to know they're dead.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T02:33:34-08:00","id":1028469,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Informed (Stannum), Inspired, Disconnected, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble)<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 9/12 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 1/5</b></div> <br /> Hearing a speech from a stranger about herself is weird, like the first time she saw her own photo. Earth elbows the Ulgan during Scout's Ramble. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Hey, I'm famous!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She's transfixed by Satin and their silk that changes from frilly to steel-strong. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I keep seeing butterflies this year. I had this dream after the Canyon- I get these weird vivid dreams- where I was broken and twisted at the bottom, with butterfly angels all around me...uh, anyway, I like spiders better. Everyone says spiders are scary and ugly and poison, so they stay away, and the spider gets to build a web all by its damn self.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> That dare in their smile is inviting. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;You're not like other chicks, you know that? I'm into it. I say Satin's a spider. She'd look good with eight legs.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> After she gets all quiet and Satin speaks up more, playing with their braid: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">&quot;i dunno. don't really like the stories, but it's okay if they keep folks away. if i hadn't met mark 5 and adonis, i probly would've bug-zapped that little guy who said he was looking for me. still might. don't want everybody thinking i'm safe to poke, y'know? the threat's real, i'm not acting. i about killed mark 5 the other day when we wrecked a bad pack of unborn, real storm god shit. didn't even mean to.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> It's probably good that Satin was so careful about it, because Earth gets antsy when Dead Girl comes up. She doesn't know what to say. So she brings a spark to her fingers and burns a shape in the dirt, a stylized design that looks like a pair of wings being bound by chains.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;That used to be on my arm, right here above my inscription. It's wings breaking out of their chains. She made the Pyros brand but she swore she didn't pick it, it's what the Elpis decided our bond looked like. That meant we were together.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Have you ever been so close to somebody that you saw through all their lies and bullshit, how ugly they really were inside- but you loved that about them? No one knows me like she did. Not even the one who made me- <i>especially </i>not her. Heartsblood only saw how I failed to be what she wanted. Dead Girl saw <i>me</i>. Not a Role, not a human, not a failure. And I saw her. Not the sweet beautiful doll her throng thought they knew: the vicious vision waiting to be carved out of the marble, the harpy, the thing she <i>wanted </i>to be. So when she decided to brand us, she wouldn't take no for an answer.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She laughs, even though it's not very funny. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I mean- she actually did not take 'no.' I wouldn't do it, I said to stop bringing it up. But when she wanted something, she obsessed over it. Typical Muse, right? After a few weeks I got torn up really bad by some loner Fury. Like, my guts were out. She reached into me. Her hand was <i>on </i>my heart. I thought she was gonna- I mean- <span style=\"font-size:11px\">the lacuna. ha.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;She looks me in the eye and says: <i>'Just say yes.'</i>&quot;</span><br /> <br /> That lingers. She won't forget the way her eyes were like mirrors. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I couldn't actually <i>say </i>it, 'cause I was hurt too bad, but I gave her my hand. I sent my Pyros to meet hers. That's what we needed. The wings burned themselves on. We were a branded throng, just us two.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Late this summer we uh- there was a real bad Firestorm. We got separated. I don't remember exactly what happened. But I didn't have the Pyros brand anymore. She always said that only happens if the throng chooses to dissolve it. I don't think I chose to, and there were only two of us, so...I dunno. I looked for her, but without the brand I couldn't find her Azoth. The fire shook me out of Flux, anyway. Haven't seen her since then.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't know if Iwant to find her. Maybe it would be better if she was off on the moon somewhere and never came back. But when I don't even know what happened, or if she's alive, or if she's pissed off at me for leaving Flux...<span style=\"font-size:9px\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">it's just</span>...really scary.&quot;</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T06:16:47-08:00","id":1028520,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Steadfast<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 7/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> &quot;Look, kid, you're obviously new at this, but let's get one thing straight. If you've been in Torment, I mean <i>really </i>been in Torment, you've done some things that most humans would probably call evil. Hell, you might have unintentionally done some things they call evil even without Torment, I don't know you, but I know a bit about Mudbreaker and she wasn't exactly the motherly type. Here's the thing- nobody can tell you what 'good' or 'evil' is, you have to figure that crap out for yourself, but I'll tell you one thing I know for sure. When you start talking about evil and sin, it really all starts with treating people like <i>things</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mark 5 just... stared ahead, numb. This was like being told you will die, or worse, won't ever manage to end the Pilgrimage. He just wanted to be liked! He wanted people to be nice to him! And now it looked like he had lived a lie. He might have done, most likely he HAS done, very bad things. Evil things. He called himself a hero, but in the end, was he just another thug, harming people because he could? Was he just a <i>monster</i>? He <b>wanted</b> to help! He <b>wanted </b>to improve their lives! And he never treated people as things. did he? He has always seen them as someone who made their own choices, and sometimes those choices were to hurt other people. That was evil, wasn't it? That needed to be stopped, no? His large hands covered his face as he crouched. Why did this have to be so complicated! Why did it not make sense? After all he just <b>wanted </b>to do good!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">&quot;I meant well!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> </div> <br /> That sentence lit up in his mind. <i>I meant well. </i> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Sometimes, people do bad things without meaning to. If they knew what they were really doing, they would probably stop. So you need to see if people realize what they are doing. And if they don't, you need to show them what's really going on. But you need to be... subtle about it. You can't just shove their nose in it.&quot; </span></div> <br /> Adonis voice echoed in his head. He realized. He had been shown. The old man had hit the girl... but maybe he had just done the same as Mark 5 himself? Punished her because she did something she shouldn't do. Was he right to punish him? Had he been right to punish her? Scenes went through his head, and the Titan realized that many of his actions, seen by someone else, someone not understanding why he did what he did, could be considered Evil. And he was not so sure about some of them anymore. BUT! His intentions were pure! He was no monster, nor was he Evil, just another person trying to be good! Strangely, this was a relief. The sudden weight of fear for his identity, his... soul? was gone. Even though he wasn't a Hero, he did not lose hope.<br /> <i>Because he could still become one.</i><br /> Like Earth, who did bad things, but means well, he could become Better than he was.<br /> He would need to learn more about intention. He would need to be more careful with his judgement. He would need to find out what is Good, and what is Evil. He might even need to atone.<br /> And then, he would be Better.<br /> And, maybe, a Hero.<br /> A tear dropped from his eyes, and his sight became... clearer.<br /> The Titan smirked to himself as he stood up, then looked at Adonis and the Nepri, and let out a long sigh. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Ahh~... I think I see. Maybe. A bit.&quot;</span><br /> Then, Mark 5 gathered Adonis in a hug. It was over as quickly as it started. It was weird to do this. But it seemed.... appropriate. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Thank you.&quot;</span><br /> He nodded at the Nepri <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Both of you, too.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> Rambles... what a wonderful thing they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":"01-08-2017, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T07:42:21-08:00","id":1028544,"title":"","content":"\u200b <div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> Scout took out a notebook, and flipped a few pages, before he came to the right one. He carefully extracted a picture from where it was paper-clipped in, and held it up. &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">He called himself Highwinds.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Scout was in the picture with another native american looking man- much taller and broader than he was, though Scout did not have a goatee in this picture, and had a head full of dark black hair. Both Osirians were smiling. Scout was in blue jeans and a black t-shirt- much like today. The one that was Highwinds was dressed similarly, in basic jeans and a t-shirt pronouncing his spirit animal to be a shotglass.<br /> <br /> The little nepri looked to Mark 5 in surprise, his near-monotone voice clipped with curiosity, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">For what?</span>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8122,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","user":"ArchonAres","date":". 01-11-2017, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T22:33:44-08:00","id":1029478,"title":"","content":"Regret<br /> Conditions: Introspective (Refinement)<br /> Alembics: Externalize (0), Plumb the Fathoms (0), Prime the Vessel (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO<br /> Willpower: 4/4<br /> Pyros: 5/10<br /> Beats: 0/5<br /> Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> <br /> <br /> ???: &quot;When you start talking about evil and sin, it really all starts with treating people like things.&quot;<br /> <br /> War. Us. Them. The Enemy. Evil. Regret understood. For the first time in a very long time he didn't need to try to understand. He already did. He looked to Mark 5 and saw the realization too. He was like Frank after all. He did want to understand, instead of just perfect. Prime used a lot of fancy words to describe the process but Frank just called it finding your soul. He missed Frank.<br /> <br /> And then Regret had an idea. It might not have been the wisest idea given the circumstance, but Regret wasn't that wise of a Promethean. <br /> <br /> Taking a step closer to Mark 5 and Adonis, Regret let the dead soldiers memories inform his posture. Standing at attention before the Tammuz and the Galatea he spoke what he, Regret, felt and intended. <br /> <br /> Regret: &quot;I understand. I came here to learn about our kind, so that I may understand myself and the world. You came here for the same reason, although you pursue it in a different way. I think we can help eachother. I will aid you in your mission, fight on your behalf, protect you and your friend, and stay with you through your Torment. But I will not go to war. War is evil. War is...&quot;<br /> <br /> The words came not from Regret, but from a brief memory from the Fire. <br /> <br /> Regret: &quot;...always a step backwards.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> The dead soldiers followed the statement up with a salute. Regret felt it was an appropriate response. Whether or not it was would remain to be seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 01-10-2017, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T12:43:12-08:00","id":1029708,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Steadfast<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 7/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> &quot;For what?&quot;<br /> Mark 5 smiled. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;For helping me realize something.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> &quot;I understand. I came here to learn about our kind, so that I may understand myself and the world. You came here for the same reason, although you pursue it in a different way. I think we can help each other. I will aid you in your mission, fight on your behalf, protect you and your friend, and stay with you through your Torment. But I will not go to war. War is evil. War is...always a step backwards.&quot;<br /> Mark 5 looked at the Not-Soldier. What a strange guy. What War? His first instinct was to send the Not-Soldier away. But then he hesitated.<br /> His intention was to learn, to understand. Something that the Titan himself now wanted, in a way, too. Maybe what they wanted was different. But first he needed to be patient, and observe, and learn.<br /> Additionally, he offered to help in his mission-<i>&quot;How does he know about the Mission?&quot;</i>-, which was a bit eery. Maybe the Principle send him, too? The lean figure scratched his head, small stones falling out of his hair. Earth seemed to be really important to the Principle. Big statement, maybe? Anyway, there is no reason to send someone away willing to help. He wanted to help others, too, and would love to not be send away.<br /> So, accepting his help was... Good? or just...good?<br /> He reached a decision. In any case, someone who looked like he could fight was always welcome. The Pilgrimage was dangerous.<br /> That he did not want to fight was maybe a good thing.<br /> <br /> He nodded to Regret and said: &quot;Alright, fine with me. You need to ask Earth and Adonis, too, though.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T14:55:52-08:00","id":1029774,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 9/10<br /> Beats: 4/5 I Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis tenses in surprise as Mark 5 embraces him, but immediately returns it. It's quite a difference, between yesterday when Mark 5 didn't even want to be touch, and now he is now touching others. Who knew that behind the tough exterior, the Titan was a big softie? He can't help but notice that he's been making a big impact on both Mark 5 and Earth today. <br /> <br /> He considers Scout and Regret. Scout is reserved and languid like all Nepri, but Regret seems... different from other Wretched. He carries himself like a speaker, but his an Originist. A strange combination. Mark 5's choice seems natural, and so does Earth's. But a soldier who has become a scholar? Well, that's something you don't see every day. <br /> <br /> But it makes sense. Adonis is trying to understand what they are trying to become, Regret is trying to understand what they already are. He turns to Regret. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;None of us know where this is going to end up. But we'll take all the help we can get. From both of you.&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T08:54:42-08:00","id":1031179,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div><br /> <br /> Scout listened to Regret's speech unsure, but Mark 5's response made him suddenly rivet his attention around back to the Titan. When Adonis mentioned 'both' of them helping, he turned his attention again. Was that the invitation he'd been waiting for? He looked to Adonis and tried to smile.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I think I can perhaps assist with the matter of the missing, at least. An elpis vision, using the athanors you have as a guides. Between Regret and myself, we could perhaps learn much of the missing. It could give us more clues about the company, but will likely be quite painful. I also have gathered rumors about the locations of several Athanors- though the way would be quite perilous.</span>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T09:46:36-08:00","id":1031219,"title":"","content":"<b>Evening-</b> Friday November 4<sup>th</sup><br /> <br /> <b>Earth</b><br /> <br /> Satin's smile grows when Earth latches on to the visual of the spider and the butterfly. &quot;You know, butterflies are alchemical marvels. They grow, they develop, and then they cocoon themselves. They melt down in a solvent of their own making, and restructure themselves into a new shape. They come out of the cocoon as a butterfly.&quot; They see Earth's face and raise their hands &quot;No joke, I read it in a book once. Point being, Azoth remembers, Azoth <i>knows </i>things. Maybe the Messengers are trying to tell you something.&quot; Their face falls, however, as Earth continues to speak about Dead Girl. Such ugliness that can grow on the inside, where it can't be seen, only felt.<br /> <br /> The Riven looks at Earth very carefully, with focused intensity, and takes a calculated risk. They give Earth a hug. &quot;I was wrong,&quot; they whispered &quot;you do have ghosts, it's just they live inside you. Listen, Earth, you need to know that what happened, what Dead Girl did? That's on her, not on you. We will keep an eye out for her, trade the stories, pass along the news. The stories about you are already out there, but we'll let you know where she is and if she's coming. We <i>all</i> will.&quot; Satin stands, patting Earth on her arm, and shakes out their hair. They move as though standing to leave, and then they stop, as if there was something important they forgot to say.<br /> <br /> &quot;Look, we aren't human, and never were, you know? Even if we will be, one day. But these bodies aren't <i>ours</i>, and we aren't them. We're in here,&quot; they tap their head &quot;and in here,&quot; they tap their heart &quot;and that means that we are who we make ourselves to be. I'm not a dude, I'm not a chick, I'm <i>me</i>, and I get to decide who that is. You do too.&quot; Satin finally stands, and begins to walk away. Before they leave, they toss one more comment over their shoulder<br /> <br /> &quot;There's one other thing people use butterflies to represent. They used to stand in for souls.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Mark 5, Regret, Adonis &amp; Scout</b><br /> <br /> Even as the Titan has his dawning realization, a responding flare of Azoth in his gut, the warm trickle of Vitriol suffusing his flesh, the two Originists and the Muse discuss the potential of uniting their Flames in an alchemical pact. The blue Nepri's eyes widen at the mention of Highwinds, and they turn aside, stiff as the mummified corpse they were made from. How long does it take to make a Nepri, really? Does it start when mummification does, or does it start when the Azoth and phlegm flows into their bodies. The blue Nepri looks stiffly towards Mark 5 and nods curtly before turning to Scout &quot;I'm sorry,&quot; he says &quot;Highwinds will be missed.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's getting late. Adonis has to meet with Erwin soon, and talk is dying down. Some of the fellow Pilgrims are dispersing, in throngs, in smaller groups, and alone. The Ramble is dying down.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it's time to get going.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: <b>Mark 5</b> experiences a Milestone and gets three Vitriol Beats out of it. As a more general note, the scene (and the Chapter) is wrapping up, so decide what you guys want to do, and where you're going to go after this. Feel free to write a little vignette describing how you spend the rest of the night. We'll do a time skip of two to three weeks before the start of the next Chapter, so let me know in the OOC Thread if there are any particular Extended Actions you want to get done. The start of the next Chapter will also be an opportunity for another vignette establishing your characters' more typical, day to day lives.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T11:31:39-08:00","id":1031268,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 9/10<br /> Beats: 4/5 I Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> When the Ramble wraps up, Adonis makes his way back Erwin's apartment to keep his date. He spends the night listening to Erwin talk about his day, and tell more about his life. He asks what questions he thinks won't be too prying: where he stands after last night's events, how many people work for Amalgama, if they have offices in any other cities, who his superiors are, what he thinks of them. The stuff he's heard humans ask each other on dates. He isn't really chatty about the details of his own life. He keeps the details general- he doesn't outright lie, either. He mentions that he was a former soap actor who dropped out of the public eye, got into a relationship that went bad, moved to Winnipeg, started a new relationship that ended amiably. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Now, I'm looking for something where I'm on more... equal footing.&quot; </span>He doesn't spell out that he was Lily's submissive, but doesn't lie as answer to any of Erwin's questions about the phrasing. When the dinner ends, Adonis follows Erwin back to his place. They spend the night together and Adonis rejoices in the feel of another person, the thrill of hearing &quot;his&quot; name whispered in his ear. After, as he falls asleep to the sound of Erwin's light snoring, he still can't decide if his interest in Erwin is just as the guard of the truck containing the athanors and potions last night, or as just Erwin the person, separate from all of that.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis attempts to get information from Erwin regarding the inner workings of Amalgama. 3 Manipulation + 3 Persuasion = 6 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/476266\" target=\"_blank\">4 successes</a>. That's an Exceptional Success for Adonis and he imposes the Swooning Condition on Erwin thanks to the Eros Persistent Condition.<br /> <br /> Disquiet roll: 2 Azoth = 2 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/476293\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes</a>. This relationship might actually go off without a hitch!</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 01-17-2017, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T13:18:25-08:00","id":1031299,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Informed (Stannum), Inspired, Disconnected, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble)<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 9/12 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 1/5</b></div> <br /> Aww.<br /> <br /> As the Riven leaves, Earth feels the urge to channel that spark of power inside her in a more positive direction. She tries to suggest they discuss this further back at Satin's place:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Manipulation 1 - Socialize 1 + Willpower 3, resolving Inspired. 3 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/474974\" target=\"_blank\">nope</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It comes out as a noncommittal &quot;maybe i'll see you around sometime&quot; that leaves her with no plans for the rest of the night. Still, the Ramble went so well overall that it doesn't resonate with her Torment too much.<br /> <br /> She ambles over to Mark 5 and Adonis and their new hangers-on, having completely missed their philosophical conversation. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Hey, nerds. That Ulgan with the hair is called Satin. I guess it's a kind of fabric. They seem...y'know, decent.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She's a little wary of Scout and Regret while they make introductions, but Mark 5 and Adonis knew her through Repute and things have turned out okay so far, so she's warmer to them than she might have been. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I said enough already today. No lectures about Flux right now. You guys should hang around with us for a while, though. We got a good thing going.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T07:07:49-08:00","id":1032115,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> Scout gave the Nepri his smile, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Gone, but not forgotten, I believe is the term, yes? And from him we learn.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> When Earth made a seemingly genuine offer for him to stick around, his smile was a little less blank, and a little more hopeful.<br /> <br /> He promised to meet Earth 5 and the others later, before departing. Scout had many things to do. Starting with writing down the ramble. He walked for a few hours, searching for an out of the way spot to hide and write in his journal. The Nepri liked small spaces, and good views- eventually he chose to huddle up under the bridge over the Red River, finding a spot where he could look it over. The rumor about their depths played through his mind, and he wrote down the rumors he'd heard first. His writing was neat, if small, he ensured he had enough detail for anyone to<br /> <br /> Scout was not a good artist, but he added descriptions to each Created he had seen there. Added names where he had found them. Everything he learned about his fellows, every motivation, he wrote down. Those he did not know he marked guesses for. He made note of Adonis, Mark 5, Regret, and Earth. Regret had perhaps stumbled on the wording, but Scout was certain the other Originist had wanted for them to band together as a Throng. Scout rote that into the journal, and considered it.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I do not yet know the people with whom I shall work. That will take time, trust, and surveillance. Further, I do not know this Amalgama, LTD they seek. This will also take time,trust and surveillance. I have offered to assist them in forming an elpis dream around the Athanors which they have obtained.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Scout finished his journal and made for the nearest library after that. He would use computers and search out this Amalgama, LTD. Find what he could and bring information that he had gathered to the table when next he met with them. Yes. That would do.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Let me know what if any rolls you want for Scout to go googlin' spree. He'll start with spending a while looking into Amalgama, learning anything he can- from the corporate web page to the conspiracy theory stuff. After that he'll move to looking into the fire in the church to see if there are any news articles from when it happened. Finally, he'll try and get the best map of the city and the tunnels printed out, in case folks want to go there.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8122,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","user":"ArchonAres","date":". 01-15-2017, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T09:30:02-08:00","id":1032165,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Steadfast<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 7/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Hey, nerds. That Ulgan with the hair is called Satin. I guess it's a kind of fabric. They seem...y'know, decent.&quot;</span><br /> Mark 5 blinked. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;What is a nerd?&quot;</span><br /> He felt like there was a layer to the comment on Satin he did not understand. Was he supposed to say something? Rather than commit a mistake, Mark 5 decided to just nod.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I think I can perhaps assist with the matter of the missing, at least. An elpis vision, using the athanors you have as a guides. Between Regret and myself, we could perhaps learn much of the missing. It could give us more clues about the company, but will likely be quite painful. I also have gathered rumors about the locations of several Athanors- though the way would be quite perilous.</span>&quot; Ah. That sounded familiar. The Titan gave the small guy a smile. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Nothing worthwhile is easy to reach. Thank you for your offer - I think we shall take you up on that!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Several things went through the Tammuz head. A lead on Mudbreaker, at long last! People flocking to them to help - like that comic, League of Justice! Or was it Justice Friends?<br /> Anyway, their group grew in size, and he took it as a good sign.<br /> Tonight, however, he needed some time alone. Time to think on what has transpired.<br /> The day had been wearing him down. No heroics for now - he had to think some more, first.<br /> He might even sleep for once.<br /> Once the Titan has said his goodbyes for the day, he kept thinking about the Ramble. His path took him outside the shelter of the city - at least, it was less urban, and there was more green, more resemblance to his 'home'. People even let their dogs run freely here during the day. This seemed like a good enough place. Laying down directly on the open dirst he scratched up with his hands, Mark 5 went to sleep for the first time in what seemed like an eternity.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Mark 5 will have a Pyros-restoring dream. Azoth 2 + Composure 3 = <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=c89da4a4\" target=\"_blank\">1 sux</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T11:49:32-08:00","id":1032251,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Informed (Stannum), Disconnected, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble)<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 9/12 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 1/5</b></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;<i>Nerd,</i> definition: you four are <i>nerds.</i>&quot; </span><br /> <br /> She cackles. Apparently this is funny.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> For the rest of November, she doubles down on venting her rage in the North End. Sometimes with Mark 5, sometimes on her own. One difference between them is that she's not really trying to <i>help </i>anyone, just leave a trail of fear. People start to whisper about a figure in a ski mask and hoodie with hands wrapped in duct tape, attacking muggers in the dead of night, stealing nothing but their weapons. They say you can see fire glowing under his clothes. They say he always smashes windows because he can't stand to see his own reflection. They say it's not safe to do deals in the train yard anymore, someone is watching.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'll treat this as an equipment building action from the CofD core. Strength 4 + Intimidation 3. I take -2 on Social rolls with humans from Disconnected, but I think if I declare that Earth has caused Disquiet in the neighborhood, I get +2 on Intimidation rolls from Weaponize. Spending 1 Pyros to activate Inscription for +3 Intimidation. And I'll go all the way with a -5 penalty for intended equipment bonus. 5 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/475845\" target=\"_blank\">5 successes!</a><br /> <br /> I was planning to resolve Informed (Stannum) but I guess there's no need. Can my x-success benefit be a Vitriol beat for understanding the Vigilante better? If not, I'll take Inspired.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> When she's not doing that, she does some research.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Researching how humans use the Divine Fire. Intelligence 1 + Occult 3 + Library 1 + Transhuman Potential 3. [now at 5 Pyros]. 4 rolls with 8 dice. 15 successes needed.<br /> First: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/475849\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a><br /> Second: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/475850\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a><br /> Third: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/475851\" target=\"_blank\">4 successes</a><br /> Fourth: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/475852\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a><br /> <br /> 9 successes accumulated. Apparently there just isn't enough about humans in her Library, which makes sense.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Not as much useful information as she hoped. But she stumbled on the name of a Manitoban independence leader during her search, speculated in some recorded rumor to be one of several humans whose seemingly mad &quot;divine inspiration&quot; may have sprung from the Pyros, the Messengers, or a stranger source. She asks around over the next few weeks, taking advantage of her connection to the Ramble as an information-sharer.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Researching the supernatural side of hometown hero Louis Riel and his endeavors, which were seemingly motivated by her Elpis of Faith. Manipulation 1 + Occult 3 + Connected (Winnipeg Ramble) 2 + Library 1 + Transhuman Potential 3. 4 rolls with 10 dice. 15 successes needed.<br /> <br /> First: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/475854\" target=\"_blank\">8 successes</a>. Dang. I'm feeling lucky, so I'll apply that as an exceptional success for the whole action rather than reducing the target number.<br /> Second: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/475856\" target=\"_blank\">4 successes</a><br /> Third: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/475859\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a><br /> Fourth: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/475860\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>. Barely made it! 15 accumulated.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> She spends some time hanging around with Scout during their intellectual pursuits. He came all this way to find her, it seems like she should at least get to know him. They don't get into the big stuff yet, but she confirms that most of the stories he's heard are true, and shows off her more visible Flux scars. Yes, she used to be able to mutate her body and command Pandorans. No, she can't do it anymore, and usually she doesn't want to. But she does show him some Polaroids of Earth-Dies-Screaming with four arms and a mane of bony thorns, and a winged Dead Girl silhouetted against the moon. There are more that she doesn't show him. All she asks in exchange is: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;So, what's your deal?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The interesting thing happens when they go to St. Boniface in the course of his research. She's at least stashed her backpack at Adonis' place (to which she frequently invites herself), but she's still Disconnected from humanity, and it shows. She's showing some scarred and discolored skin, her clothes are torn and muddy, her hair is filthy, she stinks.<br /> <br /> While she's looking around inside the sanctuary, a woman is brave enough to approach her. &quot;How can you come here looking like that? This is God's house.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;God's house?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Earth trips on her tongue and stutters. The woman speaks more slowly, like she thinks the Named can't understand. &quot;I think you need to go home. I don't think you're honoring this space. You're showing yourself to God this way- you're <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parable_of_the_Great_Banquet#Narrative\" target=\"_blank\">coming to the wedding feast without a garment.</a>&quot;<br /> <br /> Earth feels something stir. This human is seeing something in this situation that she can't see. She points up at the ceiling and ventures a guess: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;God is having a feast here?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The woman reiterates as an embarrassed human takes her aside: &quot;This is God's house.&quot;<br /> <br /> Earth is overtaken with the Spirit.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Elpis Aspiration leads to Elpis Vision, I assume. Wits+Azoth: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/475897\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>. If possible, I'll resolve Informed (Stannum) to gain insight from the Athanor and make it an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> First question: How will I know when I have completed my Role?<br /> Second question, if possible: What major or superlative milestone will I face soon?</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 01-16-2017, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T02:01:30-08:00","id":1033238,"title":"","content":"Regret<br /> Conditions: Introspective (Refinement)<br /> Alembics: Externalize (0), Plumb the Fathoms (0), Prime the Vessel (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO<br /> Willpower: 4/4<br /> Pyros: 5/10<br /> Beats: 0/5<br /> Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> <br /> <br /> It was a good start. <br /> <br /> Regret had come to Winnipeg to discover more of his kind, and he had. In fact, he had done much more than that. He had discovered more of his kind that would actively help him understand like Frank had. Kindred spirits who not only wanted to understand the Refinements, but also help and protect other Prometheans. <br /> <br /> Their Rambles lingered in the Flame's memory alongside as much as Regret could muster, his own link to the Refinement of Lead allowing these memories to not fade until they could be put down onto something solid. And there was only one item Regret had that could do that: his own Journal. And in order to retrieve that, he needed to go back to the Far Place. <br /> <br /> Leaving the Ramble he headed away from the city, into the wilderness for several miles. Regret had made sure to leave markers at certain parts of his makeshift trail, so that he wouldn't get lost again, and after about three hours of hiking he found it. Hidden in the wilderness was what he called the Far Place: a makeshift campground that he had made himself using what the dead soldiers remembered about hiding out in the wilderness. &quot;Wilderness training&quot; was the exact words he heard in his head when he drew upon those memories. All of the soldier had memories like it, and he used those memories when he set up the tent he stole so many months ago. He camouflaged it with tarps and trash bags and anything he could find in the wilderness. Provisions, he also stole, hung from a net in a tree several yards away, carefully held inside more trash bags and tarp. It wasn't the largest camp, and truly it could only last for so long before the temperate environment ruined the tent and tarps and trash bags just like the last camp he and Frank had, but it was surprisingly well hidden for a young Promethean's first work. <br /> <br /> Retrieving some rations from the food net, Regret retired for the night into the hidden tent in the hidden campsite. Inside he found his most cherished belongings: A sleeping bag (stolen), blankets (also stolen), a portable lantern that's almost out of battery life (need to steal more batteries), a CD player with headphones and a Jazz CD (a gift from Frank, which had the last and newest of the stolen batteries), and a personal journal with several pens of varying degrees of ink (all stolen with the exception of the words that were written within.) After consuming the rations he set to writing down the Rambles he had heard hours previously. He recorded each name at the top of the page that contained their Ramble, and wrote so much down that by the time he'd come to Mark 5's he was completely ran out of ink. A disappointment welled up inside of Regret, he had very much hoped to record all of them tonight. But with that disappointment, a realizations. Because this sadness was his, truly his, it meant that he had truly enjoyed his experience at the Ramble. He had learned so much, and was so eager to put it down into writing that he had an emotional response all his own. Sadness was unpleasant, but it reminded people of what's truly important. And that's why it is precious to Regret. It's why Regret is Regret.<br /> <br /> Looking down at his journal, with the words Mark 5 written at the top of the page with nothing underneath, Regret had an idea. Tomorrow he would journey into town. He would steal some more pens and batteries, and he would accompany Mark 5 on his mission so that he would both help his fellow Promethean in his Mission to find a Home and so that he would have more stories to write about after he had completed writing down the remaining Rambles. <br /> <br /> [OOC: Well, it's been a while since I've had to do extended actions so some advice would be appreciated in the OOC Thread. As for downtime, Regret is kinda going to shadow Mark 5 and actively help him when he can. Whether it's research or thug punching. Also, he needs to steal some new pens and batteries. I can't imagine this not going well. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T09:26:18-08:00","id":1033404,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Steadfast<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 10/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> Upon being woken by the sun's first rays, the Tammuz felt...invigorated.<br /> The following days, Mark 5 returned to his 'duty'. The new approach proved hard at first. It was like re-learning something you were deeply familiar with. It took the Titan quite some time to get a success, and even then, they were smaller victories than he was used to. However, it was more <i>satisfying</i>, because he knew that he was doing it <i>better </i>now.<br /> <br /> Regret came along. A strange one, but obviously trying to help out.<br /> <br /> Mark 5 smirked. <i>&quot;Heh. Trusty sidekick in the making? Maybe.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> +1 Pyros for Sunrise, +1 Pyros surrounded by his element<br /> Vigilantism: Str+Streewise - 2 (mandatory for getting an equal bonus on future vigilantism rolls)<br /> <a href=\"http://Vigilantism 1 = 0 sux\" target=\"_blank\">Vigilantism 1 = 0 sux</a><br /> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=80c66c2c\" target=\"_blank\">Vigilantism 2 = 0 sux</a><br /> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=bf7e2152\" target=\"_blank\">Vigilantism 3 = 1 sux</a><br /> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=e5359446\" target=\"_blank\">Vigilantism 4 = 2 sux</a><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T11:17:33-08:00","id":1033482,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div><br /> Scout was mildly surprised when Earth was willing to answer his questions about firestorms, pandorans, and Flux. He had expected there to be far more 'observation' than actual talking. &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">My deal? I'm a scientist. I want to see how the world works, so I know how we work within it. We, Pyros, and Flux are a part of the world. I want to know why, and what that means for our pilgrimage. If we do not understand ourselves, how can we hope to understand and become human? You are... like a solid piece of knowledge. A living library of the taboo. Also, a very nice person to answer so many questions, and give me pictures. I appreciate your time very much, Earth. Will you mind if I jot down what you have told me in my journal? Highwinds says-said I must give credit to informational sources. But given the topics, I can leave that out, if you like.</span>&quot; there was a slight pause, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Also, does Adonis's apartment have a bath tub? Knowing that the Red River may lead to the realms of death, I am suddenly loathe to sleep submerged in it, even partially.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Under the bridge became Scout's most frequent hangout, an easy place for the others to find him when he wasn't looking up Amalgama or the Church. His digging on Amalgama's corporate actions didn't go well- too much he did not yet understand. However, the supernatural side for both places was... interesting.<br /> <br /> On the trip to the church, the woman's treatment of Earth was harsh, or so Scout thought. It made him angry, though whether it was because the woman completely overlooked him for Earth, or because the way she treated Earth, the outside world couldn't tell. Still, he drew upon the Azothic Memory, searching for clues about Athanors in this twice burned place, when he was done, he gently lead Earth out. Then they were away he tried for another smile, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">God, Highwinds used to say, was in the details. That woman does not understand the details of our journey, so she knows nothing of God. Or at least, I think that's how that works.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> It was only days left in the month when he finally chose to attempt the Elpis vision on the Athonors left behind by the missing.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <br /> Using Transhuman Potential to bump intelligence, patience to get +2 rolls per extended action.<br /> Amalgama's Supernatural Goings ons: Int+Occult - <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/476163\" target=\"_blank\"> 8 rolls, 22sux</a><br /> Amalgama's Corporate Actions: Int+Academics - <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/476210\" target=\"_blank\"> 6 rolls, 4sux</a><br /> St. Boniface Cathedral Historical Articles: Int+Academics - <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/476214\" target=\"_blank\">6 rolls, 10sux </a> <br /> St. Boniface Cathedral Supernal Rumors: Int+Occult - <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/476211\" target=\"_blank\"> 8 rolls, 20sux</a><br /> Map: Int+Academics-1 - <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/476215\" target=\"_blank\"> 1roll, 1 sux </a><br /> Pilgrim's Landmarks <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/476216\" target=\"_blank\"> 1 roll, 2sux </a><br /> Elpis Vision from Athanors if we have time: Wits+Azoth - <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/476213\" target=\"_blank\"> 1 roll, 1 sux</a> <br /> He'll mostly be looking through this vision to try and get details about the promethean who had it last, but since he can ask a question, we'll ask: Which universal milestone is Scout closest to?<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T15:07:56-08:00","id":1033669,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 9/10<br /> Beats: 4/5 I Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b><br /> <br /> </div> For the rest of the month, Adonis spends his time seeing Erwin. He also spends his days as he usually does: people watching. He spends hours sitting in place, watching humans speak to each other. Each person has their own way of moving, way of talking. Sometimes, he invites some of the others to watch. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">\u200b&quot;Just follow one person. Where are they coming from, where are they going? Who are they talking too? Notice what they say and don't say to each other. Sometimes they say more with their gestures than they do with words.&quot; </span> <hr />Scout is... strange. Muses are blood and air. Nepri are phlegm and water. They are both fluid, but Scout is cold, where he is hot. Earth mentions Scout's fear of slumbering in the river. He meets Scout and offers to let him stay at his apartment when he can manage. He can't help but think that his apartment is becoming a hotspot for Created in Winnipeg. Maybe Scout could share the apartment as a Hovel. It's supposed to be a one-person apartment, but he could use Eros to convince the land lord to let Scout stay with no problems. The only problem with that plan is it could cause Disquiet, and he doesn't want to cost himself and the others a safe haven. <br /> <br /> The first night Scout stays, Adonis asks, <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">\u200b&quot;Could I... watch you? Undress? I'm just... curious how we compare. I know we're all made different ways, I just... want to see if it's true.&quot; </span>He removes his clothes without prompting, and then allows his true form to shine through. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;My creator... she had a thing for some actors. Most of them died young, so she salvaged their body parts, stitched them together.&quot; </span>He recites the names of each man who makes him up. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;My head... she killed the one she liked the most to get it. She told me so.&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T03:02:51-08:00","id":1034496,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div><br /> Scout blinked his heterochromatic eyes a few times at Adonis's request, unsure how to process it, or the fact he'd just disrobed. He'd never really... well it wasn't something he thought about. Perhaps he should have- it was a part of their condition, after all. He rarely bathed really, despite the fact he was in water fairly often. Truth be told, he'd been in the same clothes since old Mexico, when Highwinds had passed.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I... normally just lay myself down clothed. Nudity in public is frowned upon, and draws attention,</span>&quot; the osirian said slowly, his voice quiet. Then he slowly began to strip his old clothing off, unsure of what the Muse was hoping to learn. He considered the story Adonis had imparted. Was this called 'small talk'? It seemed right. Scout looked over Adonis's face for a moment to decide on how to participate. When he continued, his voice was back to normal.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I was constructed from a pair of young brothers who were slain. Not twins, but near enough- Highwinds said there were parts missing, though I am not sure which parts where missing, and which were simply less than usable.</span>&quot; Scout allowed Adonis to see him fully, turning slowly. the nature of what the osirian was missing was perhaps the most obvious, though Scout seemed either unaware or simply didn't care. His limbs were small, and lean. The Nephri was either from bodies with proportionate dwarfism, or the two were just very young. The stitching was immaculate, if Adonis cared to notice, as if the person who had put Scout together had either truly cared, or simply was very good.<br /> <br /> As Scout stepped into the warm water of the tub, and settled in, he glanced up to Adonis again, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Would allow me to watch you interacting with people? Many ignore or dismiss me, but it would be nice to study your technique. Especially as you are what you are, and I would prefer not to have closer interaction until I have studied more- and learned more of Lead. I have some notes, as well. Perhaps you could assist me in filling in some of the details, places where I have had to guess?</span>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T09:02:44-08:00","id":1034642,"title":"","content":"<i>Interludes</i><br /> <br /> <b>Adonis</b><br /> <br /> It isn't too difficult for the Muse to get Erwin talking. He has very strong opinions about his job and his employers, and it seems like he hasn't had the chance to vent in a <i>very </i>long time. The Amalgama office in Winnipeg is fairly small, especially compared to the one in Toronto and, ultimately, the home office in London. There's maybe a hundred, two hundred, people working for the company in the city. They only really have offices in the UK and former British colonies, reportedly since Amalgama was once a metallurgy guild, back in the day. Erwin isn't overly fond of his superiors, but he's uncomfortable with sharing any particularly salient details. What he <i>does </i>share is that he had to pay through the nose for the privilege of using certain materials that only Amalgama really has access to, and that taking a job with them was a way to reverse the cash flow. The way Erwin speaks, you think he might even still be indebted to them.<br /> <br /> Erwin still doesn't know, exactly, where they stand. It's far too soon. Of course, he isn't impartial to going on a few more dates to figure it out. There's something different about the way they share information, the back and forth, the exchange. It's very different to what he had with Lily, but it's... similar in some ways too. He can't quite put his finger on it, but his Azoth flares in response. By some small miracle, the Divine Fire hasn't scorched Erwin yet. Disquiet hasn't set in. But Adonis can't dare to hope... can he?<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Adonis gains a Beat for resolving his Aspiration to go on a date, and he gains three Vitriol Beats from a instinctive Milestone progressing towards Follower. What did Adonis learn in his interactions with Erwin?</i><br /> <br /> <b>Mark 5 and Regret</b><br /> <br /> The Titan and the Originist wander the streets of the North End and Point Douglas, one in a rough mask, and the other tallying along with journal and pen never far behind. Regret rarely gets himself involved, but when he does, he handles himself admirably, the Dead Soliders giving him a fighting chance at lives that were cut short. He thinks he was a little <i>too </i>effective, at one point. He came close to acting on his Torment, and the whispers of the Dead Soliders were very loud indeed. Some people got scorched by the Divine Fire, and Disquiet set in.<br /> <br /> Mark 5 was more discerning in how he chose his targets. He didn't just roam the streets and deal out his own brand of roughshod justice on anyone he thought needed it, he spoke to those he had already made connections with, he tried to determine who was an actual risk to the community. He spent several days gathering information with Regret, and then the two struck out. They came upon an abandoned warehouse, a known hideout of a violent, unsophisticated local gang. They are brutes and thugs, interested in armed robbery, arson, drug dealing, and murder. Of course, they were all but helpless against the might of the Titan's Transmutations. They all bore tattoos of the letters &quot;IP&quot; on their arms, and all wore red bandannas. Some had crossed weapons tattooed on their arms as well. Mark 5 earned some repute from this, which has improved his standing in the neighbourhood as the vigilante known as the Breaker, but perhaps he aimed a little too high.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: <b>Mark 5</b> gains the Reputation (Vigilante) Equipment, which gives him a +2 bonus to suitable rolls with those who know of his reputation. The Reputation needs to be maintained, so you need to make at least one action as a vigilante once per Chapter to upkeep it. <b>Regret</b> on the other hand, takes a Vitriol Beat from inflicting Disquiet, and takes the Disquieted (I.P. Stage 1) Condition. The <a href=\"https://markosun.com/2010/10/17/winnipeg-criminal-gangs/\" target=\"_blank\">Indian</a> <a href=\"http://thepoliceinsider.com/wolfe-brothers-founding-fathers-forgettable-street-thugs/\" target=\"_blank\">Posse </a>is a particularly nasty street gang in the Winnipeg North End in real life, and the story behind it is a really important one for the city. I chose this group in particular partially for their significance to the city, and partially for the fact that the way they express themselves is a somewhat twisted variation on the Ferrum ethos.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T11:31:15-08:00","id":1035332,"title":"","content":"<i>Interludes</i><br /> <br /> <b>Scout</b><br /> <br /> It is exceptionally easy to track down information about Amalgama LTD, and Scout is rather uniquely qualified to be looking into their particular brand of occultism, and what he's found is nothing but endless arrays of exploitative ugliness. Back and back, those in charge of Amalgama have left a trail of fire, blood, and broken bones, all the way back to the 15<sup>th</sup> Century Netherlands. Rumour has it that they are a triad, the alchemists in charge, and that they found their own Vitriol-fuelled waters of life back then. Since then, they have done nothing but try and control as much of the Divine Fire as they can. They want to <i><b>own</b> </i>alchemy. The syndicate started simply, but it quickly grew. They seek out alchemists of sufficient talent, regardless of whether they hunt the Created or whether they are on their own curious Pilgrimage, and offer them a position as a &quot;client consultant&quot;, meaning that they end up paying Amalgama for the right to practice alchemy without being abused or murdered by Amalgama thugs. However, if you agree to work <i>exclusively </i>for them, as a &quot;partner&quot; they'll pay you. You can rely on a steady paycheque, but it comes at a cost. You'll be expected to perform alchemy for the corporation, crack the heads of fellow alchemists, and even be called upon to hunt the Created. The only way to ensure you are left alone by the corporation is to rise in the ranks, and to rise in the ranks you must capture and gut the Created. But for all that these corporate alchemists are protective of their assets, only the three immortals running the show are invaluable. Everyone else is expendable in their quest for true eternal life.<br /> <br /> Finding information about their corporate dealings is a little more difficult, but it's doable, especially since there's an office in the city. You know that they are one of the top biochemical corporations in the world, up there with the Cheiron Group and Last Dynasty International, but their product can be unstable and have unexpected side effects. People also whisper that Amalgama is a good friend to have in a tight spot, that they are troubleshooters and consultants who can take care of business and unforeseen problems.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, it is <a href=\"http://cathedralestboniface.ca/main.php?p=62\" target=\"_blank\">easy enough</a> <a href=\"http://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/manitoba/st-boniface-cathedral-given-heritage-status-1.1349485\" target=\"_blank\">to dig up </a><a href=\"http://www.winnipegarchitecture.ca/st-boniface-cathedral/\" target=\"_blank\">information</a> <a href=\"http://www.winnipegarchitecture.ca/etienne-gaboury/\" target=\"_blank\">about the</a> <a href=\"http://westenddumplings.blogspot.ca/2009/12/st-bs-cathedrals.html\" target=\"_blank\">Saint Boniface Cathedral</a> and the fire of 1968. Once upon a time, it was a magnificent feat of neoclassical architecture, a Romanesque building with homages to Byzantine church design. The soaring bell towers rose over a hundred and fifty feet into the air, and the basilica seated a little over two thousand people. The entryway was a Tyndall limestone facade of three archways, surmounted by the towers and the massive stained glass rose window. Historically, the building is vastly significant. It was <i>the </i>church of the Franco-Manitobans and the Metis, in all of its older incarnations and even to this day. It has met with an end in fire several times, but still it stands. It is said that overheating tools from the roof crew handling repairs was responsible for the fire, but rumours and urban legends of cigarettes and alcohol still circulate. What remains of the original building is the limestone facade where the bishops of the Archdiocese were intombed, though the towers have fallen and the beautiful window was melted to slag. Instead of rebuilding the original church, architect Etienne Gaboury made a point of building a new church using the wreckage of the old one. A new building, risen from the ashes of the old one, a holy relic of patchwork architecture much loved and much abused. Perhaps it isn't so strange that the Created are so drawn to it.<br /> <br /> Other rumours circulate in occult circles. That the burning was the result of a small Firestorm sparked by a Promethean attempting the New Dawn. No one knows who that Pilgrim was, or even if they survived, but the rumour persists. Some say that the old walls were crawling with Pandorans drawn to Athanors inscribed into the walls and the facades of the basilica itself. Whatever the case, the first wall still stands, and the dead bishops remain. Some say that the ghosts of the bishops protected their final resting place, the oldest cemetery in Western Canada. They also say that Marie-Anne Gaboury, first white woman in the Canadian West, grandmother of Louis Riel, rumoured witch in life, is guardian of the place, a goddess of death on the prairies, who wouldn't allow the grave of her revolutionary grandson to be defaced by flame or by misfortune. She lived through revolution and bloody trade wars to the ripe old age of 95, and many doubt she'd allow her life's work to go down the tube just because she did a simple thing like die.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> In between investigating Amalgama and seeking out the history, official and occluded, of the Saint Boniface Cathedral, Scout manages to find time to print off a map of the tunnels beneath the Exchange District, around the Manitoba Legislature, and that are established in a few other locations around the city. It isn't the best map, but it will have to do. It's the only one they've got.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> Scout also spends time plumbing the depths of Azothic Memory, risking scorching the land with the Divine Fire to find the knowledge that eludes him. His Transmutation whispers to him that there is an Athanor inscribed near, or perhaps even within, the Cathedral, but it doesn't detail where, exactly. The information is indistinct, hazy. There is so much weight to the Azothic Memory in Winnipeg that it might be difficult to tease memories of one <i>specific </i>Athanor from all the memories of Athanors that have come and gone. Perhaps he needs to take another approach. Every Athanor is burned into Azothic Memory itself, so perhaps he needs to find a way to go deeper into the Memory of the Divine Fire.<br /> <br /> He takes up the Stannum Athanor, the journal of the unknown Outcast, and tries to force his way into the Azothic Memory. The Divine Fire could come spilling out of him, burning the land, starting the process of the Wasting of the Peaceful Range, but he needs to at least try. He takes the journal, and begins to meditate on the contents, allowing his own unique understanding of the Azothic Memory as an Originist to guide his path. Scout <i>sees</i>.<br /> <br /> He sees himself as a man containing a thundercloud in a thin bag of human skin, made of separate, angry parts and held together by sloppy stitches. He needed a way to let it out, before it killed him and anyone around him. He bleed out the storm, bit by bit. He let electricity crackle with bitter sneers, he let loose lightning with hateful bile, but nothing ultimately worked. He needed to become the eye of the storm, but he didn't know how. He sees landmarks, a viking in stone, a lake, a serpent in the water. He sees himself with a hammer, with gloves, with a weight lifter's belt. He channels the storm but he flays himself from the inside. He can feel it building, the calcifying acid of Flux, the twisting churning engine of Torment. It is a burning in the gut, the taste of vomit on your tongue, orange juice after toothpaste, the shudder of revulsion, bones cracking under tensed muscles. There is a rift between himself and others, a chasm created by lightning and thunder, tended to by a river of Flux. He turns the storm without, focuses his rage on others, he throws Flux like mud, like hateful words, and people seek to come close anyways.<br /> <br /> He finds the eye of the storm, and he becomes it.<br /> <br /> Within the storm, all is anger and rage, buffeting winds and arcing bolts keeping everyone out, and himself within. A wisp of a face appears in the storm, elongated arms of white lightning stretching wide. Electricity arcs between fingers like tears in the world, a noise loud enough to split the world, until it is silent within the storm, until the storm doesn't matter, until the storm doesn't exist. White and golden flames burn within the clouds, following arcs of lightning, breaking down walls. Vitriol, green and slick, falls like rain, stinging your skin. The storm walls fall. The vision ends.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Scout gains the <b>Informed (Amalgama LTD) Condition</b>, from an Exceptional Success, learns all the above information, and (if you so desire) fulfills his &quot;Study a Centimanus&quot; Aspiration and earns a Beat. He successfully forces an Elpis Vision from the Stannum Athanor, and learns that the Universal Milestone he is closest to is Separatio (Division). If you force an Elpis Vision again before the next Story, it will immediately start a Wasteland. I can be persuaded to grant Vitriol Beats to Scout if you can explain what he learned from the Elpis Vision and how it impacts his own Pilgrimage. Ultimately, any Milestones you encounter are interpreted by the characters themselves.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T20:29:54-08:00","id":1035931,"title":"","content":"<i>Interludes</i><br /> <br /> <b>Earth</b><br /> <br /> The Fury vents, and cows anyone that crosses her. Divine lightning and Flux-scarred talons leave burns and dreadful tears throughout the train yards at Dufferin Industrial and the Weston Shops. Terrified rumours escalate into urban legend, and then into the occasional police report. They call the dreadful, seemingly protective, terror Darkstorm, a raging storm front of lightning, aggression, and self-hatred. Earth doesn't target anyone in particular, she just vents her wrath on acceptable targets, and the foot soldiers of several local gangs end up on the wrong end of a fist or a thunderbolt. <a href=\"https://markosun.com/2010/10/17/winnipeg-criminal-gangs/\" target=\"_blank\">The African Mafia, the Central, the LHS,</a> Earth has upset the activities of them all. They all use the train yards as a place to deal drugs, to traffic illegal weaponry, and to beat the hell out of any dissidents who need their heads cracked. More often than not, the police end up in the train yards because they heard someone was beating the hell out of people, only to find groaning, battered bodies wearing gang colours on the tracks.<br /> <br /> The Golem is improving the neighbourhood, undoubtedly. She's cleaning up the streets. She's following her code, doing what she deems to be right, and damn the consequences! Earth doesn't take care for how she does it, and people get scorched. Disquiet actually makes it <i>easier </i>to get this done. When they're tense and Disquieted, she can reach out with alchemy and make them <i>hurt</i>, make them feel what she feels, alienate them, crush them, leave them in torment on the ground, Divine Fire ripping through their guts. The North End is in awe, and Earth smoulders in the heart of a hurricane.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: You can absolutely take a Vitriol Beat for understanding Vigilante better, and you can take the +5 Reputation Equipment as well. What lesson does Earth take away from this? How does this help her understand Vigilante? You also take the <b>Disquieted (North End Stage 1) Condition</b>.</i><br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> Her studies into how humans wield the Divine Fire go... poorly, which isn't unexpected. It defies definition or categorization, it defies attempts at control, which makes the fact that there are people who can steal fire from the heavens <i>at all </i>even more significant. Earth has already heard of Alchemists and Demiurges, the mad occultists who steal Vitriol from the Created, and the strange humans who build them. There are common threads in the stories that Earth hears. The Divine Fire is drawn to desperation, to creation, to madness, to passion, to an intensity of emotion that could set the universe ablaze. It looks for people trying to accomplish the impossible, and it uses them as conduits into the world. What little Earth has written of them doesn't detail the how or, more importantly, the why. Wasn't Adonis made by a human woman? Perhaps he has some insights.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> It is easy to find things about <a href=\"http://law2.umkc.edu/faculty/projects/ftrials/riel/fourmond.html\" target=\"_blank\">Louis</a> <a href=\"http://law2.umkc.edu/faculty/projects/ftrials/riel/rieltrialstatement.html\" target=\"_blank\">Riel</a>. He is easily one of the most written about early Canadians, and one of the most controversial. Canada was a country born of peace, that was immediately tested in the crucible of resistance and war. The Hudson's Bay Company sought to give away land that wasn't their to give, and the people who lived on that land disagreed rather vehemently. It was Riel who led the resistance, Catholic, French, Metis against Protestant, English, Canadians. The Quebecois, a conquered people unbroken, roaring support a nation away, the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_Order_in_Canada\" target=\"_blank\">Orangemen</a> snarling threats in the ears of Ottawa. His mortal life is fascinating, but the details of the rumours of any potential supernatural influence are hard to find.<br /> <br /> You have heard that his grandmother was supposed to have supernatural power, and that when he was executed a well-loved statue of a saint that he owned lost its head in his St. Vital homestead. You have heard that he was considered for the priesthood, before he was expelled from the seminary for contrary beliefs and rebellious attitudes. He was already a firebrand in the Red River Resistance, but in his exile he became something more. An absentee member of parliament, an outlaw politician. He was committed to an asylum in Quebec under an assumed name when he suffered a breakdown. Priests sent missives, they whispered in his ear, they persuaded him he was the chosen spiritual leader of his people, a new Moses for a New World. When he suffered outbursts of manic megalomania, he wrote extensively on spiritual matters. He was a heretic who supposedly kept a book of prophecy written in the blood of the last Canadian bison. You've read his writings, you read transcripts of his final statement to the court. Assertions that he wasn't mad, but chosen by God, guided by angels. His last confession shows confusion. Apparently, he had misinterpreted his spiritual mission, as told to him by the Church, and in the end renounced heresy and any breaks he may have made with Rome.<br /> <br /> The book in buffalo blood is conspicuously missing.<br /> <br /> The Principle has agents, advocates, really, that work Its will across the world. The <i>qashmallim</i>, the Dominions, the angels, the Messengers, and more names besides. You have heard stories about how it has sent god-like beings to protect a single human life, and sent tiny wisps of flame to alter the fates of nations. Their Missions are unique, unable to be duplicated, and are attempted only once. They exist only for the Mission, no matter what the Mission is. They do not question, but neither are they omniscient or omnipotent, they may only operate with whatever knowledge they possessed when they were born from the Divine Fire. They command obedience, they offer advice, they make earth-shattering revelations. And they lie. As often as they tell the truth, the angels lie. And when they come not with blazing revelation, they come with a fiery sword. They are inscrutable and implacable, but the Messengers always, always, produce change, good or bad. It is the nature of the Divine Fire.<br /> <br /> It would be trivial for a <i>qashmal </i>to alter the contents of a letter, or impersonate a priest. It would be trivial to nudge a man on a ledge one way or another. There is that lingering book of prophecy that has yet to be uncovered. There is only one place left to look really. Riel's grave at the Saint Boniface Cathedral.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> You see Riel's grave in the churchyard and it seems remarkably modest. The Church itself is a beautiful work of stone, iron, and wood, the new sanctuary built within the burned out husk of the old one. Wouldn't hurt to look inside. The ceilings are lower than you would have thought, and the room is more claustrophobic. Abstract stained glass windows in minimalist style depict the Stations of the Cross, and the floor slopes gently downwards towards a small stage with barely enough room for a piano, drum set, chairs for the choir, and a pulpit. Hanging over it all was a fairly crude wooden statue in cruciform, rough hatchmarks outlining the suggestion of a beard, eyebrows, and nose. Arms outstretched, feet pointed downwards as though suspended. A little placard indicates the piece is called &quot;Christ of the Red River&quot;.<br /> <br /> When the overzealous parishioner speaks, you notice something rather odd. She talks about God as if God was a person she knew, a person she trusted and respected, a person who was <i>right here </i>in the church and that Earth was offending by her current state. Wasn't that an act of faith? Wasn't that trusting in a person who wasn't present, or trusting that someone <i>was </i>present, or some crap like that? Whatever it was, it set something on fire inside of Earth, and it triggered an Elpis Vision.<br /> <br /> The world was made in various shades of flame and ash, burning in a black void. Earth was alone on ground made of packed ash, with a banquet spread out before her. It's not like any human meal she's ever seen in her wandering, but it speaks to something in her, of nights spent wandering and sharing meals with fellow travellers. The raw, coppery taste of blood, the fatty succulence of pork that isn't pork, the citrus-like tang of Vitriol, all rising up in the back of Earth's throat. A body, stretched out on the ground, Pandorans a mass of tentacles and thorns and tusks and other spastic riots of flesh tearing at it. Dead Girl, beautiful white feathered wings spread, viscera caking her full lips, her pianist's hands, moaning as she sucks at sweetmeats carved from someone's back, draining the Vitriol, draining the humours, draining the Pyros. Memories. Unpleasant ones.<br /> <br /> Earth is brought back to the table and the spread banquet by a sudden crackle of flame. A figure of flames in white and gold, a shining void of a person, sits opposite her. You notice one hand made of darker flames, deep indigo and purple so dark as to appear black, forming a clawed right hand. The figure is broad shouldered and powerful, and they gesture at the food, encouraging the Named to eat. They don't speak, they never speak. Earth wants to lash out. This is more trickery. This is more manipulation. More <b>mOcKERy</b> and she won't stand for it. She beats at the figure, and the figure changes, and splits, and becomes many. She is shattering a veritable army of figures made from calcified ash, and whenever she strikes down a statue, a flame alights on the dirt, and rises as a peculiar flower. A garden grows in Earth's wake. She smashes open furrows into the dirt, and the plants grow of their own accord. The figure with the blackened hand waits in the middle of the garden, a corona of white flames about their head. They beckon to you to come closer.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: You absolutely resolve Informed (Stannum) to get that Exceptional Success, which gives you another Beat. Feel free to interpret the vision, and describe how it will impact Earth's Pilgrimage. Earth will know that Vigilante is completed when you see the fires that have been lit. Earth's next Major Milestone is &quot;Plant a garden and help it grow&quot;. Let me know if this more surreal take on Elpis Visions works for you. You'll need three new Aspirations. Two regular Aspirations and one Elpis Aspiration.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 01-21-2017, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T19:10:00-08:00","id":1036992,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Disconnected, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Disquieted (North End, Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 2/12 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <div align=\"left\">It's not exactly Rabbi Loew's creation defending the Prague ghetto, but the North End has seen worse protectors. The trouble is that &quot;Darkstorm&quot; is still Disconnected from humanity, and it's keeping her from seeing clearly. She's been targeting the humans who seem like they're strong enough to be a threat. Her code is solidifying: <i>humans are pure and beautiful. when they prey on each other, they betray their own humanity. i can hurt them because i am not human. i reinforce the boundary between human and monster. </i>This gives a logic to her Torment. It becomes something she can direct and own, not the wild thrashing of a Savage. Certainly not the meaningless chaos of the Centimani, when Torment was just another shade of endless gray and black that she passed into and out of as easily as sleep.<br /> <br /> What she's missing, Disconnected as she is: humans have more subtle ways to prey on and betray each other than direct physical violence. But that doesn't happen in the trainyards in the dead of night.<br /> <br /> With the Arc-spark in her fingers, she leaves Pilgrim Marks on the side of the trains at Dufferin. It blends in with the graffiti to mortal eyes, but those clued-in will notice the symbols: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pilgrim Marks</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>&quot;Darkness + Stormcloud&quot; = Stannum. Tammuz. Centimani (negated). Stay away (author is dangerous).</b></div> </div> </div> </div>---<br /> <br /> She gleans very little about Demiurges and Alchemists, but quite a lot about Louis Riel. A lot of it comes from Thomas Barebone, a salt-encrusted Tammuz Follower who works at the city library and provided her with a series of books and lectures during successive Rambles. They turned out not to be &quot;related,&quot; but Tom was compliant enough to help anyway. It's a shame Adonis isn't a Follower anymore, she could get used to this.<br /> <br /> Riel was, obviously, chosen by the Principle. His apparent failure at achieving his mortal goals, betrayed by the very angels who pushed him over the edge, only proves her bitter certainty that the Principle is the architect of all suffering. Better to keep your head down and hope its <i>qashmallim </i>pass you by.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i>wait hang on </i><i>but </i><i>what if, like him, there's a meaning behind my failures? what if the principle set me apart, too? did he see those butterflies? did the fire animate me so i could do great things?</i><br /> <br /> <b>NO. </b>Pathetic. Get that out of here.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> She shares her insights into Riel and the Messengers with Scout while they're at St. Boniface. When they pass through the sanctuary together, she studies the stained glass Stations of the Cross sequence, hands shoved in her pockets. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Digestio...sublimatio...separatio...ceratio.. .uh. ..I think there's too many windows. There's supposed to be twelve, right? I can never keep 'em straight. What a shocker, right?<i> Ha!</i>&quot;</span><br /> <br /> After the parishioner comes, her eyes go wide and she seizes up. Scout has to lead her outside while she follows in a daze, arms draped over his shoulders, babbling unconnected words under her breath. Most people give them a wide berth, but a few Good Samaritans approach him over the next hour or so:<br /> &quot;Is your [sister/mom/nanny/friend] alright, young man? Is she having a seizure? Do you need me to call someone?...&quot;<br /> <br /> ---<br /> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Earth Crisis is at the banquet, but she forgot her wedding dress. Her eyes are like saucers. She says: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I'm sorry- I'm not ready. It's gonna turn to ashes in my mouth. Right? I read that somewhere.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> A feast of viscera. The pack's all here: Zigzug, Prettymouth, Meatstain, Ammut- Dead Girl named that last one. And her <i>voice. </i>For the first time, Earth perceives DG's pleasure as disgusting, vile, wrong...<i>sad. </i>Her beautiful wings are slick with gore. Earth sinks to the ground, pleading: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;god, babe, please no, don't do this to your body, just let them eat-&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Dead Girl is <i>wearing</i> the wedding dress. It's filthy. Earth-Dies-Screaming lurches at her, ten feet tall, and her bellymouth slobbers: <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>&quot;t\u035c\u0489\u0328h\u0327\u0341i\u0489ef\u0361\u0338&quot;</b></span><br /> <br /> Earth is at the banquet, in the bloodstained wedding dress. There's a fiery figure opposite her.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>[FIGHT] | [MERCY]</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>[FIGHT]</b></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Just another trick. She shreds it, but it <i>separatio</i>'s and <i>multiplicatio</i>'s until it's a whole field of ashen figures, as faceless and unworthy and weak as the humans she's been venting her Torment on. When will it end? The harder she tears into them, the more the fires spread. Will the Vigilante culminate in torches and pitchforks from an angry mob of her foes? Or, because the garden is so beautiful, will it be some sort of Take Back the Night candlelight vigil of hopeful citizens inspired by her actions? At least she would understand a torch-bearing mob.<br /> <br /> No matter how much she rages and throws lightning and digs her claws into the ash, the garden keeps growing, until she's choking on it. Lesson: she can't kill her own sense of hope for the New Dawn. It's always there. Taunting. Inviting pursuit.<br /> <br /> She's tangled up in a verdant hedgebush, and has to shed the tattered dress to escape. She's facing the Other. No more running.<br /> <br /> Earth grunts, breathing hard, bleeding Vitriol. Flowers are growing out of her wounds. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;You're my Azoth,&quot; </span>she reasons. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;When Satin said this body wasn't me...I get it now. You're like- the Fire beyond the flesh. You're what stays when the body warps and the brains get blown out. You're not a woman or a man or anything with words. You're all power. You're above it.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;But...I think you're stuck. You can inspire, but you can't act on your own. If you wanna work in the world, you have to use this wretched clay. And that means you're guilty when the flesh goes wrong. You can be corrupted by your tools.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She flexes her twisted claw. It matches the Other's blackened appendage. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;You can't burn out Flux, huh? All that stolen Vitriol made it part of me. I poisoned you with it.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;That won't go away. Ever. Unless you go through the chrysalis, and my soul fills up with butterflies.&quot;</span></span></span></div> </div></div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><br /> ---<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;wub- b- buh- butterfly! Butterflies!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Earth jolts up and gasps like she woke up from a nightmare. She and Scout are on the banks of the Forks. She digs into the mud and gravel to center herself. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Okay. It's okay. I'm here. I had a vision- the Flux is in my Azoth, forever. I need to stay in Stannum until they come to me with fires. And I need to go back to the garden. And...get a wedding dress...or a haircut...&quot;</span><br /> <br /> They get caught up on what she missed.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">God, Highwinds used to say, was in the details. That woman does not understand the details of our journey, so she knows nothing of God. Or at least, I think that's how that works.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Earth shakes in the negative. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Nah. No way. That human knew God like we never will. God doesn't want anything to do with us. That's why we poison the world. We're in Hell, where God doesn't touch you, but you're still part of the plan. Hell is the Pilgrimage. It's like Sisyphus. Gotta keep pushing that boulder, no matter how many times it slides back down. At least you can say you're trying.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She dips her bare toes in the frigid Red River. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Speaking of Hell- I'll tell Adonis you can use his bathtub, but we gotta go down into the river sometime, man. Can't be any worse than Winnipeg.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">+1 Beat for end of Chapter. Current Aspirations: Use vigilante reputation against Amalgama; Work at the community garden; Learn what's become of Dead Girl (long-term). Elpis Aspiration: Take a leap of faith.<br /> <br /> Currently have 2 Experiences and 1 Vitriol Experience. Spending 2 Experiences on Vivid Dreams 1&gt;3.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 01-24-2017, 03:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T06:48:39-08:00","id":1037168,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama)<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 6/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div><br /> <br /> Scout shrugged off the religious spiel, not really all that sure about the whole 'God' thing himself. He flinches when she mentions fire, &quot;I would not like to burn.&quot; Then he changed subjects, &quot;I believe this church to holds secrets. Ones that will progress my pilgrimage.&quot;<br /> <br /> When Adonis finally leaves him with the Athanor, he lays back, and welcomes the vision it gives.<br /> <br /> Flux, the storm... A fury like Earth. Apart, with flux separating them from the world, not so unlike how Scout separates himself. Just... angrier. More emotionally charged.<br /> <br /> He wakes up feeling drained, and staggers to the tub, needing it's familiar cool. Apart. He too is apart, and he has limited what he can learn- he must complete this separation, and rejoin. But people still try to close with you, even when you push them away. Is this what Adonis and Mark 5 do for Earth? He will do it too then. But first...<br /> <br /> Scout laid out in the tub, and thought over all he had learned. He needed time to think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T09:15:38-08:00","id":1038934,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Tormented<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 9/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> The Indian Posse had gathered Mark 5's wrath. Not only was what they did wrong, their <i>intention </i>was despicable, too.<br /> The self-declared Hero had been waiting for such an opportunity, he had been burning with the desire to set something right. His newfound understanding of intention was incredibly limiting, however, because it took a lot more time and effort (trying to understand someone's position, what he was thinking, was <i>HARD</i>) to dish out justice, and what had been a source of immediate gratification turned into a long and tiresome process. Thus, when a suitable goal finally presented itself, he threw himself into the frail with more enthusiasm, passion even, than ever.<br /> But his eagerness might have been burning too hot. In trying to make the IP stop their doings, Mark 5 went to ever-more extreme measures, until he finally started hunting them down and beating them up viciously, until they passed out, telling them <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">This is your <b>punishment</b>! Stop, or I <b>will </b>come back for you!</span>&quot;</span>. Then, he didn't even stop at that point.<br /> When the Black Bile rose, the very idea of holding back... didn't even occur anymore to him. Mark 5's conscience took a backseat to the auto-piloting Torment that took him all over the city, searching for IP members to beat down, never taking a break, never resting, never stopping. Mark 5 knew something was wrong, but he didn't get the luxury of stopping to think about it: the next IP member might be just around the corner! <span style=\"font-family:courier new\">They will strike back, he needs to strike first! They will not take him down, he will take THEM down, because he ALWAYS SURVIVES.</span>The disharmony of humours left him aggressive and brutal, and unlike other Tammuz that fall prey to exhaustion due to not sleeping, this Titan was <i>made </i>to carry on for long stretches of time, and his Motus Alembic allowed him to not suffer from sleep deprivation at all. Thus, the Breaker struck at any possible time, all around the clock: a true nightmare for IP.<br /> <br /> How will his teammates react to the irritable Soldier not appearing at the agreed-on time and place?<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Accepting Torment to open 3 Doors via Hard Leverage. Breaking Point Roll at 3 dice (5 Base, -2 for Horrific Action to open 2 Doors)=<a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=65a64e70\" target=\"_blank\">1 sux</a><br /> And against all expectations, I did not get 6 sux on my dicepool of 2 for Disquet. I actually got <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=2da5db79\" target=\"_blank\">none</a>.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  Disquiet Roll added 01-28-2017, 04:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T08:22:39-08:00","id":1042426,"title":"","content":"<b>Noon- </b>Monday December 5<sup>th</sup> <a href=\"https://www.zomato.com/winnipeg-mb/red-top-drive-inn-winnipeg/menu\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Red Top Diner</i></a><br /> <br /> Four Pilgrims meet for lunch at an old diner. The walls are dark, the windows covered in condensation, and the place is built around the galley kitchen. It still hasn't snowed in Winnipeg. It still hasn't properly dropped below zero degrees. It was currently raining in a light mist. This is not normal. This is not good. What the hell is going on? The seats are all hard benches and metal chairs with red cushion topped in red vinyl, the tabletops are surfaced with a slick varnish. The glasses of water they bring you are made of old, faded plastic, and it taints the taste of the water. You are surrounded by a shabby crowd of raucous high school students and worn out senior citizens. Outside, a cement bear, no longer on Broadway, is bolted to the parking lot. You can see an inflatable red figure flailing in panic at the used car dealership right next door.<br /> <br /> They share what they've learned, and what comes through clearly is that the people in charge of Amalgama LTD are abusing alchemy (Does that put Erwin at risk? Will they break him to be like them?) and that there are secrets that are near and dear to the Created that need to be protected. The Ramble will keep their collective heads down, but can the Throng? Only one question remains.<br /> <br /> Where's the Titan?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T13:10:54-08:00","id":1042563,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Disconnected, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Disquieted (North End: Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 12/12 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> Earth was planning to meet the others at the train yard this misty Monday morning, but it was persuasively argued that a restaurant would be more hospitable, so here she is. Hair barely tied back, wearing an oversized rain jacket and trendy <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>MAKE AMERICA NATIVE AGAIN</b></span> hat courtesy of a fleeing carjacker. This place is in the Forks, not the North End, but she still doesn't feel like advertising her identity here.<br /> <br /> She gets caught up with everybody, since it's mostly been one-on-one when their ships passed in the night lately. Louis Riel was an agent of the Principle and buried at St. Boniface, his ancestor Marie-Anne Gaboury is maybe a ghost haunting his tomb, she had a weird vision when she visited and knows where her Role is leading her now. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I gotta keep fighting 'until I see the fires that have been lit.' Which doesn't mean anything to me. Stupid angel dreams.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The Fury clams up as soon as a waitress asks for their order. All she can do is mumble incoherently, tap her non-gnarled hand on a picture of pancakes, and shove some crumpled bills across the counter. It's become increasingly obvious Earth has a major inferiority complex around the Muse, the way she lowers her eyes and sulks in embarrassed frustration at Adonis' conversational skills. When the server leaves, she whispers: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;How do you <i>talk</i> to them like that? I don't get it. You Disquiet them just like we do. They know you're not one of them. Is it because of that face?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She tugs on her cheeks, Mario 64 title screen style, for emphasis. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Or- is it because they created you? You're the only one of us a human made. How does that even work? Did she tell you how she did it? How would they even...&quot;</span> Literally grasping at straws. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;How did she <i>get </i>your Fire?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The wacky waving inflatable arm flailing tube man next door holds her attention for a while. Talking to the humans who made that thing seems as easy as walking to the moon right now. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Not that I, y'know, care whether he's alive or anything, but where's Mark 5? He should've been lecturing us about inner strength by now.&quot;</span> She accuses Regret with a syrupy fork. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Talk, sidekick. What's up with the Big Damn Hero?&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T03:40:41-08:00","id":1042875,"title":"","content":"Regret<br /> Conditions: Disquieted (Stage 1), Introspective (Refinement)<br /> Alembics: Externalize (0), Plumb the Fathoms (0), Prime the Vessel (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO<br /> Willpower: 3/4<br /> Pyros: 5/10<br /> Beats: 0/5<br /> Vitriol Beats: 1/5<br /> <br /> <br /> The diner is nice. Much nicer than any place Regret had eaten in before. The Thief who Died in War's nose picks up scents he recognizes and Regret can almost remember the sounds of laughter, maybe some of it the Dead Soldier's own. A phantom moment the ears recreate in response to the smell of cheap plastic and long worn out leather. It's not fancy, or pretty, but there's something holy about it's simplicity. Something warm and safe, something that resonates on some level with all of the Dead Soldiers. Something that fills all the incomplete pieces with a familiar sadness. Something that reminds them of home. <br /> <br /> Across the table from Regret a syrup fork is pointed at him as a question he was dreading is asked. And with it Regret feel shame and sorrow well up inside himself, bitter sweet in that it is truly his own and not another phantom of the Dead Soldiers. How could he even begin to explain what happened...<br /> <br /> It had all started off quite well, he shadowed Mark 5 as he roamed the street and fought those who intended to do harm to the innocent. Even a few times he himself would lend assistance in a fight, allowing the Dead Soldiers to flex their muscles in a visceral manner that made them squirm and pulse with delight (or so he thought.) He recorded Mark 5's progress to the best of his abilities each night after a successful patrol, patrol felt like the right word, and marveled as new ideas began to occur to himself as he realized each patrol changed the city streets in some small way. It must be the work of his Refinement, or maybe the act itself was a step towards the Mission? Either way, Regret was overjoyed to share in this experience Mark 5 was making for himself, and considered maybe continuing to assist him after he'd finished recording his patrols.<br /> <br /> But then they discovered the gang. Then they discovered their fortress, then they discovered a name and face to associate with the evil Mark 5 wanted to clear off the streets. This is when things went bad.<br /> <br /> First they tried strategy, and there was some success with that. The Scientist who Died in War called it &quot;Fabian Tactics&quot; and it was meant to monitor and contain the IP rather than directly attacking them. It involved caution, clever thinking, and a lot of stake outs...<br /> <br /> [Equipment Creation Roll: Wits + Streetwise + Willpower expenditure - Equipment Bonus &amp; Disquieted social penalty (2+1+3-2-2=2), 1 success (results: <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=e1e41f67\" target=\"_blank\">http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/Wik...?hash=e1e41f67</a> )]<br /> <br /> ...and it was exceedingly far less satisfying than Mark 5's usual methods of implementing justice. It's toll began to visibly affect both Mark 5 and Regret as weeks of hands off stake outs and shadowings slowly began to yield recognizable names, faces, and locations as the two Created began to disrupt the IP's operations within Mark 5's territory. But not all of their time was dedicated to containing the gang, Mark 5's normal patrols continued as planned and somewhere along the line, at least for Regret anyways, the patrols became less about helping people and more about striking out against something the Prometheans had control over.<br /> <br /> It all culminated for Regret as he assisted Mark 5 with attacking a large group of thugs and nearly beating one of them to death with his bare hands. Only stoping because he heard a baby crying from a nearby building. All of the Dead Soldiers writhed within him as his target lay broken and bleeding upon the floor, all of them sending the same message to his patchwork brain:<br /> <br /> The Dead Soldiers: &quot;It'S kIlL Or bE KiLleD!&quot;<br /> <br /> Regret looked upon the beaten man as he shook in the fetal position. He didn't want to die, and as Regret looked down at him he realized that he didn't want to kill him. He wanted to destroy IP, and somehow he though that killing this man would allow him to do that even though it clearly didn't. This wasn't the Alchemy Mark 5 had taught him. This wasn't what he set out to do. This was...<br /> <br /> The Dead Soldiers: &quot;HE'd KiLL yoU iN a heARtBeAT! THIs Is WaR!&quot;<br /> <br /> And that's when Regret left. To his shame he abandoned Mark 5 that patrol and fled to the Far Place for the rest of the night. Filled with sorrow, but more himself because of it he vomited up yellow bile and calmed his mind as the Dead Soldiers slowly returned to their own mournful dreams. That next day Regret desperately sought out Mark 5 to apologize and see if he was alright, but he never found him. Only his message to the wicked. <br /> <br /> Regret, looking directly into Earths eyes frowned and replied:<br /> <br /> Regret: &quot;He's working some stuff out right now. We both kinda went to a bad place there for a while, I stopped myself from going there at the last minute...&quot;<br /> <br /> And then he kinda trailed off, ashamed that he didn't have the strength or will to save his newfound friend from being drawn into Torment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 02-03-2017, 06:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T06:01:07-08:00","id":1043939,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama)<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 13/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div><br /> <br /> Scout listened and watched as the others spoke. He opened his mouth to speak a few times, then just took a bite of his greasy burger and waited again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T06:45:06-08:00","id":1043956,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 10/10<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b><br /> </div> <br /> <br /> The talk at the table has been troubling. Scout has shared what he has learned about Amalgama on his own, and it lines up with what he has learned from Erwin.<br /> <br /> Erwin... Adonis looks down at the table. That night he went out to dinner with Erwin, he felt the Azoth stir in him, recognizing a Milestone on his current Role. The relationship between Erwin and him is different from the one he had with Lily. With Lily, she led, and he followed, like a dog on a leash; a willing dog, but an unequal partner. With Erwin, it's much more push and pull, both of them giving and taking in equal measure. Is this what it means to be a Follower?<br /> <br /> The waitress walks over and asks for their orders. Lineage and Refinement pushes Adonis to take the lead in the conversation, rattling off orders for everybody with a smile.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'll roll for Disquiet. 2 Azoth = 2 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/482242\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>. Let's see if the waitress gets a success to resist. He'll spend a Pyros to delay the onset of Disquiet as per the Masked Condition.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But just as he finishes, he sees a slight change to the waitress' posture. She stiffens and jerks back a fraction of a centimetre, like she just sensed the Divine Fire swirling around him. Adonis doesn't let his smile fall, but inside he feels a pang of guilt.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;How do you <i>talk</i> to them like that? I don't get it. You Disquiet them just like we do. They know you're not one of them. Is it because of that face? </span><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Or- is it because they created you? You're the only one of us a human made. How does that even work? Did she tell you how she did it? How would they even... </span><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">How did she <i>get </i>your Fire?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Adonis gives Earth a slightly morose look. Over the past several weeks, he has noticed that Earth seems to envy his ability to move among humans with ease. Maybe Earth will find her way to Aurum one day, after she ends her time with Stannum. He shakes his head. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;No, I'm not immune. My Azoth can scorch humans just as much as yours can. It's just that as a Mimic, I can delay it for a little while. But there have been... a couple people actually, who seem to resist Disquiet. But they were people I spent a lot of time with, building a relationship. I don't know if it was the relationship that I built with them that protected them or not. But if you ever meet a human who doesn't get spooked the first couple times you talk to them, hold on to them.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> The mention of Sharon brings a distant look to his face. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;My maker... she never talked about Azoth or Pyros or Created. She wasn't- isn't- an alchemist. She was playing with things she didn't understand. She must have wanted to make me so badly that Pyros was attracted to her.&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T12:54:24-08:00","id":1044143,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Disconnected, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Disquieted (North End: Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 12/12 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> Earth dismisses Adonis' advice about relationships out of hand. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;No way. The harder you hold onto a human, the better chance you'll choke them. It's just a matter of time. You're gonna live to regret meeting Erwin. I'd never let someone get that close to me. Ever.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> But she's obviously thinking about it while she chews her flapjacks. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;How bad does a human have to want something before they attract Pyros? Why couldn't she just get with the guy your head used to be on? They're both human, she wouldn't scorch him or anything. You see someone you want, and you take them. That's how relationships work.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> About Mark. Regret sez: &quot;He's working some stuff out right now. We both kinda went to a bad place there for a while, I stopped myself from going there at the last minute...&quot;<br /> <br /> Earth cackles. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;That bad place is where I <i>live</i>, man. If you run away from storm clouds, the lightning's always gonna hit you on the ass. You gotta <i>ride </i>the lightning. Or...you gotta <i>be </i>the storm. Or...something.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Me and him are cut from the same clay. When we're in Torment, we work on one job and don't stop, ever. If he's digging holes, he'll dig a new river. If he's cracking skulls...uh. Humans are gonna die. He won't like that when his bile settles. But he's gonna stay in that bad place until it does.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She muses. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;We get out of Torment when we feel hope. <i>Elpis</i>. What gives Mark hope?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She waves at the resident Osiran Originist. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Hey, Scout. How do you find out what gives one of us hope?&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 02-05-2017, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T06:09:10-08:00","id":1044462,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama)<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 13/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div><br /> <br /> Scout nodded at Adonis's words, and snorted at Earth's dismissal. But what she said next...<br /> <br /> Scout's eye widened in shock and he froze, &quot;Be the storm, and others will burn. Can't ride the lightning. It is inside of you. Demanding to get out. Can't run, or it will burn you. Master the storm within. Quell it.&quot;<br /> <br /> He blinked a few times, and nodded. Maybe his vision was for this. Was that the secret of Torment? The truth of the fury was that mastery brought peace?<br /> <br /> Scout took out his notepad and started scribbling his thoughts. He was not sure where they would lead, but he had to write it, and lost himself in that, not hearing Earth's question at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T07:30:44-08:00","id":1044492,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth</b></div><br /> <br /> Scout is...writing down the dumb stuff she said. Again. This is weird, because she's garbage and has nothing to teach anyone. Earth stares in disbelief and slumps down on the vinyl seat.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:Goldenrod\">&quot;I'm surrounded by <i>huge nerds.</i> We need the hero back so I can just punch stuff with someone normal* again. Scout! Can you use your Lead alchemy to help Mark, or not?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <i>*for certain values of normal. ask your doctor before calling mark 5 normal.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T13:21:38-08:00","id":1045338,"title":"","content":"Regret<br /> Conditions: Disquieted (Stage 1), Introspective (Refinement)<br /> Alembics: Externalize (0), Plumb the Fathoms (0), Prime the Vessel (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO<br /> Willpower: 3/4<br /> Pyros: 5/10<br /> Beats: 0/5<br /> Vitriol Beats: 1/5<br /> <br /> <br /> Regret blinks several times as he slowly comprehends what Earth is asking Scout.<br /> <br /> Regret: &quot;Lead alchemy? I have Lead alchemy, but I don't think I can do what your asking. I can make the Storm gather outside of myself, I can see the Flame's memory, I can even link people like you and I together, but I've never heard of someone being able to help people out of that bad place. Can you do that Scout?&quot;<br /> <br /> Regret is filled with amazement at the prospect that brings. His fascination with Mark 5, Adonis, and Earth came from him believing that he'd learned everything there was to know from the Refinement of Lead. But, Scout's mysterious powers proved that there was still much for him to learn, and that perhaps he should turn a little more attention to the fellow Originist in the group. <br /> <br /> Regret then noticed how intensely Scout was writing in his...journal, he probably didn't hear a single word Regret said. He was in a good place right now, and with first hand experience Regret didn't even know if he could pull him out of it without a good wack to the shoulder. Not wanting to do that, Regret looked out the rain-spattered window at nothing I particular and then ate a spoonful of the bowl of chili he had in front of him. <br /> <br /> [OOC: Chili, of course being the one thing all the Dead Soldier and Regret could agree upon to have for lunch. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 02-07-2017, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T16:44:31-08:00","id":1045485,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress, Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 9/10<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b><br /> </div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;How bad does a human have to want something before they attract Pyros? Why couldn't she just get with the guy your head used to be on? They're both human, she wouldn't scorch him or anything. You see someone you want, and you take them. That's how relationships work.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Adonis feels a little bit of Pyros slip out of himself, and wrap itself around the waitress like a warm blanket. Yes, she is being affected by Disquiet. He knows where that leads: obsession and paranoia and attempted murder. He gives Earth a wan smile. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Sharon wasn't... right in the head to begin with. And human's don't react well to crazy. That's why she didn't just ask him out.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> Mark 5's Torment saddens Adonis, but some of Earth's ideas worry him. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>Last time they threw down, it caused a brown-out. </i>&quot;I think we need to keep Mark calm. When Created fight, humans grab their guns. Regret, Earth, you guys have been around him the longest. What do you guys have any clues about what his Elpis is?&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T18:50:06-08:00","id":1045558,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 13/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div><br /> Scout heard the words, after a fashion, but didn't assign meaning to them until his scribbling was complete.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Sorry, I was jotting down notes about my last Vision. I can help him.</span>&quot; Scout said as he finally looked up, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">We just have to find him first.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> He turned his attention to regret, recalling as much of his words as he could, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Branding a Throng, no. That is beyond me, I'm afraid. Calming him might be difficult... but I will try. It could get dangerous but... I rest assured that the Principle will lead us to the right path.</span>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T22:16:05-08:00","id":1045618,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth</b></div> <br /> Regret sez: &quot;Lead alchemy? I have Lead alchemy, but I don't think I can do what your asking.&quot;<br /> <br /> Earth talks around a mouthful of pancake. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;That's 'cause you're a fresh corpse, Gretel. A whole stack of fresh corpses. Scout's been around the block.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Adonis sez: <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;I think we need to keep Mark calm. When Created fight, humans grab their guns. Regret, Earth, you guys have been around him the longest. What do you guys have any clues about what his Elpis is?&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Calm is the problem. Melancholy, black bile, all that. We came from mud. Calm and slow and steady and sinking back into the dirt is what the corpse <i>wants </i>to do. That's why I got, <span style=\"font-size:11px\">y'know,</span> </span><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">all depressed and sad and shit </span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">when I was in Torment. We need to light his fire, get him mad. Get him fighting! That's what he was made for! <span style=\"font-size:10px\">(it's what <b>i</b> was made for, too!)</span></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> Scout sez:<span style=\"color:#0000FF\"> &quot;Branding a Throng, no. That is beyond me, I'm afraid.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Earth looks from Scout to Regret. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;You can make the Brand? Huh. Dead Girl could do that, too.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Gears turn.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;uh, anyway. This place sucks, let's just go find him.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T07:21:27-08:00","id":1049283,"title":"","content":"<b>Meanwhile... </b><i>The North End</i><br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Did you ever notice how, in the Bible, whenever God needed to punish someone, or make an example, or whenever God needed a killing, he sent an angel? Did you ever wonder what a creature like that must be like? A whole existence spent praising your God, but always with one wing dipped in blood. Would you ever really want to see an angel?</i>&quot; - Thomas Daggett, <b>The Prophecy</b><br /> <br /> The Titan Mark 5, the Breaker, perches atop a building. He is watching a couple of gangsters muttering to one another, discussing how to deal with this guy, this <i>one </i>guy, who keeps hitting their club houses, who keeps cracking heads and laying out anyone who gets in his way. They're <i>still </i>talking about what he did to those boys at the train yard. Limbs torn clean off, bodies hurled through box cars. Who the hell can do something like that? <i>What </i>the hell can do something like that?<br /> <br /> He doesn't understand why they aren't getting the message (what isn't there to get?), especially since he has made it so clear. If you step out of line in the Breaker's neighbourhood, then you find out why he got the name. It was easy to do what he did, anyone who knew how could have done it, the human body is a delicate instrument, when you get down to it, and Mark 5 is the fist of a god, shattering everything in his path. The Titan's wrath could level buildings, if he desired it. His Alembics filled to the brim with the Flame Immortal, Mark 5 is invulnerable, unstoppable, invincible. What do these petty things of flesh and bone, who are as broken as the Unborn, think they can do to him?<br /> <br /> People avert their eyes when he calls on them for aid, now. They know what he can do, but they are glad that it is directed at those who deserve it, and not at them. The Breaker is a wrathful guardian angel, an avenger of injustices. If downtrodden youth aren't smart enough to stay away from those who trade them a sense of belonging for their lives, then by God they are going to stay away from the human predators who take advantage by fear alone.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Due to succeeding the Breaking Point roll, Mark 5 gains the Disconnected Condition. As a result of the horrific actions taken against IP, Mark 5 gains the Tormented Condition. Mark 5 also gains a Beat from Tormented due to having killed some humans while in Torment. You can also make a <b>Wits + Composure </b>roll to assess the situation further.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 02-15-2017, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T11:44:46-08:00","id":1049393,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Tormented, Disconnected<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 11/11 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> The Breaker tried to assess how to best get down to the Evil men, how far to jump. They did not understand? Then he was going to tell them <i>again</i>. And <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>again</i></span>. And <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i>again</i></span>. However many times it took, because unlike them, he was Iron, and he. would. never. stop.<br /> Gathering the Fires of Creation in his body, the Titan crouched down, ready to jump: <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><i>&quot;When humans speak different languages, they start getting louder, so it's easier to understand them. Maybe I need to <b>scream </b>my message, too.&quot;</i></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>OOC:<br /> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=f9c72547\" target=\"_blank\">4 Successes on Wits+Composure</a></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T13:59:05-08:00","id":1049461,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 13/13 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 3/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> Scout took his food with him, leaving his crumpled dollars on the table, and followed Earth quietly, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I don't know... I think it was better than some of the places I've been in Mexico. Although I do miss the food in old Mexico. We should go there some day, and get some proper food.</span>&quot; The little guy looked up almost pleadingly at his companions at that statement, and gave a smile. Scout was fairly sure he had just successfully completed 'small talk', so he returned to the business at hand, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">So once I get into mutual azothic radiance contact range with Mark 5, I should be able to slowly erode his Torment. If I'm lucky.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> The little man looked up to Regret and settled a hand against his fellow Originist, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Now... I'll need to focus a little, so I would really appreciate if no one let me get run over by a car while we walk, okay? And if all goes well... maybe after this we can learn something from each other about our chosen Path, yes?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Scout hesitated, afraid to look bad before his newly forming ring of friends, before pressing his mind to the task of looking for Mark 5's azothic radiance. The Osiran sniffed at the air, and turned slowly, before stopping and pointing &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I can smell him. Like molten steel, in a forge. This way.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/486377\" target=\"_blank\">2 Successes to detect Mark 5.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/486380\" target=\"_blank\">1 Success to Pinpoint Mark 5 via Heed the Call</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8122,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","user":"ArchonAres","date":". 02-18-2017, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T12:07:50-08:00","id":1050637,"title":"","content":"<b>Scout</b><br /> <br /> It is easy enough for the potent Azoth of the Originist to find sympathy with Mark 5. It just took a bit of the Osirian's attention to start on the trail. It's a long walk up Saint Mary's road through Norwood, and across the Queen Elizabeth Bridge that crosses the point where the Red and Assiniboine Rivers meet and mix before diverging again. It's a dusty road, one that takes them past the Forks, past the towering gothic edifice of the Fort Gary Hotel, past the artistically rusted iron-workings of the Upper Fort Gary Historical Park, past the limestone opulence of Union Station and the looming, squared-off government buildings, and past the Exchange District. The better part of two hours passes as they make their way towards the errant Titan.<br /> <br /> <b>Mark 5</b><br /> <br /> You can hear them whispering about inducting a new member, a scrawny-looking kid with a badly tied bandana, and debating about whether they can risk the usual method of making the pledge into a Striker. The usual method, as you know from interrupting several initiatory 'missions', is arson, armed robbery, or homicide. Commit a violent felony, do it in front of witnesses. It means the pledge hands over blackmail material to their direct superior, trauma bonds them with other members of the gang, and it demonstrates they can follow orders. Very nasty. Very effective. The leader of the group, a shaven-headed Warrior with a red bandana tied across his face and bloody arrows tattooed on his forearms, suggests they go with an older method. The Strikers, who you can see have IP tattooed into their necks or the backs of their hands, glance at one another, but they nod, steel in their expressions.<br /> <br /> The three of them turn on the fourth, laying him out with brutal punches to the upper body, and when the kid drops, kicking him as he curls up into a ball to protect himself. He is enduring the worst of it, just lying there, and it's hard to tell if he's unconscious or just letting it happen. They want to see if he can take the pain. They want to see if he can endure.<br /> <br /> They want to see if he's made of Iron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T12:57:38-08:00","id":1051622,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Tormented, Disconnected<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (Exemplary Athleticism), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 8/11 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> They were testing their own. They were looking for rods of Iron in sheets of paper. Admirable attempt, but completely absurd. Maybe someone needed to show them, show them how easily they break. Show them what <i>real </i>Iron can do.<br /> They wanted a chance at escaping his Punishment? Fine. HE would put THEM to the test.<br /> <br /> The Breaker used the gathered Pyros, fired up his Motus Alembic, and jumped down, landing infront of them. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">This is your <b>punishment</b>!</span>&quot;</span> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Without another word, h</span></span>e started his attack.<br /> <br /> <i><a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=bfd172ef\" target=\"_blank\">1 sux on jumping down</a></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T13:31:50-08:00","id":1051636,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Disconnected, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Disquieted (North End: Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 12/12 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> She's been trudging in silence with the others for a couple hours, enjoying the misty rain, hands shoved in her jacket pockets, when her Azoth starts to resonate as well. They're in the neighborhood she's gotten to know, and made a mark on herself.<br /> <br /> Was that the sound of someone leaping off a building, and thudding onto the pavement? She warns the others. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Shit- you hear that? Gotta be him.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">If it's okay, I want to take a Beat from Disquieted (North End) to &quot;draw some kind of negative attention to me at an inopportune time.&quot;</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T15:16:49-08:00","id":1051707,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama LTD)<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 9/13 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 3/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> Scout nodded when he felt their Azothic radiances come into mutual range, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I should probably have mentioned that if I do this, I could potentially hurt Mark 5, and myself, if I screw it up. Also that I've never done it before. And that it could start a wasteland.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Then Scout closed his heterochromatic eyes, and pushed out with his Azothic radiance, trying to harmonize it to the proper frequency to calm Mark 5's misery.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Spending 1 Pyros for Transhuman Potential (manipulation), and 3 Pyros to activate Sublimation by Fire. Also spending a willpower on the first roll.<br /> Mark 5 will need to make a reflexive automatic Resolve+Azoth roll each turn to contest Ending Mark 5's Torment will require sux = his Azoth x3.<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/487773\" target=\"_blank\">Sublimation by Fire 1: 2 sux</a><br /> That is... auspicious. Failure on my end will get Mark 5 4L damage. If something goes miserably wrong and I dramatically fail, we both take 4 and we start a wasteland. Yay!</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8122,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","user":"ArchonAres","date":". 02-20-2017, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T18:29:13-08:00","id":1051795,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress, Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 9/10<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis bites his lip in concern as they walk. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">\u200b&quot;You guys do realize there's a good chance he's killed somebody, right? Multiple somebodies. What's that gonna do for his Pilgrimage?&quot; </span>He shoots Earth a look. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Let me try and talk him down first. Remember the Ramble? People tend to listen when I talk. If he's not in a listening mood, I guess you and Regret can handle him together. Think that's going to be a problem, big guy,&quot; </span>he says to the Frankenstein. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T02:41:26-08:00","id":1051910,"title":"","content":"Regret<br /> Conditions: Disquieted (Stage 1), Introspective (Refinement)<br /> Alembics: Externalize (0), Plumb the Fathoms (0), Prime the Vessel (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO<br /> Willpower: 3/4<br /> Pyros: 5/10<br /> Beats: 0/5<br /> Vitriol Beats: 1/5<br /> <br /> <br /> Regret looked at the Muse and seriously considered the implications of having to fight Mark 5. He didn't like those implications, but the Dead Soldiers were focused on survival and the coming battle. <br /> <br /> Regret: &quot;I'm not as strong as Earth or Mark 5, but I am strong. Plus, I can call the storm to slow him down.&quot; <br /> <br /> Regret looked up at the sky and grimaced. His first Alemic was the ability to make the weather go from bad to worse, he didn't like it all that much and preferred the inner warmth of the Flame and it's memories. The power was there though, and if need be he wouldn't hesitate to use it. <br /> <br /> [OOC: Can start powering up Externalize to potentially set the potential battle on more favorable terms for the non-Tormented Prometheans.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T13:37:42-08:00","id":1052159,"title":"","content":"<b>Mark 5</b><br /> <br /> The Titan sails off the roof and lands heavily on the asphalt, heavy-soled boots making a flat smack on the pavement. There's a slight jarring shock to his knees as he absorbs the impact, but it's nothing that will prevent him from being to fight. His Azoth seethes as the Flux-taint of Torment sets it boiling. He is merciless, and that suits Flux just fine. It destroys, it breaks down, and isn't that the first step to making something new in the first place? The Titan says it's for the Mission, but is it really? What does this have to do with protecting Earth? What does this have to do with being a Soldier? Is this all a Soldier is, a killer, a weapon pointed at acceptable targets by the Powers That Be? He doesn't have much time to contemplate as the three gangsters standing let out terrified yelps and jump backwards.<br /> <br /> One of them goes for a gun in the waistband of his jeans, pulling it with a frantic motion, the loud click of the hammer acting like the first punch of a stopwatch. Who finishes the fight first? Mark 5, the Titan, the Breaker, or these three gangsters? Two of them make as though to run, but there won't be any escaping. How will they get the message otherwise? Evil should be punished. Even as he leaps towards his targets, the Titan can feel the encroaching Azothic Radiance of his friends, and the strongest of these, Scout's, reaches out to his, trying to burn the Torment from him. He doesn't want to get rid of it, he <i>needs </i>it, it helps him do what must be done.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Mark 5 takes three bashing damage from the fall, reduces by one due to the Dexterity + Athletics roll, suffering a total of <b>two bashing damage</b>. Declare an <b>Intent</b> and roll <b>Strength + Brawl</b>, we're resolving this as <b>Down &amp; Dirty Combat</b>. Gangster with the gun rolls <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=2be000dd\" target=\"_blank\">Dexterity + Firearms</a> for two successes, the escaping gangsters roll <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=3aac19e7\" target=\"_blank\">Dexterity + Athletics </a> for three successes. You need to get four or more successes on the roll to handle all of them. Also roll <b>Resolve + Azoth </b>to contest Scout's Sublimation by Fire.</i><br /> <br /> <b>The Throng</b><br /> <br /> A single gunshot rings out, and there are cries of pain that echo from buildings into the dreary late afternoon sky. The Breaker is at it again, but at what cost, to him or to others? The Throng starts to make their way towards the noise, moving with urgency, planning going out the window, when a rather disheveled looking man, eyes wide, staggers towards them, waving wildly with his arms and yelling with the slurring voice of the drunk. Somewhere in the background, a beer can blows in the wind and rolls under a bus shack bench. He lurches towards Earth, howling obscenities at the top of his lungs.<br /> <br /> &quot;YOU GODDAMN FUCKING <i>BITCH! </i>WITCHU DOING BACK HERE?! SAID I'D FUCKING <i>KILL YOU</i> IF I SAW YOU AGAIN <i>BITCH! </i>YOU AND ALL YO FREAK FRIENDS!&quot;<br /> <br /> She can see the flickering, like flames, dancing in his bloodshot eyes. Her Azoth has scorched this community <i>hard </i>as she scourges the criminal organizations that plague them with whips of divine lightning and hands that can tear cripple, rip, and tear with the corrosive Flux-taint of her own Torment. People are peeking out of windows and screaming down at the Throng. They heard the gunshot, and now they see a heated argument involving death threats. The police will be called, and the right questions probably won't be asked. Time to get Mark 5 out and go.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Earth gains a Beat from the <b>Disquieted (North End: Stage 1) Condition</b>. I just want you to keep in mind <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> that the Condition also gives you a -2 Social penalty to your rolls affecting the people who are impacted by this Condition.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T16:56:09-08:00","id":1052278,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Disconnected, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Disquieted (North End: Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 12/12 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">&quot;I should probably have mentioned that if I do this, I could potentially hurt Mark 5, and myself, if I screw it up. Also that I've never done it before. And that it could start a wasteland.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Earth throws up the horns and rolls her also-heterochromatic eyes. In her ongoing quest to attain the humanity of a surly teenager, she's been experimenting with irony. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Awesome. Love it. Good stuff. <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(adonis am i doing it right?)</span>&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;You guys do realize there's a good chance he's killed somebody, right? Multiple somebodies. What's that gonna do for his Pilgrimage?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Ugh. I dunno, help it, probably? I've killed people too, and look how I turned out. Humans kill each other all the time.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> &quot;I'm not as strong as Earth or Mark 5, but I am strong. Plus, I can call the storm to slow him down.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;You're stronger than World's Smartest Boy and Me Talk Pretty One Day, you'll do fine. Maybe. Or you might get stomped.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Gunshot. Drunk human stumbling towards them. People coming out the windows to look. Humans on the prowl.<br /> <br /> Earth tenses up- <i>kick his ass? no, humans watching- </i>and decides to fire her Alembic. It's all instinct, just bubble up the oily residue of Disquiet and stain somebody else with it for a while. She turns her fire inward so her awful face doesn't show, and it scorches her inside, but the psychic residue comes tangled up into her warty fingers. She shoves him as they hurry past, muttering <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;tag, you're it.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Spending 1 Pyros to charge Externalize, taking the Irritable condition instead of showing disfigurements. Manipulation+Persuasion+Azoth, 5 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488168\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 02-20-2017, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T23:44:58-08:00","id":1052415,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Tormented, Disconnected<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (Exemplary Athleticism), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: //OOOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 8/11 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Breaker was determined to let none of the four IP members get away- Punishment must be met out. As one was already on the ground, he only had to deal with the other three, really. One had a gun - he might as well have lifted his arm and volunteered with a hearty &quot;Here, I want to be the first!&quot; for all the good it would do him. The other two tried to run -<span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Cowardice won't help you now!</span>&quot;- </span>but they had not even a snowball's chance in hell, either, for a Titan is not only strong, but swift, and his wrath inescapable.<br /> <br /> They wanted to claim they were made of Iron?<br /> He was going to show them how much pain they <i>really </i>could take and how easily they <b>break</b>. When they are down, he will place his foot on the knees of those trying to run away from Punishment, grab the ankle, then both pull and kick. He was going to break their backs like a bundle of twigs on his knee. He was going to stomp the ribs of the one on the ground into splinters: that one wanted to be IP, after all, so he should get a taste of what that entails. He was going to rend every joint, every bone, before he'd leave them with his message on the ground.<br /> Before the fight, a voice, his voice, screamed something in the back of his head, something about Intentions, and Soldiers, and Protection, and a Mission, but the voice made no sense to the Breaker, and the violence drowned it out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Azoth reached out to him, trying to burn away the Flux in his own. His Torment reared up, causing his Azoth to fight against Scout: It cannot leave <i>now</i>! It was Punishment incarnate, it made him better, it took out the useless brakes. He refused the tiny one's betrayal!</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=8e9fbcfd\" target=\"_blank\">Strength+Brawl+1 Willpower = 8 Sux</a> on Down &amp; Dirty with the intention of Killing / Torturing all IP members + the helpless boy on the ground.<br /> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=437ef5ed\" target=\"_blank\">1 Sux on Azoth + Resolve</a><br /> <br /> Since it was an Exceptional Success on Down &amp; Dirty: Is replenishing the spent Willpower okay?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T16:00:26-08:00","id":1052868,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 9/10<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b><br /> </div> <br /> Adonis looks around. <i><span style=\"color:#00ff00\">Guns. Only a matter of time before they all reach for them. They'll call the cops. Need to get out. Need to keep this from getting ugly. </span></i><br /> <br /> He draws on his Pyros and pours it through his stolen larynx out his mouth and into the air. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Look, folks. We don't want trouble. We're just looking for our friend, and we'll be leaving. We would really appreciate it if you folks didn't call the cops on us.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Adonis spends a point of Pyros to activate Transhuman Potential and increase his Presence to 4. He will then attempt to persuade the neighborhood to let them pass in peace.<br /> <br /> Presence 4 + Persuasion 3 = 7 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488574\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes</a>. Let's make this interesting and switch that to a Dramatic Failure for a Beat.<br /> <br /> So that's a point of Pyros spent and a Beat in exchange for the neighborhood trying to kill us.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T10:30:25-08:00","id":1053307,"title":"","content":"<b>Mark 5</b><br /> <br /> The Breaker is faster than the gangster, and the Titan lunges forwards with incredible speed, grabbing the ringleader's wrist with one hand and shoving it upwards and to the side, squeezing hard enough to grind bone. The evildoer screams and manages to get off a useless shot before the Breaker snaps his wrist with a casual twist of his arm and leaves the man gasping, breathless, in too much pain to actually draw breath. The leader taken care of, he runs after the other two. He grabs one by the back of his shirt and pulls backwards and down, hard, hurling him to the pavement with the sound of a splitting skull. The second he trips with a swift forward kick to the back of the knee, and the man falls forwards with a yelp that turns into a gurgling scream as his face hits the street and his nose cracks. The Breaker grabs a leg, plants his foot on the knee, and twists it like removing the cap from a bottle until the limb falls in a way that a leg shouldn't. He flips him over, and hits him in the head. And then hits him again. And again. And again. The man feebly throws up scrapped and callused hands to defend himself, but to no avail. The fists come down like an iron hammer until blood sprays with every blow, cast backwards with every recoil of the arm, spattering across his face, his jacket.<br /> <br /> He turns on the other coward who tried to flee his just punishment and steps with heavy boots on an ankle, starting the man awake with pain as the Breaker plants his foot and starts to grind in with his heel. The bone cracks, so he moves upwards, systematically dismantling his limbs at every joint until all that is left is a screaming torso with the limbs of a marionette, and that ends when he grabs the throat with both hands and squeezes until the blood that's been bottled up in his face turns purple and black. The leader comes next, grabbed by the hair and the red bandanna he was so proud of, as he gets slammed into every surface the breaker can reach. Alchemy makes him easily strong enough to pick up this man and throw him around, and he only stops once blows to the head fail to produce twitching. He lets him fall, and he sees the man's face as nothing but a slump, loosely hanging patchwork mess. Worse than any Created he's ever seen.<br /> <br /> The would-be initiate comes last. The Breaker brings down his boots repeatedly until his torso is a hole of red ruin, with splinters of bone and gobs of clotted blood and connective tissue caked onto the bottom of the shoes. Mark 5 has been stained red, a bloody weapon, iron covered in rust, and stands motionless amidst the corpses.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Alright, so, Mark 5 gains a point of Willpower for the Exceptional Success on Down and Dirty Combat. I would also rule that he needs to make another Breaking Point roll at five dice, and that he gains another Beat from Tormented due to causing a massive problem for the Throng.</i><br /> <br /> <b>The Throng</b><br /> <br /> The screaming keeps getting worse, and the humans keep getting more distressed because some of them can <i>see </i>what's going on. You need to get over there before Mark 5 goes too far, before he does something that he can't undo or run away from. Earth acts first, and though the drunken man offers some <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=dd58d1cd\" target=\"_blank\">resistance</a>, she still manages to pass off the oily muck of Disquiet onto him. The man stumbles backwards, crashing into a public garbage can and tumbling onto the ground.<br /> <br /> &quot;Stupid bitch,&quot; he mutters, before raising his voice back into a howl and slowly swaying back onto his feet &quot;you STUPID BITCH! I'M GONNA KILL YOU!&quot; He hurls himself to his feet, somehow managing to draw a pocket knife and open it with something resembling dexterity, and careens after Earth.<br /> <br /> Adonis' pleas fall on deaf ears, but they don't go <i>precisely </i>as badly as you'd expect due to Earth's alchemy. There are people on phones and sirens in the distance, but people are shouting abuse from the windows down at the drunk with the knife, with well-meaning pleas to Adonis and the others to just stay put because help is coming. After all, they all heard that guy threatening them, and he's a creep and a menace to the community anyways.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: I think you mean the Redirect Alembic <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a>, it's <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> who has Externalize. Additionally, Adonis gains a Beat from his optional Dramatic Failure, but passing the Disquiet buck to this random guy shifts the situation a little bit.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T15:09:38-08:00","id":1053451,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Disconnected, Irritable, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Disquieted (North End: Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (1)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 11/12 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> The guy comes at her with a knife and she just lets him swing. She grabs the blade in her fat claw and totally no-sells it, like he's trying to play-fight and she's not playing along.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;darkstorm says no. go away.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Taking the hit and presumably some damage. Stamina 5+Intimidate (Leave Me Alone) 4+Reputation 5-Disquiet 2-Disconnected 2. 10 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488910\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> She wipes blood off on the bill of her hat. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;C'mon, let's go go go. Where's he at, Scout?&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><i>&quot;...why don't humans ever call you guys 'bitch'?&quot;</i></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 03-09-2017, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T15:49:22-08:00","id":1053472,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama LTD)<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 9/13 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 3/5</b></div><br /> <br /> Scout kept his hand on Regret when the shouting started, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Can't concentrate with people yelling!</span>&quot; he complained. And then it clicked. He saw the harmony he was going to need in the wavelengths, and focused on it.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhen Earth shouts for him again, he glances up and stammers, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Uhm... uhm... I think I got it! Maybe... it's close...</span>&quot; he pointed.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Extended action continues! Exceptional Success!<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/488915\" target=\"_blank\">Sublimation by Fire 2: 5 sux<br /> Me and Mark 5 both regain a willpower!</a><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T01:05:52-08:00","id":1053690,"title":"","content":"Regret<br /> Conditions: Disquieted (Stage 1), Introspective (Refinement)<br /> Alembics: Externalize (0), Plumb the Fathoms (0), Prime the Vessel (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO<br /> Willpower: 3/4<br /> Pyros: 5/10<br /> Beats: 0/5<br /> Vitriol Beats: 1/5<br /> <br /> <br /> Regret grabbed onto the arm that Scout was using to touch his shoulder. He recognized the look Scout had, he knew it to mean that he needed his concentration. He also recognized what he was saying to Earth. Mark 5 was definitly near by. Most likely where the sound of gunshots were coming from. Regret HaTeD the sound of gunshots. But, he made a promise that he would help. And the escalation of events kicked the Dead Soldiers into overdrive. <br /> <br /> Using his arm to indicate that he would lead Scout to where he wanted to go. Regret began to move, taking the Nephri with him as he moved along the nearest wall and right past where Earth and the drunken man were facing off. He would not allow anything to interfere with Scout now. He had a mission to fulfill. The Dead Soldiers many senses gave him the information he needed about the battlefield.<br /> <br /> The Dead Artist: (fEAr AnD ANgEr aRe OveRfLOwIng hEre. IT wiLl bE More DaNgeRous To sTAy heRe bY thE MiNuTE.)<br /> <br /> The Dead Thief: (CopS wIlL pRObaBly Be oN tHeir Way bY NOw. yOU HaVe aT LeASt 5 MinUteS.)<br /> <br /> The Dead Scientist: (gUnsHotS haVe CeAsED. TArgeT hAs MoSt lIKeLy nULlifIEd anY ThrEatS. pRoBAbiLiTY oF CIviLiAn cASuAltIes: HIGh.)<br /> <br /> Regret: &quot;Understood.&quot;<br /> <br /> Regret said this last part aloud. And though he said it mostly to himself in response to the sensations of the Dead Soldiers, he said it while looking back at the concentrating Scout, grappling Earth, and mob soothing Adonis. Any one of them might have misinterpreted it as him saying it to them, because the look of focus he had on his face would be something that none besides Mark 5 would have seen before. <br /> <br /> The battlefield was set, it was time for action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T01:09:59-08:00","id":1053695,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Tormented, Disconnected<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (Exemplary Athleticism), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: //OOOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 8/11 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b></div> <br /> This was the Breaker screaming his message. They deserved it.<br /> And wasn't their first action to go for a weapon to attack him proof for that?<br /> The red on the ground was a curious sight. It always surprised him how strongly it stood out against whatever it was on.<br /> So puny. So weak. So incomprehensive it was infuriating.<br /> <br /> <br /> Justice had been served here. But there were still IP around, still in the city, still unpunished....<br /> <br /> The Breaker's work was far from done.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=9e825724\" target=\"_blank\">1 Success on the Breaking Roll.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T07:10:45-08:00","id":1054297,"title":"","content":"<b>The Throng</b><br /> <br /> The drunk stumbles away in stupefied terror as black bile drips from the inconsequential knife wound he inflicted on Earth. Some people have come down out of the apartments and are shouting at him, reminding him that they saw everything. They offer sincere questions after her health, and instead of alighting to <i>her </i>they turn their scorn inspired by Disquiet on the man instead. It was... not what Earth was used to, nor what she was expecting. She has little experience with this particular kind of alchemy.<br /> <br /> Scout's own alchemical working manages to find an opening, and plunges on through. His powerful Azoth worms its way into Mark 5's Radiance, burning out the Flux taint of Torment where it finds it. It is cathartic, good for the soul, it revitalizes both the little Osirian and the Titan, refreshing their will. The Muse and the Wretched stand to one side, and the Dead Soldiers mutter anxiously in Regret's ear. They're on edge. The Dead Thief remembers a buddy who went ballistic, just started killing <i>everyone</i> that came towards them if they looked sufficiently foreign. That was not a good day for the Canadian Armed Forces.<br /> <br /> They need to move ahead, Mark 5 is close and they need to get him out of here. The sirens are getting louder.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Scout regains a point of Willpower</i><br /> <br /> <b>Mark 5</b><br /> <br /> The Breaker barely even registers the stumble along his Pilgrimage, he shrugs it off with justifications, with Torment, with the destructive, murderous rage of Flux. The fog of it is closing in, caustic and cloying. He isn't done yet. There's still IP to deal with and when they've been finished, the Mission will not be. He'll move on to the next gang, and the Breaker will give them a reign of terror the likes of which the city wouldn't be likely to forget. He is contemplating his next move when the fog lifts. Azoth worms its way into his Radiance, burning out the Torment where it lies, and the Titan's Azoth exults. His dampened senses return to him.<br /> <br /> He can feel the gentle rain pouring down from the sky, and the slight chill of the December air, but Mark 5 isn't cold, he's actually quite warm. Wet, but warm. There's heat rushing to his knuckles, to his feet, to his knees, and black bile pumping hard through his body. He's short of breath, so he takes in some air, and nearly gags on the copper and iron smell of blood, the decay of human waste. It won't get out of his nose, his <i>mouth</i>, it's all over him. There's steam rising from the wreckage of human lives that surrounds him, faces, or what's left of them anyways, wide with terror.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Mark 5 gains a point of Willpower which will fade at the end of the scene, and gains a Beat from passing the Breaking Point roll. If you would like to roll another Breaking Point, you're welcome to, but as an alternative, perhaps you could take the Guilty Condition.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T00:11:48-08:00","id":1054671,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Disconnected, Guilty<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (Exemplary Athleticism), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: //OOOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 7/6 | Pyros: 8/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b></div> <br /> <br /> The hazy fog lifted, Flux no longer tainting his sight and feelings.<br /> It could not have come at a worse moment.<br /> Mark 5 went to his knees, his arms pushing hard into the ground as the Black Bile forced its way out. He tried to get the smeel, the sticky warm liquids off of him, rubbing furiously at his face, his arm, confused and disoriented. The Titan found himself exhausted, in the middle of carnage, of lives ended - <b>by him!</b>- and all he could think was <i>&quot;What kind of Monster does such things?&quot;</i><br /> Something inside of him pulled itself together, causing him to feel empty and hurt at the same time, an experience he hitherto had not. It was horrible, and he wanted it to stop.<br /> He wanted to stop looking at what he saw, what he <i>caused</i>, he would give anything, <b>anything</b> to turn back time, to have another chance, to make it right...<br /> but he knew he couldn't. If not for the rain, he would've felt himself leaking.<br /> <br /> This was something he could never atone for. This was proof he could never be like them.<br /> <br /> Mark 5 broke down in deep, heavy sobs. &quot;<span style=\"color:#000080\">What have I done?&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T14:51:23-08:00","id":1054948,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Disconnected, Irritable, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Disquieted (North End: Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (1)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 11/12 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> Round the block, turn the corner and there's the hero, covered in blood. Here's something Earth is starting to learn about humanity: it's easy to accept that <i>you're </i>monstrous and give up hope that <i>you'll </i>be better, and even to say that you don't care what others do with their (stolen) lives. But it's very, very hard to watch someone else actively do the things you hate and fear in yourself.<br /> <br /> She looks at the Titan breaking down in tears, and suddenly she gets him in a way she never has before. She knows what's on his mind. And seeing that in someone else <i>hurts.</i> She reaches out her hand. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Mark. I get it now.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Charging Imperatus with 3 Pyros, showing disfigurements. Sucking up some electricity with Remote Absorption to charge Power Sink. Stamina+Survival+Azoth: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/490093\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>. +4 temporary Health, +2 temporary Willpower.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Lightning crackles out of a nearby socket just for a second, gathering in newly blackened pockmarks on her flesh. They glow and crackle with Pyros. She reaches down and grabs a wet, strong-looking bandanna off one of the bodies.<br /> <br /> What do Vigilantes do? They punish people who kill humans. Even when she understands. Even when she's been there, too. Even if she almost can't bring herself to hurt him. The Code says: punish. Justice demands it. Maybe this will get those fires she has to see lit.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I get it, man. You showed me. Being Good means punishing monsters like <i>you!</i>&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Cops or not, we're not leaving without a fight! Initiative, just in case: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/490097\" target=\"_blank\">6</a>.<br /> <br /> Earth's Intent for this fight is to get Mark 5 grappled and restrain him with the bandanna! Starting out with the Fallen Pillar move from Brute Force, +2 dice and 8-again but Earth has Defense 0 this turn. Spending 1 Willpower. Strength 4+Brawl 3+All-Out 2+Willpower 3-Defense 7. 5 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/490098\" target=\"_blank\">failure</a>. Let's make that a dramatic failure, as Earth remembers why she shouldn't pick fights with Titans.<br /> <br /> If this counts as suffering a setback or putting the throng at a disadvantage due to anger, +1 Beat from Refinement Condition.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 03-09-2017, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T17:25:03-08:00","id":1055007,"title":"","content":"Regret<br /> Conditions: Disquieted (Stage 1), Introspective (Refinement)<br /> Alembics: Externalize (0), Plumb the Fathoms (0), Prime the Vessel (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOO<br /> Willpower: 3/4<br /> Pyros: 5/10<br /> Beats: 0/5<br /> Vitriol Beats: 1/5<br /> <br /> <br /> Round the block, turn the corner and there's the target, shaken but alive. Regret lets out an audible sigh of relief, his new found friend managed to keep himself out of serious trouble. Judging from the battlefield it was only a minor skirmish, and the look of sorrow an pain upon Mark 5's face confirmed that Scout must have been successful. This was probably the best outcome the could have hoped for, all they had to do was retrieve the target and...what is Earth doing? <br /> <br /> Earth: &quot;I get it, man. You showed me. Being Good means punishing monsters like you!&quot;<br /> <br /> And then as quickly as it happens the battlefield comes alive again. Regret just stands on and beholds, with profound confusion at why Earth would be attacking her friend, witnessing the fight play out. He wants them to stop, can't they see the bodies that surround them? Crushed and broken, humethean lives lost to Mark 5's Torment? What would their fighting accomplish? They're already dead, they are no longer suffering. Their regrets moving on with them to the other side. Only their friends and loved ones would hold onto that sorrow now. Only the ones to come after will feel the tears fall.<br /> <br /> But there was something else to this fight, something Regret felt down deep within himself. Something the Flame was trying to tell him. A process so primordial and essential that it bears a thousand different names. <br /> <br /> Iron being forged by a blacksmiths hammer. <br /> <br /> Tectonic plates crashing against one another. <br /> <br /> A maximum speed car Chase by the police along the freeway.<br /> <br /> These were all reactions to what Regret was witnessing by the Dead Soldiers, who only knew sensation and couldn't possibly comprehend the Flame's message. Could Regret? <br /> <br /> Regret: &quot;Why?&quot;<br /> <br /> He said it aloud but more to help himself find context to the process that occurred before him. One that involved two people who were supposed to be friends. <br /> <br /> <br /> [OOC: Regret is going to be completely absorbed in Earth and Mark 5's potential fight from his Introspective Condition. He will simply watch on in awe and horror until it concludes, or until something life threatening occurs.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 02-25-2017, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T06:01:44-08:00","id":1055204,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama LTD)<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 9/13 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 3/5</b></div><br /> Scout thought the scene reminded him of the day High Winds had died, but in reverse. Mark 5 had taken apart the gangsters like his genitor never could have. And now he sat, mourning his sins, just as Scout had sat mourning his loss. It was both terrifying and beautiful to see Mark 5 on his pilgrimage. Remarkable like none other.<br /> <br /> And then Earth spoke.<br /> <br /> Moments like now were the ones Scout remembered that other Prometheans were a good study, but not a good control group. This was why he looked inside for answers. Earth was going to need to learn to do the same, eventually. This was one of those moments where he saw the rare things that made prometheans and humans so completely obviously different. A human, surely, wouldn't run up on their friend, broken, and then threatened them to a fist fight. That wasn't how humans operated, was it? He'd never seen that before, at least.<br /> <br /> He looked to Regret, saw the look on his face. There would be no help here. Scout understood that, and it was okay. Regret was learning. The problem was, what was his fellow Originist learning?<br /> <br /> Scout's deadpan voice echoed louder than he could have thought possible, and his inner thoughts becoming external for once in his life, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Earth... chill the fuck out. Mark 5 is already in pain and hurting for exactly the actions he's caused. No punch you throw will make him grieve the way he does now. If you want to punish someone, let's go punish Amalgama for the shit they've done. Hell, if you just want to get into a fucking fistfight, hit up the tunnels and check out the unborn- I've got a base-line map to help you get there. But this? This isn't the pilgrimage. Beating up your friends while they are in agony isn't walking towards humanity. You said it yourself- I've been around the block. So listen to me now- let me help you get back on the road before we step off again. Would Mark 5 punish you for hurting someone- no matter how bad- while you were in Torment? Or would he take your hand, and help you back on the road?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Scout hoped he knew the answer to that last question. If he didn't... maybe he was the one missing something. He looked to Adonis, two different colored eyes pleading for help from the Muse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T08:17:42-08:00","id":1055247,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 9/10<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b><br /> </div> <br /> Adonis follows the others around the corner and finds Mark 5 standing over the bodies of the IP members. Something starts rising in him: not Pyros, not an emotion like anger or fear, but gorge. It's a strange and awful feeling. Ironic that, as the Mimic, he is feeling the effects of this in a very human and physical way. He doubles over and clutches his belly has he vomits up coffee and bits of donut mixed with bile onto the sidewalk. He takes a deep breath and brings a shaking hand up to his mouth to wipe away the rest.<br /> <br /> He looks at Mark, who he realizes is crying. He's out of Torment, but at what cost? He stands there for a second, at a loss for words. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Mark...&quot; </span>he spreads his hands. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">\u200b&quot;Shit, man. Just... shit.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I get it, man. You showed me. Being Good means punishing monsters like </span><span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><i>you!</i></span><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot; </span>Earth's fist lashes out at Mark. Regret seems transfixed, and Scout looks over at him with a pleading look.<br /> <br /> Earth is pissed. Royally pissed. And a fight between a Fury and a Titan isn't going to end well. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>When Created fight, humans start reaching for the torches and pitchforks. </i></span>He looks around desperately. Earth isn't in a talking mood right now. Then it hits him. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>Aw, fuck it. </i></span>Without further thought, he launches himself at Earth and grabs for her.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis is going to be very stupid and try to grapple Earth.<br /> <br /> Initiative: 1d10-&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/490401\" target=\"_blank\">8</a> +4 = 12. <br /> <br /> Strength 3 + Brawl 2 = 5 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/490324\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>. Earth will need to roll Defense to see if she breaks free or if we're grappling.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 02-26-2017, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T10:51:21-08:00","id":1055311,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Disconnected, Guilty<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (Exemplary Athleticism), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: //OOOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 8/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> Mark 5 hardly registered the others coming along.<br /> Then, something tore him out of his pain.<br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;... punishing monsters like <i>you!</i>&quot;</span><br /> Memories flashed before his eyes, deep, personal experiences. Experiences that made him who he was, to a degree.<br /> The first sounds he heard, while something pounded on his ribcage like a crazed gorilla on steroids: his progenitor making noises he was yet to understand. <span style=\"color:#2F4F4F\">&quot;Live! Live,<i><b> GODDAMNIT!</b></i>&quot;</span><br /> A human mob, running him out of his place, throwing stones, even shooting guns at him. &quot;This is no place for freaks like you!&quot; &quot;We don't want you here!&quot; &quot;Die, <b>Monster</b>!&quot;<br /> The moment he passed the group of parkour-practising thieves, because of his hard work.<br /> <br /> The Titan's eyes grew hard.<br /> Was he a monster? Maybe. He looked at the scene infront of him. Probably.<br /> But he would not- not now, not ever - let<i> someone else</i> decide that for him.<br /> If somone was to punish him, he would decide who had the right.<br /> <br /> Until then, he would do what he always did. <i>He survived</i>. Ignoring the others, he went for the one who attacked him (was that Earth or Adonis?), intend on showing why he was no easy prey, intend on disabusing them of the notion they could take him. &quot;<span style=\"color:#000080\">Bad call.&quot;</span><br /> Mirroring the attack, Mark 5 lashed out without holding back one bit, friend or no friend. They were soon to understand why he was ingraved with <b>SURVIVOR</b>.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=5e9278a5\" target=\"_blank\">Initiative 8 (in case it matters)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=f12870b4\" target=\"_blank\">Brawl + Strength + All-Out + Willpower = 6 Successes!</a><br /> Losing Defense to go All-Out and using Falling Pillar, to add some Symbolism for the exchange.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T07:11:33-08:00","id":1055636,"title":"","content":"<b>The Throng</b><br /> <br /> Things go from bad to worse very quickly, as they come across the charnel ground that Mark 5 has produced in the rainy streets of Winnipeg. The human crowd is distracted by pursuing and berating the drunk, but in time they'll make their way over here, and then things will get ugly. More than ugly, downright violent. There will be police, and there will be more fighting, and chances are if the Created try to stay free there will be more death, more suffering, more Torment, more Disquiet. A Wasteland would begin to fester and bubble, and the fires would start smouldering.<br /> <br /> Fire and blood, that's what will come from this. Fire and blood, ash and death. No creation, only destruction. No Azoth, only Flux. No Pilgrimage. No New Dawn.<br /> Just futile stagnation.<br /> <br /> Earth flares with alchemical might as electricity arcs from nearby outlets and starts blazing like flame in holes burned into her skin. She seems to swell, to become <i>greater </i>than the sum of her parts, something mighty and divine, glorious and terrible. She lunges at the Titan, fists raised over her head, and that's when the Muse, surprisingly agile, and sanguinely, foolishly, reactive, leaps onto her back and weighs her down. Mark 5 rises and unfolds like a volcanic peak, both arms batting aside Earth's before grabbing hold of the collar of her shirt and hurling her to the ground, hard, with almost contemptuous ease. There's blood on her clothes now, and black bile in her mouth, she bit her tongue in the fall, and Adonis has fallen off, a little bruised and battered. The Titan is stronger than her, <i>better</i> than her,<i> mocking </i>her, like <i>Heartsblood </i>did. Well, lightning took care of Earth's genitor, and it will take care of Mark 5 just the same.<br /> <br /> All she needs to do is reach for it...<br /> <br /> Scout can feel something stirring in the overlap between their Azoth, a swirling cauldron of terror the likes of which he's never felt before, but which Highwinds warned him about. The wrath and creative energy of the Divine Fire unbound, the Flame Immortal let loose on the world in its purest form. <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=9c5ea3bb\" target=\"_blank\">Firestorm.</a><br /> <br /> An explosion of Pyros erupts between Earth and the Titan while Adonis lies on the ground, huddling to try and protect himself from the worst of what is to come. Unfolding like a beautiful and terrible flower, the rain roars into a torrential downpour, each droplet laced with Divine Fire, burning at their skin, setting their humours alight, while the winds of a hurricane lash out and buffet at the still-standing Titan, screaming like an offended god. The sound, the <i>sound</i>, is a screaming loud enough to drown out even the sound of your own voice, sheets of rain so thick that all you can see if the glowing of the divine lightning in Earth's skin, and the hand in front of your face. The Firestorm tears at the environment around them, hurling debris at the bodies, tearing skin and flesh from the bone with whips of wind. You swear you can hear a <i>voice</i>, a small still whisper, somewhere in the heart of the hurricane. Your flesh starts to writhe, and to Earth the sensation is sickeningly familiar as it starts to twist and manifest into sublime monstrosity, the Firestorm shaping you like plague-ridden clay into something like one of the Unborn.<br /> <br /> The Dead Soldiers murmur in Regret's ear, and something within the rain calls to Scout. The whispers sound like 'Witness Them'.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Alright, so, <b>Earth </b>gains a Beat from the Dramatic Failure, and a second Beat from her Refinement Condition.<br /> <b>Earth </b>also suffers the Knocked Down Tilt, and six points of Bashing Damage.<br /> <b>Mark 5 </b>gains a Beat from the Exceptional Success on the grappling roll.<br /> <b>Adonis </b>gains a Beat for putting himself at significant risk throwing himself at the two Created-of-Mass-Destruction.<br /> <br /> <b>Earth, Mark 5, Scout, and Regret </b>are each experiencing a Milestone, and are also having an Elpis Vision that will last through the Firestorm, which will last the next three turns.<br /> <br /> The <b>Firestorm </b>is a <b>Extreme Environment 4</b>, which means that after a number of turns equal to your Stamina you'll start taking Lethal Damage. The Firestorm also grants the <b>Heavy Rain</b> and <b>Heavy Winds Tilt. </b>Because it is Strength 3, the Heavy Winds inflict 3B damage per turn from debris and sheer wind strength. Roll Dexterity + Athletics -7 due to Environmental Penalties if you'd like to avoid damage. The Flesh-Warping aspect gives each of you three dots worth of Pandoran Dread Powers, so describe the mutation however you would. This will likely cause Earth to revert to her most familiar shape as Earth-Dies-Screaming. Learning to control the mutations takes a Stamina roll, for which Earth gets a +2 due to being a former Centimanus.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 02-27-2017, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T10:34:01-08:00","id":1055702,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 9/10<br /> Beats: 1/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b><br /> </div> <br /> Adonis jumps onto Earth and holds on for dear life. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;EARTH, STOP IT!&quot; </span>The Tammuz he is wrapped around seems to grow into something even bigger and more intimidating. Then Mark 5 responds. He throws Earth- and Adonis too- to the ground. Adonis gives a cry of surprise and pain as Earth falls hard onto him. He rolls out from under her and looks up at them with a furious look. He is about to call on the power of his Pyros to bring the both of them under his thrall- when suddenly Earth tries to call down lightning to smite Mark 5, and then the sky explodes into a storm. He is flattened by the force of the wind and his anger turns to pants-shitting terror. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>Firestorm. </i></span>He's never seen one, but he's heard whispers of them, seen symbols that have marked places out on the Canadian Prairie that were ravaged by them. Now the conflict between the Fury and the Titan has spawned one <i>right in front of him. </i><br /> <br /> He tries to hunker down and avoid the debris blowing around him.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Attempting to avoid damage from the debris.<br /> <br /> Chance dice = <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/490641\" target=\"_blank\">nope</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But Adonis is struck by garbage and stray bottles, hard. He feels a sudden, horrid sizzling inside him. He spits out blood, but watches with horror as he sees his blood turn to a fluorescent green that starts to each at the blacktop beneath him. But mixed with the horror is a twisted fascination. He feels like he's starting to slip down into an inky mud that could suffocate him... and the thought gives him a sick satisfaction. The thought of giving in, giving up on the Great Work and sinking into the monstrosity of Flux... it's seductive. More exhilarating and frightening than the first time he was on his knees for Lily.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis takes three dots of the Breath Attack Dread Power, which manifests as acid that has the Extended damage option. He will attempt to control the mutation.<br /> <br /> Stamina 2 = 2 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/490646\" target=\"_blank\">failure</a>.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 03-04-2017, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T14:30:54-08:00","id":1055786,"title":"","content":"Regret<br /> Conditions: Disquieted (Stage 1), Introspective (Refinement)<br /> Alembics: Externalize (0), Plumb the Fathoms (0), Prime the Vessel (0)<br /> Dread Powers: Armor (1), Bizarre Weaponry (1), Camouflage (1)<br /> Health: ///OOOOO<br /> Willpower: 3/4<br /> Pyros: 5/10<br /> Beats: 0/5<br /> Vitriol Beats: 1/5<br /> <br /> <br /> It happened faster than Regret could ever imagine. Like a volcano, like a squall, like a artillery round falling from the sky, the Firestorm was upon them. <br /> <br /> The Flame infused the rain and wind and debris as it scoured the Created who had worked so hard to find and recover their friend. All brought about because of some process that Regret could see but just not put words too. <br /> <br /> Another gust of wind, faster than Regret or the Dead Soldiers could react, and another piece of the battlefield knocks Regret to the ground, completely blind siding him.<br /> <br /> (Roll to avoid debris: failure. <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=5d4ba54f\" target=\"_blank\">http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/Wik...?hash=5d4ba54f</a> )<br /> <br /> From the ground where Regret tries to catch his breath he begins to hear sounds coming from within the Storm. The Dead Soldiers writhe and squirm in reaction to the danger and the Flame. Every piece of the body that constitutes &quot;him&quot; is screaming, &quot;RuN! rUN For YoUr mISeRaBle lIFe!&quot; But Regret remains transfixed. Transfixed at the other battles taking place amongst the torrent and winds.<br /> <br /> Regret sees a man who always wanted to be an artist. He beholds his struggle through the torrent as his work is mocked and dismissed as garbage. He sees the artist, desperate, fall in with a bad crowd of humetheans. He sees him offer sacrifices to the Buried King, and hears the non-words of the thing beneath the ground. The artist will never forget what he heard. Even as bullets rain down upon him in the battlefield, his biggest regret is ever joining that cult. The price must be paid. A life of fame and renown in exchange for the appointed death at the appointed time. The Dead Soldier cries out for salvation, but finds only an end. Regret felt the transformation happen as Flux seared away his fingers into elongated hooks. The artist screamed without a voice, only sensation.<br /> <br /> The Dead Artist: (tHe PRicE wAS PaID! ThE pRiCe WAs pAID!!!)<br /> <br /> Across the battlefield Regret sees a man who always wanted to be a doctor. He struggles to look after his ailing mother but cannot hold down enough jobs to pay for school and his mother's medical bill. So, he turns to crime in order to survive and look after his mother. He's caught. He's shown little mercy, and when he returns home he's forever branded as a criminal. A thief. An undesirable. He joins the army to support his dying mother, and to erase the criminal check mark from his history. Instead, he is erased. Regret feels the rain draw the Flux to the surface, hardening it into an exoskeleton, a shield to keep out the pain. Tears are in his eyes, the Dead Soldiers rise in concord.<br /> <br /> The Dead Thief: (It wAs aLL A JoKE, a SIck FUcKinG joKE...)<br /> <br /> Further away still yet dangerously nearby Regret sees a man who always wanted to be an astronaught. In the end he never got his wish, but he settle for second best as a theoretical physicist. Compared to the others this man had a truly good life filled with friendship, companionship, and love. Yet it all turned to ash because his father could never accept that his son was a homosexual. He went to war to redeem a part of himself that was a natural to him as breathing, and lost his life because of it. Because he wanted the one who created him to be proud. To be accepted as humethean...no, as human. Regret felt a rejection from the different parts that make up his being as Flux pools underneath the skin and changes his appearance until anyone looking at him could see straight through him. The Dead Soldiers rebelled against the inhuman thing that wore them like cheap clothing, they wanted to live again. Every fiber of their being wanted to breah again and be whole again.<br /> <br /> The Dead Scientist: (i aM NoT tAINteD! I am A HuMAn BeINg! I dESerVE tO eXIsT!)<br /> <br /> Regret tries to stand but the wind is so strong, and his body has never felt less his own than now. He looks down at himself and sees each individual Flux tainted part as the bullet wound that it is, cold and making him less than he was before. It was aweful, and yet...exhilarating. Somewhere deep down inside Regret could finally start to see where he began and the Dead Soldier's ended. But he shook off these notions as he remembered what he had witnessed, the part of the Dead Soldier's past that could never be expressed through sensation alone, and exerted his titanic strength to stand despite his malformed body. He felt sorrow for them, they felt sorrow for the choices not made and the people they would never see again. That's what held him together. <br /> <br /> Desperately, Regret called out to the storm. To his friends locked in combat, to the process that shapes the very fabric of the world.<br /> <br /> Regret: &quot;Why!?! Why does it have to be this way?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Firestorm rages on, like an earthquake. Like a protest rally against a corrupt system. Like a child being born. Like fire being exposed to oxygen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":"Polish 02-27-2017, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T15:21:15-08:00","id":1055827,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama LTD)<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Dread Powers: Camouflage 3<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 9/13 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5</b></div><br /> Scout stood, slack jawed as the firestorm hit. He'd felt it building. He'd always wanted to see one. Just... not necessarily this close. All thought of the fighting friends was washed away with the pouring fire.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Marvelous... fascinating...</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> He stumbled back from the Firestorm as best as he could, trying to keep his eyes everywhere at once, see every change. The raw fuel of creation, so visceral and powerful. And painful, he noted as something slammed into, knocking him silly. Oh that hurt. Yes. study. But also... don't stand inside the firestorm.<br /> <br /> The voice... yes it called to him. Witness! He would witness this. He would witness it and write soooo many notes.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/490725\" target=\"_blank\">http://orokos.com/roll/490725</a> Chance die and fail with a 1. Even if it wasn't a dramatic I'd totally take one though :P. Once he's more safe, he'll be more apt to get into Introspective again. Which begs the question... how easy is the firestorm to escape from? </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T05:18:34-08:00","id":1056064,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Disconnected, Guilty<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (Exemplary Athleticism), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: //OOOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 7/11 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Titan prepared to defend himself further against Earth, when suddenly the cosmos exploded.<br /> Pure creation, chaotic, unbound, <i>destructive</i>, raged all around him. A <span style=\"color:#000080\">Firestorm.</span><br /> He had heard a lot about them, but he had never even thought he'd be close to one someday.<br /> If you heard other Titans talk, this was among the strongest forges there are.<br /> Under different circumstances, he would have relished the chance to survive this, to prove his sturdiness.<br /> But as Mark 5 looked around, the red on the ground became lumiscent, giving off a faint glow. A grotesque painting, trailing all the way to him, the centerpiece of it. His handiwork. His &quot;message&quot;.<br /> His fault. All of this - the dead, the fight, even the Firestorm - was the consequence of him losing control. He felt like someone had slashed deep gashes across his chest, but that someone was sitting inside his body, chewing, gnawing, festering. Guilt. Regret.<br /> He had ended many lives. What he did was Evil. He had no excuse, and even looking back, he couldn't pinpoint the moment control slipped out of his grasp.<br /> Was that how humans ended up Evil? With good intentions, and good actions, and then slowly becoming something else without really noticing what was happening to them?<br /> Despite the pain and sorrow, the Tammuz felt a sense of elevation, of finally having understood something essential, of being able to relate.<br /> He has learned a lesson, one that threatened to leave his grasp at all times. <div align=\"center\">Sometimes, even when doing your best, with good intentions, you make a mistake. It can cause great pain, because some mistakes cannot be undone. <u>You are responsible for that.</u></div> <br /> <br /> He looked at Earth, and felt another pang of regret. &quot;<span style=\"color:#000080\">I do not want to fight you. Don't force me to.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The empty calm he felt was in contrast to the raging storm, and despite everything, Mark 5 felt the need to persevere through the storm, show that this did not dominate him, that he was unbroken, that Iron would never bend - not even to the forces of the Divine Fire itself. Channeling his own Pyros, the Titan set about evading the debris, the faint glow of SURVIVOR visible underneath his black shirt.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=27ba6055\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes on avoiding debris.</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> Stones, the gun, cloth, pieces of wood - none of it was too much of a challenge to the Traceur as he jumped, changed directions, sidestepped, evaded the flying pieces around him.<br /> <br /> However, where the physical effects of the Firestorm were unable to touch the Titan, it's metaphysical power proved insurmountable - he felt himself changing, felt Flux and its seductive force, and suddenly his flesh twisted beyond his will, beyond his control. Muscles twitched, grew in size, in density, and he started to sweat a sickly yellowish-blue liquid on his hands.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=69a27b26\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes on Controling the Mutation.... lets go ahead an make that a dramatic failure!</a><br /> Getting 2 dots worth of Briareus' Prowess (Stamina) and 1 dot of Paralyze.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 02-28-2017, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T00:23:28-08:00","id":1056516,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Disconnected, Irritable, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Disquieted (North End: Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (3), Weaponize (0), Redirect (1)<br /> Health: BBBBBBOOOOoooo | Willpower: 6/5 | Pyros: 8/12 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> She raised her fists in anger, only to get brutally double-dunked on by Mark and Adonis. <u><i>Adonis!</i></u> She hit the ground, shirt torn and bloody, coughing up black bile as her breath was stolen. Charged up and walking tall and immediately knocked on her ass by superior firepower. Happy memories.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Heartsblood used to plant her craggy mitt on Earth Crisis' unscarred face, holding the runt in place while she spat and scratched and swung her fists over and over and couldn't even reach her genitor's leather apron. It's never &quot;play fighting&quot; with a Titan like her, it's 100% Iron on Iron until you become as strong as they are or shatter. But she just wasn't built strong enough. She used to think the lesson was &quot;quickness beats brute force,&quot; but there was no lesson. She wasn't quick, either, and Titans are quicker anyway. Her genitor would let her speak freely and ask questions for every time she could land a hit, but she never landed hits, so she couldn't ask. She would run off toward Phoenix or Sedona for a couple days, hitchhike, talk to humans at the bus station like she wanted to, but Heartsblood never taught her how to talk to humans right, and so her cursed creator always had to drag her back from trouble. She just wasn't <i>good </i>at anything, and Heartsblood made sure she knew that she was <i>supposed </i>to be good at fighting, good enough to pose a challenge and let her continue the Pilgrimage. Kick, stomp, arm lock, hurl into the briar patch, over and over and over, with no hope of getting better. <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b><i>You're not even trying. Is it because you know you're already a failure?</i></b></span><br /> <br /> That was Heartsblood's big thing. Her creation didn't just miss the mark sometimes: she was fundamentally flawed, came out of the ground wrong. A human might have been able to pour it all out on the therapy couch. <i><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">I feel like my mom really messed me up.</span> </i>For the Created like Earth Crisis, there was just Torment.<br /> <br /> Some spring night in 2013, Heartsblood put her to work digging holes in the desert. They had to be the perfect size, not like the one Earth Crisis came out of. Even EC knew that HB wanted to build a replacement. It was tense. As she worked, the Titan said something about a vision from an angel in Sedona (she didn't get vivid dreams like her progeny), and EC got the idea that HB had decided to kill her to fulfill a Milestone. The holes must be graves, and her creator was just waiting for the perfect one to bury her in for good. Heartsblood berated her for letting sand fill in the hole again, and Earth Crisis suddenly realized that she could turn her failure state into a weapon. She wasn't a failed Titan, but the perfect Fury with plenty of charge built up. Her hands crackled with lightning as she let the shovel drop into the grave. Once a Martyr, now a Savage. Now the creation got to talk, and the creator had to listen. She was going to make her regret the day that she was born.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> In the bloodstained alley, knocked down on the asphalt, Earth's claw-hand conjured up a charge. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I'm right. I <i>know</i> I'm right. He's not leaving unpunished!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Hard to say whether her Pyros was the spark that lit the match. Maybe Scout would know, or maybe only the angels. But once everyone said their piece, the storm opened up like a beautiful flower. The quake of an oncoming Firestorm was familiar. Like an old friend who knew her name and all her secrets.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">1 Pyros to charge Arc.<br /> <br /> Avoiding wind damage, chance die: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/491301\" target=\"_blank\">fail</a>. 3 bashing.<br /> <br /> Trying to stand up and recover from Knocked Down as my action for the turn. 2 Pyros for Transhuman Potential on Dexterity,and 1 Willpower. Dexterity 3+Athletics 3+Willpower 3-Environment 7. 2 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/491302\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>.<br /> <br /> Let's say Beastly Mutation 3 to glom all her stuff into one power. How about +3 to attack and grappling rolls, and Brawl attacks do lethal damage? Stamina+2 to control it: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/491309\" target=\"_blank\">fail</a>. Weirdly happy to fail that roll! Earth ain't like that no more.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> She dug her claw into the asphalt, pulling herself to her feet as her lips flapped like a dog on the highway. Just having her eyes open stung, but she saw changes through the torrent. Her hearts (plural, her organs were dividing) beat faster. The corruption was spreading up her right arm. A deep gash ripped open along her belly and the leftover flesh and ribs congealed into a third arm on the left side. The phantom nerve endings, those were old friends trying to come back, too. Adonis puked acid, Regret grew claws for fingers, bricks and body parts shredded her bubbling flesh. Earth's eyes were wide open and she was sobbing and screaming herself hoarse. She couldn't hear herself think over the apocalyptic winds, but maybe the small, still voice in the center heard her begging: <b><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;no no no NO GOD PLEASE NO! NOT AGAIN! PLEASE GOD NOT LIKE THIS! I'VE BEEN TRYING SO HARD PLEASE DON'T SEND ME BACK I BEG YOU, (you are the principle, you are the creator, everything is in your hands and i can't change it,) BUT PLEASE DON'T MAKE ME BE THIS THING AGAIN--&quot;</span></b><br /> <br /> Earth, bent double and raging against her mutation, looked more like a crab than a person. Her whole right arm was an oversized crustacean claw ending in a fleshy armored pincer, bristling with bony quills from her bicep to her back. Two left arms sprouting from her shoulder, only one of them with her tattooed Inscription, the lower arm twitching and writhing loosely. She was taller and stronger on thick tree-trunk legs of corded muscle and bone. Her hair was wild and randomly pierced by thorns. And there was an awful wide gash like her belly had been slashed open, only it had a wet slobbering tongue, and <i>teeth.</i><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> The howling wind and rain is so loud that she can't hear or see anything real right now. The storm just drowns everything out into undifferentiated gray chaos. Same way that the &quot;Refinement&quot; of Flux dissolves distinctions between right and wrong, self and other, purpose and nihilism, human and monster. And now she's going to dissolve back into that worthless gray, worse than Heartsblood could have ever imagined.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;this is all my fault. i'm the one to blame.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The sound of wings, beating gracefully, rises above the shouting and the storm noise.<span style=\"color:#DAA520\"> &quot;I used to catch you flying with this claw and drag you back down to Earth. Took everything I had to keep us chained together, all my strength. Why didn't I just let you go?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The wind howls. Someone familiar is laughing.<span style=\"color:#DAA520\"> &quot;I was like this for so long. This is how you saw me. And you knew me better than anyone.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> There's something dark and blissfully solid amidst the endless gray storm. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;If you were the one doing this, it would be okay.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Earth stumbles through the maelstrom. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Where are you? Are you still alive?&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 03-09-2017, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T13:39:56-08:00","id":1057748,"title":"","content":"<b>The Throng</b><br /> <br /> <b>Adonis</b> can't hear anything above the wind and rain, the screaming force of nature that hurls debris about like a toddler going through a particularly vicious tantrum throwing their toys at the wall. He spits blood from his mouth and watches as it transmutes, changes into an unnatural green colour as Flux courses through his humours, and it begins to etch into the pavement. He can feel it, building up in his throat like so much spit and phlegm, like he's heard humans talking about when they have a cold. He needs to spit it up or it will consume him whole. Splinters of bone dig at his skin and go flying away as the Muse fights to his hands and knees, but he is barely aware of that. There is just the shuddering, ecstatic vileness that needs to boil out of his throat.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Adonis takes three points of Bashing damage, and can make another Dexterity + Athletics - 7 roll this turn to resist further damage. He also needs to make a Dexterity + Athletics roll to expel the Flux-based Breath Attack, or he'll suffer the damage himself.</i><br /> <br /> The wind lashes out, hurling <b>Scout</b> clear off of his feet and into a wall, cracking his head against stucco and brickwork. He can feel the rain burning against his skin, the Flux worming its way under his flesh, as his skin ripples and textures itself based off of ceramic and stone instead of human flesh. Was this what it was like being a Golem? Being totally in contact with the earth at all times? It was a strange feeling. The wind seems to pin him against the wall as the Firestorm howls its fury, and in the heart of the storm he can see a being curling in on itself, a creature with four legs, four arms, and two torsos seemingly melded at the spine. The <i>rebis</i> weeps piteously, arms reaching around and behind to try and offer comfort to a conjoined sibling it cannot see. The storm beats at it, with wind, with rain, with debris, with seething Flux rain that corrupts and melts the flesh (Are those tentacles starting to rise from the flesh and wave in the wind? Are those teeth starting to grow from the skin, tearing into the hands that seek out the comforting touch of another blindly?) There is <i>meaning </i>here, if the Osirian can find it.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Scout takes three points of Bashing damage, and can make another Dexterity + Athletics - 7 roll this turn to resist more damage. Scout takes a Beat from the Dramatic Failure. Scout can also make a Wits + Occult roll to recall the alchemical symbolism of the rebis, and things he has recalled. You can't escape the Firestorm, it's attacking Pyros-based stuff in the immediate area, so you'll just have to take it for now. However, this is also an Elpis Vision for Scout- what does he do next? How does he interact with the rebis? I'll answer a successful roll in the OOC to leave this thread for you to proceed with the Elpis Vision.</i><br /> <br /> A particularly heavy chunk of loose masonry torn free of a nearby building by the Firestorm strikes <b>Regret</b> and staggers the Wretched Originist. He can <i>see </i>the Dead Soldiers, warped by the storm, Flux eating at them, and at him by extension. The Dead Artist tears at himself with hooked talons of jagged bone as the flesh melts away from his hands, howling wordlessly at the unjust creditor that was the universe, while the Dead Thief snarls his rage to the uncaring storm, standing proud in the chitinous plates. The Dead Scientist stood, imploring the world to see him even as flesh and bone seemed to fade into the wind and the rain, leaving him a wraith barely visible in the torrential downpour. They suffered, they died, and to what end? For what purpose, for what design? Where does all the suffering, all the pain, lead in the end? Why does Regret need to carry <i>their </i>pain with him? There is a twisting column of white flame dancing in the rain, swirling on the breeze, as razor-thin lashes of fire spin off of its core and score the earth, tear at the Dead Soldiers. Molten lead falls like tears where it flows. Three little coals of hot black flame have established themselves on one end of the fiery column, flickering about like eyes, floating above the surface like a crown of dark stars. It makes its way towards Regret, tendrils drifting like the tentacles of a jellyfish along the pavement, leaving a trail of bubbling asphalt. The Dead Soldiers cringe in its passing as it looms, snake-like, over Regret, tendrils spread, hovering close enough to his skin to burn hair and set stitches smoking. The pain is nothing compared to his body trying to rip itself apart, but it is a distraction. It obstructs the Dead Soldiers from view.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Regret takes two points of Bashing damage, as the point of Armour granted by the Dread Power protects him. You can make another Dexterity + Athletics - 7 roll to resist further damage. Seeing as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> is going to be unavailable for a little while, I'll just leave this here for them. They can come back and assess the Elpis Vision later.</i><br /> <br /> The Titan <b>Mark 5 </b>dances through the storm, standing upright in the race of wind and torrential rain, standing defiant even in the face of a Firestorm. He stands with defiance even as Flux soaks into his flesh and increases the density of his muscles, dragging him closer to the earth, holding him back, but the word <b>SURVIVOR </b>blazes through his shirt, even as the Flux starts to turn on him, burning in his veins, he stands triumphant. As the storm lashes out he can see the corpses thrown to and fro, until the storm starts to... congeal them. Ruined corpses are torn to pieces by hurricane winds, and sewn together by blood and flame and molten asphalt into a hulking monstrosity of ten arms and five heads that float above the shoulders, charred skulls blazing with flame and rotating slowly in a ring, each of the ten arms holding a weapon made from destroyed masonry and charred leg bones with a flowing column of pavement and flame for a lower body. It looks at the Titan expectantly, and then it turns towards towards where he last saw Earth, flowing slowly towards her, weapons raised in judgement.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Mark 5 avoids the damage from the Firestorm, but takes a point of Bashing damage from the Flux-based poison backfiring. Mark 5 takes a Beat from a Dramatic Failure, and takes three Vitriol Beats from the Milestone.</i><br /> <br /> Meanwhile, a transformed <b>Earth</b> feels familiar perversions digging their way into, and out of, her flesh, Flux following well-used channels that remember the almost reflexive transformation from days gone by. Earth-Dies-Screaming, promise or prophecy? (Neither. Please, Flame Immortal, be neither.) She becomes a twisted goddess, a rakshasa, mighty and dreadfully hideous to behold. Beautiful, once, to Dead Girl, who had tangled tongues with the second mouth for the pleasure of the experience, for the pure Flux and black bile in the saliva. There are beating wings in the dark, and white feathers drifting through the storm, brushing Earth's face like the fingers of a forgotten lover, before the feathers become white butterflies, and the shining broad-shouldered figure of white flame with the black hand (My Azoth) waits silently for Earth, arms spread wide, blocking her path. She can see the dark and blissfully solid figure waiting somewhere ahead in the storm, in the heart of it, laughing quietly, delightedly, without judgement. Her Azoth reaches out with one flaming hand and latches on to a chain of blood and black bile that Earth had somehow ignored, tied to her left arm where the Brand used to be, and to her heart. It tugs, hard, driving Earth to her knees with the wrenching pain of detachment, of the gaping holes of something leaving and distant. She can hear the sibilant, seductive whisper of Dead Girl in her ear, and she can feel the ache, the vise-like touch of her hand caressing her heart, arm jamming up through her ruined torso. Earth can feel the citric acid of Vitriol bubbling up in the back of her throat, the taste of bile on her tongue. The Azoth waits expectantly for Earth to make a decision, make a choice, as thorny plants and flaming flowers grow up through the pavement. Where is the Breaker- he can't escape punishment! But is he <i>more </i>deserving of punishment than <i>she </i>is? <br /> <br /> Earth can hear something at the edge of the Firestorm, drifting above the wind. A small, still voice says, <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>see the fires that you have lit</i></span><br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Earth can roll again to resist the Bashing damage from the flying debris. How does what Earth feels about Dead Girl (and herself) influence how she wants to punish Mark 5? How does it influence how she feels about being a Vigilante? What does she see when she looks behind herself to see the humans that are looking upon the scene, the ones who rose to her defence against the Disquieted drunk?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T13:45:22-08:00","id":1058132,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: BBBOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 9/10<br /> Beats: 1/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b><br /> <br /> </div> The wounds go unheeded by Adonis. The fascination he felt at the changes Flux was forging in his body turns to fear. <i><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">I can't control it... </span></i>He can feel the awful green acid building up in his throat, his esophagus, his stomach. He must expel it. It's a compulsion, a necessity, an urge. He must share this perversion with the world, like some bizarre exhibitionist. He tries to stagger to his feet and avoid the debris that the Firestorm has whipped up. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis will attempt to avoid damage from the storm again. Dexterity 2 + Athletics 2 - 7 = chance dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/492282\" target=\"_blank\">nothing again, crap</a>. He takes another 3 points of bashing, which will be updated next post.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But the glass and wood and refuse continue to pummel him. He can't stand against this much longer. He tries to expel the entropic sludge boiling in him, trying to induce himself to vomit again, desperately. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis will try to force himself to vomit to expel the acid. Dexterity 2 + Athletics 2 + Willpower 3 = 7 dice, -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/492283\" target=\"_blank\">that'll do</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He succeeds, and the acid goes flying, and he feels a twisted satisfaction and completion. <br /> <br /> He turns and looks at the others, taking in the chaos. He's not going to last much longer in this Firestorm- and he would rather not waste his ability to return to life on this bullshit. All of them are transfixed by something. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>Elpis vision? </i></span>Scout looks fascinated, just as he always does by something new. Regret looks near catatonic. Mark 5 seems to be continuing to grow, the additional mass no longer muscle but tumorous. But his heart skips a beat when he sees Earth. No, not Earth. Earth-Dies-Screaming come again to terrorize the world. He can't hear what she's saying, but she's crying, screaming. The meaning is clear: she doesn't want this again. He stands for a moment, uncertain of what to do, but then he rushes forward and grabs her again- not to restrain or strike, but to simply hold. He looks up into that awful face, and tries to pour countless feelings into his expression. <i><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">I get it now. The pain, the anger, the bitterness. This is what you've been fighting against. This is what you were, what you fear. But you've come so far from this. I'm so proud of you. This isn't forever, Earth. Come back to us. Please. I'm not running. Not without you.</span></i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T14:25:19-08:00","id":1058146,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama LTD)<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Dread Powers: Camouflage 3<br /> Health: BBBBBB | Willpower: 3/6 | Pyros: 5/13 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5</b></div><br /> Scout stared at his hands as he watched them change- texture, color, all new. It reminded him of the octopus he'd seen in an aquarium one time. The little man was easy to overlook in the best of times- now he was nigh impossible unless you actively looked for him. Then the rebis came into being before him. Torn by the firestorm he wished to study. It would tear itself apart- be lost forever. Scout could not allow this. But... he also couldn't do anything. The wind and destruction pinned him. He was helpless- no worse. His inaction earlier and jotting down notes, that had been the flaw. It had torn their would be throng apart. Had he acted sooner, perhaps, they would have had time to stop Mark 5 from killing those people.<br /> <br /> Scout had heard words once- for evil to succeed it requires only that good men do nothing. Had he moved sooner, focused on the right details, this would never have come to pass. The rebis writhed before him, and he watched it for a moment as it tore at itself. Would he do nothing again, and watch? He looked to the rebis as it destroyed itself. Azoth and Elpis together as one, but forever tearing at one another. The perfect alchemy, condemned by flux, by... by...<br /> <br /> Of course. Inspiration struck his mind harder than the he had struck the bricks. His body was helpless, but his Azoth was not. His divine fire was powerful, despite his size, and he often looked inward for answers. His fire could calm torment- drive out flux from his fellow prometheans. He had just done it after all. Perhaps he could calm the world- drive the Flux from this Holy Storm. If he could find the frequency.<br /> <br /> The tiny man rose to his knees and screamed wordlessly to the winds throwing his straight out arms, and let his Azoth pour forth, trying to find the right azothic frequency as quickly as he could. It might kill him- but so might the firestorm. He had to focus, and feel the firestorm's frequency- it was azothic in nature, so it had to have a frequency.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">We'll just take the damage this time instead of trying to avoid it, and he's not going to collect enough thought to try controlling the camouflage- he's focused on his new task. Once again burn pyros on Inhuman Potential for Manipulation. Then more pyros to Activate Sublimation by Fire against the Firestorm. And this feels super important to Scout, so lets throw more willpower at it.<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/492297\" target=\"_blank\">http://orokos.com/roll/492297</a>Sublimation by Firestorm<br /> EXCEPTIONAL SUCCESS!</div></div> </div> </div>[/QUOTE]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T14:55:20-08:00","id":1058162,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Disconnected, Guilty<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (Exemplary Athleticism), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: ///OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 3/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> For a short moment, Mark 5 was overcome with fear when the flux-based poison hurt him.<br /> This was his body, and it <i>hurt him</i>. It refused to <i>obey</i>. Stubborness prevailed. This was <b>his </b>body. It would do as he pleased, for he forged, shaped it into what it is now!<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=ed8c1e36\" target=\"_blank\">2 sux on Controling Mutation</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> The flow of poison stopped. His body, tainted by Flux, belonged to him again- and it moved with more resilience than he remembered.<br /> <br /> Then, the Monstrosity formed. His malfeasance took form, and it was a Terror to behold: the heads of the IP he so easily stomped, so carelessly killed, stood atop a being that seemed made to kill, to destroy.<br /> <br /> <br /> His Punishment had come.<br /> <br /> <br /> However, it didn't go for him. It turned, and approached... Earth?<br /> Was it going to punish him through her? Was it trying to <i>protect </i>him from her?<br /> Whatever she might have done wrong in the past, he could understand her actions, he even appreciated them.<br /> Mark 5 now knew there was someone that will stop him should he ever go off the deep end.<br /> <br /> He screamed at it &quot;<span style=\"color:#000080\"><b>NO! </b>LEAVE HER BE! <b>SHE </b>IS <b>NOT </b>GUILTY!&quot; </span>as he tried to outrun it, place himself between it and her. He would take the hits, if necessary, if that meant she stayed safe.<br /> Before, the Firestorm was a challenge, an inconvienence...<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=e074594f\" target=\"_blank\">2 Sux on avoiding debris</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> ... but now, his mind was less focused, and he paid slightly less attention to it, more intent on getting between that <i>Thing </i>and Earth.<br /> <br /> <br /> He had to protect her. It was his mission, was it not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 03-04-2017, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T19:24:37-08:00","id":1058740,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Disconnected, Irritable, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Disquieted (North End: Stage 1)<br /> [Extreme Environment 4, Heavy Winds 3, Heavy Rain]<br /> Alembics: Arc (1), Imperatus (3), Weaponize (0), Redirect (1)<br /> Health: BBBBBBBBBOoooo | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 5/12 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> Rip and tear, rip and tear. Even flesh like this can't stand up to a Firestorm.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Avoiding damage, Dex+Ath-7, chance die: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/492095\" target=\"_blank\">fail</a>. 3 more bashing. Really glad Created don't have wound penalties right now.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The chain pulls her to the pavement, gutted. Earth thought the old Brand was gone and forgotten, but she also thought her old twisted form was gone. The shape was still coiled up inside her, apparently, waiting to emerge with the right reagent. Maybe there's another inscription encoded in the black hand burned into Her Azoth. A flux inscription? Or maybe everyone is built to devolve and degrade in one specific way, and the mutations of the others are just a preview of coming attractions if her bad example leads them off the Pilgrimage.<br /> <br /> Humans are watching. They're looking through the burning sunflower stalks. Of course they would see her like this. A white feather (or hurricane-blown newspaper?) brushes her face, and she thinks in that soft voice: <i>you can't lie to them. this is you. this is what the drunk saw. what they're really afraid of. you tricked them, babe. they protected you from him because they thought he was this. you.</i><br /> <br /> The beautiful Galateid, marred by Flux scars, embraced her. Looking a little more like Adonis than usual. She shifted her great claw away, tried to explain herself to the Muse over the chaotic howling of the storm: &quot;I liked taking everything out on you. I had to. I hated you! But we had the same fight, over and over and over, and nothing changed.&quot;<br /> <br /> Torment is real, and it's always going to be there, but it needs direction. It's so <i>easy </i>to lash out at Dead Girl, but just like in the vision at the cathedral, she can lash out at those weeds all day and never get anywhere. They just keep coming back, same as before. Their roots grow together until they're perfectly evolved to hurt each other in the worst ways, but never break the chain for good. When Torment is directed properly, on the other hand, it can actually <i>end.</i><br /> <br /> When she makes a choice to aim her Torment at the right targets, by following a Code, she can rise above the chaos. She can decide when the Fury comes and when it goes away. She doesn't need to struggle against a chain that never breaks. Sometimes that means channeling her Torment through the Code, even if her conscious mind doesn't want it. Especially then. That's purpose.<br /> <br /> Her bellymouth growls and hungers, snapping at Adonis of its own volition. She sees him clearly for a second. Not Dead Girl, Adonis. And because it's Adonis, she looks him in the eye and shoves him back. It's easier to tell who the real target is this way.<br /> <br /> She reached out her least-corrupted hand, aimed at where she thought Mark 5 might be, and let the lightning fly. One good hit, that's all she needed. One good hit.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Arc on Mark! Dexterity+Athletics+Azoth-7, +3 Willpower, +3 Pyros for Transhuman Potential. 6 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/492584\" target=\"_blank\">3 success</a>. And it's 1 lethal damage base.<br /> <br /> I dunno if the Firestorm affects this, but Earth's burned enough Pyros this scene to trigger a Wasteland.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 03-09-2017, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T14:49:25-08:00","id":1060289,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: BBBOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 9/10<br /> Beats: 1/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b><br /> <br /> </div> The embrace was not pleasant, if only because the horrible second mouth that had formed from Earth's navel to sternum was trying to lick and bite him. But he held on in discomfort. Earth-Dies-Screaming's eyes seemed distant- there was recognition, but she was not looking at him like Earth looked at Adonis. With a shiver, Adonis recalled the stories of the Centimanus Muse Earth-Dies-Screaming had traveled with: a winged horror named Dead Girl, as beautiful and terrible as a black mamba, as cruel and cunning as Earth-Dies-Screaming had been savage and feral. Did Earth now see in him some echo of Dead Girl? He realized that she was what he would turn into if he turned himself over to Flux: cruel like Sharon, but worse, because Sharon had been insane. Whatever sick urges he indulged would be because he felt like it... <br /> <br /> Then, her expression changed, and there was true recognition. Earth-Dies-Screaming was no longer looking at her old friend, Earth was looking at Adonis. A strange look crossed her face- regret? Thankfulness?- before she pushed him away, and raised her hand to shoot lightning at Mark 5- who had his back turned to Earth, his arms outstretched as if to protect her from something. Adonis screamed in frustration and fear, the sound merging with the howl of the storm and covered by the crack and boom of Earth's lightning. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T17:52:31-08:00","id":1060353,"title":"","content":"<b>The Throng</b><br /> <br /> The Firestorm raged, and the manifestation of <b>Mark 5's</b> brutality, a blood-spattered god of flame, blood, and bone, lurched towards Earth. With little more than sheer will, the Titan forced the tumorous expansion of his flesh to obey him, to let him act. He is lumbering compared to the lithe agility he had before, but a Titan he remains, and his body is his to command. He is <b>IRON</b>, iron in flesh, and soon iron in will, he is his own to command, and thus his actions were his own to suffer for. The flaming horror swelled as Mark 5 blocked its path, arms spread wide, Flux-wracked body obeying the Titan by force of will, gazing with apparent as <b>Adonis</b> gaped at the Titan's prowess. He was untouched by the Firestorm, by sheer force of will, standing defiant in the heart of the stormwall, in the worst of the fury. All the Muse could see was the Titan standing, arms outstretched overhead like an invocation, facing <i>into </i>the wind, as if defying it to hurt him. He can see the Titan vaguely mouthing words, and while he cannot hear, the set of Mark 5's face is one of perfect resolution. The white hot flames stoked hotter, the rain sublimating into steam with an outraged hiss as it neared the heat of its wrath. Heads burned away for a wheel of burning eyes, dismembered arms and legs torched into limbs of molten steel and spears of lightning. It tore free of the black sludge of molten pavement, and rose up on a funnel cloud of swirling flame. The flaming horror thrust holy spears with a battle cry of screaming winds and shrieking steam that shattered sound at the Titan... as <b>Earth's </b>lightning bolt struck him in the back.<br /> <br /> Earth's Azoth steps closer to her, and with the black hand gives her the end of Dead Girl's chain and closes her hand over it. It lays its white hand on her shoulder, and presses its forehead to hers.<br /> <br /> Pinned against a wall by the blind wrath of the Firestorm, <b>Scout</b> reaches out with a Distillation, an attempt to speak with the ineffable. He makes contact with something in the heart of the storm, in the space between wind and rain, beneath the miasma of Flux. The <i>rebis </i>raises its head in surprise and <i>looks</i> at the slight Originist, and he gets the slightest suggestion of something impossibly large tearing at itself, engaging in dreadful acts of self-arm, bleeding Divine Fire and humours in a way to purge its Torment, and he can hear a pained scream and the choking, breathless weeping of a child in complete despair in the space between the wind. There's a bright flash of lightning and a sound like the world splitting in two.<br /> <br /> The Firestorm explodes.<br /> <br /> A wave of Azoth burns through rain and wind and Flux, leaving the block silent, deafened by blind fury and pain. In the wake of the storm, the Pilgrims feel drained, exhausted, as the Pyros in their flesh burns away in a sudden void, Divine Fire rushing to fill a vacuum left by the Firestorm. But there is a flush of humours rushing beneath their skin, the Azoth that burns in their hearts working overtime, bodies and spirits (dare we say souls?) tempered in a crucible. The Created, and everyone relatively nearby, are utterly soaked with rain, and now with stranger things. As the rain flows down their skin, Flux taint melts away. Earth-Dies-Screaming melts away, leaving Earth-Lives-Again cleansed by water and fire. The blood has been scourged from Mark 5's clothes, the bodies torn beyond all recognition by the freak storm (an Act of God, some would say), flesh fluttering in the dying breeze like flags, bones splintered and shattered into a mosaic of biological hailstones. There's a piece of scalp here, what might be a finger there, but they are beyond recognition, and the human crowd doesn't seem to know how to react. They are huddling closer together, still grumbling at the drunk slumped gobsmacked on the sidewalk, panic and confusion written across their faces along with something a little stronger, denial. Earth's coat hides the flickering, flaming abscesses of her alchemy, though the coat has started to steam. Somehow, a police officer has arrived in the meantime, the young woman's curly hair pulled back into a rough bun, baggy blue cadet uniform off-set by her dark complexion. She goes to pull Earth to her feet, and something wondrous happens. Her Azoth doesn't flare and burn. It doesn't reach out to scorch her soul.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, ma'am, are you alright? Someone said a transformer blew and a water main broke after you went after some guy hassling you and your friends here.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Alright, so, everyone lives! Some bookkeeping to handle now.<br /> <br /> - Firstly, <b>Mark 5</b> takes 4L damage from the lightning blast. Only <b>Earth</b> and <b>Adonis</b> know the truth of what happened. <b>Mark 5 </b>gains a Beat from the <b>Tenacious Condition</b> due to <b>Adonis</b> observing.<br /> <br /> - <b>Scout </b>takes a Beat from having his Health boxes filled with Bashing Damage, and gains the <b>Inspired (Azoth) Condition</b> from the Exceptional Success on Sublimation by Fire.<br /> <br /> - <b>Earth</b> gains a Vitriol Experience from completing the Vigilante Role. How does the Vigilante, who just obeyed her Code over her personal attachments and struck out at a friend, react to encountering an empowered officer of the law? And how does she react to the strangeness of not risking Disquiet?<br /> <br /> - The Firestorm has effects that apply to <b>everyone.</b> They are as follows.<br /> <br /> <b>+ Everyone</b> loses six points of Pyros<br /> <b>+ Everyone</b> gains a Vitriol Experience<br /> <b>+ Everyone</b> gains Three Dots of Physical Merits</i><br /> <i><b>+ Everyone</b> loses their Pandoran Dread Powers</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T23:36:45-08:00","id":1060429,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Darkstorm, Completely Normal Vigilante<br /> Health: BBBBBBBBBBbboo | Willpower: 4/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;uh-&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She takes the officer's hand and gets up. The stocky woman in the steaming coat is utterly bewildered, like she just fell out of a plane. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;We're...alive?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Everything is way too quiet and calm and still, inside and out. This has to be a trick. She'll prove it by Disquieting this human. She pulls her hand back and scowls.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;We're alive. Thanks for nothing. Where are cops when you actually need 'em? We could've been killed!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">golly, that's a lot of stuff. currently at 1 Experience, 3 Vitriol Experiences.<br /> <br /> definitely staying in Vigilante for a while.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 03-21-2017, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T00:16:25-08:00","id":1060438,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Disconnected, Guilty<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (Exemplary Athleticism), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: XXXX///OOOOOO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 0/11 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 3/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 2</b></div> <br /> <br /> The flaming horror attacked from the front, but it actually struck the Titan in the back. How fitting for a creature of Flux to decieve. Then, suddenly, the world exploded.<br /> <br /> When Mark 5 regained his orientation, he felt drained and hurting in every sense of the word: physically, mentally, spiritually, alchemisticly.<br /> And yet, the moment he heard Earth complain - <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;We're alive. Thanks for nothing. Where are cops when you actually need 'em? We could've been killed!&quot;</span><br /> - he smiled and felt a small instance of joy. <br /> <br /> She was save. It did not get her.<br /> <br /> This... happening, changed a lot of things. He would have to think.<br /> Most of all, about how through all the pain and regret, he felt a strange sense of completion, of having reached something, of understanding more.<br /> <br /> Should he leave now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T07:14:34-08:00","id":1060502,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: BBBOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 3/10<br /> Beats: 1/5 I Vitriol Beats: 1/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b></div> <br /> <br /> The Firestorm ends. The awful sizzling in his stomach and the back of his throat fades. Adonis looks over at Scout, who has fallen to his knees, his arms outstretched. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>Wait, did he... stop it? </i></span>But before Adonis can say anything, he hears a voice in his head, calm and soft but loud at the same time. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><b>&quot;YOU ARE STRONGER THAN YOU KNOW, JUST AS STRONG AS THEY ARE. BUT YOUR STRENGTH IS DIFFERENT. YOU WILL REALIZE ITS SOURCE IN TIME.&quot; </b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The Firestorm was a crucible, and he was fired in it. He went into it made fully of gold, but the gold is receding, with some other metal that he does not yet know forming underneath. But he senses that, once he masters Aurum, it will show itself. But already he feels... firmer. More confident. A Refinement of strength. Cuprum? Ferrum? Stannum? Aes? </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">He sees Mark 5 shift uneasily. He looks like he's about to slink away, and Adonis reaches out a hand and grabs him by the arm, and then gives him a long hard look. </span><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;<i>Stay. </i>We've had enough trouble trying to find you once today.&quot;</span> His voice doesn't rise above a whisper, but it is firmer than it has ever been, especially towards either Named.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Earth seems bound and determined to make at least one person hate them today. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>Fuck, Earth. Do you always have to be at somebody's throat? </i></span>He walks over and all but butts Earth out of the way, placing himself between the policewoman and the Fury. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Yes, we're fine, officer. Don't mind her, she's always pissy and she's rattled from the storm.&quot; </span>He flashes the cadet his trademark grin.<br /> <br /> He's done flinching at the site of Earth's fist crackling with lightning. He doesn't act it, but his body isn't just for display. There are human men who would envy his physical prowess, and he's had to punch his way out of a couple tight spots before. It's time he started acting like it.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis will take three dots of the Brutal Force Style Merit. He's also going to try and sweet talk the police officer to go away.<br /> <br /> Manipulation 3 + Persuasion 3 = 6 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/494012\" target=\"_blank\">yowza, nothing</a>.<br /> <br /> Rolling to see if she suffers Disquiet. Azoth 2 = 2 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/494013\" target=\"_blank\">nothing</a>.<br /> <br /> So she's not leaving, but she's not freaking out, either. Might try to hit her with Lure on the next post.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T14:10:11-08:00","id":1060657,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama LTD), Inspired (Azoth)<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: BBBBBB | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 2/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b></div><br /> The explosion rocked Scout back against the wall, and he felt more than a little dazed from it. When he'd blinked the stars out of his vision, the world was as it should be once more. The firestorm was gone. He'd done it. The look on the Rebis' face... interesting. It had responded to his Azothic call. But... not in the way he'd expected or hoped. And that scream... strange. Was it the Rebis or something else? He'd have to think this vision and his last over. Learn from them. There were things there he just... wasn't getting yet. Perhaps Regret or Adonis could help him understand? Earth and Mark 5 didn't seem like they'd really understand it.<br /> <br /> The little Nepri pushed at the wreckage pinning him. When he found he couldn't get out, he cleared his throat. Scout had to note that felt oddly sore as he called for the others, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Uh... little help here? I seem to be stuck.</span>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T07:21:52-07:00","id":1061812,"title":"","content":"<b>The Throng</b><br /> <br /> The police cadet keeps a perfectly neutral face that still manages to convey, with little more than the twitch of a facial muscle, a massive eye roll. She puts up with <b>Earth's</b> irritable grumbling, and then, very calmly, speaks up. &quot;The call came in less than a minute ago, and we were only a few blocks away. Whatever happened, it happened incredibly quickly, so we could not have been here sooner unless we were already on the scene.&quot; This is just ordinary human irritability. Nothing is happening. Her Azoth isn't setting Disquiet smouldering. What does that even <i>mean</i>?<br /> <br /> When <b>Adonis</b> tries to charm his way past whatever social blunder Earth is currently wading into, he finds that a soaked, bruised, and blood-spattered person, no matter how good-looking they are under it all, just isn't that appealing. &quot;Storm? I was told it was a water main break and a blown transformer. That's what everyone over there saw,&quot; she gestures off-handedly towards the crowd &quot;unless you're saying otherwise.&quot; She narrows her eyes, almost leaning in to the Muse as if trying to see past water and the slowly welling purple bruises. &quot;You look familiar. Have we met before?&quot; She shakes her head, thinking it over, before looking to survey the group as a whole, and noticing <b>Scout </b>trapped under some small bits of masonry. The cadet jogs over and takes a look at the damage, a frown across her face. &quot;You doing alright sir? Can you wiggle your toes for me? I'm not supposed to move you, so we're going to wait for the paramedics. They'll be here in a minute.&quot;<br /> <br /> The cadet looks back at the rest of the throng &quot;Why don't you all take a seat? Paramedics and fire department will be here soon to check you out and get your friend out from under this debris.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: As a reminder, those of you who experienced an Elpis Vision can roll Wits + Azoth to interpret what you saw and ask a question (or two if you get an Exceptional Success)</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T12:55:16-07:00","id":1061928,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Disconnected, Guilty<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: XXXX///OOO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 0/11 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 3/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 2</b><br /> </div> <br /> <br /> The Titan was taken aback. Was Adonis always this determined, this... decisive? Mark 5 didn't think so. <i>&quot;He grew a pair!&quot;</i> went through his head. He heard people say that to indicate someone became tougher, braver. Though he still wasn't sure why courage came as a pair.<br /> He nodded. Bravery he could respect. &quot;<span style=\"color:#000080\">Right.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> He took a second to reflect on what he had seen. That hadn't been real, even though it had felt so real, right? After all, that thing actually <i>hurt </i>him.<br /> But he lacked something to make sense out of what he saw; maybe it was experience, maybe he was to confused, maybe being surrounded by people that watched them reminded him of being cast out all over again too much... the meaning of the Vision eluded him.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=ef744448\" target=\"_blank\">Shucks, failed the roll </a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;Why don't you all take a seat? Paramedics and fire department will be here soon to check you out and get your friend out from under this debris.&quot;<br /> The Titan rolled his eyes and went to get Scout out of the curious place he had gotten himself into.<br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000080\">No need to wait. Officer. You alright down there, yeah?&quot; </span><br /> He felt sore, his Alembic having run out, and he hurt... but there was physical labour to be done, and he was best suited for that. They might have to leave soon, after all, and they couldn't do that with Scout being stuck.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=44abab69\" target=\"_blank\">Strength + Stamina to lift Wreckage= 5 successes</a><br /> If I should've rolled Str+Ath, the result would be <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=e1816f6d\" target=\"_blank\">4 successes</a><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  Additional roll 03-13-2017, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T13:56:41-07:00","id":1061971,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama LTD), Inspired (Azoth)<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: BBBBBB | Willpower: 3/6 | Pyros: 2/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b></div><br /> Scout looked blankly at the police officer for a moment, working his jaw as it frying to find the right words. This human was... talking to him. Caring about what was going on with him. That as unusual, to say the least. And they were police. Hadn't High Winds warned him that the police couldn't always be trusted? He just... didn't know how to handle the woman treating him nicely. Thankfully, Mark 5 saved him from having to actually talk to her for very long.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Thank you, Mark,</span>&quot; the little Nepri said with a smile and a nod, before he glanced to the police officer and stood up dusting himself off. He tried to sound grateful, but he wound up with 'only slightly less monotone', &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Only bruised officer. Mostly in my pride at not being able to pick up rocks as easily as my guardian here. Unfortunately, we will be late for our meeting again if we do not get on the move.</span>&quot; There was a short pause and then another smile for the police cadet, then added in fluent french, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Thank you for for checking on me, though.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Once he was certain he could, he got out of Mark 5's way so he could put the rubble back down, and started walking with only a slight limp. They needed to get out of here, and an electrical source would be a good thing to work on finding. Once they were away from the cops, perhaps, he could see if anyone knew a good generator or something. Ohhh... they put a generator in Adonis's apartment. Or maybe on the roof or something. Chain it down and fire it up when they needed some juice. That would be brilliant!<br /> <br /> As he walked, he turned his mind back to the vision, and the rebis. The Look into stannum had made him realize that separatio would be coming soon, and the rebis... it was certainly an interesting beast. Perhaps if he could recreate a firestorm on his own, he could summon it in a more controlled environment. Force it's manifestation and then find a way to calm it- speak with it. Learn from it. That'd be brilliant.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/495788\" target=\"_blank\">1 wp spent, 1 sux</a> for understanding the vision. Scout would like to know about his next superlative or major milestone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I'm also going to play up Scout's Torment soon I think.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T16:09:09-07:00","id":1062044,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Disconnected, Irritable, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Disquieted (North End: Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: LLLLLBBBBB | Willpower: 4/5 | Pyros: 0/12 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Earth deflated. The human law-enforcer was unbothered. Even Adonis was unimpressed. Hell, he sounded <i>tough</i>. No wonder she'd mistaken him for...y'know...<br /> <br /> Wait, what exactly happened back there? She backed off from Adonis and the cadet, her ears burning, rubbing her forehead with a bent and bloody but non-monstrous hand. Mark 5, looking surprisingly healthy, was lifting Scout out of the rubble. Nothing monstrous here. Did she set him straight?<br /> <br /> Her manifest Azoth had given her both ends of the old chain. Trusted her. Was that supposed to be good, or bad? And why twist her flesh again? Was this a vision of the past, the present, the future? What was she supposed to do with this?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Wits+Azoth+Willpower: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/495866\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes</a>. Wish I had Inspired right now.<br /> <br /> Question: Which Role must I take on soon?</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 03-21-2017, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T14:03:57-07:00","id":1062471,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress, Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: BBBBBBO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 3/10<br /> Beats: 1/5 I Vitriol Beats: 1/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b><br /> </div> <br /> The police cadet's words send Adonis' stolen heart into overdrive. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>Paramedics. No no no. Shit. Shit shit shit. </i></span>Created could pass for human when they did not invoke the Divine Fire, but no amount of Divine Fire can fool a physical: they would see that Earth and Mark 5 bled black bile and not blood, and Scout, Regret, and himself would be seen for the stitched-together creations they were. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>She needs to let us leave, </i>now. </span><br /> <br /> It had been a long time since Adonis had used a Distillation on a human. There weren't a lot of situations that called for it. Few people could resist his charms. But desperate times call for desperate measures. He looks at the woman and smiles again. He calls up a bit of what Pyros he has left after the Firestorm. His stitches and mismatched limbs threaten to show, but he keeps them hidden, and suddenly his mind turns almost to clockwork. The woman is no longer a person, she's an obstacle. He would rather remove her without fuss- cleaner that way.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis will spend a Pyros to charge Lure, the first Distillation of his Eros Alembic. He will not flare his disfigurements, and so will take on the Callous Condition.<br /> <br /> Manipulation 3 + Persuasion 3 + Azoth 2 = 8 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/496287\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>. Now the police officer will have to roll Composure to see if she resists the effects of Lure. If she doesn't, any Persuasion rolls that Adonis attempts on her will receive a +2.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 03-14-2017, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T08:41:14-07:00","id":1063228,"title":"","content":"<b>The Throng</b><br /> <br /> The cadet curses under her breath as <b>Mark 5</b> moves to lift the wreckage and effortlessly tosses it away. She gapes a little, surprised by the dominating might of the Titan, even burned and battered as he is. She gazes dumbfounded at Scout, who seems perfectly fine with his current state, and just nods when the Originist addresses her. Flesh bruised and battered by the swift warping into and out of a Flux taint, tossed by a storm, the Throng are barely standing. <b>Scout,</b> is much worse off than he thought, nearly half dead and half drowned by the storm itself, but his mind is alight at the prospect of learning something new, discovering an aspect of the Flame Immortal that might not be entirely self-evident. He thinks he can hear the rebis whispering to him, promising him wisdom, promising him progress on the Pilgrimage, and he will record it for the posterity of the Created, burn it into Azothic Memory.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: <b>Scout</b> takes another three points of Bashing damage, wrapping around to Lethal. He learns from the Elpis Vision that his next Major/Superlative Milestone is the Ascetic Role. He also gains a Beat from his Health track filling with damage.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> Strength + Stamina was correct. Strength + Athletics is to throw something you've lifted. As a result, <b>Mark 5</b> gains the Inspired Condition.</i><br /> <br /> Meanwhile, <b>Earth</b> is teasing wisdom from her own Azoth. Surely it knows the way better than she does, it <i>must </i>know the path to the New Dawn. Where does she go from here? What does she do? Who controls the Fury? Who watches the watchwoman? She needs distance, she needs perspective. Earth needs to turn inwards, she needs to control her interactions until she knows what to do with the leash (a leash for <i>what?</i>) that her Azoth trusted her with.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Earth learns that the Role she must take next is the Hermit from Cuprum, Refinement of Self. To paraphrase Uncle Iroh &quot;Who are <b>you</b>, and what do <b>you</b> want?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The cadet walks quickly after the retreating Titan and Originist, while <b>Regret</b> simply hangs back, observing, lost in thought. &quot;Hey, I can't let you leave until my superiors get here and release the scene. You need medical attention and we need a statement about what the hell just happened here!&quot; <b>Adonis</b> catches her eye and smiles. The cadet stops dead for a second and <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=41645aed\" target=\"_blank\">blinks</a> for a moment before colour rushes to her face, blood sparkling with a cocktail of alchemy flooding her brain as the warmth of Adonis' Azoth draws her in like a moth to a flame.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: So the Distillation works on her. If you'd like to make it a Social Maneuvering action, she has four Doors. You could Force Doors (making a roll with a -4 penalty) or just make a Manipulation + Persuasion roll to up your Impression to Excellent meaning you could make a roll once per turn.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 03-20-2017, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T14:53:03-07:00","id":1063535,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama LTD), Inspired (Azoth)<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: LLLBBB | Willpower: 3/6 | Pyros: 2/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b></div><br /> Scout stopped paying attention to the officer and the others as soon as the words of the rebis hit his ears. He started walking, not paying much attention to his injuries as he should have.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Yes, yes. I will record every word, every step. Not a problem. Name. We need to give you a name. Regis the Rebis? Too pun-like. How about... Olmec. The Olmec peoples invented many things. Like rubber and vulcanization, which is a sort of alchemical process. Yes. We shall call you Olmec.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Scout didn't look back for the others. the police officer had stopped talking to him, so that meant he was free to walk.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Excuses to talk to yourself don't come along every day.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T18:48:28-07:00","id":1063701,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress, Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Eros (1), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: BBBBBBO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 2/10<br /> Beats: 1/5 I Vitriol Beats: 1/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis has never fished, but he gets the basic concept. And he can't help but picture a fish swallowing a hook as the cadet's face flushes. <i><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">There we go. Much nicer to just smile and agree with me, isn't it? </span></i>His mind felt... clear. It wasn't swirling with emotion like it usually did. It felt like he had replaced his blood with fresh cold spring water. Did the Nepri feel like this? If they did, he was jealous of them. Well, only a little- phlegm was clear and shifting, but it left them slow and lazy. He felt like water in a mountain stream. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>Humans really are chumps, aren't they? </i></span>No matter how much they tried to pretend, humans were still animals. And they had urges like all animals. He had offered the woman the smallest amount of his power, and she was already over the moon. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>To think I want to be one of them. </i></span>The thought caught him off guard.<span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i> I do... don't I? </i></span>The ice water pumping through him made him unsure. Yes, he understood on a theoretical level why he had to follow the Pilgrimage. You were on the Pilgrimage, or you weren't. And if you weren't, you were a Centimanus. And he didn't want to be one of those. Not like that moron Earth. <i><span style=\"color:#00ff00\">Earth Crisis. Always trying to snarl and smash your way out of a problem. One day, you may find a problem you can't just smash your way out of. And then what will you do? </span></i>Run to him, probably. She liked pretending he was a useless tag-along until someone needed to do the talking. But he could wait until later to give her a piece of his mind. Right now he had a flustered human to dispose of. <br /> <br /> His smile grew wider and he moved a little closer to her, trying to keep her attention on him and not the others- especially not Scout, who seemed like he was still experiencing an Elpis Vision. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Officer, really, we're fine. Look at us, we're all still on our feet. We're not in pain. Yes, at first I thought it was some sort of storm, but we were disoriented. I'm sure you don't need us to give a statement. Or our names for that matter. Unless... you want to go somewhere else?&quot; <i>I defy you to not not listen, lady. </i></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis is going to try and raise his impression with the woman, and he's not leaving anything to chance. He'll throw a Willpower onto the pile just to make sure she takes the hint. Manipulation 3 + Persuasion 3 + Area of Expertise (2) + Lure 2 + Willpower 3 = 13 dice-&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/496984\" target=\"_blank\">6 successes</a>. I think this is my first double-digits dice pool and oh man does it feel good. I believe that's an Exceptional Success twice over because of Eros' persistent ability.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T20:33:45-07:00","id":1065073,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Disconnected, Irritable, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Disquieted (North End: Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: LLLLLBBBBB | Willpower: 3/5 | Pyros: 0/12 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Holding her own chain? So there <i>is </i>more on the horizon. Always more to do. Why? She felt like she was at something like a stopping point. She made the right decision, and now the Fire had gone quiet. She could talk to humans-<br /> <br /> Oh. She could go back to the garden now.<br /> <br /> Wait. Wait wait. Don't jinx it- she got this far by channeling her Torment. Would a Vigilante plant a garden? Would being at peace knock her off the road again? Uuurrgh. She'd never <i>wanted </i>to interact with humans before, not like this, when she actually had a plan beyond wandering into their houses. Her instincts said she had to keep moving forward as a Vigilante, or trouble would come when she crashed. What <i>would </i>a Vigilante do? She should know this, now. Find another cause. Keep her Torment churning in a useful direction. Go after some Amalgama LTD branch office, or maybe the catacombs of Unborn. The garden could be too risky.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">[but she wanted to go there so bad, talk to the human again, work the black soil]</span><br /> <br /> Is that cop still here? Ugh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 03-21-2017, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T07:54:23-07:00","id":1065236,"title":"","content":"<b>The Throng</b><br /> <br /> <b>Scout </b>continues to wander the streets, water dripping off of him, heading farther afield from the throng. The humans are letting him pass, a little too frightened by his darkening bruises and his open wounds that are slowly bleeding a pale, cloudy liquid. Eyes darkened by internalized thought, he looks the part of a walking corpse. No one meets his gaze. No one even acknowledges his presence. He names the rebis (Are they me or am I them?) Olmec, after the Pre-Columbian civilization. Highwinds had nothing but admiration for the Mesoamerican civilizations, the blood-letters, the pyramid-builders, people who knew Torment and the Saturnine Night and tried to brighten it with the fires of sacrifice. He suggested there were secrets to be found in Mexico, which is where they were heading when the unpleasantness with their hired guards happened. Perhaps this is a sign. Earth mentioned a Named librarian in the city, didn't she? Perhaps they are a fellow Originist, walking a similar path.<br /> <br /> The police cadet, <b>Adonis</b> notices a name tag saying 'Katerina' on the heavy blue jacket when he gives her a clinical overview that could be (purposefully) mistaken for lustful, blushes and shakes her head, furrowing her brow as she takes a step back from the Muse to breathe. &quot;No, it's alright sir, you and your friends can go. Just give me some contact information,&quot; this is said almost with embarrassment, through heavily lidded eyes and fluttering lashes &quot;and you can go.&quot; She smiles a little, bemused, before her eyes widen in <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=06617cc8\" target=\"_blank\">recognition</a> &quot;Wait. I <i>do </i>recognize you from somewhere! You're Mark Austin! What are you doing in Winnipeg?&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: <b>Adonis</b> gains a Beat from the Double Exceptional Success, and imposes the Swooning Condition on <b>Katerina</b>, the police cadet. Adonis also gains the Callous Condition from using a Mesmerism Distillation without revealing Disfigurements. However, she manages to get a success on a roll to recognize Adonis, and confuses him for his Famous Face. This means that further Social rolls against this character will benefit from the 8-again quality and gain an additional +1.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 03-20-2017, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T08:32:00-07:00","id":1065254,"title":"","content":"Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Disconnected, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: XXXX///OOO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 0/11 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 3/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 2<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Geez, that woman was still keeping them up? At least Adonis' silver tongue seemed to work, so maybe they'd get out without a fight. Or further bloodshed.<br /> The Titans guts clenched involuntarily at the memory of what took place only minutes ago.<br /> He'd have to find someone he could to about this.<br /> Maybe Adonis? He had help es him with understanding intention, after all.<br /> <br /> &quot;You're Mark Austin!&quot;<br /> ...wait, what? Mark 5's eyebrows knitted together. What was that woman on about? HE was Mark, Mark 5. THAT was Adonis over there. He shook his head.<br /> The Girl must be confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T10:12:15-07:00","id":1065297,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress, Stage 1), Callous<br /> Alembics: Eros (1), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: BBBBBBO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 2/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 1/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b><br /> <br /> </div> At the officer's- Katerina's- words, Adonis smiles bashfully and rubs the back of his head, the other hand in his pocket- from what he can remember, this was a pose that Mark Austin once struck in a photo shoot. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Ah, you got me. Well, honestly, I came to Winnipeg for a fresh start. I'm trying to lay low and work on this new project I'm working on.&quot; </span>It's vague as hell, but all true. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\"><i>Crap. </i></span>This isn't the first time somebody has recognized him as Mark Austin. Adonis knows that he can usually use that as leverage to charm and persuade others, but then again, there's always the chance that Sharon is on the lookout for him. Maybe she's following reports of him across Canada. Will he have to leave Winnipeg for a while? <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>I ran because I was young and scared. A meat cleaver didn't exactly help matters, either. </i></span>But that was before he had a Throng on his side. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>I'd love to see her try and take on Mark. Or better yet, Earth. </i></span>The thought of Earth visiting her usual brand of vicious on his Demiurge was very satisfying. <br /> <br /> But that didn't change the fact that he knew next to nothing about Mark Austin. Sharon had only mentioned the names of the bodies she had maimed and the man she had murdered towards the end, as Disquiet gripped her more and more. Apparently, Mark had been an actor, a teen heartthrob on some soap opera who had basically disappeared after his big show got cancelled. So he lived by himself working some dead-end job until Sharon showed up at his door and killed him. He needed a way to find out more about &quot;himself.&quot; <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Well, uh- Katerina...&quot; </span>He gave her another big smile and gave her his contact information. He then leans in and whispers, <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;If I could ask a favor Katerina, don't tell any of your friends you bumped into me </span><span style=\"color:#00ff00\">today, alright? It'll be just our little secret.&quot; </span>Then he gave her a wink.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis is going to try and make her keep quiet. Manipulation 3 + Persuasion 3 + Lure 2 + Famous Face 1 = 9 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/498003\" target=\"_blank\">holy crap, 3 successes on a single dice!</a> That's another Exceptional Success and the Swooning Condition all over again. I am so glad I decided to Calcify Eros. Hoping to try out Assimilate and Stalker, and Eris for that matter, in the next chapter.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T08:22:52-07:00","id":1065777,"title":"","content":"<b>The Throng</b><br /> <br /> Katerina almost shudders as the Muse's- Mark's -lips brush her ear, and he slips a piece of paper into a hand that reflexively curls around it to brush his fingers. A little higher up, and she would have felt the ridges of his stitching that attached a pop star's talented hands to the sculpted arms of a heartthrob actor. <b>Adonis</b> might be prettier than the rest of them, his sutures cleaner, but he's as much a patchwork as <b>Regret</b>... maybe even more so. The police cadet nods vigorously, and beams a smile when he offers a wink.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes, of course! Take all the time you need, I don't want to hold you up. Besides, you need your privacy, right? That's why you never did anything after your show.&quot;<br /> <br /> She walks off to fetch a roll of yellow police tape to mark off the street corner torn apart by a Firestorm, and what is left of the bodies of the men that <b>Mark 5</b> tore limb from limb. The street has gone quiet, the crowd is already dispersing, except for the drunk, lying on the pavement, propped up on one arm, cursing and spitting and weeping just a little. Some people offer <b>Earth</b> a suspicious look or two, but most don't care. Whatever animosity they had for her seems... lessened. <b>Scout </b>wanders ahead, muttering to himself, out of sight, but not out of mind, easily close enough for his potent Azothic Radiance to butt up against theirs. Apart from Katerina, absent-mindedly, as if in a dream, following procedure, the street is empty now. <br /> <br /> Five Pilgrims standing still on a road, looking for a way forwards.<br /> <br /> There are sirens getting closer. The paramedics will be here soon. Time to get out of the area and find themselves a secluded place to heal.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: </i><i><b>Adonis</b> gains the <b>Connected (Katerina) Persistent Condition</b>. Everyone can make a Wits + Streetwise roll to find an out of the way source of electricity. A generic success will give you the equivalent of a Wall Socket (4B per turn), a roll with a -1 will give you the equivalent of a Protective Fence (6B per turn), a roll with a -2 will give you the equivalent of a Junction Box (8B per turn), and a roll with a -3 will give you the equivalent of a Main Line Feed (10B per turn). Most of you, to heal fully without shorting the source, won't need more than the equivalent of a Protective Fence.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T13:28:59-07:00","id":1065913,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress, Stage 1), Callous<br /> Alembics: Eros (1), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: BBBBBBO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 2/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 1/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b><br /> <br /> </div> Part of Adonis knew that what he was doing with this Katerina person was flirting and wrong, considering his relationship with Erwin. But now, he wasn't really bothered. Earth and Mark 5 had been insisting that Erwin was nothing more than a lead. The feelings he had for Erwin were real- at least, until a few minutes ago. Now, he wasn't sure if he cared about Erwin because he was one of those rare humans who could resist Disquiet and he had been desperate to be in contact with one, or because he had sensed that he was a means to complete his Role as a Companion? Both?<br /> <br /> When Katerina walked away, his smile turned into a grimace. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>I don't have time to deal with this. I have enough to think about already. </i></span>He turned to the others. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Let's move. The other police will be here soon, and I don't want to be here. Where's Scout? Oh, he's up ahead. We need to find a power source.&quot;</span> With that, he walked off, keeping a <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis tries to find an electrical outlet. He'll take the -1 to find one equivalent to a Protective Fence. Wits 2 + Streetwise 1 - Source 1 = 2 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/498261\" target=\"_blank\">no successes</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> As Adonis walked, he tried to keep his eyes peeled for a power source they could use, but his mind was too preoccupied. Finally, the question was too much. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Earth.&quot; </span>He took her by the arm and looked at her. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Can we... talk? Let's just... walk a little behind the others.&quot; </span>When they were out of earshot of the others, he sighed. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;That... thing you turned into back there. That was what you were like as a Centimanus, right?&quot; </span>He gave her time to answer. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;When... all that stuff happened back there. I was scared. But... part of me was kind of excited. I </span><i>wanted </i><span style=\"color:#00ff00\">it. Well, up until I had to start vomiting it up to not get melted from the inside. But after feeling all of that, I can't believe you walked away from Flux. So I want to know... how? Because when I used my Distillation on that police officer, I hid my Disfigurements from her. And now... I'm having trouble thinking of people as anything but tools. And I'm having trouble remembering why I need to stay on the Pilgrimage.&quot; </span>His voice grew more and more emotional as he walked. He looked at Earth with fear and pleading. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Please. You're the only one of us who knows what it's like, and you're the only Centimanus I know who left it. I need your help.&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T14:54:03-07:00","id":1065956,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Disconnected, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: XXXX///OOO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 0/11 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 3/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 0</b><br /> <br /> </div> Finally that girl left them alone!<br /> What was all that &quot;privacy&quot; business? How come she knew Adonis? And why did she react so strangely to him? His mind control sure was fearsome.<br /> For that matter, what was going on with him lately? He seemed so decisive? Questions upon meaningless questions.<br /> None of that mattered to the dead. Sadness creeped on his face, and his movements slowed down.<br /> Dead by his hand. How to atone? Could he?<br /> Was it something that could be forgiven?<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#00ff00\">We need to find a power source.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <i>Good point. Let's be useful. </i>Mark 5 kept his eyes peeled for something<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Wits+Streetwise-1 for something equivalent to a protective fence:3 dice--&gt; <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=e013b7c6\" target=\"_blank\">2 Sux!</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> and actually managed to find it. When he reached out for it.....<br /> Scout looked like he was hurt the most, his Created-ness showed the most, so the Titan called out to him: <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Scout! There's a source here. Come on up!&quot; </span><br /> <br /> When being honest with himself, it wasn't that he cared about someone else's wellbeing. That was not why he resolved not to charge himself up.<br /> He wanted to punish himself, for the horrible crimes he committed. Not getting rid of his wounds wasn't much, since he didn't feel them as a human would - but it was a start.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:28:56-07:00","id":1065984,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama LTD), Inspired (Azoth)<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: LLLOOO | Willpower: 3/6 | Pyros: 5/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> Scout realized he'd gotten a little ways too far ahead when he heard how faint Adonis's voice had gotten. He stopped to at least make sure Mark 5 and Regret had caught up, and took the moment to burn his injuries into more pyros, healing at least some of the minor battering on his form. As his fellows caught up he looked up to each in turn, craning his neck to catch their eyes, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Regret, Mark 5... would you please assist me in some additional study? I could use some hearty minds- and hands. Olmec has called to me, and I wish to answer. To do this will likely require quite a bit of work- especially since that firestorm may have drawn in any local Alchemists. With Amalgama around, we cannot be too certain there will not be far worse. Given the... nature of what I have discovered, I may eventually need to make a trip back to Old Mexico- a very dangerous proposition, but the pre-Columbian civilizations understood much of the Saturnine Night. I believe that they know will be very helpful in all Pilgrimages. The answer is not needed now, of course. But I want you to think about it.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> The tiny native looking corpse smiled at his friends, then glanced back towards Earth and Adonis, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I will ask Adonis and Earth as well, when they have done what they wish to do. But for now... yes electrical outlets.</span>&quot; Then Scout started rambling again, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">If only it stormed on a good strong basis. Then we could just put up a lightning rod on Adonis's apartment complex. If I ever find the money, I believe I shall purchase a car battery and see if I can utilize that. I understand some stores recharge those for free.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/498281\" target=\"_blank\">2 dice, 2 success</a>holy crap, dice rollers love me lately. I've been rolling hot all month.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T19:56:38-07:00","id":1066101,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Disconnected, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Disquieted (North End: Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: LLLLLBBBBB | Willpower: 4/5 | Pyros: 0/12 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Staying away from the others was a quiet way of indulging her Torment. After the Flux atavism brought on by the Firestorm, it was grounding to fall back into her pattern of alienation from others. Even Torment is more part of you than Flux, that's the lesson of the Furies.<br /> <br /> Earth still smoldered with envy at how easily Adonis spoke to humans, just as she had that morning at the diner. When Katerina finally left, she lurched after the throng in search of life-giving lightning. She was expecting to be alone, but Adonis fell back with her. Apparently that disturbing, fleeting connection in the Firestorm wasn't the end of it. He took her arm. She begrudgingly listened.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;That... thing you turned into back there. That was what you were like as a Centimanus, right?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Her hands were shoved in her ruined jacket pockets. As usual, she was tongue-tied. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I wish you guys hadn't seen that.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Yeah, though. That's what Earth-Dies-Screaming did to this body. When you hear the stories about me, picture that thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I didn't know that shit was still inside me. This body remembers that shape. Flux is always changing, but the change leaves marks. Does that make any sense?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;When... all that stuff happened back there. I was scared. But... part of me was kind of excited. I </span><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>wanted </i>it.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She slumped and closed her eyes, but didn't interrupt.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Well, up until I had to start vomiting it up to not get melted from the inside.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Okay, she <i>snrked </i>at that despite herself. But this was going nowhere good.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;But after feeling all of that, I can't believe you walked away from Flux. So I want to know... how? Because when I used my Distillation on that police officer, I hid my Disfigurements from her. And now... I'm having trouble thinking of people as anything but tools. And I'm having trouble remembering why I need to stay on the Pilgrimage.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Earth was growing visibly tense. She picked up her pace to get near the others. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Don't fuck with me, man. Not right now.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Please. You're the only one of us who knows what it's like, and you're the only Centimanus I know who left it.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Her Inscription burned like it was trying to crawl off her skin. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Too much. Too much. I gotta dig a hole, gotta get underground-&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;I need your help.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> She stopped dead and dug her hands into her hair. Her eyes were itching. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;God, you even <i>sound </i>like her!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Earth remembers this one moment very well. It's from a few months after she met Dead Girl, before DG had deeply embraced Flux, before her eyes were like mirrors. She doesn't dwell on it, but she remembers it because it doesn't fit the narrative she's made of her other memories. It's like a sewn-together body with one piece that's too big.<br /> <br /> Dead Girl was writing in one of her moleskine journals with a fancy ink pen she kept in those days, she and Earth were arguing about something, and suddenly she ripped out the pages she was writing on and smashed her precious pen and fled back to the van they were staying in with her hands covered in ink. Earth followed after a while and asked if she was okay. Dead Girl said: <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;No, I'm not. Something is seriously wrong with me.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Earth didn't know what to say to that. She sounded exhausted and miserable and not at all elegant. She continued: <span style=\"color:#800080\">&quot;I can't think straight. I feel like I'm falling off a cliff. I <i>really </i>need to get help before I hurt someone. I <i>need </i>help.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;The only other Muse I've known as well as you was Dead Girl. We were bound together as Centimani. Branded. When you talk about, uh, whatsername- 'Sharon'- that's what she was like to me. You're beautiful and Gold like she was, but she started to hate the humans who saw her beauty. <i>Tools, </i>she said the same thing you did, they were <i>tools</i>. She wanted to throw the beautiful things in their faces and remake her own flesh. When I see you talk to humans, I think of her so bad. In the Firestorm, I <i>saw you as her</i>. And then you say you felt the same thing we felt- just, <i>fuck, </i>it feels like I'm back in Flux with her!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She was shuddering as they walked. Her stolen body craved a cigarette, like it always did on the rare occasions she got excited in this way. As Mark 5 pointed out an electrified security fence around a vacant lot, she continued, quiet and agitated:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I'll be dead straight with you, pretty boy. I can't help you, or anyone. I never could. I can't tell you why you need to stay on the Pilgrimage. I don't even know why I'm doing it, except the only other choice is worse and I'm too stubborn to quit. I wish I'd never given myself the option of leaving, made it real in my mind, because I think about giving up every single day. And that's what it is: giving up. Flux isn't strength. It's not liberation or evolution, or...or a new tool, or however you're thinking about it. You're killing your own hope for a rush of power. You forget the past and cancel the future and everything becomes an endless gray <i>now.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;There's so much I could say. Like when you first enhance- <i>corrupt </i>your body with Flux, you feel this horrible dead guttering mudpit of shame and guilt, and you can't tell anyone what you've done, so it pushes you away from anyone you knew before. And it kills your mind. That's why those Freaks in the wild running with packs of Unborn are so savage. You can't think right, and remembering your hope just hurts you. I would lose <i>weeks, </i>just hunting and killing and feeding. It's not like Mark 5 did. You just kill like an animal and it doesn't mean anything. You pass in and out of Torment and you don't even notice. The whole world dissolves.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She watched the others shock their dead flesh in silence for a while, hands buried in her pockets. The whole idea of her flesh stuffed into human clothes seemed like a sick joke for a minute.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;What you do- the way you talk to humans, just talk to them and laugh and smile and all that- I mean, I never stopped dreaming about humans. Even as a Freak, I had those dreams. The dream of doing what you do right now is what got me through. Do you get it?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A Firestorm shocked me out of that gray, and cut me off from my baggage, but remembering those dreams gave me something bright to climb back to. If you don't have faith in something, you'll never get out, no matter how many chances you get.&quot;</span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> She clapped Adonis on the back, too hard. But he's probably strong enough to take it lately.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Uh- listen. You can talk to me about this, okay? Even if it's scary. C'mon, everyone's waiting for us. That car wash looks empty...&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Wits+Streetwise+Willpower to find a basic wall socket somewhere. 5 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/498367\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>.<br /> <br /> Gonna try to recharge for 4 turns depending on power availability, with my handy dandy Efficient Conductor merit to help.<br /> <br /> 1st: heal 2+1 lethal, regain 1 Pyros<br /> 2nd: heal 2+1 lethal, regain 1+1 Pyros<br /> 3rd: lethal healed, regain 1 Pyros<br /> 4th: lethal healed, regain 1+1 Pyros</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 03-21-2017, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T07:13:18-07:00","id":1066847,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress, Stage 1), Callous<br /> Alembics: Eros (1), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: BBBBBBO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 2/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 1/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b><br /> </div> <br /> Adonis walked beside Earth, listening to her story. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I wish you guys hadn't seen that. </span><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Yeah, though. That's what Earth-Dies-Screaming did to this body. When you hear the stories about me, picture that thing.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The thought of Earth being a Centimanus even looking normal was scary enough. Thinking back to the stories he had heard of her, and replacing the familiar image of Earth with the image of that... thing was even worse. He shivered. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Yeah, I figured. And when I ran to you, hugged you during the Firestorm... that's what I was trying to tell you. Because if that's what the bottom looks like, you're so far above that now.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> Earth's words about Dead Girl rattled him. Not enough to stop thinking about humans in a cause-and-effect way, but enough to turn the ice water that was flowing through him back into blood- sluggish, cold blood, but still blood. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>I need to get rid of this. Because I don't want to be like that. If I keep this up, I'm going to be just like Dead Girl. </i></span>Not really the same as wanting to become human, but not turning Centimanus would cut it for now. But Earth's words about still loving humans even as a Freak comforted him. <br /> <br /> The hand on the back was sudden, but he now knew what Earth at full force was like. This was like when human men punched each other in the shoulder- a gesture of affection for those who weren't used to showing emotion. He smirked at her and pushed it away. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Careful, Earth. You can take more hits than me, but I'm not your average pansy Muse. I can knock some heads together too. Yeah I know. Strong <i>and</i> pretty?&quot; </span>He flashed her a friendly grin and a wink to tell her he was doing some friendly teasing. <br /> <br /> He followed Earth to the car wash. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis will follow Earth and try to find a regular wall socket. <br /> <br /> 1st round: 4 Bashing healed, +1 Pyros<br /> 2nd round: 2 Bashing healed, +1 Pyros</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> His body surged with intense vibration as the electricity coursed through his body from the finger stuck in the socket. He stood and clapped his hands together. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;So. Looked like you guys were having an Elpis Vision. It tell you anything important?&quot;</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T08:55:05-07:00","id":1066912,"title":"","content":"<b>The Throng</b><br /> <br /> The Titan leads <b>Scout </b>towards an electrified fence guarding an industrial workshop, something a little heavy duty for the area, but a strike of good fortune for the two. Empowered in the wake of the Firestorm, the Osirian finds himself a more potent conductor than he had been before. In seconds, his mummified flesh knit together with impossible speed, his humours invigorate with Pyros. Though <b>Mark 5</b> seeks to punish himself by avoiding healing for now, stray bolts of electricity, no longer needed and no longer contained, arc out towards the nearest conductor, Mark 5. Snaking up his arm, it immediately repairs bruised and battered flesh, and the Titan, implacable, invincible, flinches backwards, avoiding the healing blessing of the Principle.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Because of the Efficient Conductor Merit, <b>Scout</b> heals all three points of Lethal damage immediately, as well as regaining a point of Pyros. Because <b>Mark 5</b> is the nearest conductor, the excess electricity spreads to him, healing two points of Bashing damage and regaining a point of Pyros.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Earth</b>, lost in thought, uncomfortably trying to offer what insight she has to the perplexed and numbed Muse, latches on to a hardline at a nearby serve-yourself car wash. Her potent humours repair her body, invigorated with Pyros, healing swiftly and surely. A stray arc lances out from the battered Earth and lances towards <b>Adonis</b>, starting the process of healing. The Muse is lured towards the siren song of healing and power, latching on to repair himself. He heals, his humours empowered by life-giving lightning, but two Created drawing on the source <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=f8480069\" target=\"_blank\">shorts it out</a>. Before Adonis can draw on it for more power, the electricity fails, and a grumbling employee stumbles out of the convenience store to flip a breaker.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Just a correction or two. <b>Earth's</b> first turn heals three points of Lethal damage, and gains one point of Pyros. Earth's second turn heals two points of Lethal damage, two points of Bashing damage, and gains two points of Pyros. Earth's third turn heals the rest of the Bashing damage and gains another point of Pyros. Because Earth gained four points of Pyros (one in excess of her Azoth) she gains the <b>Degaussed Condition</b>. The source <b>really</b> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=02a843e6\" target=\"_blank\">doesn't short out</a> the first time. On Earth's last turn healing, <b>Adonis </b>heals a point of Bashing damage and gains a point of Pyros. On Adonis' first turn of healing, he heals four points of Bashing damage and gains a point of Pyros. On Adonis' second turn of healing, he heals his last point of Bashing damage and gains a point of Pyros. There is no third turn, as the source doesn't short out.<br /> <br /> Final totals. Both: All Healed. <b>Earth:</b> Four points of Pyros + Degaussed Condition. <b>Adonis:</b> Three points of Pyros.</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T00:17:23-07:00","id":1067433,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Disconnected, Degaussed, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Disquieted (North End: Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 4/5 | Pyros: 4/12 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Because if that's what the bottom looks like, you're so far above that now.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> That got a crooked smile out of her. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I'm trying. I sure hope so.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Yeah I know. Strong <i>and</i> pretty?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Still not used to Adonis being this punchy with her, but hey, everything changes. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Oh, uh, for sure! Erwin's a lucky alchemist. You're the whole package. Except brains! <i>Ha!</i>&quot;</span><br /> <br /> After she charged up, her tongue was smoking, so the banter died off quick. Also, her natural electromagnetic field was all freaky. That's what happens when you drink from the hose! Probably shouldn't hang around Adonis' apartment right now. Wouldn't want to screw up the TV at Castle Frankenstein, <span style=\"font-size:10px\">or the electronic stuff in her library.</span><br /> <br /> She ran for it when the human wandered out. Disquiet or not, she wasn't feeling conversational. The rest of the throng wasn't too hard to find and catch up with.<br /> <br /> Scout: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I haven't been too far south of the border, but if the angels are calling you down there, you gotta follow. You should talk to Tom Barebone at the library if you wanna learn stuff here. You can trust him, he's Tammuz. Can't miss him. Looks like rock candy.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Mark 5: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Hey, hero. Next time you go out there, I'm coming with you. You said we'd be a team when I got here, remember? But uh- I wanna go back to the garden first. You should come too. The human there has lots of stuff to do.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I dunno if we're about to skip ahead, but I'll roll a supporting action for Mark 5 dealing with I.P. once and for all. Looking forward to the Breaker/Darkstorm teamup comic to show up in Winnipeg zines in 2017!<br /> <br /> Spending 1 Pyros for Inscription to add to Intimidation, and 1 Willpower. Strength 4+Intimidation 3+Reputation 5+Inscription 3+Willpower 3. 18 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/499058\" target=\"_blank\">6 successes.</a> +6 dice for Mark! If I can, I'll also give him a custom Condition as on 305: <b>Backup</b>, which gives him 9-again on relevant rolls and resolves when he completes the Social Maneuver.<br /> <br /> While out on the prowl, can I resolve Degaussed to make a mortal hunter/alchemist/nasty fella notice that Darkstorm isn't human?<br /> <br /> Build Equipment: Strength 4+Crafts 1+Teamwork 5+Willpower 3-Difficulty 5, 8 dice. <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/500012\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 04-04-2017, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T01:07:30-07:00","id":1067441,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Disconnected, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: XXXX/OOOOO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 1/11 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 3/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 0</b></div> <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Regret, Mark 5... would you please assist me in some additional study? I could use some hearty minds- and hands. Olmec has called to me, and I wish to answer. To do this will likely require quite a bit of work- especially since that firestorm may have drawn in any local Alchemists. With Amalgama around, we cannot be too certain there will not be far worse. Given the... nature of what I have discovered, I may eventually need to make a trip back to Old Mexico- a very dangerous proposition, but the pre-Columbian civilizations understood much of the Saturnine Night. I believe that they know will be very helpful in all Pilgrimages. The answer is not needed now, of course. But I want you to think about it.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>What is an Olmec?</i><br /> Anyway<i>, </i>it was not a lot of things kept him to his place. What he did... He nodded and simply said.<span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Need to take care of some stuff first. Then, sure.&quot; </span><br /> To his unending frustration, the electricity found its way to him when Scout healed up, and even though the worst damage stayed with him, it was still annoying to no end that he couln't even redeem himself the way he wants to.<br /> He took a step back, only to be surprised by Earth's sudden proposition.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Hey, hero. Next time you go out there, I'm coming with you. You said we'd be a team when I got here, remember? But uh- I wanna go back to the garden first. You should come too. The human there has lots of stuff to do.&quot;</span><br /> True, he had promised her they'd be partners. Maybe if she had been there, this wouldn't have happened? <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Yes. Please do so. But... I will not go out there for a while.&quot; </span>He looked down at his hands. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;What I have done... I must atone. Even if they were Evil, to end their lives, and end it like that... I had no right. I was lost, but that is no excuse. I must face it, bring this whole business with the gang to an end. No more death. No more Bloodshed.<br /> But not now. I need time.&quot; </span><br /> He smiled sadly, at the thought of peaceful work. He'd never been that drawn to silence and nature since... ever? <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Gardening sound nice. Yes, let's help that human. Just tell me what you need done.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=47b051e8\" target=\"_blank\">Helping out Earth: 5 successes</a> so +5 for Earth. Wow, they're a good team xD<br /> <br /> Edit: Social Maneuver: <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=7ba5ae13\" target=\"_blank\">1 Sux</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Looked like you guys were having an Elpis Vision. It tell you anything important?&quot;</span><br /> Mark 5 shook his head. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;The... gang members... their bodies became a giant monster with five heads and ten arms, and went to attack Earth. It carried weapons out of debris and bones. I jumped in between them, told it to get lost, to leave her alone.<br /> Told... I told it I was the one it should attack.<br /> <br /> And it did, got me good, in the back. Can't make head or tails out of it.&quot; </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 03-30-2017, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T16:53:56-07:00","id":1068122,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama LTD), Inspired (Azoth)<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 3/6 | Pyros: 6/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b></div><br /> Scout glanced to Adonis, then Earth, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I saw my Rebis. It... showed me how to end the Firestorm. I still hear Olmec speaking to me actually. So... I'm going to see if I can summon them. Without the firestorm preferably. I will speak to this Tammuz. With any luck, we can exchange information, and all will progress.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Mark 5's words... Scout hesitated, but spoke again, slowly, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">There are people in Old Mexico who need your help. And people so evil... well to call them human would be only to refer to their biology. They are worse than Centimanus, and mad like alchemists. They killed my genitor, Highwinds. I don't think they were even in disquiet when it happened. They just shot him up and cut him to pieces out of cruelty.</span>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T08:33:07-07:00","id":1073137,"title":"","content":"<i>Interludes</i><br /> <br /> <b>Scout</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Osirian makes his way to the </span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Millennium_Library_(Winnipeg)\" target=\"_blank\">Millennium Library</a><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, the central branch of the Winnipeg Public Library system. As Scout ascends the stairs, passing lamplit alcoves adjacent to the wall of windows looking out onto the empty reading garden, he keeps a weather eye out for </span><b>Tom Barebones</b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, a fellow Tammuz that Earth had directed him to. The fourth floor was where the primary historical section was, as was the local Historical Room, where the most records outside the Manitoba Archives were kept. The reading garden was, in extremely late autumn (should be winter), a destitute wreck. The urban marsh was drained, leaving the brown and black rot of algae baking in the sun against cement, chairs were stacked haphazardly by tables covered in a thick layer of dust and salt, and woven wicker balls holding darkened lights swayed in the empty, skeletal branches of the trees.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Wandering the fourth floor, you seem him, Tom, quietly filing books in the deep shelves. He is rail-thin, wearing a tattered canvas coat and several scarves of riotous colours- you think you can see </span><i>writing </i><span style=\"font-size:13px\">inked onto the back of them. His face is pock-marked and scarred, with raised lumps of acne, warts, and other growths. To your Created eyes, past the Azothic Mask, you see salt crystals and lumps of clay crawling along his skin, breaking up his outline. In fact, it looks like he might be more clay than flesh where you can see the yellowed ivory of bone poking through. When the coat sleeve on one arm rides up, you think you can see a block of text tattooed there. You approach, and the Named seems startled, eyes darting for a place to run to, until your Disfigurements become clear, and then he visibly relaxes. You mention what you're looking for, and why, and that Earth sent you, and Tom just </span><i>looks</i><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> at you, as though attempting to memorize something, at which point he pulls out a well-worn and well-cared for sketchbook from a massive pocket he has sewn into his jacket. With an sketch artist's precision, he drafts a portrait onto a page, and then very carefully writes down a sentence before he speaks it.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;Jussst follow me, pleassse. Religion and Esssotericisssm are right over here.&quot; He rolls the words around in his mouth like a stone, drawing out certain sounds with a far-away look on his face, as though trying to reach a memory he cannot quite recall. A Word that had been spoken to him once, in the Dreamtime before life, deep in subconscious Memory.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">For the next several hours you work side by side, Tom pulling down books, handing them off, and then disappearing for a while, though behind a bookcase you can hear the scratch of pencil on paper, a quiet whisper, the flutter of cloth, the click of a tape recorder, the static of a well-worn recording, and the breathy sounds of someone trying to follow along word for word without being heard. It becomes relatively clear that Tom is not an Originist, but with his subtle guidance your research goes well.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">You find that rebis is, etymologically, from the Latin &quot;res bina&quot; meaning dual or double matter, and that it saw the most use amongst a group of European mystics called the Rosicrucians, a fraternal lodge that first pops up in the late 16</span><sup>th</sup><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> and early 17</span><sup>th</sup><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> centuries with the publication of several texts proclaiming the existence of a hitherto unknown esoteric order that is &quot;built on esoteric truths of the ancient past&quot;. It had a seminal influence on emerging Freemasonry, and the philosophy merged and flowed with the Masons, the Golden Dawn, and the Theosophists as the years wore on. There was scepticism regarding the claims of the Rosicrucians, but that didn't stop people from joining... or from alchemy becoming the latest fad. Alchemy is built off of three axioms &quot;As Above, So Below&quot;, &quot;As Within, So Without&quot;, and &quot;Know Thyself&quot;. The rebis was a symbol of the </span><a href=\"http://www.sacred-texts.com/eso/sta/sta40.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Chymical Wedding</a><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> (one of the core parables of the Rosicrucians), the ultimate merging of Soul and Body into an idealized, perfected being. </span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">In the 1750s, a Rosicrucian and Masonic secret society called the Order of the Golden and Rosy Cross rose to prominence among proponents of alchemical philosophy. It espoused alchemy-as-spiritualism, touting the mystical science\u2019s physical processes as a metaphor for the enlightenment of the human soul, and imagined that one day it would accomplish the ultimate \u201cChymical Wedding\u201d \u2014 the unification of the mundane with the divine. Rosicrucianism began among doctors who viewed themselves as mystical philosophers on top of their earthly mandate to heal the body, and the trend continued; many of the Order were physicians as well as spiritualists. Like its predecessor, what the Golden Thorn wants more than anything is to achieve the Chymical Wedding. Unlike its predecessor, it views this ultimate enlightenment as a literal process. Its members believed that only by merging, body and soul, with other human beings can one achieve spiritual perfection. Each strived to find a person with whom he can create the most ideal amalgam, and then to mix an alchemical formula that they can both imbibe to complete the human compound. Not all Chymical Weddings are presumed to have only two components, and some in the brotherhood have spent lifetimes trying to find exactly the right set of people to make the compound work. No successful Chymical Wedding had been confirmed, but rumours circulated of those who have managed it.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Scout gains the Informed (Alchemy) Condition from the Exceptional Success</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Before Scout leaves Tom shyly approaches, a series of papers from his sketchbook carefully stapled together. It is part thesis, part bibliography, and part alchemical worksheet. It is scrawled with equations and observations and stream of consciousness thought processes connecting books, experience, and philosophy. Scout can see, from where the sketchbook is sitting on the nearby table, cover flipped up, that the page that started with an introductory sentence and a portrait of his face has turned into a snapshot of his time at the library. Further sketches of him pouring over texts, thoughts, hopes, fears, phrases carefully constructed and others scratched out with frustration and shame.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;Thisss isss for you Ssscout. It isss everything I could remember my Genitor told me about sssocial alchemy. Ssshe thought it could help dampen Disssquiet... ssshe was wrong. But maybe a Mussse could make more sssenssse of it than me. I hope that you find what you're looking for.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Tom gives Scout an alchemical thesis that is worth a +3 Equipment Bonus to research Alchemy.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T14:02:37-07:00","id":1073868,"title":"","content":"<i>Interludes</i><br /> <br /> <b>Mark 5</b><br /> <br /> Rumour has it that the Breaker is going around the North End again. He's an urban legend, a boogeyman, someone the police can't (or perhaps won't) track down, and the story keeps on growing. They say he's not a man, they say he's not even human, they say if you burn a picture of someone you hate and chant &quot;Breaker, Breaker, Breaker&quot; into a walkie-talkie that person will end up dead. That one's gained some traction, since the source of many a young person's ire is the gangbanger on the corner just a few years older than them, and these days they're turning up dead. They say he can't be killed and that his fists and feet are made of steel. Some people are saying he's an experimental super-soldier from the 'deserted' Kapyong Barracks, but everyone <i>really </i>knows that weird shit goes on in those empty old buildings over on Kennaston Boulevard.<br /> <br /> Now, far more fearsome, are the stories of the one that calls themselves Darkstorm. No one even thinks that <i>they're </i>human, but exactly <i>what </i>Darkstorm is, no one is exactly sure. Some people, who have relatives out in British Columbia, say that maybe Darkstorm is a thunderbird who has lost their mask and their feather cloak and is stuck in human form, or is someone with thunderbird blood, but either way Darkstorm is just as wrathful as they are. They say that Darkstorm's voice rolls like thunder, and when they blink that lights flicker. Someone was standing on the Desraeli Bridge one day when someone down below in the trainyards let out a wrathful scream and the doors of nearby train cars and buildings were ripped towards them as if they were a massive electromagnet. They're sure it was Darkstorm, and they believe. After all, aren't thunderbirds supposed to punish the wicked? Hasn't Darkstorm just gone after the local gangs, driving them from the relative safety of the train yards to places where they can be caught?<br /> <br /> A local Indian Posse warehouse was found with a message tagged on its door, scorched into the metal itself by a massive current of some kind. Their Hell's Angels patrons are none too pleased with how the gang has been kicked around so badly by two people (there are just two of them, and they are really people, right?) over the last couple of months. They need to fix this, now. When one of the local leaders, a 'Chief', shows up in the trashed parking lot of an industrial park, he has backup. Warriors, their arms tattooed with arrows, guns tucked into waistbands, red bandanas tied across heads, over faces, around legs, leather jackets and leather gloves and steel-toed boots for the intimidation factor. They end up squaring off with just two people. One of them is hanging back under the shadows of the building in a long rain coat, arms folded, one arm thickly corded with muscle, a hat saying MAKE AMERICA NATIVE AGAIN pulled down tightly over their head. Behind them is some kind of weird-ass graffiti, but they can see the stylized tag of Darkstorm in there, and that gets a few of the boys nervously reaching for their guns. The other is on the roof and leaps down to the pavement, rolling forwards effortlessly like it was nothing and looming up in the Chief's face. He's wearing black pants, a black shirt, both of which are stained with... they aren't sure what, and he has a black ski mask on his face, with duct tape around the eyes and mouth. What the fuck is this? A fucking superhero mask?<br /> <br /> The Chief laughs in the Titan's face, a face scarred by acne (and muzzle burns, in a few spots) impassive in the face of the flashy parkour shit. You're close enough to see the shield tattooed on his neck and the dull outline of IP beside it, the arrows and knives fading away on his forearms, the spots of shockingly pink skin where frostbite and burns did their dreadful work. This guy has lived hard, and he's not impressed. When he pulls his gun and puts it to the Titan's head, he isn't ready for this crazy bastard to grab him by the throat and just <i>lift</i>, ever so slightly. Now he's dancing on the tips of his toes, choking on his own body weight, and seems to have forgotten he's holding a gun. Would the gun even help? Darkstorm takes a step forwards out of the shadows and makes a show of clenching a fist, sparks flying from fingertips as a haze and the smell of ozone gathers around them. The backup scatters. The Breaker informs him, very clearly, that the Indian Posse is not to do business in the North End anymore, and if they stay here, well, then they're going to have a <i>problem</i>. Because next time, he's not going to go after the Strikers he sees roughing people up or dealing, it's going to be a war. &quot;I'm going to give you a week. Clear out.&quot; He lets the Chief go, and the man falls back towards the ground, gasping for breath, and IP scatters.<br /> <br /> Over the next week, warehouses empty, safe houses are abandoned, and people either ditch patched jackets and red bandanas or decide to leave town.<br /> <br /> Tattoo parlours sell removals or coverups at a premium.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: And Mark 5 does it! Take a Beat for completing this Social Maneuvering action. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> replace the Degaussed Condition with the Watched Condition and take a Beat.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Earth</b><br /> <br /> The Named needs a space of her own. She goes back to the community garden at the Ross House and finds the same woman working there that she met a while back. The weather finally looks like it's going to turn and so they need to get the garden ready for winter. Mark 5 comes along, and he seems a little... odd... to her, but he works hard and he's strong, so they can get a lot of stuff done. Earth learns that her name is Dymond. Not a terribly great name, she admits, but it was either go by her middle name of Dymond, or go by her first name, Rain, which got her bullied relentlessly at school. (Rain, rain, go away and other such unimaginative but cruel crap) The weirdness fades for both Named, spending actual time with a human, and they start to trust in their ability to connect, to comprehend. Mark 5 is standoffish because Disquiet is still an issue, but Earth's Azoth is strangely stable. If she manages to keep her fury at a low simmer, let it boil over a little when she sees someone breaking a rule of some kind, give them a bit of a slap upside the head or a solid tongue-thrashing, then Disquiet isn't a problem. Over the course of a week of work (where Earth sets up a Zen garden with rocks and pebbles and stoney sand), Dymond let's her know no less than three times a day what a hardass she is, and how she needs to go a little easier on people, because not everyone is going to be cool with that kind of intensity.<br /> <br /> The garden is Earth's idea, because somewhere deep inside she knows she needs to level her head and let some of the Torment go too, even if she isn't quite ready to let go of this small miracle just yet. Pyros doesn't like to sit still, even if Vitriol does. Mark 5 doesn't know what she did here, and if Earth gets her way, he's never going to. But one day, while they finishing uprooting some particularly gnarly shrubs to pot and put inside a greenhouse for the winter, Earth spies something writhing in the cold mud...<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Mark 5 and Earth both resolve the Disconnected Condition and each gain a Beat. Earth also resolves her &quot;Work at the Community Garden&quot; Aspiration and gains another Beat. However, there's a bit of interaction to go here. Roll for Initiative...</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T23:18:28-07:00","id":1074027,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\">Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Disconnected, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: XXXX/OOOOO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 1/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 3/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 0<br /> <br /> </div> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=9fbd17bf\" target=\"_blank\">Initiative 16</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T02:19:04-07:00","id":1074063,"title":"","content":"<b><div align=\"center\">Earth</div></b><br /> Initiative <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/502927\" target=\"_blank\">14</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T07:38:27-07:00","id":1074120,"title":"","content":"<i>The Garden</i><br /> <br /> <b>Earth and Mark 5</b><br /> <br /> The Fury leans in closer towards the mud, brushing away at the dirt, when a root thick with thorns and slick with black bile lashes out of the ground, whipping towards Earth. It misses <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=397c9f3d\" target=\"_blank\">by a long shot</a>, groping madly in the mud, churning it into a slurry of fluids and earth as more thorned roots emerge and drag the thing forwards with a sucking sound like the world was trying to keep this thing from emerging into the light. Dymond screams, fleeing into the Ross House and locking the door behind her with a long list of hissed expletives. You can <i>feel</i> the twisted, yawning void of this thing's Fire, hearing its ragged, rattling inhalations as it scents the air, trying to breathe with malformed lungs. It drags itself into the light, a tangled nest of thorns, roots lashing from every angle where there isn't a gaping maw opening and closing. The Unborn's back blossoms like a flower with a wet creaking sound, thorns rising up like teeth, like the spires of a crown, black bile coating the insides as a tangled mat of thorned roots rolls about like a tongue. It heaves itself forwards, finally free of the ground where it had slumbered, and stretches roots as though it can <i>see </i>with them, scenting the air. It turns towards the Titan and the Fury, roots along its dorsal side drawing back and pointing forwards like aimed arrows.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: The Pandoran has an Initiative of 7. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> you attack first, then <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a></i>. The Pandoran has a Defense of 6","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 04-06-2017, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T09:45:46-07:00","id":1074715,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (1)<br /> Health: XXXX/OOOOO | Willpower: 3/6 | Pyros: 0/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 3/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 0</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Seeing the Pandoran, Mark 5 immediately fired up his Cyclopean Might with his remaining Pyros, and threw himself at the beast without abandon, trying to stomp it into the ground, unleashing a flurry of punches the likes of which only a Titan could throw.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Str+Brawl+All-Out+1WP <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=c835e62a\" target=\"_blank\">4 Sux </a>with Cyclopean Might, that makes 4 Lethal</div></div> </div> </div><br /> And he did hit hard - however, he left himself completely open to retaliation in return.<br /> He didn't care.<br /> It should focus on him, not Earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T11:13:02-07:00","id":1074755,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Watched, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Disquieted (North End: Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 2/5 | Pyros: 3/12 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> Dymond (she hears it as Diamond) isn't such a bad name. Rain's good, too. They're simple, clean, natural-world words that everyone knows. Like Earth!<br /> <br /> She gets confused and defensive when Dymond calls her out. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I'm doing the best I can here, alright?&quot;</span> Living the Role is keeping her in balance, so what's the problem? Is she <i>not </i>supposed to practice her new insight into humanity? How is this stupid Pilgrimage even supposed to work?<br /> <br /> That's on her mind while she and Mark 5 dig up shrubs. Working with him doesn't suck. This feels more her speed than the dust-up at the parking lot, if she's being honest. She doesn't think of it as working toward the Pilgrimage. It's just...work. And there's no job too big for two golems, wait,what's that moving-<br /> <br /> Dymond's Disquieted screaming barely registers. Teeth, tongue, thorny spines, black bile- her guts churn- <i>oh god she made this. It's hers.</i><br /> <br /> Mark 5 seizes the initiative while she's stunned. Using those stony fists, <i>no no no, stupid hero-</i> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Mark, no, it's <i>hungry, </i>it <i>wants</i> you in close!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Her body sparks as she generates a charge inside herself. She's holding back, hoping she doesn't wreck the garden even worse.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Charging Arc with 1 Pyros. Spark, 7 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/503705\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>. 3 lethal damage before armor.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T11:54:44-07:00","id":1074775,"title":"","content":"<i>The Garden</i><br /> <br /> <b>Earth and Mark 5</b><br /> <br /> The wooden body of the abomination bends but doesn't break under Mark 5's flurry of fists, and it lets out a creaking warble of outrage, like a stiff breeze rushing through the trees and smashing branches together, creaking and moaning. The Unborn doesn't seem terribly perturbed by the Titan's onslaught, as it simply heaves itself forwards out of its hole, thorned roots clutching at the ground the way a drowning man grabs any plank in a storm. Earth hurls a thunderbolt that chars the creature's hide and sets it smouldering, but that doesn't seem to slow it in the slightest. Thorns dig into the off-balance Titan's limbs as the roots lash at his arms and legs, whipping back with black bile and flesh hanging off the cruel hooks and being threaded through snapping maws that greedily swallow every loose morsel. The creature seems overjoyed at what it tastes, rising up a little on the tentacles, preparing to launch itself forwards. It's tasted the sweet tang of Vitriol in your blood... and it's coming for it.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: The Pandoran <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=cc3cd10f\" target=\"_blank\">attacks Mark 5</a>. Its root-tentacles are a 1L weapon, so Mark 5 takes 3L damage and he is now grappled. The Pandoran also has 2/2 Armour, so after your attacks its Health looks like this:<br /> <br /> [B][B][B][ ][ ][ ][ ]<br /> <br /> \u200bYour move <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> \u200band <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> </i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 04-07-2017, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T15:18:15-07:00","id":1074876,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (1)<br /> Health: XXXXXXX/OO | Willpower: 2/6 | Pyros: 0/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 3/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 0</b></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Mark, no, it's <i>hungry, </i>it <i>wants</i> you in close!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <i>That so?</i> That's fine with him. Let it try. Iron will not give way to wood, even if its blood-rusted iron.<br /> Its attacks caused pain, like strings of burning fire on his skin, in his flesh - but he was a Titan. It did not debilitate him, it made him feel more of his body. And a Titan aware of his body is a dangerous one. He didn't even attempt to get away from the Pandoran. Rather, he did his best to tear into it, to rip it asunder.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Str+Brawl + WP + 1 (from Hygeius) = <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=f62f2d12\" target=\"_blank\">5 sux</a><br /> That would be two moves due to exceptional success if I am not mistaken. If so, move one is dealing Damage. Move two is holding him in place, so Earth gets a clean shot. Assuming the Thing doesn't get more successes, of course.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000080\">What are you waiting for? Shoot!&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T16:46:37-07:00","id":1074907,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Watched, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Disquieted (North End: Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 2/5 | Pyros: 2/12 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> It's not a vision, a memory, or a horrible dream: Mark 5 is getting eaten. But as long as he's wrestling the thing into submission, she might as well take her shot. Earth shocks the thorny mass again, and hopefully not her throngmate.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I forgot that I'd optimized Earth for fighting Pandorans, let's try a bigger dicepool for Arc this time. Dexterity 1+Athletics 3+Creatures of Flux specialty 2+Azoth 3+Willpower 3, 12 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/503795\" target=\"_blank\">4 successes</a>, 5 lethal damage before armor.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T20:34:48-07:00","id":1074970,"title":"","content":"<i>The Garden</i><br /> <br /> <b>Earth and Mark 5</b><br /> <br /> The Titan manages to overpower the creature, grabbing onto roots even as the thorns dig into his palms, pummelling it with fists that strike like heavy iron mauls, but the Unborn abomination <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=bce3c258\" target=\"_blank\">rises up</a>, roots wrapping around his arms and digging deep, long strips of flesh ripping as slick roots already wet with black bile soak in it some more, limbs carrying flensed sweetmeats into its many waiting mouths and more roots striking just as quickly to replace them. The creature is seemingly crawling up his body now, as the roots dig in, many mouths opening and closing, thorns catching on his clothing. You can feel the roots writhing under your skin, twinning around the bones of your arm and <i>squeezing</i>. It is going to suck every last piece of Pyros from his flesh, and then it's going to crack his corpse for Vitriol once it's done.<br /> <br /> Another lightning bolt streaks forwards, blasting away at the Unborn one, Earth's mistake come back to haunt her. It hits hard into its wooden flesh, and she can see it smoulder like charcoal as some lasting damage manages to blast it down. The creature lets out a warbling cry that falls flat as it suddenly goes limp, elongated limbs still embedded in the Titan's flesh. He is free, for the moment, as the creature, starting to calcify around the wounds, flesh flaking away like ash, sits in a daze as it is overwhelmed by the Flux of refined Torment. The largest mouth along its back (if this thing even has a back) <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=41bc8329\" target=\"_blank\">spasms</a>. The tongue of balled roots, thorned and slimy, lashes to and fro, and then it tears free, slithering from the back of the Unborn and moving as fast as it can towards the nearest source of Azoth it can find, a trail of black bile, mud, and bubbling Flux leaving a swathe of dead grass in its wake as its flesh glower with heat, still warping and twisting. Slithering towards Earth. She had seen this before, in her Pandoran pack, in the days of Earth-Dies-Screaming, when they were well-fed and exposed to her magnificence. The raw creative energy of Pyros couldn't sit still, it desired to create more life. There were <i>two </i>of them now. It <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=332099eb\" target=\"_blank\">lunges towards her,</a> coiling like a snake, a newfound maw tearing open from one end, eyes starting to open up along its length, beautiful, clear grey eyes. So grey they were almost silver, and glazed over with confusion and uncontrollable hunger. It flops wetly onto the ground, missing by a longshot as Earth flinches back away from it, recoiling, reassessing, gathering its bearings.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Mark 5 gets a Beat for the Exceptional Success, but it's no dice. The Pandoran kept a hold on him and it inflicts 6L damage, meaning he's at full Lethal and wrapped around into 4A damage. Things aren't looking good for him, but Earth inflicted enough damage to impose the Stunned Tilt (for the next five turns), so Mark 5 is no longer grappled. Get some distance. The new Pandoran doesn't have any Armour at the moment, but it has a full Health track and Initiative 9. So it's getting to act right now. Here's the Pandoran's Health at the moment:</i><br /> <br /> <i>[L][L][B][B][B][B][B]</i><br /> <br /> <i><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> Your move again.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 04-07-2017, 11:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T07:45:51-07:00","id":1075125,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (1)<br /> Health: AAAAXXXXXX | Willpower: 1/6 | Pyros: 0/11 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 3/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 0</b></div> <br /> <br /> Iron was stronger than Wood. But this wasn't wood, this was a Pandoran. To think otherwise, to underestimate it, had been a mistake. A horrible mistake, as Mark 5 realized when all his sapped might could not help him. The Titan's tortured body screamed at him to get away, screamed danger, screamed death. Never had he been this hurt, this much in pain.<br /> This close to an early end. The Pandoran held him in its grasp, ready to devour.<br /> Regret made its presence known again, though this time, he was regretting for his own sake. Then, a spark of hope.<br /> When Earth's lightning struck, he furiously punched at the thing, aware of every fiber in his being. He didn't fight a monster as a Hero. He simply fought as a man trying to survive.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Str+Brawl+3(Hygeius)+3(WP)-3(Defense)=<a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=c274843d\" target=\"_blank\">1 sux</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> His frantic attempts didn't achieve much, however, and once he realized it didn't have a hold of him any longer, scuttered to get away as far as possible. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Which would be 13 yards.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T09:05:00-07:00","id":1075141,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Watched, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Disquieted (North End: Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Arc (0), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 1/5 | Pyros: 2/12 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> For a second there, she hoped the Titan had overpowered the thing with raw strength. But as always, hope is a mistake. She tagged the creature too late to keep it from undergoing division, and now there was a fresh one in a hunger frenzy. And with such <i>beautiful</i> eyes.<br /> <br /> At least Mark 5 got the message, finally. She'd never seen him turn and run like that!<br /> <br /> She forced more Pyros into her Alembic, and her internal charge built up until her hair was wild with static. Gotta follow the lesson of the Vigilante: follow the code of punishment, even when she risks destroying the things that she's built. The garden's gonna have to be collateral damage.<br /> <br /> (and yet she holds back from going full thunderbird. the gardener is more precious to her than the vigilante.)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Putting 1 more Pyros into Arc. Moving such that I can hit both Pandorans and ignite some loose wood without hitting Mark 5. Dexterity 1+Athletics 3+Specialty 2+Azoth 3. 9 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/503941\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>.<br /> <br /> It's just charged to Shock, so everything within 9 yards takes 2+2 Lethal damage this turn.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T19:47:40-07:00","id":1075329,"title":"","content":"<i>The Garden</i><br /> <br /> <b>Earth and Mark 5</b><br /> <br /> The Titan, with panic, desperation, and pain, beat on the Unborn that had him limply in its grasp until the thorned roots tore free from his flesh and the thing slumped to the ground. Without his Transmutations, he had no doubt he would be in incredible agony right now, but with his alchemical insight into the body, pain is elevated into controlled bursts of adrenaline. He gets out of the way, moving towards the piles of old, weather-eaten beams that used to form the framework for a garden bed.<br /> <br /> The Fury stalks forwards towards her mistake, limply twisting on the ground, roots futilely digging into the mud, maws gaping like a landed fish, struggling to breathe. The newborn creature slithers after her, carefully reassessing and stretching its newfound mouth, opening and closing it, running a tongue that looked more like tar than wood along teeth of thorns, silvery eyes blinking in confusion and wonder and pain. So much pain.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It was <i>h\u0341\u0300\u0311\u0311\u0300\u030f\u0360\u0357\u0330\u031e\u033b\u034e\u0323\u0332\u0348\u0319u\u0357\u034a\u0342\u035b\u0314\u0312\u0303\u035d\u035a\u035c\u031d\u0348\u033a\u0332\u0324\u0326n\u0307\u030b\u033e\u0360\u034a\u030a\u0350\u0360\u0321\u0316\u035c\u0319\u033c\u0325\u0325 \u0359g\u0304\u031b\u031b\u0360\u0346\u0308\u0344\u0340\u033c\u0339\u0330\u034e\u031c\u033c\u0319\u034er\u030f\u034c\u0309\u0313\u0358\u0315\u0360\u0344\u0325\u0354\u0345\u0317\u0359\u034d\u0324\u0320y\u0315\u0342\u035d\u0357\u0342\u0304\u034c\u034b\u0348\u0318\u031e\u034e\u031e\u0347 \u032e\u0333</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The little creature slithers close, far too close, and Earth vents her rage. The charge gathers, setting her hair whipping about her head in a corona, until she releases it. It is the most measured and controlled use of her Transmutation that she can recall. She has always thrown lightning with the wild abandon of an outraged and particularly touchy god, but this was clean, this was pure, it was <i>controlled</i>. This was her Torment, refined into a white-hot spear, a weapon carefully honed, carefully forged, well-stored and left to build until it could be released. She lets loose, blasting the limply twitching Unborn and smiting the newborn with the full force of her might, its softer flesh charring, fat bubbling like bacon in a pan, skin peeling with a sound like popcorn as superheated air escapes. It writhes in pain, a high-pitched keening escaping as it lies limply in non-Euclidean coils, silvery eyes wide and afraid. A nearby pile of dead brush lights into flame, a small campfire, beautiful, creative.<br /> <br /> Cleansing.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Mark 5 takes another Beat for having damage in his rightmost Health box. The newborn Pandoran took damage in excess of its Stamina and it is Stunned for the next couple of turns. Nothing for Earth to worry about. Their Health, after the two separate attacks, looks like this:</i><br /> <br /> <i>Thorned Unborn: [L][L][L][L][L][B][B] Newborn: [L][L][L][L][ ][ ]<br /> <br /> The new fire is Size 2 (Bonfire) Heat +1 (Torch), so it would deal 3L per turn to a human... or 3A per turn to a Promethean or Pandoran. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> ball's back in your court.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T00:18:16-07:00","id":1075393,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (1)<br /> Health: AAAAXXXXXX | Willpower: 0/6 | Pyros: 0/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 3/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 0</b></div> <br /> Once Mark 5 got some distance, he calmed down a little. <i>If only I had recharged, if only I wasn't this stupid...</i> went through his head again and again, throwing him for a loop - until the wood caught fire.<br /> Something inside him went click. He grabbed a log on its unburning end, and forced himself to look at the monster<i>Face your fear</i>andtook careful aim.<br /> He threw the fire<i>burningwooditwasburningwoodnotfire</i>with the last of his strength, and sunk to his knees as it arced in it's flight.<br /> The Titan felt exhausted, depleted.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Dext+Ath-3Defense= <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=8980d351\" target=\"_blank\">2 sux</a><br /> +3 three dice from Hygeius I forgot about in the first roll= <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=5b150280\" target=\"_blank\">1 sux</a><br /> Total of 3 Successes for throwing burning wood at the Thorned Unborn</div></div> </div> </div><br /> But his aim was true. The wood struck with its burning end.<br /> Despite everything, that got a smile out of him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T08:03:13-07:00","id":1075482,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Watched, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Disquieted (North End: Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Arc (2), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 1/5 | Pyros: 1/12 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> Hey, that's not a bad idea. Earth scrambles after the big guy, clutches a sharp branch of burning brush with her bare hands, feels her flesh bubble and her spirit stir, and hurls the makeshift javelin at the newborn.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">3 aggravated damage and +3 Pyros.<br /> <br /> Dexterity 1+Athletics 3+Creatures of Flux specialty 2-Defense 2. 4 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/504171\" target=\"_blank\">fail</a>.<br /> <br /> Resist Torment from fire aggravated damage. Resolve+Composure 5-Azoth 3+Willpower 3. 5 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/504172\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes</a>. At least I got a beat for risking torment!</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T20:55:11-07:00","id":1075703,"title":"","content":"<i>The Garden</i><br /> <br /> <b>Earth and Mark 5</b><br /> <br /> The Unborn burn in the dirt and the mud, leaving behind nothing but ash. To people on the street attracted by the loud not-quite explosions of Earth's lightning, and the burns on her hands and forearms, with Mark 5 wrapped in a tarp to cover the worst of his injuries, it looks like an accident with accelerant using fairly common protocols for disposing of chaff within the city and outside city limits. Burning is usually the right idea, because it leaves ash that can be churned into the ground, give something back to the soil for next year. Mark 5 is too battered and exhausted to say, or do, much of anything right now, his Alembic and Created constitution basically the only things keeping him conscious. Divine Fire is hard to extinguish. All he can do is reflect on his brush with death and with pain. Earth can't feel her horrifically burnt hands and forearms, damaged more so from the inside out than outside in, as the Pyros in her humours catalyzed explosively in the presence of flame, sending her Azoth into overdrive, burning through her flesh to bring enlightenment and power.<br /> <br /> Dymond eventually comes out from the Ross House, bewildered and sweating. &quot;Oh, hey Earth, Mark. I... I don't know what happened, I just had to get out of here, you know? Thought I'd put my panic attack days behind me, but I guess not. Thanks for finishing up and, uh, leaving me to freak out in peace, I guess.&quot; The words sound honest but her face has a look of confusion, as if she's <i>missing </i>some critical details. (You are, Dymond. You missed an Unborn monstrosity crawling from the garden.)<br /> <br /> <i>\u200bOOC: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> now would be the time to go through Mark 5's thought process and decide if he's fulfilled the Soldier Role or not. Earth gains three points of Pyros and a Vitriol Beat. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> if Earth is going to shift to Cuprum, this would be a good time to go through that thought process and philosophical shift. This would be the end of the Interludes up until <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> rejoins and details what Adonis has been up to. Hopefully we'll get to the next Chapter, starting on December 21<sup>st</sup> at another Ramble at the Forks.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T22:11:19-07:00","id":1075734,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Enraged, Watched, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Disquieted (North End: Stage 1)<br /> Alembics: Arc (2), Imperatus (0), Weaponize (0), Redirect (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 0/5 | Pyros: 4/12 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As the monsters burn, but before any witnesses come, Earth sits silently next to the flames with Mark 5. She lifts her hand, fires her Alembic, and soothing silver lightning crackles out to him like a Tesla coil.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Putting 1 Pyros into Imperatus, then spending 2 Pyros to heal Mark 5 with Lightning Therapy. The stubborn SOB recovers 6 Lethal damage whether he wants to or not!</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> She can't bring herself to come clean about the indirect lacuna, drinking the Vitriol here. She just says: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;This was my fault.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> For all the work she's put into controlling her Torment, she still has effects on the world that she didn't plan. She doesn't care about herself- how could anyone?- so she doesn't try to do better. But her careless self-loathing almost got her and Mark 5 killed, not to mention wrecking the garden. She's pushed her Torment out. But where was it coming from?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I'm tired of being pissed off all the time.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She trudges to the center of her newly made zen garden, plops down, and thinks.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Let's use that new equipment. Wits 3+Composure 3+Equipment 3, 30 minutes per roll, target number 4.<br /> First: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/504298\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a><br /> Second: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/504299\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a><br /> Third: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/504300\" target=\"_blank\">6 successes</a>! I'll take the Informed (Cuprum) Condition.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So, the world sucks. The past is a wasteland. The Pilgrimage is fool's gold. She'll always be alone in the end. All she has is herself.<br /> <br /> Why not get to know her?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 04-10-2017, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T23:24:24-07:00","id":1075746,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0)<br /> Health: AAAAOOOOOO | Willpower: 0/6 | Pyros: 0/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 3/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 0</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Titan didn't fight the healing. He couldn't have, had he wanted to.<br /> He mumbled his thanks to Earth, and since her comment did not make much sense to him, simply shambled on to a quiet patch of dirt to lay down and rest.... and think.<br /> Never before, not even as a Martyr, had he been this close to his end. To his surprise, it was a dreadful sensation. The idea of not being anymore was, for all the pain and suffering his life was right now, horrifying.<br /> Mark 5, called into the world without his consent, into a life of misery and hate and exclusion, valued his life very, very much.<br /> How, then, could humans throw it away in the name of a mission?<br /> Simple: like himself, they didn't expect their life to end. That happened to other people. Like himself, the promise of glorious fights for justice pulled them in. However, he now knew that fighting monsters is not glorious at all. It is dirty, scary, painful, unseemly and all in all to be avoided. He had always wanted to fight a monster, to prove himself as a Hero (because that's what heroes do, right?!), and now that he did it... it was a bitter and painful experience. He learned something from it, alright, but he didn't experience the uplifting feelings he thought he would.<br /> <br /> As a Titan, he had always placed his power as his most important trait.<br /> Now he knew better. A soldier can be as strong as he wants to: just catch him in the right moment, when he is weak and hurt, and he will be easy prey, as will those he cared about. Raw strength is not nearly enough to ensure your own (and other's) safety.<br /> You need to <b>Be Prepared.</b><br /> Letting his bad conscience get the better of him nearly got himself killed, and who knows what would have happened to Earth after that thing would've fed on prime Titan?<br /> No. The Created's life is dangerous, and people were relying on him now. He was no longer alone, so Mark 5 had to make sure he would life up to that.<br /> This was an important lesson, he could feel it in his core. This is what Iron had to teach him. This is what it meant to be a Soldier: To be ready to fight at all times. That was the secret of how to defend yourself.<br /> But was Iron enough?<br /> He knew that sooner or later he would have to leave the Path he was set upon by his Progenitor. He knew what was left on the path.<br /> And Mark 5 did not feel very exemplary, with his showmanship of panic, self-pity, and recklessness. Maybe it was time to try something new?<br /> But, leaving the (emotional) comfort of Iron? A scary thought.<br /> <br /> Other thoughts crept up, too. The Tammuz realized with dread, that his feelings of panic and fear... those were the things his - the Breaker's victims went through, too. The horror of what he did gained a whole new dimension, now that he could empathize with them. However, there was an undeniable thrill in it, something that left all other experiences pale in comparison. A horrific thrill, scary and painful, yet he found himself returning to those thoughts due to some morbid fascination.<br /> <br /> What was he to do?<br /> Whatever it was, he was sure it would change everything.<br /> And there was one place where he might get answers. His mentors. Maybe Towne 8 had something that could help him?<br /> The Soldier resolved to go take a look - when he was healed up. When he was prepared. So, he got up and went looking for a source to use.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There had to be more to Heroes than fighting monsters. There just HAD to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 04-10-2017, 02:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T10:49:03-07:00","id":1075963,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama LTD), Inspired (Azoth), Inspired (Alchemy)<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 3/6 | Pyros: 5/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b></div><br /> Scout had to admit, he'd been few places as amazing as the Millennial Library. When he found Tom, he gave the man his best smile, which wasn't saying much, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Thank you for your assistance in this matter. I have some potentially helpful things, knowledge to share, if you wish it.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> cout produced a copy of his own journal. Every note he'd taken on the pilgrimage, the map that Highwinds and later himself, had made of their travels and finds, every Ramble either of them had recorded. It was all within those pages, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Knowledge is for sharing. That is why humans build libraries, isn't it? This is all the knowledge that I have to trade with you- including notes on my Elpis visions, and some interesting analysis of Centimani and Firestorms. If you ever choose Plumbum, this may help you.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> It was an offer, but Scout didn't push too hard. People had to make the steps forward on their own. At the very least he hoped that a copy of his journal would be something that Tom would like in trade for the assistance he was offering.<br /> <br /> The knowledge he gained was fascinating. He'd understood some of the core tenants of old time alchemy, but the entire chymical wedding piece was something in and of itself. The <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Order of the Golden and Rosy Cross was most fascinating- perhaps these early alchemists were on to something. He'd been thinking of Olmec as a piece of himself that was removed, but in this light, it made him wonder if perhaps it wasn't removed at all- just not visible from where he now stood, and the Elpis vision had acted as a sort of... mirror that allowed him to see.<br /> <br /> No, mirror wasn't the right word. The Firestorm Elpis had been a microscope that allowed him to exam himself from without. Humans sometimes spoke of out of body experiences. Was that what he was having in that moment? It was plausible. Especially with all the talk of the Chymical Wedding he was reading about. Much of what was said also reminded him of his current condition. Being a single person of two bodies with the divine fire inside... the only difference was that the divine fire burned instead of a soul, and granted him alchemical prowess. He shook his head. Tom's voice brought him forth from reverie.<br /> <br /> &quot;</span></span><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Social alchemy... fascinating. Thank you so much Tom.</span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot; He reached out and put a hand on Tom's shoulder, &quot;</span></span><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I have looked within for so long, it is hard to look without at times. But I know someone who's good at this sort of thing. I will send you notes on any insights I achieve post-haste.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> He shouldn't have been so worked up over Tom handing over his own journal but... no one had ever given Scout anything before. Much less such a work of art as this book. The copy of his journal felt so barren now, looking over Tom's sketches. He gave Tom an awkward hug, then straightened up, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Thank you, Tom. I'll forward any other notes I have to this library. I'll mention you and the Library at the next ramble- perhaps in time, we can create our own secret little library within a library. That would be... nice.</span>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T07:55:50-07:00","id":1077738,"title":"","content":"<i>The Forks</i><br /> <br /> <b>Evening-</b> Wednesday December 21<sup>st</sup><br /> <br /> The Ramble normally gathers on Friday nights, but the Winter Solstice is a special date for the Created. It's been passed word of mouth and in Pilgrim Marks from Created to Created across the city. Special meeting, come if you can. The Created have no religious observances beyond those they put together themselves, they have no unifying faith or creed, they have the philosophies of the Refinements to help identify kindred spirits, and they have the tenuous tangled family trees of Lineage to look back on. But still, the turn of the earth around the sun <i>means</i> something to them. All of them know that the sun is a symbol of the Flame Immortal, and of the New Dawn. They feel their humours invigorate whenever dawn breaks. But as winter deepens, the nights lengthen, and the Saturnine Night seems deeper and blacker than ever.<br /> <br /> There is comfort to be found in fellow Pilgrims. Azothic candles shining into the darkness.<br /> <br /> Winter has finally come to the (in)famously frigid city. The many rivers are frozen over, snow blankets the city. Night has already fallen, and the pale purples and deep blues of twilight colour the night sky, the <a href=\"https://i.reddituploads.com/ef31487593eb46b68211b05077a174ea?fit=max&amp;h=1536&amp;w=1536&amp;s=c7b0b68aef8e534e13eb4848d410ac26\" target=\"_blank\">moon shining luminously silver behind a pale shroud of clouds</a>. The cityscape seems to <i>glow</i> from the distant vantage point of the riverbank, the heat of people living and working streaming bright mist into the heavens. A few stars, bright enough to be seen above the blazing bonfire of humanity, wink down. Rigel, brightest star of Orion, is framed by the southwest armature, and the aeolian harp moans with a different pitch, the metal frigid with frost.<br /> <br /> You can see <b>Satin</b> in the crowd, wearing a heavy winter coat. Antique keys have been tied anywhere they could fit, and when the sleeves ride up you can still see the ribbons, different coloured ones than before, wrapped around their arms. A necklace of strange and various charms are around their neck, and the mist that is <i>always</i> around them seems thicker due to the cold, and you think you can see... things... moving through it. They offer a crooked smile and wave to Earth.<br /> <br /> Sitting cross-legged in the snow with the other Tammuz is <b>Tom Barebones</b>, wearing precisely what Scout last saw him in, except he is wearing a heavy sweater now, and more scarves. The coat seems thicker, as if it has been stuffed with something. You can see him, scribbling away on a smaller notepad (nothing so precious as his sketchbook) testing out sentences, listening to his tape recorder, and when he's filled a page, tearing it out and stuffing it in the lining of his jacket. Tom is warming himself with words.<br /> <br /> When someone is ready, they will speak, but for now, the Ramble is enjoying each other's company. If there is news to share, it can wait until after they've cast light into the Saturnine Night, and offered what comfort they can.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Everyone has completely refreshed their Pyros and Willpower pools, and are fully healed. Mark 5 has gained a dot of Pilgrimage and a Vitriol Experience. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> you can choose another Alembic from Vitality and another Alembic from Corporeum.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T11:24:05-07:00","id":1077815,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Patient, Watched, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Informed (Cuprum)<br /> Alembics: Verto (0), Stereo Humor (0), Arc (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 12/12 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> Earth has been noticeably more chill for the last couple days. It's weird, even to her. But at least no one's been electrocuted!<br /> <br /> She came with the rest of the throng, but she's been sitting and watching more than talking. Seeing Satin sparks her interest enough to head over. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;You're looking witchier than ever. How's the ghost world look tonight?&quot;</span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T14:00:11-07:00","id":1077907,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Charites (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0), Unfettered (0)<br /> Health:OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 11/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 0</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This was... nice.<br /> Mark 5 didn't know if he deserved something like that, but he enjoyed the comfort of the others. It made him feel less alone, and it certainly made him feel more ready to tackle problems.<br /> <br /> The cold weather didn't bother him really, so he wore the same things he always did: black shirt and a pair of jeans. People recently started looking at him funny, so he carried a worn, dirty old mantle someone discarded under his arm. Out there, the Created had to fit in. But here, he didn't need to hide himself, like he does when he goes out as the Breaker.<br /> Unlike last time, he was less at rest at the Ramble. He was... looking for someone. Searching. But he didn't know who he was looking for - and neither did he know how to approach them and ask them.<br /> So if he could not find one, he'd just do the same as last time, and would speak to the whole of them. Maybe someone among them could help. Maybe - hopefully - there was a Light-Bringer among them.<br /> He just hoped his other message would not ruin his chances.<br /> <br /> For now, he just enjoyed the company. He waved at any Promethean he knew, and everyone that seemed friendly or unusual.<br /> He greeted some of them with a slightly-off jovial <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Hi. I am Mark 5. How are you?&quot; </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T18:44:25-07:00","id":1078081,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent; Katerina, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress, Stage 1), Callous<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 10/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 1/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b><br /> </div> <br /> Adonis returns to his apartment at the day's end. He thinks back over the events of this insane day: inflicting Disquiet on the waitress, finding Mark 5 amidst the shredded corpses of the IC members, and the brawl that had erupted between him and Earth as a result. The end result of the battle he had prevented a month ago, the flood he had tried to hold back a month ago. He had known that a full-on fight between the two Named would be terrible to see, but he hadn't expected a <i>Firestorm</i>, to feel his blood turn to acid and feel an awful excitement at it. <br /> <br /> He had tried to stop the fight again, endangered himself when Earth's fury was at its greatest. And seemingly, the Divine Fire had rewarded him for it. He had felt more confident, like his gold had been put into a crucible, and come out all the better for it. But he had lessened himself almost- he had turned his blood to ice water to make Katerina compliant and useful. And she was, no doubt about it- if they ever needed an ally on the police force, all he would have to do would be to talk to her and she would do anything in her power for them. She was the perfect in. So why did that bother him? The crowds of people he passed every day... even Erwin... tools or obstacles to be manipulated as he saw fit. He hadn't been this way last time yesterday. He had done it to himself by letting his Azoth scorch himself, rather than Katerina. He had to undo it, but how? How did he <i>let it go</i>?<br /> <br /> Adonis slams his mattress in frustration. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Fuck!&quot; </span> <hr />The days and nights he spends with Erwin are... nice. He knows Erwin cares about him, maybe even loves him. He can fake the emotion, but it's so hollow. But he's happy for any contact with a human who actually likes him, one who seems resistant to Disquiet. He frequently steers their conversations towards learning more about Amalgama: who the employees are, what everybody is like. He even visits him during the work day, getting the lay of the land and a sense of the atmosphere. <i><span style=\"color:#00ff00\">Tie up this loose end. End this threat. So long as Amalgama is operational in Winnipeg, we are all in danger. </span></i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis will attempt to get more information from Erwin about Amalgama, in anticipation of bringing down the Winnipeg branch of the company. He'll be attempting ten Social Maneuvering rolls on Erwin, as an extended action over the course of the Interlude to represent time spent with Erwin. Manipulation 3 + Persuasion 3 + Area of Expertise 2 = 8 dice. <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/506147\" target=\"_blank\">5 successes</a>, <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/506148\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>, <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/506149\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes,</a> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/506150\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>, <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/506151\" target=\"_blank\">6 successes</a>, <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/506152\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>, <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/506153\" target=\"_blank\">4 successes</a>, <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/506154\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes</a>, <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/506155\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes</a>, <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/506157\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes</a>. If that doesn't get Adonis plenty of information he can use on Amalgama, I don't know what will. <br /> <br /> I'll also spend that normal Experience to get a dot of True Friend for Erwin. I also realized that I needed another Aspiration, so I want to add &quot;Bring down Amalgama in Winnipeg&quot; as Adonis' new Aspiration.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T14:57:58-07:00","id":1080025,"title":"","content":"<b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama LTD), Inspired (Azoth), Inspired (Alchemy)<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 3/6 | Pyros: 5/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b><br /> <br /> Scout had spent every day after meeting with Tom planning. He'd spent a solid day on how to get back to Old Mexico and where he should look. Another on what to do about the situation with Amalgama. The next day was nothing but reviews about what he'd learned in that day with Tom Barebones. By the time the Ramble came around, everyone had at least suffered through some of Scout's unusual talkative moments. He'd practically demanded that after the Ramble he speak with Adonis about the notes Tom had given him.<br /> <br /> As he arrived at the Ramble, however, Scout had gone quiet again. His outfit hadn't changed much- a blue hoodie sweater that made a strange face with dark eyes, large white teeth, and long floppy ears when it was pushed over his head. One of the people at The Salvation Army had said it looked cute, but when he put it on and looked up at her, she'd given him this strange look then bustled off. The hood was pulled up, and he wandered over to his fellow Nepri, listening to them. He waved at Tom when he saw him, but didn't approach him right away. He was supposed to get to know more of his fellow Nepri- or at least, he thought that sounded like what he was supposed to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8122,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","user":"ArchonAres","date":". 05-10-2017, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T12:17:41-07:00","id":1080479,"title":"","content":"<b>Adonis</b><br /> <br /> For now, Erwin seems to be holding out against Disquiet, but you have no idea if it's a side effect of his alchemical experimentation, or a matter of will to maintain the relationship against the scorching obsession of the Flame Immortal. He already knows that Erwin is likely working for Amalgama under duress, and one evening, when he first turns his callous and analytical mind towards the problem, turning the charm onto Erwin, it seems like a dam simply gave way under the pressure of his discontent. Erwin starts telling him everything, about how the company was more mercenary than he had let on, how working for them as a 'consultant' was the only way to reverse the cash flow from spending absurd amounts of money getting materials he needed, how the pharmaceuticals were mostly just good press and padding for their shadier corporate mercenary contract dealings. He'd seen some files. They were willing to do anything... for the right price.<br /> <br /> When Amalgama first got their hooks into him, Erwin was working on something he called Crucible Theory, the idea that the body's immune systems reacted viscerally and unusually to certain biologically active chemical compounds, working its way into immunological memory, and would eventually be passed along to the organism's offspring. The results, Erwin proposed, could be fantastical, but nothing that much stranger than what the body could <i>already</i> do. It almost got him kicked out of med school. He experimented on himself with spagyrics and tinctures, he looked into biological uses of different metals and how that could affect the results, he even (he said this with a chuckle) looked into alchemical practices. When he finally started getting real results, Amalgama scalped him. Erwin finally realized what he was telling his boyfriend, and clammed up. Amalgama was <i>dangerous</i>, he's seen his coworkers, and the higher-ups in the company, can do <i>impossible </i>things; things that Erwin had never even <i>dreamed</i> of being able to accomplish with Crucible Theory.<br /> <br /> The next couple of days, with little success, Adonis gets nowhere with his boyfriend. He even shows up at his workplace, only for Erwin to quickly, and in something of a protective panic, ushers him out of the building almost immediately, though security gives Adonis something of a peculiar look. But, finally, Adonis gets Erwin to open up again. It seems the alchemist has been plotting an escape from Amalgama, and wants to hurt them on his way out. Turn over as much information on their... peculiar and illegal activities to the government as he can. Adonis has convinced him that he can be trusted, and so Erwin and Adonis conspire together.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Adonis gains the Informed (Amalgama LTD) Condition and the Steadfast Condition.<br /> <br /> The Forks</i><br /> <br /> <b>Satin</b> grins at their Named acquaintance, pulling back the hood on their parka and readjusting their braid, offering a hand to shake &quot;It's good to see you Earth, we haven't seen much of you all here on the Friday meetings. Figured you all wanted to space. Been hearing some interesting rumours going around the city about someone calling themselves Darkstorm- the tags look a lot like Pilgrim Marks. That wouldn't happen to be you, would it?&quot;<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, <b>Mark 5 </b>found himself mingling with the other Named that were there by a carving of a lion. They are among the most numerous Lineage, and each have their own peculiar markings and tattoos, for they have all been inscribed with the Word that brought them from the fires of the Principle and into life. <b>Tom Barebones</b>, something of an isolated recluse, is curled up with his notepad and tape recorder, while the other Tammuz share stories. He sees a newcomer, sitting in the middle, a little girl in a filthy white dress, caked in hardened red clay that moves like flesh even though it possesses the durability of terracotta. She seems to be sharing her own Ramble, with the other Named taking her Measure. She isn't obviously inscribed, but where the clay is cracked, flaking, and missing, you can see writing on the underside of the clay.<br /> <br /> And <b>Scout</b> has mingled in with the other Nepri, aloof and intellectual, trading bits of folklore, testing the keenness of one another's minds. There is a particular tall man, gaunt and with a shaved head and large, square, curly beard. His skin is a deep dark blue, and he wears a long canvas coat, his chest bound in bandages, arms crossed. This is <b>Solomon</b>, senior-most Osirian in the city, and a (relatively) well-known Cathar. Impurity is the focus of his study, and the intimate knowledge of how easily people are manipulated, and how they can break socially and psychologically, has left him a little disillusioned, but he isn't going to turn from the Pilgrimage. He needs <i>context</i>. &quot;Eagle Scout,&quot; he says pleasantly &quot;nice to see you again. I put the word out that Highwinds' child was looking for a way down south, and hopefully people will get back to us soon. Pilgrims need to help each other along the road.&quot; He notices the normally taciturn Scout practically bursting with energy and raises an eyebrow &quot;Well? What is it. Obviously you've got something you want to share.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T06:08:29-07:00","id":1080857,"title":"","content":"<b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama LTD), Inspired (Azoth), Inspired (Alchemy)<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 3/6 | Pyros: 5/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b><br /> <br /> Scout was anxious at being addressed, and bit his lip- a habit he'd picked up from a movie.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well... you may have heard about a recent Firestorm in the city. I had the opportunity to observe it, and received an Elpis vision for my pain.&quot;<br /> <br /> Scout paused and looked around to see if anyone else was listening, &quot;I saw a rebis. It, like everything caught in the storm, was in pain. Marred by torment and flux. It helped me see how to stop the Firestorm.&quot;<br /> <br /> Scout stopped again, looking nervous. This was a big claim, but soothing the Torment of Olmec had stopped the Firestorm, he was certain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8122,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","user":"ArchonAres","date":". 05-10-2017, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T11:00:34-07:00","id":1083092,"title":"","content":"<b>Earth</b> shakes. Weird ritual, but she likes it. Physical communication instead of words feels right.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;We've been dealing with our own stuff. Humans started calling me Darkstorm after I vented in the North End for a few weeks, and I went along with it. People have called me all kinds of things. I think it says more about the namer than the Named. Like, I guess Darkstorm is a thunderbird wearing a human mask? I dunno where they got that. Have you ever met a thunderbird?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I've been thinking I wanna hang up that name. I've emptied out all my Pandorans into the world, and I haven't looked at what's left in the box without Torment. All I've ever known is Stannum, though. I was built for Ferrum, screwed that up. Heh. And I was a Fury on either side of the big lacuna. I haven't really seriously tried a different Refinement.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> She scratches behind her ears. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;You're...what are you, Satin? Silver?&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T12:39:22-07:00","id":1084637,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Charites (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0), Unfettered (0)<br /> Health:OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 11/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 0</b></div> <br /> <br /> The Titan looked at the lion for a while. He could always appreciate craftsmanship, even though he was more of a wood-guy himself.<br /> He was really stalling, though, and once he realized that, became annoyed with himself. Despite wanting to talk to Tom Barebones (he was smart, he knew a lot, surely he'd be able to help), he didn't go to him immediately.<br /> The newcomer seemed intriguing.<br /> And so, he went and joined the other Tammuz and listened to her tales.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T20:59:23-07:00","id":1088616,"title":"","content":"<i>The Forks</i><br /> <br /> When <b>Scout </b>makes his announcement, the local Nepri get very, very still. <b>Solomon </b>takes a half step forwards, crossing his arms across his chest, his head at a quizzical tilt, eyes narrowed. &quot;That so, Eagle Scout? Big claim, that. How did you do it? What alchemy did you draw on?&quot; Some of the others are muttering to one another. At least one or two seem to have heard of a rebis before. One Nepri without a tongue is texting with elegantly swift fingers to a companion, who is staring intently at the screen of their own phone, nodding, and typing back, far more slowly, as they appear to be missing a finger or two. He has their attention, now he needs to keep it. Trial by fire.<br /> <br /> <b>Satin </b>flashes <b>Earth</b> a proud smile. You can see their teeth are a little bit crooked, but it fits. Satin is silk, butterfly and spider, and they live hard. There's bound to be frayed edges, places where the world tried to rip and tear, but Satin is still here. The things that tried to shred them are not. &quot;Damn. You certainly don't let the stories do the heavy lifting on your reputation, do you? Can't say I've met a thunderbird, but I haven't wandered far enough west to say for sure. Seen a lot of weird things on my road though, I've danced for the dead and in the shadow of the world, and I've danced where thorns would tear at your soul, but when they tried to grab hold all they got was burned.&quot; A fierce little smirk, a glow of triumph in their eyes &quot;Silver is right, good guess, so I'm more of a moon person than a sun person, even if the Fire blazes hotter when dawn breaks. Who knows, maybe that will change. Maybe I'll give gold a try after this, but gold is a soft metal, and I am not soft. Not sure I ever want to be.&quot; Satin pauses, thinking, and gives Earth a serious up and down, looking intently at Earth's palm in the one hand they have a hold of, as if seeing something no one else can.<br /> <br /> &quot;You've tilled yourself well, but you need to know the soil before you plant the garden. Learning the Earth, eh? Moving to Copper? That's good. New is good. Change is good. Onwards towards the dawn is good. Just take care of yourself. You look close enough and <i>anyone</i> can find imperfections. Just... don't stare too hard at yourself, alright? Promise me you'll take care of yourself Earth?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Titan <b>Mark 5 </b>stands amongst his kin, and listens to the newcomer, so small and doll-like, but radiating a decent amount of Azothic heat. It might be her Inscription giving off a bit of a burn to give weight to her words, and you can see the exposed writing glower a bit, but it might just be that the little Golem is hiding a potent furnace in that tiny body. She chose the name Isla, she was saying, because everyone is an island; she read that at the Manitoba Museum, it was on one of the first signs. She didn't know who her genitor (or Demiurge) was, just that they had been ever so careful to wrap her in clay, inscribe her in a way she couldn't see. Were they ashamed of what they wrote? Was she not meant to see it? Isla doesn't know, but she keeps every piece of her shell that breaks off. Woke up in a coffin underground and stayed there for a good long while, hammering away until the seal cracked and the loose dirt let her swim to the surface. She's made her own way for many a long day now, she's not sure how long, careful to bury herself back up in the earth every night. The earth is supposed to be the mother of the first humans, isn't it? And what kind of girl would she be if she stayed away from mother. She keeps trying to go to a school, but she can never quite pull off being a &quot;kid&quot;. It's hard enough figuring out humans, how was Isla to know that humans thought they were different at different ages? From what Isla can tell, it's a load of crap, people are people, but it matters to the humans, so it's the sort of thing she wants to know.<br /> <br /> She came to the Ramble hoping someone could tell her about parents and siblings. A Muse, maybe, who had given it a shot, or gotten up close.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T12:23:25-07:00","id":1089310,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent; Katerina, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress, Stage 1), Callous<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 10/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 1/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b><br /> <br /> </div> At the Ramble, Adonis leaves the others to mingle as they wish. He sees Earth talking to Satin, the Ulgan. Does Earth have feelings for Satin? Even with the effects of the Divine Fire turning his blood cold, he has never found another Created attractive. He has marveled at the construction of some, but in the same way humans admire the artistry of a stone statue. Maybe it was a consequence of Sharon making him for the purpose of being her lover, or because of his Refinement of Aurum. He doesn't judge Earth for any fascination she has for Satin. <br /> <br /> He walks over to the other Muses, and spreads his hands in greeting. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">\u200b&quot;Hello, everybody. It's been a while. Some of you may have heard about what my Throng has been up to in the past few weeks.&quot; </span>He launches into a retelling of the events of the Firestorm- Mark 5's murderous rampage, Earth's violent response, his own attempt to stop them, the horror of the mutations, the small voice that whispered to him afterwards. He leaves out the part about his arousal at the effects of Flux on his body, and how Earth attacked Mark 5 even as he tried to shield her from the monster of his vision. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;I feel different. Like my time in Aurum may be coming to an end soon, and something is starting to show through. The members of my Throng... they need guidance. I feel like more and more, I am trying to preserve their progress on the Pilgrimage. Is there anyone among us who has taken Bronze?&quot; </span>After the Muses answer, he licks his lips. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;There's something else. I feel cold, cousins.&quot; </span>He explains the encounter with Katerina, the way he hid his Disfigurements and froze his blood. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Any Mimics or Cathars here who know how to deal with this? Please. I have a... a boyfriend. And I don't want to keep treating him like a tool.&quot;</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T06:37:49-07:00","id":1090706,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama LTD), Inspired (Azoth), Inspired (Alchemy)<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 3/6 | Pyros: 5/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b></b></div><br /> <br /> Scout nodded slowly at that. Okay that was a good sign. &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I... drew upon the same energies that my fellow Originists do. As I can calm the torment of a Promethean and drive the flux from his flames, and had done so moments prior to this Firestorm on Mark V,</span>&quot; Scout paused to point out Mark V for the record, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">So did I call upon it in that moment of clarity. As I watched the Rebis, twisted in agony, I reached out with my energy and sought to calm the Torment within it, and drive out it's flux. I wasn't even sure it would do anything to the firestorm, at first. But then Olmec reacted to me, and spoke to me, and the firestorm subsided. It promised me wisdom, and spoke of how to progress along the path.</span>&quot; he paused, then shrugged as he considered an alternative, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I suppose it's entirely possible it was Olmec that ended the firestorm once it's torment was ended. But I cannot know for certain until I speak with them again.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Scout waited now, to see how the others reacted to this information. He liked to believe his actions had directly ended the firestorm, but there was the off chance that Olmec had done so once it had been freed. He hadn't thought of that before now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T15:30:14-07:00","id":1092541,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Patient, Watched, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Informed (Cuprum)<br /> Alembics: Verto (0), Stereo Humor (0), Arc (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 12/12 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> Earth nods slowly with wide eyes at the <i>dance for the dead-shadow of the world-thorns tearing souls </i>bit. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I dunno what half of that meant, but it's badass. Whenever I listen to you talk about your world, I get this feeling like...fuck humanity, man. I want what you have so, so bad. Aurum is fool's gold. You've seen what's <i>real.</i> You shine better in the dark, anyway.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Satin's doing a palm reading. Earth, terror of the Manitoba plains, is slowly turning red. The Ulgan's words are buzzing and not really registering all the way, in the way that words fade away for Named when something more important is happening. She says: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;You're still holding my hand.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Her humors are out of balance, so blood rushing to her face and heart is hard to process. Hopeless melancholic black bile is easier to fall back on. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I'm <sub>uh-</sub> probably being a fucking moron <sub>like always-</sub> but if you're trying to tell me you <sub>uh,</sub>want something- it's not good to get close to me like that. I hurt my last girl really, really bad. Tying my chain to somebody else won't help me change. This'll only work if the only one I'm letting down is me. So- no promise. Bye.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> With her cheeks and brow hot in the dark, Earth pulls her hand back, shoves it in her jacket, and scurries off to the riverbank. <b>Cool! Gold star! Great job! Embodying the Hermit!</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T07:17:24-07:00","id":1093230,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Charites (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0), Unfettered (0)<br /> Health:OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 11/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 0</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> Mark 5 listened to the tale, and found himself reminiscing about those very first days, when all was confusion, and nothing made sense.<br /> He hadn't realized it so far, but he DID make progress on his Pilgrimage, didn't he? He had learned so much about humans.<br /> Maybe, he will even learn what it truly means to be human one day.<br /> Not knowing about your inscription, though? That was hard. The Tammuz imagined not knowing his Inscription - SURVIVOR- and what'd mean for him.<br /> He shook his head. Poor thing. He remembered how he learned about how his body works, how the muscles function, let him move. All he had to do was pry them free, and what little pain he endured had been well worth it. So, Mark 5 apporached Isla:&quot;<span style=\"color:#000080\">Have you tried pricking the clay off, to look at what lies beneath?&quot;</span><br /> The Titan has a smattering of experience to share when it came to humans, too: <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Kids are small humans. Their bodies are weaker, more frail. You will often see adults and old humans try to shape the new ones, to give them form, make them learn something. Like when you take a piece of wood, and carefully carve it into something that is useful, or fun to look at. And that takes time, which is why they are sad if something happens to the small ones. That's at least part of why they are treated differently.&quot;</span><br /> If he was honest, he didn't know what the other parts were. He had to think about how someone spend a lot of time in shaping the ones he broke, and his mood fell again. Searching for a Muse? Well, there was a Muse he could direct her towards, couldn't he? &quot;<span style=\"color:#000080\">I know a Muse. The name's Adonis.&quot; </span>He pointed the Muse out.<span style=\"color:#000080\"> &quot;If you want to talk to him, tell him Mark 5 sent you. Maybe he can answer some of your questions.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> With that, the Titan sat down, and waited for his turn. He'd talk about some things, about the Torment, about the massacre he commited, about the Firestorm and his Vision. Then he'd go see Tom Barebones, he told himself.<br /> For now, thoughts bubbled in his head. Parents and siblings and children worried sick somewhere, waiting for someone to come home... who will never come back. Because he made it so. Not only did he take their lifes - he'd harmed others, too! Was that more guilt he'd have to carry?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T21:02:30-07:00","id":1095012,"title":"","content":"<i>The Forks</i><br /> <br /> <b>Adonis</b> has never really mingled with his Lineage here before, but he certainly wasn't expecting them to all be so... different. Beauty is in the eye of the beholder, but would you really want to see through the gazes that had crafted such a beautiful and grotesque chorus? There is a man built to be the ideal for certain men, built not for love, but for adoration, a muscle-bound hulk ready to burst his skin, folding carefully the paper in his hand over and over until it becomes something new. There is an androgynous child with curled ringlets, a perfect wig sewn into their scalp with tiny sutures from translucent deep sea fishing line who looks like they've been living hard intentionally, trying to look less like a doll. A woman whose body is covered in razor-thin scars, nip here, tuck there, shave bone, inject silicone. An unfinished canvas that tore itself from a perfectionist who would never be finished. Men built by women, built for dexterity and tenderness, holding themselves tight as it afraid to fall apart. A woman, classically statuesque in her beauty, cyanosis at her lips, on her eyelids, her fingertips. Blood pooled and hardened in erogenous zones, a perpetual violet flush. A scarf around her neck. There are, after all, so few ways to die beautiful. People born for others who try to live for themselves, perfume-sweet hair and poison-heavy breath.<br /> <br /> The musclebound hulk steps forwards. He is... enormous. Bigger than any human Adonis has ever seen. Bigger than any <i>Created</i> Adonis has ever seen, and there are some pretty big Golems and Wretches out there. His voice rumbles like distant thunder, but it is quiet. As if once upon a time he did nothing but yell, until he learned what it did to others, and is frightened of the sound of his own voice. Each phrase is short and clipped, like he's preventing his chest from billowing out and accidentally roaring. &quot;I am <b>Jax</b>. I am a Sentry. I can teach, if you will learn.&quot;<br /> <br /> A <a href=\"http://images.radiotimes.com/namedimage/American_Gods_mythology_guide__Who_is_Bilquis__Queen_of_Sheba_and_goddess_of_love_.jpg?quality=85&amp;mode=crop&amp;width=620&amp;height=374&amp;404=tv&amp;url=/uploads/images/original/136240.861db352-f6d3-4274-8d0f-e9f29a8ca728.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">woman</a> speaks up from the ground with quiet command in a red silk dress, &quot;You burned yourself cousin. The alchemy wants out, the Fire wants to burn. All transmutations produce byproducts,&quot; she waves faintly &quot;and if not Disquiet then an imbalance of your own humours. You want the blood to run again, chase it where it flows. Indulge that feeling, disregard the humans around you, they do it all the time. Learn from your weakness.&quot; Her cold silver eyes, sitting behind bruised lids, are alight, &quot;I can help you find someone, if you want. I know where to find people who would worship you. But, there is another way. I am a Cathar. I know the alchemy to get inside your head, make it go away. Let me in?&quot;<br /> <br /> When <b>Earth </b>starts talking <b>Satin </b>doesn't say anything. They just stand and wait for the Named to be done. They've dealt with Pariahs before, you can just tell. The Ramble lets Earth go, but that's the way of it. They all know what it's like to need time to yourself, whether that's due to Torment, Refinement, or mood, and no one begrudges Earth the space. It is just Earth and the Red River, nearly black under the night sky, starting to freeze over. But Earth knows that in the daylight it is brown with mud and silt. The city is named for it; Winnipeg, Muddy Waters. Muddy, opaque, cyclical, predictable, wild. That is the nature of the Red. Maybe it isn't just Earth and the River. Maybe it is just Earth and their reflection.<br /> <br /> The Titan approaches <b>Isla </b>and the little Golem looks scared when Mark 5 suggests that she pick off the clay that covers her body &quot;I-I can't read.&quot; There's a little hiccupy sob &quot;And no one I've met knows what it says. I've kept every piece in this bag,&quot; she hefts a backpack that was resting in the snow, purple with a face on it &quot;but it isn't big enough for all of me... I don't know what I'll do when it all goes away.&quot; Mark 5 explains what little he knows of adult attitudes towards children, and Isla makes a face that is difficult to read, but might be disgust, you think. &quot;Shape them, like whoever made us?&quot; She seems angry with that, muttering under her breath- <i>stupid, so stupid, doesn't make any sense </i>&quot;Why can't they shape <i>themselves</i>,&quot; her voice doesn't come out as a whine, the way you'd expect, but a kind of frustrated anguish &quot;<i><b>we</b> </i>have to. We <i>all</i> have to, all of us Pilgrims. We shape ourselves, and then we make it to Dawn, and then what? What will I have? People who will just want something from me? People who will try to tell me what to be, how to change?&quot; She sits herself down, fuming a little, staring in irritation at the backpack.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'll go see your friend when I'm ready.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Nepri around <b>Scout </b>listen intently, and <b>Solomon </b>raises an eyebrow at the name 'Olmec' but none of them question it. The Created live in a world of alchemy and miracles, so what's another incredible story? They've all learned that it's safer, and far more polite, to shut up, briefly believe, and discuss doubts in private with those they trust later. Solomon uncrosses his arms, and instead places them in his pockets, looking thoughtfully at the pint-sized Osirian.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, damn, Eagle Scout. Not a bad feather to stick in your cap. You saw this Rebis when Elpis had you? You <i>do </i>know what you see when Elpis has your eyes, right? It's the Fire, the Azoth, coming from the inside. It talks to you. What makes you so sure that, uh, 'Olmec', isn't just you? Why try and talk to it again?&quot; He pauses, thinking. &quot;Highwinds ever talk about the Concordance?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T23:47:36-07:00","id":1095388,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Charites (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0), Unfettered (0)<br /> Health:OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 11/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 0</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> Mark 5 sat down opposite to her. He pitied the small Golem, because he well remembered the time letters didn't make sense to him. Oh, what a pain it was: Messages everywhere, and only he was excluded! Isolation is horrible thing. And oh, what a revelation reading proved to be - that X-Men Comic had been life-changing!<br /> He wonders about books though - he always lost interest after the first few pages. Why anyone would read them was beyond him. Comics were far better. But then, a comic only took him an hour or two, and they told a whole story. A book was wordy, and within an hour or two he would have very little of a story.<br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000080\">That won't do, you need to learn it. Reading is so very helpful. It is hard at first, but it gets easier. May I take a look at your Words?&quot;</span><br /> He knew that there were different languages. Maybe this was in a different language?<br /> The Titan took note of the indignation and the anger. This one was impatient yet. And while he could understand her, the Titan inside him felt that she was on the wrong road there.<span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Not that simple. Not the same. We are shaped by someone else, then shape ourselves. You think Humans aren't like that, too? To get somewhere, you have to start someplace else. I was made to be a Titan, but it was <i>my</i> decision to <b>become</b> a Titan, to make myself hardy, to challenge myself. I have seen humans do the same and become strong and hard, and seen humans do the opposite and become weak and soft. Decisions, big and small, good...and bad... they built up, gather, make us who we are, doesn't matter if you are human or Created. I don't know what there will be after the Dawn - how could I? But I believe that it is worth everything, for you will have a human soul. You will not be isolated anymore. And you know what? If there is just enough Iron left in me after the Dawn, I will be good! Because when someone makes life hard on you, you have to push <b>through.</b>&quot; </span>He smacked his hands together forcefully at <b>through, </b>producing a loud noise.<span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;You will be <b>better </b>for it. I am thankful for challenges: they help me understand me. They help me learn new things. People will be trying to tell you how to be? Go ahead, and show them that they are wrong. You will be human - and unlike them, you will have <b>earned </b>it, on every step on the way you will have clawed your way up! You will be able to tell <b>them</b> how to be. Humans argue about that a lot, by the way.&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 05-22-2017, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T15:19:28-07:00","id":1096048,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent; Katerina, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress, Stage 1), Callous<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 10/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 1/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis looks up at Jax, visibly spooked. In this Created he sees someone very similar to him. Adonis was bright eyes and a pretty face and a lithe body, while Jax was a paragon the masculine form. But they had both been created to be tools of fulfillment. The form had been all that mattered, nothing more. Dolls. But Jax had turned his service to other Created in other forms. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Yes, please. Not yet, I still have a roll to complete. But I </span><span style=\"color:#00ff00\">will come to you when I'm ready.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The Cathar's words scare him. But then again, Cathars scare him in general. Mimics try to understand humans, yes, but so that they might copy them, learn how to do the things that are good and wonderful about humans. Cathars peel away the gold and reveal the dark blue of imperfection and vice. Gold and blue, like the masks that those old kings were buried with. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>They do look good together... </i></span>He doesn't know if it's the stray thought or the Cathar's suggestion that makes him shudder. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;No, um... I'm good. I know what getting used is like. I don't want to do it to others. But thank you for the advice about the Fire.&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T08:47:53-07:00","id":1097143,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama LTD), Inspired (Azoth), Inspired (Alchemy)<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 3/6 | Pyros: 5/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b></div><br /> <br /> Scout frowned, and his monotonous voice raise pitch slightly in curiosity, his one eyebrow raising, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I've always found the details of elpis rather murky. Olmec are likely the voice of Azoth and the Fire within me, this much I think is likely. Why not attempt to speak to them once more? Should we not attend these voices? Listen to what they have to say?</span>&quot; The second question made him pause. He looked absently for a moment as he tried to recall anything...<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">No. I do not recall him speaking to me of anything called a 'Concordance'. Is it relevant to this study?</span>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T00:10:05-07:00","id":1098678,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Patient, Watched, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Informed (Cuprum)<br /> Alembics: Verto (0), Stereo Humor (0), Arc (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 12/12 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> Earth is laying by the riverbank. A line from the constant internal narration that Vivid Dreaming brings is playing over and over in her mind: <i>That is the nature of the Red.</i><br /> <br /> It's a very pretty thought. It reminds Earth of the embodied Azoth-figure from the Elpis visions. It's a fatalistic view, maybe, but the river flows where it flows. It doesn't matter so much where it started or where it's gonna end.<br /> <br /> The reanimated Earth-creature has been thinking about its flesh lately. Meditating on Cuprum in the garden brought changes through the Azothic Memory. The Earth-creature finds that it can discolor its skin and eyes and grow its hair as easily as breathing. This alchemical procedure is called <i>Verto.</i><br /> <br /> The creature blinks and when it opens its eyes they are one dark green and one albino pink. It blinks again and now they're matching blue. It spits at its reflection. That symmetry doesn't look right at all.<br /> <br /> The creature forces hair follicles through the skin of its cheeks and throat. Itchy like bugs crawling out of its skin. It swats its own face, but once the sting fades, the creature tries again. The facial hair comes in patchy and erratic. After a couple tries, it gets a coarse mustache and chinstrap together, but the raw material just isn't there. Maybe with Pyros, the fields would grow. It lets the hair burrow back inside.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> It lounges there for quite a while as the Ramble continues, staring like Narcissus at its own reflection in the cold Red River. Blinking and trying new eyeballs, fattening its lips, wrinkling or smoothing the cheeks, flaring its nostrils and making its nose flat or wide or pointy. It digs its fingers into its tangled white hair and pulls its mane even further out, or retracts it into the bumpy scalp. None of it is really any worse or better than the creature's &quot;natural&quot; features. Earth, the creature thinks, isn't a past monster or a future human. Earth lives in the present. They just are what they are. <i>That is the nature of the Red.</i><br /> <br /> Let's see what this pound of flesh can do when its charged with Pyros. The creature lights the fire inside that powers Metamorphosis, making its flesh truly malleable. It kneels in the cold shallow mud and cups river water in its thick palms and leers at the little mirror. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;It's you.&quot;</span> The reflection blinks in surprise. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;It's me!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The creature drinks greedily from the river and splashes its own face with water. Its flesh melts.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Spending 3 Pyros to charge Verto alembic with Body Like Clay. I'll take the Atavistic condition.<br /> <br /> Earth attempts some more radical body changes. Dexterity+Medicine+Azoth, 1 die: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/521022\" target=\"_blank\">fail.</a> I'll make that a dramatic failure for a Beat. &quot;The Promethean loses control over how her body shifts...these alterations inflict a -2 penalty to the character's actions for the remainder of the scene.&quot;</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The raw material is too complex to be manipulated so carelessly. The creature doesn't know what it's done, spilling ink all over its own canvas. Bulging eyes, one arm bigger than the other, rubbery legs, lolling tongue, skin like an oily rag...who needs Disfigurements? The creature, shocked, recoils from its own reflection and crawls away from the riverbank. Until it can get its internal organs rebalanced, it's going to lurk in the shadows past the edge of the Ramble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 05-31-2017, 03:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T20:59:06-07:00","id":1101096,"title":"","content":"<i>The Forks</i><br /> <br /> When <b>Mark 5</b> first starts speaking, <b>Isla</b> clutches the backpack full of clay shards tightly to her chest, wide-eyed with panic. The other Named shift uneasily, and one or two particularly ragged ones who are either practicing Stannum or have calcified it into their very being seem ready to intervene if the Titan presses the issue. They've heard about what the Breaker has done in the past. They don't want those iron mauls he has for hands tearing into one of their own. But the alchemy of language does something beautiful instead, and Isla beams with the radiance of a Created who has seen Hope and experienced a revelation that will lead her onwards to Dawn. She takes a couple awkward steps forwards, knees knocking against the backpack setting it gently swaying, and offers it up to him. On the periphery of the group he sees a Named he had not really noticed before, tall and seemingly rather thin, dressed in a black peacoat with a billowy black blouse that glistens like silk but is almost certainly a much cheaper material. They gesture in a way that can be read somewhere between approval and gratitude, and motion again in a fashion that suggests that Mark 5 come and find them when he is done, as the stranger wanders off towards the bonfire. Someone else is by the fire too, a woman seemingly covered in frost.<br /> <br /> The hulking Sentry inclines his head ever so slightly with a pleased rumble so low as to be barely perceptible, and <b>Jax</b> lowers himself back down to the snow-covered ground, folding the small origami paper in his hands some more, proceeding with his project. He was built for brute force, but he will shape himself into something that can act with gentleness. The <b>Cathar </b>does not say anything, but simply smiles knowingly in response, standing and walking past <b>Adonis </b>towards the bonfire, <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=f43559d4\" target=\"_blank\">brushing against him ever so slightly</a>. The Muse finds his dissatisfaction turning inwards, fear leading towards disgust as alchemy seeps its way into the impurities of his soul, reminding him of past failures.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: The Cathar has used the Guilt Trip Distillation... and she's rolled extremely well. Adonis will have to beat seven successes on a Resolve + Azoth roll, and if he fails then <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> will get the opportunity to detail the worst thing Adonis has ever done, including names, dates, and locations. Basically, Backstory Time!</i><br /> <br /> When <b>Scout </b>speaks up again, <b>Solomon </b>looks extremely uncomfortable, scratching at his head. The other Nepri either look uneasy, curious, or gaze at Scout with something like pity. Like he should know better. &quot;Look, Eagle Scout, best way to get the Fire to talk is to chase Milestones or be one of the lucky ones that the Principle speaks to in dreams. Maybe track down a Messenger. But if you really want to, you can always go looking in Azoth. You're an Originist, you know the details of Azothic Memory. You can always open yourself up to Azoth and Elpis, see what happens... The Fire wants to burn, though. It always wants to burn. Dive too deep too often, and you ignite a Wasteland, and that's bad news for all of us. We can all gather here because we're careful.&quot;<br /> <br /> When Scout can't recall anything about the Concordance, Solomon curses under his breath in a language that the Originist doesn't recognize. Solomon runs a hand across his scalp muttering, <i>thought they were on better terms than that... could he... no, no, he'd never. </i>The Elder Nepri stood resolute and then gave Scout a piercing look &quot;The Concordance is probably the biggest group of Pilgrims anyone's ever heard of. Like if the whole Ramble were a single Throng. Mostly Plumbum and Aes, but when members shift Refinements and go wandering they usually stay in contact. They live out in the Arizona desert, these days. Know more about the Flame Immortal than anyone. Collect records, Athanors. Heard they might worship the Seer, first Pilgrim to ever reach Dawn. All anyone knows about the one in charge is that they're called the Monk and they've been burning for longer than just about any Pilgrim anyone's ever heard of.&quot;<br /> <br /> On the banks of the Red River, a creature of melted flesh and Flux-tainted clay conceals itself from beings that are like it and not like it. The creature once called <b>Earth</b> is barely sapient, barely even conscious, operating purely on instinct, animalistic in a way that only the Unborn can match, but more natural yet than those unholy abominations. A two-legged being they recognize is coming down the bank, the one with keys and multicoloured hair. Spider? Butterfly? Something... something they need to remember. Web? Cocoon? The insect-that-isn't looks around the bank, looking for the creature, just trying to see where it got to. Their eyes catch the creature as it hunkers down deeper into the shadows of some bushes, and there is something profound in their eyes. A thing from before words, if only the creature could describe it. Something flutters by the insect-that-isn't, and then there are many more. A flock of gauzy white butterflies.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Roll Wits + Empathy to figure out Satin's emotional state. Remember that you have a -2 to the roll from Atavistic.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T21:52:42-07:00","id":1101105,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Patient, Watched, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Informed (Cuprum), Atavistic<br /> Alembics: Verto (3), Stereo Humor (0), Arc (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 9/12 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <i>gurgle.</i><br /> <br /> The Earth-creature digs under the bushes with misshapen shovelhands, one of them still more twisted than the other. Some instinct is saying to burrow into the dirt.<br /> <br /> A fly is buzzing in its brain. Spiderfly? That's it. It won't be good if the spider sees it like this. Better keep digging.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, they make eye contact. Its bulging bloodshot eyeball meets the spider's deep dark gaze. It wants to run, but this feels weighty. There's something there. The alchemy of Copper has refined it for reading these things.<br /> <br /> Butterflies. Those are good. Chase the butterflies.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Wits 3, -1 from Empathy 0, -2 from Atavistic, but +2 from Stereo Humor! Spending 1 Willpower because this seems important. 5 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/522664\" target=\"_blank\">squeezed out 1 success.</a><br /> <br /> I think that resolves Atavistic?</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T05:42:41-07:00","id":1105040,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama LTD), Inspired (Azoth), Inspired (Alchemy)<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 3/6 | Pyros: 5/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b></div><br /> <br /> Scout nodded, considering Solomon's words, then shrugged, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I understand your concerns. But my question is- who has determined that it is the best way? Perhaps it is only the best way we know of. I believe this research, the Chymical Wedding, may lead us not only to helping understand our own condition- but also into the more perfected creation of progeny. That is, a reduced chance of Pandorans, and increases the odds of a New Dawn for all. This... Concordance, perhaps they know more. But I am worried that they would worship the Seer. That seems... counterproductive, but I will consider making contact with them.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> The idea of worship was not one Scout really understood. So many humans did it in such different ways. Highwinds had always told him that to seek god he must look inside, and that was what he was doing, wasn't it? Scout bit his lip, frustrated. How did he put that into words? What was the right way to explain it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T05:39:49-07:00","id":1105345,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent; Katerina, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress, Stage 1), Callous<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 10/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 1/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b><br /> <br /> </div> The Cathar's touch is light, but Adonis can feel a memory start to well up from deep in his mind like... a monster from a lake shore...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis tries to resist the effects of Guilt Trip. Resolve 3 + Composure 2 + Willpower 3 = 8 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/525463\" target=\"_blank\">4 successes</a>. A valiant effort, but not enough. He's spilling his guts to her.</div></div> </div> </div> <hr /><i>It was eighteen months ago, exactly. The day of the Summer Solstice, 2015. It was the end of the week he had spent at Devils Lake in North Dakota. </i><br /> <br /> <i>Adonis had passed over the U.S.-Canada border about a month before arriving at the lake. Or maybe a little longer. He couldn't tell, the days and nights had started to blend together after a while. Some days Adonis had been on foot, but most of the time he had been hitching rides with truckers. Those first conversations pretty much all went the same way: <br /> <br /> Where you going? Winnipeg? Shit, that's way out of my way. But I can take you along my route, that'll at least get you a little closer. Hold on there, I'm not giving you a free ride. Company doesn't like it when we take hitchhikers, gotta make it worth my time. No money? Shit. Well, I guess... Hm. I... guess I could let you ride. Yeah. Yeah I'd be happy to. I mean, I ain't queer, but if I were... well. Wouldn't mind getting a little handsy with you. What's that? Oh sure, I'll shut up. Whatever you want. Yeah, anything you like. Just... God you're good-looking.<br /> <br /> But it always got worse from there. His instinctive ability to make people do stuff for him won him plenty of fans, truckers practically making declarations of undying love- well, overwhelming lust, really. That was the first time the idea of exploring the company of a man crossed his mind. But he never got a chance. Maybe they were frightened by how easily this incredibly attractive man made them swoon and blush. Maybe the Divine Fire burned too hot for them to handle. Maybe a bit of both. But they always snapped, get-out-right-nows accompanied by slurs and fists and sometimes guns. After that, Adonis always took off on foot for a couple days, but desperation and a strange new desire to find a trucker who didn't pull away from him drove him to find another one... and another... and...<br /> <br /> He had arrived in North Dakota, drawn to the banks of Devils Lake by Pilgrim Marks that he recognized on a gut level. He had been looking south to the far bank when she came: Elektra, a Muse like him, made from the body of a ballerina by another Promethean. She had taught him about himself, why he could bend people to his will. About the Lineages and the Refinements, the Great Work. About Centimani. About Pandorans.<br /> <br /> It was about an hour before sunset on the Solstice. Adonis and Elektra had been sitting on the lakeside in the sand and mud. The silence was shattered by the sound of something bursting out of the ground, an awful thing of tentacles and twisted growths, and a mouth where a person's belly would be, lined with awful meter-long teeth of glass and bone: a Pandoran. They had both jumped up screaming with shock and horror. The creature had stood for a second, as if thinking about which one to attack. Then it picked- Elektra. It sprang at her with a feral yowl as she </i><i>shrieked. Adonis had jumped backwards, out of its clutches. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#4B0082\">&quot;Adonis, help!&quot; </span>she had screamed, but then Elektra had gotten a look in her eyes, a look of understanding and betrayal and anger. Because both of them had realized: Adonis was going to leave her. He was going to let it have her. He was going to run. <br /> <br /> And he did. He didn't look back, didn't stop until his lungs felt like they were filled with lava and his legs stopped moving, and he collapsed covered with sweat, not moving until dawn as he wept with remorse for Elektra and horror at the Pandoran and anger at himself. And then he had gotten up on trembling feet and started walking north again. And he promised that he would never tell anybody what had happened. </i> <hr />All of it flashes through Adonis' mind in a second. And he's furious. <i><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">She knows... she knows! That fucking bitch! </span></i>He knows what she was trying to do: this was a sort of flirting, showing him what she had to offer, what she could teach him. Fists clenched, he follows her to the bonfire. He stands beside her and looks her in the eye. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Cute trick. That wasn't very nice.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> \u200b<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis is royally pissed with the Cathar, so he's going for the Fog Distillation from Eris. Presence 3 + Subterfuge 1 + Azoth 2 = 6 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/525473\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>. Hopefully her Resolve doesn't knock that down.<br /> <br /> He's spent 1 Willpower and 3 Pyros in this post.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T00:26:43-07:00","id":1105626,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Charites (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0), Unfettered (0)<br /> Health:OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 11/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 0</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> He noticed the theatrically dressed Named, and gave them an ever so slight nod. He didn't know what they wanted, but the Tammuz wasn't one to shy away from the unknown.<br /> <br /> Very, very carefuly, the Titan took up the backpack, and nodded towards her gratefully. He didn't know why the nod came out that way, but he knew she shared something important to her with him. This obviously wasn't easy for her. He respected that.<br /> Opening the zip, Mark 5 took out just one shard, treating it like a delicate, fragile flower, and looked at it, turning it so the writing made the most sense.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Mark 5 tries to read or at least make out anything about the language that could help, like whether it looks like spanish or chinese or something he might have seen on his journey so far. </i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=4f87be3e\" target=\"_blank\">so close...</a>failure with a 9 on chance die</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He shook his head, and said with a sad voice &quot;<span style=\"color:#000080\">I am afraid I do not know this language. I have never even seen anything like it. I am sorry, Isla.&quot;</span><br /> The Titan, being a Titan, didn't give up, however. He looked hard at the symbols, trying to get one burned into his mind, and tried drawing it with a finger in the air. Once he was satisfied with the image in his head, he nodded, put it carefully back, and handed her backpack back to her. &quot;<span style=\"color:#000080\">However, do not give up now! By knowing what it is not, you can maybe more easily find what it is. It is not English. It does not look like anything I usually see, so my guess is it is rare, or old, or both. Find someone who knows about rare languages, they might be able to help you more.&quot;</span><br /> The Tammuz gave his fellow Created an encouraging smile. &quot;<span style=\"color:#000080\">I tried to remember the scripture. If I ever find someone that knows more, or find out more myself, I will let you know when we meet again. If nothing else will stop me, I will seek you out.&quot;</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 06-20-2017, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T09:22:22-07:00","id":1108425,"title":"","content":"<i>The Forks</i><br /> <br /> With recognition comes clarity, and the creature in the mud comes back to itself. <b>Earth</b>. Its name is Earth. The spiderfly is <b>Satin</b>. Satin is seeing them like this. The Riven's face is one wracked with deep empathy. They exhale slowly, and their facial features warp in subtle ways. Cheekbones emerge as sharp planes along the face, pale facial hair extends from their face, framing it with a beard. A wordless display of Copper alchemy. Satin seats themselves and adjusts the ribbons that are wrapped everywhere there is exposed skin; this new presentation of Self is bulkier, muscles more defined. Earth can briefly see gaping holes in that flesh, tears made by the limbs of things that were never human, wounds that will not heal, leaking mist. Aether sublimating back into the world around them. Has Satin always smelled so strongly of evaporating alcohol? Or have they just done a good job of hiding it? White butterflies swirl over the Ramble's bonfire.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Earth gains a Beat from resolving the Atavistic Condition</i><br /> <br /> <b>Solomon</b> shifts uneasily at <b>Scout's </b>line of questioning. The elder Nepri has been around for a while, it's generally polite not to ask how long. Unlike other Lineages, many Osirians have the peculiar gift of an enduring Flame, a relic of their origin, perhaps. Those Nepri blessed with chthonic power needn't fear their Azoth guttering and dying, they can always replenish themselves with a descent Below, to find more kindling to sacrifice to the Divine Fire. An Osirian can theoretically live forever, if they are content with dying with relative frequency. &quot;Experiments into the Lineages usually don't end well. My Genitor was interested in that kind of work. Don't know if he's still at it after I burned his latest batch of <i>children</i> to death in escaping.&quot; He spits the word 'children' out like a curse, with such venom that you can almost <i>smell </i>the Flux starting to rise in him as Torment rears its head. Solomon closes his eyes and takes several deep breaths, and the bubble of Flux subsides. When he opens his eyes, Solomon seems old and worn out. &quot;If you think chasing the Chymical Wedding will help, then the Concordance is your best bet. The rumours of worship are just that, worship. At least the Concordance has a solid reputation. Could be worse. You could run in the Botherud.&quot;<br /> <br /> The <b>Cathar</b> is not expecting <b>Adonis</b> to respond to her alchemy with a transmutation of his own, and her eyes widen in surprise before they dull into confusion. She seems puzzled as to why Adonis followed her down to the fire, and her brow furrows as she tries to remember the last hour. She turns inwards, and ignores him. There's another Pilgrim standing nearby, a Golem with dark eyes and dark clothes, looking with knowing intensity at the Muse. He says nothing, only gives that level stare with eyes that seem to be made from polished stone that have been inlaid carefully with gold leaf. On the opposite side of the fire huddles a frost-covered woman that you didn't notice on your way over. Maybe it's just the aftershocks of the Cathar's alchemy, maybe it's his own psyche, but she looks a little bit like Elektra in the firelight.<br /> <br /> With the Titan's promise, <b>Isla </b>smiles back. No one she's met yet knows what her Words say, but at least someone wants to help. She takes back the backpack and zips it up, slinging it over her shoulders. The theatrically dressed Named is waiting down by the fire, and Adonis is there too. The frost-covered woman is hunkered down by the edge, and there are snowflakes swirling above the fire. If you look carefully, they kind of look like butterflies. Somewhere up over the hill, <b>Mark 5 </b>can hear large vehicles driving up near Johnston Terminal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 06-27-2017, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T09:36:54-07:00","id":1111306,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama LTD), Inspired (Azoth), Inspired (Alchemy)<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 3/6 | Pyros: 5/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b></div><br /> Scout had his hand up in a warding motion when flux threatened the elder promethean, but when he got himself back under control he returned to his neutral posture. He stood ready to ease torment, but he was certain Solomon's torment would not be easy to overcome. The little promethean raised an eyebrow at the final mention, and his monotone voice &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Who or what is Botherud?</span>&quot; there was a slight pause, before he thought to add, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Uhm, so I can avoid that.</span>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T09:55:02-07:00","id":1111321,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent; Katerina, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress, Stage 1), Callous<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 10/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 1/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis shoots the Golem a look that says, <span style=\"color:#00ff00\"><i>I am not in the mood to be screwed with. </i></span>He turns and makes to walk away, his hands clenched. <i><span style=\"color:#00ff00\">Jeez, is this what being a Fury feels like? Damn, no wonder Earth has been such a pain in the- </span></i>his eyes fall on the frost-covered woman crouched by the fire. For a split second, their eyes meet. His heart begins to pound- her eyes, the shape of her face. Maybe it's a trick of the light, but she looks like... <i><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Elektra. But. No. You're dead. It got you, it had to. </span></i>He studies her for a terrible moment, frozen in time. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis is going to try and figure out if the mysterious woman is, indeed, Elektra. Wits 2 + Composure 2 = 4 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/530872\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T01:20:07-07:00","id":1112558,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Patient, Watched, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Informed (Cuprum)<br /> Alembics: Verto (3), Stereo Humor (0), Arc (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 4/5 | Pyros: 9/12 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> While Earth's body recovers, they spend a while talking about things with Satin that are probably not as interesting to read as they are to discuss. Very little is learned about being a Hermit, but much about being a companion. The Solstice Ramble turned out okay in the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T16:51:13-07:00","id":1112994,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Charites (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0), Unfettered (0)<br /> Health:OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 11/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 0</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Having done his part, Mark 5 said his goodbyes to Isla, hoping to see her again once he had more to offer. He got up to move towards the strange theatrically dressed Named, but the noise of approaching cars made him uneasy, and he repeatedly looked into the direction of the noise. Had someone called the police to stop the Ramble? Was an Enemy on the move? Were simple people just going to walk into an alchemical mess of a place? No matter what, if those weren't other Created, trouble was coming.<br /> He approached the impractically dressed Named and introduced himself. &quot;<span style=\"color:#000080\">I am Mark 5. By way of Mudbreaker. You wanted to talk to me.&quot;</span><br /> None of those were questions. He looked around again, fought back the paranoia and added &quot;<span style=\"color:#000080\"> We can talk.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> It took him a moment to recognize Adonis being close by, but he didn't make much of it. Other than drawing some comfort from it. Which was rather strange to him, now that he tought about it. How weird, that the mere presence of someone would make him feel more at ease. Especially when it was someone that wasn't all that great at fighting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 07-07-2017, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T07:42:16-07:00","id":1114580,"title":"","content":"<i>The Forks</i><br /> <br /> A rumbling sound, like the approach of a large vehicle, distracts <b>Solomon</b>, who wanders off to check things out, so another Nepri speaks up. This one obviously looks much more like a mummified corpse, pitch-blackened skin held tight to the bone, hardened tissue moving with leathery suppleness. They are missing an eye, and the Pilgrim in question has painted the Eye of Heru around it with careful precision. They clear their throat and straighten a shabby winter coat, the exterior layer of fabric torn and the stuffing flapping in the wind.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Botherud are a Ramble who believe the Divine Fire is limited in scope. They believe that creating new progeny leaves less of the Fire for all of us, less opportunity to condense Vitriol and attain the New Dawn. At best, the ones I've met try and isolate themselves with a couple of established, complimentary Pilgrims. At worst... they <i>kill</i> other Created. Leave more of the Flame Immortal for themselves.&quot;<br /> <br /> To<b> Scout's</b> ear, there is something between disgust and awe in that voice, that these Pilgrims could do something so fundamentally brutal, so fundamentally <i>human</i>, as the destruction of fellow-travellers for their own gain.<br /> <br /> When <b>Adonis </b>takes a hard look at the woman by the fire... she <i>looks </i>like Elektra. Exactly, disturbingly, like Elektra. But frost was not her Disfigurement. He's heard rumours that Created can come back from the dead at least once, maybe more, but that they need to do something in the afterlife first. Has she been <i>down there </i>all this time? Down in the dark, with the howling dead, wandering listless and blind, like the shades of Hades from that book Sharon once read to him, when she was still obsessed with him? When she was still the only other living being he'd ever met? If she's seen him, she hasn't reacted. Maybe she doesn't remember. Alchemy could do that (he had just done it) but there was also a River, down below, a River that stripped memories from the dead and allowed you to be reborn. Was that what Elektra had to do to come back?<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: So, I think this merits a minor Milestone. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> how is Adonis reacting to this? What decision is he going to make?</i><br /> <br /> The Named straightens himself at <b>Mark 5's</b> introduction, and you can see details of his Disfigurements that you couldn't before. His skin, where it was exposed, was dusty, clay flaking off. His hair was black, with a slight wave to it, mud forcing parts to clump and fly wild. But his eyes... his eyes were black stone, carefully carved and inlaid with gold leaf in alchemical sigils and equations that gave the impression of an iris. His Azothic Radiance seemed to glow about him. The Named smiles &quot;I am <b>Joshua.</b> By way unknown. I have a message for you.&quot; this strange Pilgrim spoke with the easy surety of someone with Purpose. Purpose like the mission the Titan believed he had. &quot;I was found by a Messenger of the Principle, and told to be in this place, for you and your throng. It was difficult to track you, for you are not branded into a pact.&quot;<br /> <br /> The rumbling is getting louder, and it seems to be coming to a stop. Which means that whatever is approaching is finally here. There's a large black van, like a moving truck, parked at the top of the hill, with an <a href=\"http://www.feelnumb.com/wp-content/uploads/2011/02/amalgamation.gif\" target=\"_blank\">oddly familiar symbol</a> outlined in beautiful gold, and prim quicksilver lettering on the side.<br /> <br /> &quot;I was told to be here when a great storm would break, because it is important for you to witness it. I apologize. I do not like deception.&quot;<br /> <br /> Men in black riot gear burst from the black of the van, carrying sleek black weapons, many of them marked with the dull grey gleam of a symbol in the shape of Iron, one who seemed slightly more important than the others marked with Bronze.<br /> <br /> &quot;I am distracting you.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Alright guys, time to shake things up a little. Roll for Initiative. At the moment there are five Amalgama thugs, each with a base Initiative of 5. Their leader has a base Initiative of 6. <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=cde73662\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the roll to gain the modifier.</a><br /> <br /> <b>Thug 1: </b>Initiative- 7 Health - 7 <b>Thug 2:</b> Initiative- 8 Health- 7 <b>Thug 3:</b> Initiative- 9 Health- 7 <b>Thug 4:</b> Initiative- 12 Health- 7 <b>Thug 5: </b>Initiative- 14<br /> <br /> <b>Captain: </b>Initiative- 15 Health- 8</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 07-11-2017, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T16:49:23-07:00","id":1114807,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Patient, Watched, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Informed (Cuprum)<br /> Alembics: Verto (3), Stereo Humor (0), Arc (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 4/5 | Pyros: 9/12 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Initiative <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/532893\" target=\"_blank\">5</a>. Spending 3 Pyros to charge Arc.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T07:07:43-07:00","id":1115077,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent; Katerina, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress, Stage 1), Callous<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 10/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 2/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis walks over to the ice-covered woman, this person who looks so much like the first Created he ever met- the first thing he met that had been like him, the greatest sin of his existence. He stops next to her and waits until she acknowledges him. He waits for her to let him sit beside her. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;I'm sorry, but... you look familiar. You look like a Muse I once knew, back in the Dakotas. What is your name?&quot; </span>He tries to stay vague, to avoid tipping her off or trigger some memory of him- assuming that she really is Elektra. But he has to know. But what is he going to do if she is? Try to make amends? Apologize? Stay as far away from her as possible?<br /> <br /> Before she even has a chance to answer, Adonis hears the rumbling truck stop. He looks up and sees the van marked with the Amalgama symbol, and the men marked with the symbols of Iron and Bronze. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;It's Amalgama!&quot; </span>Adonis jumps up, pulling the woman with him. <i><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">How did they find us? Unless... Erwin. Oh Erwin, what happened? </span></i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Initiative roll = 1 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/533017\" target=\"_blank\">5</a> + Dexterity 2 + Composure 2 = 9</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T10:02:31-07:00","id":1116000,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Charites (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0), Unfettered (0)<br /> Health:OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 11/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 0</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Something about the Created was intriguing. Was it the sense of purpose? When Joshua mentioned that he had a message, Mark 5's interest grew even more.<i> &quot;Who could be sending me a message?&quot;</i><br /> The Titan was just getting confused when the noise piped up. The Messenger's message seemed to be the real deal, because as usual, it didn't make any sense. The message must have come late, for the Firestorm was over already.<br /> His attention divided, he didn't quite understand what was happening, until Joshua flat out told him he was being distracted. About to punch Joshua in the face for this, a familiar voice set him back on track: <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;It's Amalgama!&quot; </span>Adonis! His eyes widening, Mark 5 turned and charged his Pyros, running towards where he'd last seen Earth.<i><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;</span>The Mission!&quot;</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Initiative: Mod 6 +<a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=e6d4c862\" target=\"_blank\"> 2</a> = 8<br /> Charging 2 Pyros to spent on Motus - Exemplary Athleticism </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Joshua's distraction proved effective, and Mark 5 reacted a lot more slowly than he otherwise might have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 07-14-2017, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T13:38:08-07:00","id":1116091,"title":"","content":"[<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama LTD), Inspired (Azoth), Inspired (Alchemy)<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 3/6 | Pyros: 5/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b></div><br /> Scout worked his jaw as he thought over the Brothrud. This was an intriguing hypothesis, and while he had no desire to destroy his fellow created, he was curious as to what evidence drove them to this conclusion. Surely it was simply not logical.<br /> <br /> When the truck arrived, and the men began to pour out, he started shaking. No. No not here. Not now.<br /> <br /> He sputtered as he watched the group advance, feeling helpless, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">... But how?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/533446\" target=\"_blank\">9 Init </a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T14:09:43-07:00","id":1116105,"title":"","content":"<i>The Forks</i><br /> <br /> Two dozen Created look up in panic at the men in sleek black riot gear here to peel their flesh and drain their humours, humans with the Divine Fire blazing bright behind their eyes, driving them to madness, to a hunger for Pilgrims to match even the Unborn. Many things happen at once. Sentries stand and with quick, practiced words of command, with wild abandon, charge forwards, covering the escape of their less combat capable fellow. <b>Jax</b>, sitting quietly, peacefully, in the snow rises to his full, terrifying height, and <i>roars </i>like an outraged bull, a deep bass sound that reverberates in the chests of those nearby, his Disfigurements flaring as he charges Alembics, his skin turning to bronze, as one or two other Sentries join him in preparation, lithe, athletic figures built for dexterity and speed. Titans charge ahead without heed for their action, Pyros flaring muscles as they move faster than expected. Pariahs gain animal features and animal weapons in a desperate effort to defend themselves, or else turn into beasts entirely and flee. A handful of Furies cackle with sardonic mirth at the chance to let their rage out. The less combat capable Created flee in terror, <b>Tom Barebones </b>clutching his coat tight to himself and rocking in the snow, <b>Isla </b>pulling at him and begging for him to come with her. Somewhere up on the hill you can hear <b>Solomon's </b>voice slurring and spitting obscenities in dead languages, roaring defiance.<br /> <br /> Amalgama's Captain doesn't speak, his men don't need him to. The symbols on his uniform suggest to an educated eye that he's learned some secrets of Bronze alchemy. These men act as a unit, a fist of five fingers guided by one mind, one will, one desire. He lifts his gun, sights, and fires. His first shot hits <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=01840290\" target=\"_blank\">Adonis</a>, quick to rise, looking like he's going to bring another target with him. A handful of high-powered bolts (the thought absurdly occurred to Adonis that they look rather like arrows) slammed into the Muse's torso with all the force of a car crash, driving the will to fight out of him, leaving him gasping for air on his knees, blood flowing freely. Those clothes are going to stain. The woman, who never actually <i>did</i> answer his question, and who hasn't spoken at all, stands beside him, looking down with curiosity, an errant smile playing at her otherwise impassive face. Something changes inside him, the blood feels laced with something <i>more</i>, something <i>precious</i>.<br /> <br /> \u200b<i>OOC: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> <b>Adonis</b> takes the Beaten Down Tilt and the Drugged Tilt along with 5L damage. He also gains 3 Vitriol Beats (from the Milestone) and a regular Beat (from having damage in one of his three rightmost Health boxes).</i><br /> <br /> The Captain's second shot aims for <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=ab4015c8\" target=\"_blank\">Mark 5</a>, the obviously martial one, appearance fitting the basic description of a known (dangerous) factor in the area. Given the target's known behaviour, probably manifests abilities that make him more physically dangerous, and so it would be best to take him down <i>fast</i>. Five bolts to his centre mass, but a Titan is made of Iron, and Mark 5 was already a Martyr. He is going to be hard to subdue. But something strange is happening to him, something alien to his senses. He feels... off-balance, sluggish. Drained. What did they do to him?Another of Amalgama's foot soldiers steps silently forwards, aiming for Mark 5 again. Target remains a clear and present danger, neutralize with extreme prejudice. A quick, disciplined <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=6ab1ec43\" target=\"_blank\">burst</a>, but the Titan is already moving, and is anticipating an attack. A singular dart, catching him high on the shoulder.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> <b>Mark 5</b> takes the Drugged Tilt along with 5L + 2L damage. I can't recall if the Stamina 5 on his character sheet <b>includes </b>Azoth due to his Unbroken Alembic or not, so I'll hold off on judging if he gets a Personal Tilt besides Drugged for now.</i><br /> <br /> A third man in riot gear steps forwards, hefting his own gun, and aims at a general area towards which Mark 5 and several other Sentries and Titans are charging. He swings the gun back and forth in a tight radius, letting off a <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=162755b1\" target=\"_blank\">rapid burst</a> of ten shots. There are Pilgrims laying on their backs, struggling to rise, confused by their body's inability to act according to their will. There are Created digging fingers into the snow, spitting with rage and pain and letting the whole world know it. There are Pilgrims just sitting on the ground, or kneeling, touching their wounds and staring dumbfounded at their humours. There are Created who by their screams of rage have fallen into Torment, and some who are clearly deciding whether they should fall to it entirely and revert to Stannum, to throw lightning like the wrath of gods.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Anyone trying to get closer, such as within hand-to-hand range, of the Amalgama foot soldiers will take 4L damage this turn. Anyone trying to act other than to drop prone or move out of range takes this damage as well. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> Earth is far enough away that this does not apply to them.</i><br /> <br /> Over by the banks of the Red River, Earth and <b>Satin</b> can hear the fire of the guns, and the shouts of fellow Created. The guns are silenced, sounding more like a rung gong or a massive drum than a peal of thunder, but to those who recognize the sound, it is gunfire all the same. Satin stands quickly, and their flesh flows like wet clay, reforming into a creature something like a wolf, but with platinum-blonde fur. The transformed Satin gives Earth a quick &quot;are you coming or not?&quot; glance and moves swiftly and silently through the snow.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: It is now <b>Adonis</b>, <b>Scout</b>, and <b>Mark 5's</b> turn.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 07-14-2017, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T20:26:38-07:00","id":1116224,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Tilts: Drugged, Arm Wreck<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (3), Charites (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0), Unfettered (0)<br /> Health:LLLLLLLOOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 8/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 0</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;What is that? What is happening?&quot; </i><br /> Confusion took hold of Mark 5. Not only was he sluggish, his arm had taken serious damage.<br /> With an angry cry, he fired up his Alembic and felt the Alchemy strenghtening his body, although it did not help against everything moving and turning and blurring in his head.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Spent 3 Pyros (2 from last turn, 1 this turn) on Exemplary Athleticism. +3Str/+3Sta/+1Dex, Speed doubled, Athletic rolls are rotes. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He had to move. Iron rusts when not moving. Rust is bad. <i>&quot;Keep moving!&quot;</i> Mark 5 tried to shake off the strange sensations and to get his body back under control. When those guns stop for even a moment, he'd have to get to them as quickly as possible, but right now, he needed to get out of there. Except... <i>&quot;Adonis got hit!&quot;</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Moving towards Adonis, up to 18 yards (Speed times 2 yards, right?), Mark 5 aims to provide Cover for the Muse. If Adonis drops prone, so does Mark 5. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T18:29:45-07:00","id":1118019,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent; Katerina, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress, Stage 1), Callous, Beaten Down, Drugged<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: LLLLLOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 10/10<br /> Beats: 3/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 2</b><br /> <br /> </div> The things slam into Adonis' body, and the force of the impact sends him to one knee. The hand that is not gripping the icy Promethean's hand- <i><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Cold. So cold.</span></i>- immediately goes to his chest and the pain that is now exploding through his chest. But just as quickly as the pain starts, it begins to dull and he is gripped by a sudden dizziness, and his vision begins to blur. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>What... what is this?</i></span> Prometheans are supposed to be immune to disease and wounds that would sap humans of their will to fight. But now the very thought of fighting the Amalgama soldiers is abhorrent. And why does he feel so woozy?! But then he remembers who is attacking. <i><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">I hate alchemists. </span></i><br /> <br /> He looks up at the Promethean holding his hand, and she does nothing but watch with a slightly amused smile. What is she? A spy from Amalgama? Or maybe she really is Elektra, back from the Underworld, returned to life to torment him for his sin? Just then, Mark 5 runs up and stands in front of them, arms spread wide. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Thanks, man. Give them hell, don't get yourself killed.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> He grits his teeth and stumbles back to his feet. He gives the other Created with a dirty look. He lunges away from the men, running through the snow on unsteady legs and dragging her with him. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">\u200b&quot;You a Nepri or something? Only way I can explain you not wanting to save your own skin!&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T17:42:12-07:00","id":1118322,"title":"","content":"<i>The Forks</i><br /> <br /> One of the men takes several steps forwards, seeing that their targets are getting away, and attempts to subdue <b>Mark</b> with a quick <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=93b84df5\" target=\"_blank\">burst</a>. A curse, audible this time. The Titan is just so damn <i>fast </i>that it took all the man's alchemy to just tag him with a single dart out of a burst. A second actively charges the Titan, throwing himself into a grapple. He manages to <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=915bed3b\" target=\"_blank\">hurl himself</a> onto the Titan's back, just barely locking on to Mark's wide back.<br /> <br /> <i>\u200bOOC: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> roll Strength + Brawl to contest the grapple. You need to beat two successes. Mark 5 takes another 2L damage.</i><br /> <br /> The last man charges <b>Adonis</b>, stumbling away with a woman covered in frost. He <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=33363c5f\" target=\"_blank\">tackles</a> the lithe Muse, ripping the other Pilgrim from his grasp. She stumbles half a step forwards, and then turns back to watch the grapple impassively with perfect poise, a serene half-smile on her lips. The alchemically-charged soldier, faceless in sleek black riot gear, draws a pair of handcuffs from his belt and makes a move to slap them across his wrists. These particular cuffs <i>do not </i>look like they'd be fun.<br /> <br /> <i>\u200bOOC: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> you can spend a point of Willpower to roll Strength + Brawl to contest the grapple. If that's what you choose to do, then you need to beat three successes.</i><br /> <br /> Meanwhile on the other side of the hill, a pale wolf-like monstrosity charges through the snow, <b>Satin</b> leaping to <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=0891e754\" target=\"_blank\">the attack</a>, fury in the great howl rising from their throat, teeth and claws slamming into the Captain's back. The Captain goes bowling down the hill with a cry of pain and panic, Satin keeping her grip on him, tossing him away from herself with claws hooked under the edge of his body armour. The Captain groans loudly, his blood steaming in the snow, turning the ground crimson as the snow turns back to water. A hand reaches for his leg, limp, torn, and useless from the horrifying assault. There are cries of panic from the surrounding men as they leap back, reaching for weapons they had been laying down in preparation to secure the Created they have subdued. Satin growls, a sound low and deep in their throat, their eyes gleaming and glazed over with rage and Torment. Satin isn't really in there anymore, the Fire has her. Earth knows Torment. Satin has no compunctions right now. No sense of the humanity they've learned along the way.<br /> <br /> All they have left is an all-consuming blaze.<br /> <br /> Is Earth going to let a fellow Pilgrim burn again?<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Satin rolled <b>astonishingly </b>well, dealing 8L damage to the Captain, reduced by 5B by his Armour. He is currently suffering the Beaten Down and Leg Wrack Tilt.</i><br /> <br /> <i><b>Captain:</b> [B][B][B][B][B][ ][ ][ ]</i><br /> <br /> <i><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> Earth's turn is up!</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 07-19-2017, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T22:28:06-07:00","id":1118404,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Patient, Watched, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Informed (Cuprum)<br /> Alembics: Verto (3), Stereo Humour (0), Arc (3)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 4/5 | Pyros: 6/12 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> The breath catches in Earth's throat, and it's not just because their body is still warped. The sight of Satin taking the wolf-shape and throwing the Captain to the ground, ripping with silver fangs and spilling hot blood on the snow is...beautiful? That doesn't feel like a human thought. But it's there.<br /> <br /> The misshapen Tammuz floods Pyros into their extremities, charging the wicked battery within. It was wise to keep this souvenir from the Tin road. The power of Electrification can also be a tool to end Torment in one hard shock rather than staying in a desperate fight. The sooner Satin is out of danger, the sooner they'll be restored to their senses. Hopefully.<br /> <br /> Having lurched to the crest of the snowy hill through Satin's wolfish tracks, Earth takes aim at the men surrounding Satin and the Captain. A bolt of lightning might scare them off.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Just to pick a number for range purposes, I'll say Earth is 20 yards away from the thugs. Divine Lightning, Dexterity+Athletics+Azoth 7, Willpower +3, Verto dramatic failure -2, range -1. 7 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/534567\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes.</a> I already spent my 3 Pyros this turn charging Arc, so no specials for now. One target takes 3L+2L before armor, and an additional 1L for the next 6 turns.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T07:46:29-07:00","id":1118552,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent; Katerina, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress, Stage 1), Callous, Beaten Down, Drugged<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: LLLLLOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 10/10<br /> Beats: 3/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 2</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis has no desire to fight, he just wants to run, to get away from Amalgama. But the weight of an Amalgama thug suddenly brings him down to the ground again. He rolls over and sees the wicked-looking handcuffs descending to restrain him. The last lucid part of his mind urges him to fight. But the drugs are working fast, and he can only get out a low, dazed moan and his arms just wave around like tree branches in a light breeze. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis is going to try to defend himself and spends a point of Willpower. Strength 3 + Brawl 2 - Drugged 3 = 2 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/534614\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes</a>. Hm, let's make that a Dramatic Success for a Beat.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T13:45:31-07:00","id":1118684,"title":"","content":"<i>The Forks</i><br /> <br /> Things go very wrong, very quickly. There were Created behind them, how the <i>hell </i>did they miss that?! <b>Mark 5</b> burns through the alchemical drug in his system, countering instinctually with alchemy that neutralized the toxins, quickly overpowering the mere mortal and with iron vices for hands starts to crush the man's hand for his impudence. The man grunts in pain, and you can swear that you hear his teeth grinding, but his armour protects him well and it holds, though you can feel something give under the kevlar. Other Titans and Sentries are coming to their senses, disfigurements flaring, and staggering back to their feet. <b>Jax </b>lurches upright again, his bulk gleaming in the moonlight, <b>Solomon </b>sweats blue for a few moments and manages to roll in the snow, wiping the exuded toxins from his body and slowing his breath on hands and knees. Flux breaks out in the air from Scout's leaden alchemy, Disquiet tensing the Captain's squadron. Thunder rolls as lightning blasts through the air in a shock of white, and one man in black riot gear drops to the ground as if a hand of God had reached out and snuffed out his consciousness.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> Mark 5 is no longer suffering the Drugged Tilt. <b>Thug 2:</b> [L][ ][ ][ ][ ][ ][ ]<br /> <br /> <b>Thug 3: </b>[B][B][B][B][B][ ][ ] <b>Tilts:</b> Stunned, Knocked Down</i><br /> <br /> One of the men on the hill whirls towards the lightning and makes an audible sound of disgust at <b>Earth's</b> twisted flesh and oily skin, one of those nearby pivots with him, laughs sardonically and <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VcgRaf38uCQ\" target=\"_blank\">adopts a faux-Austrian accent</a>. One of them lets off a quick, <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=7e362b4a\" target=\"_blank\">burst of darts</a>, a little more hurried and a little less tight, that sails past the Pariah as they duck closer to the dirt that gave them life. The other prioritizes, Earth or the silver wolf-beast that <b>Satin</b> has become? Captain's in trouble, the monster takes priority. He takes a moment, lines up the shot, and <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=e17c860e\" target=\"_blank\">fires</a>. The darts catch the Satin-creature high on the left flank, sending them sprawling sideways, snarling and biting, away from the Captain, trying to draw the darts from their body with teeth and semi-dextrous paws and wavering unsteadily on feet growing leaden with alchemical toxins.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, <b>Adonis</b> feebly struggles while a fellow Pilgrim looks on with what appears to be mildly amused curiosity. The man pulls what looks like an insulin reader from his belt and takes a quick sample from the Muse. The results are positive. Very positive. Adonis can <i>feel </i>the hungry stare of the man, just like he can sense the cruel smile curling under the indistinct faceplate of the helmet. He pauses, as though concentrating on something, and the Captain quite suddenly lurches to his feet, uncaring of his injuries, favouring his uninjured side. He draws a large, very nasty looking syringe filled with clear liquid mixed with what appears to be dull grey calcifications, like ash or dust, and injects it into his injured thigh, not bothering to suppress a scream as dozens, hundreds, thousands of things that vaguely resemble insects with bloated abdomens, ashen carapaces, and beautifully smooth emaciated human faces lacking noses soar forth, the swarm splitting in two and surrounding both Earth and Mark, the two most active Created at the moment. The insects bite, tearing chunks of flesh and attempting to burrow deeper.<br /> <br /> You can see many of the local Sentries making sure their throngs are alright, Titans among the only ones willing to stand and keep fighting where others are just too injured to actively continue fighting.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> Earth and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> Mark 5 are both suffering from the Swarm Tilt right now. Because of the size of the Swarms you are each taking 3B damage per turn. Remember that you can spend Pyros to reduce damage as it happens.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T05:20:06-07:00","id":1118913,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama LTD), Inspired (Azoth), Inspired (Alchemy)<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 2/6 | Pyros: 1/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> As the flux flowed from Scout, he started considering courses of action. Chaos, but there was a clear leader here. Scout charged him, even as his alembic charged with some of his last pyros. He didn't have much left, but he would not leave his friends to this nightmare.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/534891\" target=\"_blank\"> 1 sux attack </a>Willpower and 2 pyros spent last round for Tension, 1wp 3 pyros spent this round for Rampage. Not sure of their defense, but I'm 1+1L per level of Disquiet for Rampage. Hopefully with all the alembics firing and showing disfigurements, I can get some decent damage. If I even properly hit. Forgot to add All Out Attacking, so that's <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/534893\" target=\"_blank\">+1 more</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T15:36:01-07:00","id":1119350,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Tilts: Drugged, Arm Wreck<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (3), Charites (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0), Unfettered (0)<br /> Health:LLLLLLLLLBBBO | Willpower: 5/6 | Pyros: 7/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 0</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Freed from the toxin, Mark 5's thoughts clear up. He gathers Pyros in his Body, building up the heat necessary for what he had to do. Ignoring the swarm, finally focused, he wanted to give his opponent a better understanding of what he had gotten himself into: Fighting a Titan was not a smart move.<br /> Ask the Indian Posse.<br /> <br /> With sheer, brutal strength, he attacked his opponent. Despite his anger, this force was applied almost delicately: He was NOT going to repeat his mistakes as the Breaker.<br /> <br /> He had no right to kill this man, so he would try to keep him alive as much as possible.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Str+Brw+Az+Wp = <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=bb996643\" target=\"_blank\">6 Successes</a><br /> 2 Forgotten Dice from Hygeius Bonus (Bonus where Vanilla Mortals would suffer wound penalties)= <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=1c795036\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a><br /> Gathering 2 Pyros for Wrath of the Gods</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T16:39:01-07:00","id":1119671,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent; Katerina, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress, Stage 1), Callous, Beaten Down, Drugged<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: LLLLLOO I WP: 4/5 I Pyros 10/10<br /> Beats: 4/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 1 I Vitriol Experiences 2</b><br /> <br /> </div> The man's gaze is hungry, freakishly hungry. It's like the guy wants to try and do the lacuna on him- if a human even could rip his vitriol out of him. Which he doesn't think he can, but still. No point in encouraging him. Adonis raises his hands, palms outward and shaking from sudden fear. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Please! I give up. Don't kill me.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00ff00\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis is officially Surrendering. He'll take the Beat to take him up to two regular Experiences and top off his Willpower. If this goes where I think it will, Adonis is going to be a lot more useful inside Amalgama itself using Mesmerism and Deception to sneak around and manipulate employees.</div></div> </div> </div></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T21:07:47-07:00","id":1119759,"title":"","content":"<i>The Forks</i><br /> <br /> <b>Scout</b>, slight of frame and weak of arm, takes action with the kind of godlike surety his Lineage is known for, Flux weakening the Captain and leaving him brittle, open to attack. But lack of skill and well-fashioned armour leaves the Captain completely unharmed and Scout's wild swing leaves the delicate Originist open to assault. The Captain turns unsteadily with the blow, favouring his uninjured leg, and sets himself with an obvious effort of will. A right-hand cross takes Scout high on the cheek, knocking him backwards and off-balance. He parries Scout's still-moving arm with his left, brings up his right to grab onto the wrist and <i>pulls</i> forwards, lashing out with an open left-hand to snap Scout's head to the side while simultaneously driving his bad heel into the side of his leg, further destroying his balance and <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=b8d14b21\" target=\"_blank\">easily</a> taking him down. The Nepri can feel his arm cracking from the strain. The Captain tries to follow up with <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=fdf5f041\" target=\"_blank\">further fluid blows</a>, but he is unsteady after taking such swift violent action and misses, choosing instead to continue hobbling forwards slowly.<br /> <br /> \u200b<i>OOC: So that last thing was the Captain's Reflexive action for the turn, this was his Instant Action. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> Scout takes 3L damage, the Leg Wrack Tilt, and the Knocked Down Tilt.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Mark 5</b> strikes out with violent prejudice against the man who had just tried to subdue him, heedless of the swarm of tiny Unborn that are tearing away strips of his flesh, leaving him covered in free-flowing black bile that has built up beneath his skin from punctures inflicted by the darts. With brutal force the Titan drives a fist into the man's chest, and he can hear resin plates cracking under the force of the blow and the great burst of air rushing from the man's lungs, followed by great gasps and ragged coughs as he lies on the ground, digging his fingers into the Earth as though he can will himself to remain conscious.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: </i><i><b>Thug 2:</b> [L][B][B][B][ ][ ][ ] <b>Tilts: </b>Knocked Down, Beaten Down. Armour reduced the damage to 3B, but he's pretty much out of the fight now.</i><br /> <br /> There's only one man left on the hill who hasn't yet acted. His buddy beside him was just struck down in a blast of lightning, the Captain was torn open by a silver hellbeast, and he's freaking the fuck out. Rock and roll time. The mercenary switches to full-auto and lets loose <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=a2ace3b4\" target=\"_blank\">a storm of darts</a> on <b>Earth. </b>They puncture Earth's leathery hide, delivering a payload of alchemically loaded toxins that dull their mind in no less severe a manner than Torment or the Flux haze of the Hundred-Handed had done before, but drawing black bile incited the swarm of Unborn insects to frenzy, tearing at Earth's flesh. It wasn't an unfamiliar sensation, and between the toxins and the gnawing, Earth remembers days gone by when their pack drew sustenance from their very flesh. <b>Satin </b>hears the attack, sees Earth go down, and charges the man, who is still firing and flails backwards wildly in a panic, with a full-throated roar. He is <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=e99759b7\" target=\"_blank\">shooting</a> at the silver monstrosity with an audible scream as they leap at him, and the two go down together in a <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=c2de9088\" target=\"_blank\">frenzy of claws</a> and gunfire. Proximity, volume, and the speed of panic means the darts do their deadly work even as the gun clicks over on empty. The man crawls unharmed out from under Satin's silvery bulk kicking and screaming even as the gorgeous beast they have become lies panting, bleeding heavy mist into the night air that gives their body a dream-like quality, something indistinct, not wholly real. There is the smell of heat and flame, and some of the worst of the mist fades as if from the dawn, but it still bleeds, and Satin is unsteady on their paws.<br /> <br /> <i>\u200bOOC: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> Earth takes 5L damage, the Drugged Tilt, the Arm Wrack Tilt, and it's your turn. <b>Satin: </b>[L][L][L][L][L][ ][ ] + [ ] <b>Tilts: </b>Drugged, Bleeding Satin is <b>not </b>in a good way. Spending Pyros to reduce damage stopped them from having their entire Health track filled up, but they're Bleeding and that means more damage per turn. Anyone know first aid besides Adonis?</i><br /> <br /> The mercenary nods curtly, grabs <b>Adonis</b> roughly by the collar of his coat, and hauls him to his feet, booking it back towards the van, making it up the hill in record time, hurling the Muse into the back and starting to double back for the Captain who is still hobbling up the hill. The armoured man who just climbed out from under Satin, laughing hysterically from having survived that assault unscathed where the Captain had been ripped open, starts scrambling towards the van, moving to grab the unconscious man still twitching from Earth's blast of lightning. The frozen Pilgrim, seemingly heedless of her own safety, serenely walks up the hill as if dancing over the snow or strolling along a beach, voluntarily climbing into the van and sitting opposite Adonis, hands clasped in her lap, looking at him thoughtfully with unblinking eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T23:11:19-07:00","id":1119779,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Patient, Watched, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Informed (Cuprum)<br /> Tilts: Swarm (3B/turn), Drugged, Arm Wrack<br /> Alembics: Verto (3), Stereo Humour (0), Arc (3)<br /> Health: LLLLLBBBOO | Willpower: 3/5 | Pyros: 6/12 | Beats: 4/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> Earth's head is swimming. Swatting the cloud of faux-Pandorans only makes the bugs dig into their meaty palm. Feels like their brain's gonna melt out of their ears. How did human hands make something like this...?<br /> <br /> Everything's kinda moving too slow and too fast at the same time. Earth notices Scout going down after a fist exchange, Mark fighting like hell in a cloud of Fluxbugs, Adonis being rushed into a van, and the humans packing up quick. Vivid battle-fantasies of twisting their necks in front of their terrified comrades are fading fast.<br /> <br /> And besides all that, Satin's gonna fade back into the mist soon. Earth's gotta help somehow, but if they get close, the swarm is just gonna eat the wolf too, and that'll be even worse. Gotta get these buzzing beasties off their back first.<br /> <br /> With one arm hanging numb at their side, blinking back bile dripping from their brow, Earth lurches toward the retreating humans. They slur an oath, something like: <b><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;i've been fighting...since the second i broke free of the earth...&quot;</span></b><br /> <br /> The rest gets lost in the swarm. Earth just charges at the men scrambling up the hill and lets their twisted flesh become a Tesla coil.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Using the Shock distillation to make an area attack, the bane of swarms. If I can tag a few of the humans in the process, even better, but my main goal is to burn out the swarm so Earth can approach Satin safely.<br /> <br /> Dexterity 1+Athletics 3+Creatures of Flux specialty 2+Azoth 3-Verto failure 2-Drugged 3. 4 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/535364\" target=\"_blank\">1 success.</a><br /> <br /> Spending 1 Pyros to cause aggravated damage. Anything within 3 yards takes 3A+1L, and another 1L for 6 turns.<br /> <br /> Also marking a Beat for damage in rightmost boxes.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 07-24-2017, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T09:22:12-07:00","id":1119909,"title":"","content":"<i>The Forks</i><br /> <br /> <b>Earth</b> charges into the fray, their hair a wild, whipping tangle of white and dark brown lashing around their head as the lightning builds, skin virtually humming with power. One of the men struggles back to his feet, wincing as electricity courses through him, seeing only Earth's mishappen feet. The one that grabbed <b>Adonis</b> is there, helping the mercenary up, shoving them out of the way as the man stumbles back towards the van as quickly as he can. Another armed man on the hill turns, lifting a gun and aiming it at Earth while the companion he had been guarding rushes for the van with a whimpering <b>Tom Barebones</b> in handcuffs, <b>Isla </b>futilely kicking and screaming and shoving at his back. The cloud of tiny Mockeries shrieks as they smell the Pyros building, tasting the changes in Earth's humours and try to scatter to safety.<br /> <br /> The world goes white.<br /> <br /> Charred Pandorans, truly ashen now, fall from the sky with a sound like rain, smouldering in the snow. There is a sudden patch of clear earth soaked with water surrounding the Pariah now, another man on his back, paint on his body armour flaking off, smoke from vicious burns rising off of him. The Captain has managed to hobble his way back to the van, looking at the terrifying outburst somewhat impassively, judging to see if they can wait, if they can risk that, but his men are screaming at him, they're hauling ass, they're referencing something that the men have on them, something that will make them safe. The man that tried to attack <b>Mark 5</b> has fled back up the hill and is just joining them now. Things have gone very badly, but it's not a complete loss. They'll come back for them, but first priority is getting out of there, immediately, with their cargo and without dying. The van closes up, Tom shoved in headfirst, Isla dragged in by her backpack, cuffed to seats beside Adonis and the frozen Pilgrim, and starts to pull away, back up the street towards the ordinary humans who are screaming and running from the Celebration Circle, sirens howling in the distance, a panicked throng of horrified voices.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: <i><b>Captain:</b> [B][B][B][B][B][ ][ ][ ] </i><b>Tilts: </b>Beaten Down (In the Van) <b>Thug 1: </b>[L][L][L][][ ][ ][ ] <b>Tilts: </b>Stunned, Knocked Down, Beaten Down (On the hill) <i>[B]<i><b>Thug 2:</b> [L][B][B]<b>[ ][ ][ ] <b>Tilts: </b>Beaten Down </b></i><b>(In the Van)Thug 3: </b>[L][B][B][B][B][B][ ] </i><b>Tilts: </b>Beaten Down (In the Van) <b>Thug 4: </b>[L][L][L][][ ][ ] <b>Tilts: </b>Stunned, Knocked Down, Beaten Down (On the hill) <b>Thug 5 </b>(In the Van)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> it's your turns now.</i><br /> <br /> A bunch of weary mercenaries are holed up in a van quickly pulling away. <b>Adonis</b> can feel the jolt of the wheels leaping off earth and back onto cobblestone pavement as the vehicle pulls away. A Created who looks like a little girl wrapped up in a cracking shell of clay is weeping and screaming in her seat, reaching for a worn down backpack. A man who looks crusted over with sand and salt whimpers and rocks in his seat. The Captain and several of the other mercenaries tear off their helmets, letting the smell of burnt hair and something uncomfortably like cooked pork into the relatively small cabin. The Captain smooths her short-cropped hair, and rubs a jaw that has obviously seen better days, seemingly eaten away by time, burn scars crawling up one side of her face. The other mercenaries are all surprisingly... non-martial in appearance. They look unused to violence. One of them is wearing a clerical collar that is poking out from the top of their body armour. Except for the Captain they look like librarians and doctors, like the football player that let themselves go after college, like people who don't know when the rug was pulled out from under them. Is this what <b>Erwin </b>has waiting in store for him? Is this a look at who Erwin is? The Captain takes a deep breath, and you can see them start to glow with a gentle silver light, slowly building Pyros under their skin. They exhale, and it flows out from them, impacting the most badly injured of them first.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: The Captain heals Thug 3 for the equivalent of 3L damage, so <i><b>Thug 3: </b>[B][ ][ ][ ][ ][ ][ ] <b>Tilts: </b>Beaten Down (In the Van). They will still be taking an additional 5L damage over the course of several turns, but at least they aren't dying.</i></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T13:42:10-07:00","id":1120052,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Tilts: Arm Wreck<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (3), Charites (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (3), Unfettered (0)<br /> Health:LLLLLLLLLBBBO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 0</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For a moment, the Titan was distracted by the Pandorans being disintigrated by lightning, and smiled. <b>Earth</b>. He felt a mixture of what would be pride and thankfulness, if he had the connection between the words right.<br /> In this moment of distraction, his opponent had crept away.<br /> The bad guys were running!...<br /> but they weren't just retreating. Mark 5 heard <b>Isla </b>protesting, and something in his mind changed gears. Young, confused, lost Isla he just met. And others, too!<br /> People were being abducted by evil Alchemists and/or their underlings, to a horrible fate. To be made into tiny bottles with a symbol on it.<br /> <br /> There was only one thing for an Hero to do: He would absolutely not let this car get away!<br /> <br /> With an ugly expression he didn't realize creeping on his face, the Titan ran as fast as he could, focusing Pyros, pumping it in a glowing stream into his working fist.<br /> He didn't mind his Disfigurement showing here, and so a dried husk moved towards the van, dead eyes stared ahead as the dirt in his hair was falling out due to the speed, one arm dangling uselessly at his side.<br /> Spured on by determination, he reached the proximity of the car, and Mark 5 slammed his fist into the ground with so much force stones embedded into his flesh were shooting out, and the ground gave away, moving, tilting, turning.<br /> <br /> He would <i><b>absolutely not </b></i>let them get away. Even if it <i>killed </i>him.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=437d08c2\" target=\"_blank\"> Bloody hell!</a> Forgot about <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=dd3a8ff2\" target=\"_blank\">Hygeius-Bonus</a> again. That's a total of 9(!) successes, so 11 turns the Earthquake reaks havok in an area of 200 yards. Damn, if this won't come back to bite him. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 07-24-2017, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T17:35:55-07:00","id":1120161,"title":"","content":"<i>The Forks</i><br /> <br /> The driver of the Amalgama van turns on an intercom, hollering to the mercenaries (conscripts?) in the back &quot;Holy fucking <i>shit!</i> You guys never said these things were this fucking <i>fast!&quot; </i>The desiccated man of dust and stone is a blur charging up a hill and through the snow, snow banks flying into the air in hazy white clouds and falling back to earth, billowing like the dust of a stampede. <b>Mark 5 </b>easily makes it up the hill before the van can pull out of the heavy traffic surrounding Johnston Terminal and the Manitoba Theatre for Young People when Mark, flaring with Azothic Radiance and streaming dust, strikes the earth. The blow is felt all across the Forks. Car alarms go off, glass starts to crack, people scatter further, unsure of what to do. Manitoba is not earthquake country. Some people fall, bleeding, as panes of glass smash over their heads and shoulders. For the time being, buildings and vehicles are mostly unscathed, but as the earthquake continues and intensifies, they will start to crumble. The beating heart of the city will go silent. The <i>sound </i>of it is immense, like a thousand taiko drums being beaten all at once and out of sequence. Like a series of explosions, one after the other. Like a roar of disapproval from something immense living below the earth. The aeolian harp of the Celebration Circle <i>wails </i>like a swiftly vibrating bell. As if a <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aWoH_RJn9Oc\" target=\"_blank\">choir of brazen throats</a> cried out in horror at the display.<br /> <br /> The street heaves and tears under the wheels of the van, sending it trembling, and the driver struggles to maintain control of the vehicle... but they <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=ffe721a8\" target=\"_blank\">manage to pull it off</a>, driving away from the Titan with increasing speed. The mercenaries inside the back of the van look at each other, and at the Captain, who is struggling to her feet to fling open the rear doors, precariously maintaining her balance with a hand clutched to a handhold on the ceiling. The only unharmed mercenary, the one in the clerical collar, stands, bracing themselves against the door frame, and with a muttered prayer <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=136acdbb\" target=\"_blank\">exhales Divine Flame</a>. The Pilgrims in the van can <i>smell </i>the Flux sublimating off the man. What the <i>hell </i>was that? He doubles over with the effort, weak at the knees, just barely able to pull it off, but Mark 5 can feel the Pyros draining away from him, the entire Alembic simply vanishing as the ground ceases trembling. The van turns a corner, and it disappears out of sight.<br /> <br /> They're gone.<br /> <br /> Out on the Red River the thick ice that forms the longest skating trail in the world is shattering, great planes and floes of ice heaving up onto the shore as if attempting to escape the turmoil underwater. An ashen cloud starts to form over the Forks, and the remaining Created in the Celebration Circle can feel it warp and change, setting them all just a little on edge. The grey filth of Flux begins to settle over the stones like perverse snowfall, brass and iron begin to tarnish. A Wasteland is festering. This place won't be clean for a week at least, if the compounded fallout of this much alchemy being thrown around doesn't taint it for longer, but the quality that had made the Celebration Circle special, its safety, was forever gone. For now, the Ramble would have to fall silent.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> the Unconquered Alembic just lost all its Pyros charge, and the Wrath of the Gods Distillation immediately ends. Combat is now over, Amalgama has gotten away, and now it's time to start picking up the pieces.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 07-24-2017, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T18:46:37-07:00","id":1120178,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Tilts: Arm Wreck<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Charites (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0), Unfettered (0)<br /> Health:LLLLLLLLLBBBO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> Experiences: 3 I Vitriol Experiences 0</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> One moment, his might made the very earth shudder and break, and he felt so filled with power there was nothing that could stop him. He just KNEW he would save them.<br /> <br /> Then, everything went still. The Divine Fire was snuffed by Flux, and he was unceremoniously left behind in the dust.<br /> He had drawn his sword, swung it... and the Iron had been shattered.<br /> <br /> He failed to save <i>them</i>.<br /> He failed to save <i>her</i>.<br /> He failed to <i>save</i>.<br /> He <i>failed</i>.<br /> <br /> <i>Again</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Created's mind went blank, and Mark 5 dropped to his knees, staring emptily ahead.<br /> His sight got blurry with black bile rolling down his face.<br /> <br /> The Tammuz was not aware of anything happening around him. He simply... sat there.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T20:09:33-07:00","id":1120198,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Patient, Watched, Connected (Winnipeg Ramble), Informed (Cuprum)<br /> Tilts: Drugged, Arm Wrack<br /> Alembics: Verto (3), Stereo Humour (0), Arc (3)<br /> Health: LLLLLBBBOO | Willpower: 3/5 | Pyros: 5/12 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> So much for all that.<br /> <br /> First thing Earth does: go to where the Captain was wounded, pack the bloodied snow into a snowball, and store it in their ballcap. This will be important later, for reasons Earth's conscious mind hasn't quite caught up to.<br /> <br /> Second thing: hurry to Satin's side, shove the silvery barghest, and urgently say: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;they're gone! change back!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Third thing: raise their hand, light up their fingers with eye-catching sparks, and shout: <b><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Come to Earth, Winnipeg! We need a body-fixer!&quot;</span></b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Earth steps up. I wanna resolve Connected to request a general favor from those still on the field: &quot;I am in charge right now, congregate around me. And specifically I need folks with Medicine dots.&quot; In terms of the Favors chart you posted, this is like &quot;request the nonviolent service of several people for the next several hours,&quot; stick around until the crisis is resolved.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T01:49:36-07:00","id":1120268,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama LTD), Inspired (Azoth), Inspired (Alchemy)<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: LLLOOO | Willpower: 2/6 | Pyros: 5/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b></div><br /> The captain had walked right over him. Hadn't even given him a second thought, despite his direct attack against her. Ignored him like he wasn't even there. When the quake came, Scout realized why. He'd never been any sort of danger to her. Not the way a Titan like the Mark 5 weapon was. Not like Earth with the power of the storm at her beck and call.<br /> <br /> Scout looked at his damaged arm, and decided to just let it hang for now, then up to Earth, who stood just over him. Then to the wolf creature that she was trying to tame. He felt the flux pouring out over the land and winced. This would be problematic. His fault? Did he create the wasteland in trying to harness disquiet? Before his mind could wander on that further, he focused his attention back to what he was seeing and hearing instead. What was she commanding for?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">&quot;Earth, I can help... like with Mark 5. But wasteland is here. Escape wasteland, reduce torment, heal the body, then pinpoint where Amalgama would have taken Tom and Adonis and the others.</span>&quot; he'd meant to think the second part for his own sake, not say it aloud. Oh well. You can't take back words already spoken. He stood, wobbly and checked to ensure his legs weren't as broken as his arm, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I may have enough information to pinpoint their storage location, but... no guarantees.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Not Scout wouldn't love to see another, much less attempt to calm it as he had before. Perhaps he could see Olmec... but not. Not now. He would not walk away from such a dangerous thing so easily as last time. And there was also Amalgama to deal with. How had they found them? Had they tracked Azothic radiance? Did they have spies? The one had mentioned the Botherud and... oh... where was Solomon? He had gone off just before the van had showed up...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/535625\" target=\"_blank\">3sux</a> to start detecting the azothic radiances and their locations. If Scout can sort out those he recognizes or knows first that'd be his priority. He should be able to detect Adonis from a little wayas out as well, so if he can, he'll keep track of that for as long as possible.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T11:43:16-07:00","id":1120432,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent; Katerina, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress, Stage 1), Callous, Beaten Down, Drugged<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: LLLLLOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 10/10<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 2</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis watches the other Created and the Amalgama employees silently through a drugged haze. His thoughts fly from one jumbled thought. Why him? Why were the others and he taken? The others left behind- Ferrum, Stannum, Aes. Fighters, able to defend themselves. Aurum is malleable, soft. Humans use iron and tin and bronze to make weapons, gold for decorations. Gold is what wars are fought over, other metals for what they fight those war with. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>Are they going to cut us up as soon as we get to wherever we're going? Or are they going to wait for that? No, they can steal Vitriol, we know they can. That's what they're going to do. They're going to perform the lacuna on each of us, then throw us away like trash when we aren't useful anymore.</i></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T18:48:37-07:00","id":1120574,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Tilts: Arm Wreck<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Charites (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0), Unfettered (0)<br /> Health:LLLLLLLLLBBBO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> Experiences: 3 I Vitriol Experiences 0</b></div> <br /> <br /> <i>Failed.<br /> Failed. Failed.<br /> Failed failed failed failedfailedfailedfailedfailedfailedfailedfailedfa iledfailedfailedfailedfailed<b>failedfailedfailed</b>failedfailedfailedfailedfailedfailedfailedfailed.</i><br /> The loop in his head went on and on.<br /> Then, another thought came up. <i>The Breaker had never failed in achieving his goal</i>. Sure, he went overboard, but he got stuff done. And he didn't have to deal with feeling weak, powerless, hopeless, guilty.<br /> The sweet promises of Torment were seductive:<b>don't think, don't feel, just do.</b><br /> It was a sort of enslaved freedom. One that seemed rather preferable right now. Mark 5 felt a Flux-like sensation creep up in his chest...<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=71ddc17c\" target=\"_blank\">4 Success!</a> No Torment this time! </div></div> </div> </div><br /> ... and fought it down as images of flying skulls and red mist, broken bodies and life-less eyes wavered in his head. <div align=\"center\"><br /> <br /> <i>No. No more.</i><br /> <br /> </div> Having failed was bad enough. He would not also give in to Torment, and make everything worse.<br /> <br /> <i>Broken Iron is still Iron</i>. He could be reforged.<br /> But that took time. And strenght. Strength he was not sure he still had. But he would be damned if he would let everything go to waste like that. There was still too much Iron in him to give up like that.<br /> However, the Titan still took no notice of the world around him.<br /> Fighting off the Torment left him drained, and he closed his eyes, hoping against all hope for dreamless sleep, for a short escape.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T22:04:38-07:00","id":1121191,"title":"","content":"<b>The Forks</b><br /> <br /> The sirens are wailing in the distance, getting louder, getting closer, as the teeming mass of humanity slowly quiets down. The sound of shattering glass still echoes through the evening air. <b>Satin </b>stumbles on unsteady paws, lurching into a semi-upright position and morphing back into the humanoid shape <b>Earth </b>is most familiar with, the shape of daring and challenging androgyny. They are still bleeding mist, their reduced bulk making it seem <i>worse</i>, the mist billowing around them, intensifying. There's the smell of potent alcohol hanging where the mist fades away. Most of the Ramble has fled, but not all. <b>Solomon</b> is stumbling back over the hill with the woman in the red dress <b>Adonis</b> was talking to earlier, a fellow <b>Cathar</b>. They are arguing, quietly, but they are. The worn out but potent aura of command around the woman in red has intensified. She radiates command, a Scarlet Woman, as Solomon darkens with anger, going from a deep blue to something approaching purple, seeming almost apoplectic with rage. He walks over to Earth with a dark, imperious expression on his face, grabbing their arm near Earth's Inscription, he flares with a <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=8980f253\" target=\"_blank\">subtle alchemical power</a> that feels absolutely <i>vile </i>on the way down, worming its way through flaws in Earth's flesh, seeking out the toxin that was carried in the darts and drawing it out, flowing on a tide of blue-tinted bile sweating through Earth's skin. He drags a rag from his pocket and cleans Earth off with surprising tenderness, waving off all attempts to fend him off and keeping hold of their arm with a firm grip that brooks no response. The Scarlet Woman stands nearby, arms crossed, eyes alive at the sight of Satin bleeding into the cold night air, studying the injuries, the way they flow, but Solomon rushes right past her and holds Satin, guiding them to a seated position in the snow. His teeth are gritted and his eyes are dark and he is hissing like a teakettle with violent emotion.<br /> <br /> &quot;You are <i>not </i>doing this to me again. Do you hear me, Psyche? Come on, hit me for deadnaming you like that. You swore you'd gut me if I tried to hold your past life over you.&quot;<br /> <br /> He <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=75f31d97\" target=\"_blank\">brushes a hand</a> over Satin's (Psyche's?) face, causing a flood of brilliant blue alcohol to flow from their pores, and cradles their body, glaring at the Scarlet Woman, who wordlessly moves to putting Satin back together as best she can, drawing lengths of cloth bandages and a sewing kit from their purse, examining the wounds with curiosity, occasionally tasting the humours. <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=ef6822c7\" target=\"_blank\">A minute passes in relative silence.</a> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=cac2b949\" target=\"_blank\">Then another.</a> &quot;I've stopped the bleeding,&quot; the Scarlet Woman says, voice hoarse and trembling as if overwhelmed by the experience (not from sorrow or empathy, from understanding, from solace, from Elpis) &quot;but wounds like that are beyond me.&quot; She draws a handheld stun gun from her purse &quot;Beyond bottled divinity, on the other hand? I think not.&quot; The Scarlet Woman drives the weapon into a wound, watching it sparks, dance, and set the alcohol-like ether Satin has instead of blood go aflame, filling out flesh the way sugar is spun into cotton candy. Though Satin's Azothic flame could easily overwhelm the mundane little engine but it holds, and Satin jerks closer to consciousness, a hand still somewhat taloned latching on the Scarlet Woman's wrist as eyes blast open, almost incandescent with Pyros. The continuous stream shorts it out, and the Scarlet Woman shrugs, &quot;It's rechargeable <i>and </i>multi-functional.&quot; Satin is... significantly better than before, no longer sitting on death's doorstep, gaping wounds looking like little more than shrapnel lacerations, arrow-like darts pushed out of their flesh and sitting on the ground. Satin is keenly aware that they're mostly naked, wrapped in ribbons in various states of filth, and quickly glances around, eyes daring someone to say something, to make an assumption. A jaundiced Wretched went off to fetch their clothes, and wordlessly handed them back. They're alive. Everyone's alive.<br /> <br /> <b>Scout's</b> attention is elsewhere, eyes half-lidded, he is keeping a proverbial eye on Adonis' Azothic Radiance, still easily within his range of sensation. He can feel them moving and turning, and they aren't going terribly far. They're off to the main Amalgama lab in the city, a lab complex that they share with the National Research Council of Canada developing medical technology. <b>Mark 5 </b>can feel something in his alchemical makeup change. His decision was an important one, he could tell. He would endure. He always did. Why else was he Inscribed with the word &quot;Survivor&quot;?<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> Mark 5 gains a Vitriol Beat from resisting Torment. He also gains a regular Beat from Tenacious for impressing Scout with his physical prowess. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> Earth gains a Beat for resolving Connected. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> Scout gains the Disquiet (Stage Two: Amalgama LTD) Condition. I figure infecting all of the strike force with Disquiet is going to do <b>something </b>a little bit extra than before.</i><br /> <br /> <b>The Van</b><br /> <br /> Meanwhile, <b>Adonis</b>, <b>Isla</b>, <b>Tom</b>, and the <b>Frozen Pilgrim</b> are all locked in the van with the people from Amalgama. The unassuming humans in riot gear are passing around something like a heavy duty first aid kit, each grabbing a particular cocktail of dubious looking alchemical reagents. Rest and rejuvenation, you suppose. <b>Isla </b>looks over to Adonis and manages a quivering smile beneath wide eyes. &quot;I met your friend Mark, at the Ramble,&quot; she say, fighting to keep the warble from her voice &quot;he said you knew about humans. And children. And why they're so strange about them.&quot; She goes silent for a moment, glancing over at the people from Amalgama who still aren't saying anything, but from their body language are obviously communicating- some work of Bronze alchemy keeping them connected mind-to-mind.<br /> <br /> &quot;Do you know where they're taking us? What are they going to do?&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Remember, Adonis has <b>been </b>to Erwin's workplace before.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T01:01:12-07:00","id":1121221,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Patient, Watched, Informed (Cuprum)<br /> Tilts: Arm Wrack<br /> Alembics: Verto (0), Stereo Humour (0), Arc (0)<br /> Health: LLLLLBBBOO | Willpower: 3/5 | Pyros: 5/12 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">&quot;Earth, I can help... like with Mark 5. But wasteland is here. Escape wasteland, reduce torment, heal the body, then pinpoint where Amalgama would have taken Tom and Adonis and the others.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Earth is tracking, if not listening closely. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Yeah. Shine that light again. I won't get in your way this time. We need to move- hey, let go- I'm fine, I'm <i>fine,</i> it'll burn out on its own!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Solomon's bedside manner needs some work. Earth just has to stand there, retching, while the Nepri purges the alchemical impurity and quite tenderly wipes the foul blue substance clean. Earth's not really about &quot;being cared for.&quot; It's humiliating! Especially when he shares some kind of confusing but deeply felt moment with Satin immediately after.<br /> <br /> Satin, not Psyche. It's a clear case of mistaken identity. Looks like Tammuz aren't the only ones who have trouble with names.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I may have enough information to pinpoint their storage location, but... no guarantees.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;It's a start. We got a backup, too.&quot;</span> Earth holds up the red snowball soaking into their ballcap. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;It's a piece of the leader of the pack. I think I can see 'em with this. It's like, uh- smelling blood from across a forest. But with thoughts.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Earth <i>really </i>wants to be moving away from those sirens right now, but the Scarlet Woman who teased Adonis earlier is still working on Satin. Stun gun, huh? That's smart. Gotta get one of those.<br /> <br /> The Mystic's flesh jerks to life. Drawn back from the spirit world, Earth guesses. Nothing about Satin's bare body comes as a surprise, except its incredible capacity to endure. Earth wants to be happy about this, crazy happy, but Torment is a wicked beast. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><i>This is your fault. Why didn't you sew the bandages on? Your precious spider would be dead, maybe for good, if these Cathars weren't here. Solomon obviously knows Satin better than you ever will, anyway. Twisted Freak. Atavistic creature. Keep your misbegotten flesh away. You don't even know what you are.</i></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Indulging my Torment, Alienated, for +1 Willpower.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Earth spits into the snow, no longer looking at Satin now that their eyes are lively again. Intimacy and vulnerability feels wrong right now, tainted by the remains of the Verto experiment and the tight embrace Solomon already shared with Satin. They're still in danger mode.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;The pack's on the move,&quot;</span> she orders the few still around. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;We need to be out of sight, and we need a spark, so we're going to the underpass of the river bridge. There's gotta be a live wire there. Scout, try to bring Satin down. I know I saw Mark 5, someone find him...&quot;</span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> If all goes well, they make the exodus to the concrete underpass a few blocks up the riverbank, dirty with rubble and snow and shattered ice floes. Hopefully the emergency vehicles are passing it by for now. There's got to be a source of electricity here somewhere, right? A junction box for the street lights on the bridge, some emergency lights to be shattered, a parked car to be broken into...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Looking for a source of electricity, however meager. Wits+Composure, 6 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/536150\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes.</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T02:41:54-07:00","id":1121235,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama LTD), Inspired (Azoth), Inspired (Alchemy), Disquiet 2 (Amalgama)<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: LLLOOO | Willpower: 3/6 | Pyros: 5/13 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b></div> <br /> <br /> Scout kept his attention on Adonis', though he noted when it was time to move, and the interesting idea of using a taser for a charge, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I still have a fix on Adonis. I'm glad his pyros burns bright this night, though he may soon not be. They're at the primary amalgama building. As long as I keep an eye on it, I should be able to keep track of him. But I have an idea for how to deal with them. But... I would need a Firestorm Catalyst. Or we could manually create one, but I've never done that before. Well, not on purpose.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> As he thought that over, he also looked towards Solomon. Would he realize what his fellow nepri was hoping for? If a firestorm had summoned Olmec before, perhaps a second stronger firestorm would bring him forth again. Perhaps if it was strong enough, he could extract more information. More information would be good for everyone. No one could blame him for that, could they?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Resolving Inspired (Azoth) to try and work up a better way for this plan to work. Maybe some sort of timed bomb firestorm catalyst, or even just a way for the group to channel and create a large firestorm rapidly on purpose. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_results\" style=\"width: 1px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_results_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_results_td\">2017-07-27 02:40:04</td> <td class=\"text_table_results_td\">Scout</td> <td class=\"text_table_results_td\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/c-Muddy+Waters\" target=\"_blank\">Muddy Waters</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_results_td\">Making a better Firestorm (10 again)</td> <td class=\"text_table_results_td\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/536158\" target=\"_blank\">1#1d10 <b>9</b></a></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_results_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_results_td\">2017-07-27 02:39:53</td> <td class=\"text_table_results_td\">Scout</td> <td class=\"text_table_results_td\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/c-Muddy+Waters\" target=\"_blank\">Muddy Waters</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_results_td\">Making a better Firestorm (10 again)</td> <td class=\"text_table_results_td\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/536157\" target=\"_blank\">1#1d10 <b>10</b></a></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_results_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_results_td\">2017-07-27 02:39:48</td> <td class=\"text_table_results_td\">Scout</td> <td class=\"text_table_results_td\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/c-Muddy+Waters\" target=\"_blank\">Muddy Waters</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_results_td\">Making a better Firestorm (10 again)</td> <td class=\"text_table_results_td\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/536156\" target=\"_blank\">1#1d10 <b>10</b></a></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_results_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_results_td\">2017-07-27 02:39:25</td> <td class=\"text_table_results_td\">Scout</td> <td class=\"text_table_results_td\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/c-Muddy+Waters\" target=\"_blank\">Muddy Waters</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_results_td\">Making a better Firestorm</td> <td class=\"text_table_results_td\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/536155\" target=\"_blank\">6#1d10 <b>8</b> <b>5</b> <b>10</b> <b>9</b> <b>1</b> <b>3</b></a></td> </tr> </table></div> 6 success. So that worked out.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8122,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","user":"ArchonAres","date":". 07-27-2017, 06:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T13:49:59-07:00","id":1121504,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent; Katerina, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress, Stage 1), Callous, Beaten Down, Drugged<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: LLLLLOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 10/10<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 2</b><br /> </div> <br /> Adonis raises his head as the small Tammuz speaks to him. He chuckles a little as he listens to her. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Children aren't like us. What we learn in weeks or months, it takes them years. I'd say more, but... this really isn't the time,&quot; </span>he says. He flashes her a drunken smile with courage he doesn't really feel. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">\u200b&quot;Don't worry, we're going to make it out of this.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> At her question of where they are being taken, he answers, <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;To their headquarters. It's here in the city.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> At her question of what's going to happen to them, he lies, <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;I don't know.&quot; </span>He was just thinking about what Amalgama has planned for them, but maybe it's the Mimic in him, he just can't bring himself to say share it with some a young-looking person. Even if she's just as emotionally mature as he is.<br /> <br /> Instead, he looks over at the Frozen Pilgrim. He had tried to help her escape, but she had just stood there. And had she... just walked along with the humans? His head is still so hazy. Anger and frustration starts to build in him. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">\u200b&quot;Who the hell are you, anyway? Are you working for these alchemists? Answer me!&quot; </span>He lunges as closer to her as the chains will allow. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Are you the Muse named Elektra? Please, tell me.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T15:29:20-07:00","id":1122094,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Tilts: Arm Wreck<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Charites (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0), Unfettered (0)<br /> Health:LLLLLLLLLBBBO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 3 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Survivor</b></div> That's what he was. How could he forget? It was confusing how something he had known for so long could still hold new meaning.<br /> Mark 5 got up. He would not give in. Not to Despair, not to Amalgalma, and certainly not to Torment.<br /> <br /> That didn't mean he didn't still feel wretched about his inability to do anything. What kind of wannabe-Hero is he if he can't stop the bad guys?<br /> Not to mention that this might have been his chance to atone for his crimes by doing good...<br /> He looked around, searching for the next usable source of Electricity. <div align=\"center\"><b>Be Prepared</b></div> He had learned that lesson the hard way. Prepare, heal, meet up with the others - he grit his teeth, he wasn't looking forward to telling them he failed- and take down Amagalma for good.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T20:18:15-07:00","id":1122179,"title":"","content":"<b>The Forks</b><br /> <br /> The remnants of the Winnipeg Ramble shamble their way over under the Louis Riel Bridge, following <b>Earth's</b> impeccable tracking ability, augmented ever so slightly by their Copper alchemy. Earth's senses are stronger than ever, enabling them to see more clearly, feel the world more intensely. <b>Satin </b>seems much better now, far more comfortable now that they're dressed, and <b>Solomon </b>and the <b>Scarlet Woman </b>have come along with them. There's a large transformer under the bridge, a source of power for the restaurant precariously leaning out over the Red River from the sculpted stone and towering white spire. It could sustain them easily, with more than enough power to reinvigorate them all. The conveniences of the modern world. <b>Mark 5 </b>shambles along with them as well, trailing a little ways behind. The Named dressed all in black, <b>Joshua</b>, is waiting under the bridge, sitting cross-legged in the snow, meditating. His eyes open, intricate gold leaf gleaming over black stone. There is a soft smile on his face.<br /> <br /> &quot;You survived the storm of arrows. I knew you would.&quot;<br /> <br /> Storm. Yes, storm. But not of arrows, storm of flame. <b>Scout </b>is thinking a mile a minute, mind making connections, wracking his brain for ways to just... <i>make </i>a Firestorm happen. But how do you will something like that into being? He's heard Flux alchemy can do that at will, can even protect you from it. Was Earth able to do that, once upon a time? Can Earth <i>still </i>do it, even if they don't necessarily want to? Touchy subject, best to think of other options. An Athanor are an option, yes, he's read about them in Highwinds' journal (which is one itself, Mercurius, for when he was ready. Highwinds was teaching a dedicated assistant after all). But that would require precious Vitriol, all that he had. And if he wanted to modify it <i>at all</i> he would require a little more, and a little risk. The exact transmutation was... difficult. Not impossible, certainly not for him, but most certainly difficult. But the potential to <i>unleash </i>that kind of power intentionally? And to summon something from the Flame Immortal with it? The allure was... intoxicating, inspiring.<br /> <br /> OOC: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> Scout regains a point of Willpower from resolving Inspired and gains the Steadfast Condition. Take a Beat for Resolving Inspired.<br /> <br /> <b>The Van</b><br /> <br /> When the lie slips past <b>Adonis' </b>bloody lips, <b>Isla</b> frowns. Maybe it's fear coming through the Muse's expression, maybe it's the drugs ruining his persuasive ability, but he isn't convincing her. She glances down at her chained hands, hair falling forwards messily to frame her face. God, she looks so fragile, a little terracotta doll. She smiles a little, and cries, nodding happily. &quot;You're lying, I can tell,&quot; she whispers hoarsely &quot;but that's okay. You're being brave. Brave is human.&quot; <b>Tom </b>is twisting in his manacles, rubbing at his wrists. The sensation is overwhelming him. He is used to being able to pick and choose what he feels, and when. The confinement is driving him further into panic, his fingernails digging into the clay of his skin in an effort to relieve some of the pressure. Endorphins flood from Created pain as well as human, perhaps even better, because they do not normally experience pain as anything except a dull absence.<br /> <br /> When the Muse lunges at the <b>Frozen Pilgrim </b>the mercenary alchemists look over with curiosity, watching the exchange. The woman's expression finally shifts, from soft detached amusement to perplexity. &quot;I am as you see me.&quot; The still small voice creeps past her lips, drifting to Adonis so perfectly across the intervening space it is like she was whispering in his ear &quot;You saved me when you did not have to. I could not leave you.&quot; The woman falls silent for a moment before tilting her head, perfectly smooth brow creasing slightly, frost crackling.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why did you save me?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T00:13:45-07:00","id":1122252,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Patient, Watched, Informed (Cuprum)<br /> Tilts: Arm Wrack<br /> Alembics: Verto (0), Stereo Humour (0), Arc (0)<br /> Health: LLLLLBBBOO | Willpower: 4/5 | Pyros: 5/12 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Earth didn't see Joshua or hear his pronouncement before the raid, so he's a mystery. Can't be all bad if he's a fellow meditator, though.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;How'd you know? Did the angels tell you?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The junction box is more important for now. Earth climbs up to reach it, with some difficulty, and grips the wires with their good hand.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'll assume it's an 8B source.<br /> Turn 1: heal 3 bashing damage and 2 lethal, +1 lethal from Efficient Conductor. Gain 1 Pyros.<br /> Turn 2: heal 2 lethal damage and Arm Wrack. Gain 1 Pyros +1 from EC.<br /> <br /> Now at no damage and 8 Pyros.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Pariah leaps back down to the snow, crackling and fidgeting. Their bad arm's lively again. What a rush after the deadening slog of the Ramble! Earth's ready to run a mile.<br /> <br /> Feeling invigorated, Earth charges their sensory humours with Pyros to see the world even more clearly. Maybe the black-clad Named with the onyx eyes has some insights in his aura, and the others too.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I wanna play with the Aura Sight distillation and this seems like a good opportunity. Charging Stereo Humour with 3 Pyros.<br /> <br /> Dicepool is Wits+Empathy+Azoth+Persistent Stereo Humour bonus (7 dice) minus Composure. If I don't know someone's Composure, I'll assume it's 2 and let Arcanist subtract dice if it's higher.<br /> <br /> Aura Sight, Joshua: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/536502\" target=\"_blank\">failure.</a> First time's not the charm.<br /> Aura Sight, Satin: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/536507\" target=\"_blank\">1 success.</a> What's their most prominent emotion?<br /> Aura Sight, Scarlet Woman: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/536508\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes.</a> What's her most prominent emotion? What emotion is she trying to hide?<br /> Aura Sight, Solomon: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/536509\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes.</a> What's his most prominent emotion? What does he feel about Satin? Is he expecting to stay and help for a while, or waiting for an excuse to leave?<br /> <br /> Let's try the other PCs in the scene, too.<br /> Aura Sight, Scout: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/536510\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes.</a> What's his most prominent emotion? What is his attention on right now?<br /> Aura Sight, Mark 5: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/536511\" target=\"_blank\">1 success.</a> What's his most prominent emotion?<br /> <br /> Having had some practice on the others, Earth tries to read Joshua again.<br /> Aura Sight, Joshua again: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/536512\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes.</a> What's his most prominent emotion? What is his attention on right now? What is his Refinement?<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> And as long as I'm rolling dice, Earth will attempt to use Clairvoyance on the Captain, using her blood snowball as the sympathetic Yantra. So to speak.<br /> <br /> Wits+Investigation+Azoth+Willpower. 6 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/536522\" target=\"_blank\">1 success.</a> I'll resolve Informed (Cuprum) to make that an Exceptional Success, unless I misunderstood how contested rolls work. For the rest of the scene, Earth should be able to perceive the Captain and everything in a 5-yard radius around her.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 07-29-2017, 03:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T03:31:45-07:00","id":1122284,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama LTD), Inspired (Alchemy), Disquiet 2 (Amalgama), Steadfast, Tormented<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: ALLLLL | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 5/13 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b></div><br /> Scout's mind was blazing along the trail of firestorm alchemy. Flux transmutations could do it. He looked to Earth, then changed the plan again. Not efficient. An athanor yes... perhaps if anyone knew where one was already... but he hadn't heard anything about that yet. He could make one... that would be complicated, possibly take more time than he wished to spend. But to draw forth the flame immortal... yes, he could do this.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'll put that dramatic failure for sublimation by fire here, if it hasn't already hit. Seems like a great spot for it.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The distraction was probably why his half-hearted attempt to to sublimate Satin's torment failed so spectacularly. The wasteland crept out around them again, and the scorching of Azoth left him with a lot of damage, but despite that his flesh tore and left him looking just as when he'd weathered the small firestorm from before, his attention was entirely focused. Focused on the thought process he had going. He felt excited at the prompt of discovery. Oh, perhaps amalgama had a device that could generate the flux for a firestorm. It would run on sacred vitriol, but if vitriol had already been stolen, why not put it to use? But for that to work, he'd need for them to already have such a device... or perhaps he could use the vitriol that had already been stolen on the spot. But he would need to find their vitriol storage. And was this blasphemy? Or was it doing the right thing? Surely the research he pursued was worth the potential risk, and furthermore, it would also destroy the Amalgama building. And free their friends. Yes, free Adonis and the others. That was important to Earth and Mark 5, so it would have to be at least a secondary goal.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'd like to use this as a moment of Obsession to refill Scout's willpower. However, with the already chosen dramatic failure of Sublimation by Fire that putting up another wasteland, that drops me to 1 dice to resist.<br /> <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/536530\" target=\"_blank\">Well that went worse than expected.</a>. I'm going to hold off on using steadfast for now. I feel like it's going to be important later when he's trying to do something that could get everyone killed if he fails, like forcefully generating a firestorm from scraps of amalgama technology. I will for kicks, make this one a dramatic failure though. Because being double-ly tormented as an Osirian is awesome! I don't think I can get another beat from a dramatic failure that fast? But still this is amusingly worth it.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T10:09:35-07:00","id":1122382,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Tilts: Arm Wreck<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (1), Charites (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0), Unfettered (0)<br /> Health:LLLLLLLLLBBBO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 3 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b></div> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000080\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u><b>YOU!</b></u></span>&quot; </span>Mark 5 near exploded, as he grabbed Joshua by the collar. Power still flowed through his body, and his wrath and confusion at being betrayed by his fellow Pilgrim made him lash out. He wanted to bash that treacherous head in! If it hadn't been for him, he would have been able to save ...<br /> Mark 5's<b> rage evaporated. </b>No. He wouldn't have been able. Not when they had someone that could spew Flux and render him harmless, powerless... useless.<br /> For what use had he been? He had achieved nothing. <b>Guilt</b> filled his head. He needed to know more before acting. He needed to know his <i>Intention</i>. Something he said. Something about a mission.... <div align=\"center\"><br /> <i>&quot;I have a message for you. I was found by a Messenger of the Principle, and told to be in this place, for you and your throng.</i></div> <div align=\"center\"><i>I was told to be here when a great storm would break, because it is important for you to witness it.&quot;</i></div> <br /> His mighty shoulders slumped, and he let go of Joshua. &quot;<span style=\"color:#000080\">Why? Why did you betray us?&quot;</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T14:27:36-07:00","id":1122487,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent; Katerina, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress, Stage 1), Callous, Beaten Down, Drugged<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: LLLLLOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 10/10<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 2</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis winces when Isla points out the lie. No, she definitely isn't a child. So he should stop treating her like one.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Nothing good, I know that. They've figured out a way to make Alembics into drinks.&quot; </span>He doesn't say more, because he figures the others can figure out what that means. <hr />The Frozen Pilgrim's words take Adonis by surprise. He blinks a couple times. <i><span style=\"color:#00ff00\">She let herself be captured because she felt grateful to me? </span></i>Her question leaves him silent for a few moments as he thinks it over. He stares at the floor of the truck and responds. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;You look like a Created I knew. A Muse named Elektra. She was the first other Created I ever met. She was my first true friend, taught me a lot. But I let her down. I failed her.&quot; </span>He's surprised at himself for saying this: he's never brought it up to any other Created before. He doesn't say any more; he raises his head to look her in the eye again. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;I guess I'm trying to make up for some sins I'm carrying around.&quot; </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T21:06:10-07:00","id":1122895,"title":"","content":"The Named known as <b>Earth </b>stretches their alchemical range, tapping into the practical aspects of Cuprum they had not yet experienced. They could <i>see </i>what others could only guess at- what would they see if they turned that gaze inwards? <b>Joshua </b>neither flinches nor moves when <b>Mark 5 </b>rushes to grab him by the throat, his mind is perfectly placid, and Earth can see nothing. The Golem seems perplexed at Mark's outrage &quot;But I did not betray you. I did not lead them to you. Angels told me to wait, to speak with you, so that you would not flee the storm. I did so, because I was told it would show me where to step next on my Pilgrimage, and it did! &quot;<br /> <br /> The ground shudders and warps as the snow seems to curdle into frozen scum under their feet, Divine Fire bursting forth from <b>Scout's</b> battered and bruised body, ripping its way out of his flesh, doing horrific damage his slight frame. Fire bursts from <b>Satin's</b> flesh as well, sublimating fresh skin and blood back into mist, and they grab hold of the generator, letting a single, clear burst of the charge undo the damage and the flow of the Flame Immortal healing them completely. Satin steams, melting the snow around them, and Earth can see the heavy black storm clouds of Torment gather around them like thick storm clouds. It would be shocking, horrifying even, if they hadn't just stepped off the Fury's road. It was a wave of absolute fury, a disregard for life so complete that it almost reminded Earth of a Pandoran in a feeding frenzy. Almost. A fleeting image flashes by, the silver wolf-beast emerging again, a massive, dextrous paw engulfing Scout's head and tearing it clear of his shoulders. It would be easy to do in that form, and he was weak enough that it was feasible.<br /> <br /> Earth's gaze shifts again, focusing on the <b>Scarlet Woman</b>, her Azothic Radiance burning with the pale blue flame of calm curiosity, a carefully controlled ghost of a smile on her lips, but smouldering underneath the robin's egg blue, bleeding into it to form a halo of imperial purple, is a visceral deep red. Red like raw meat, red like blood bright from the wound, red like arousal, red like <i>need</i>. The interplay is... complex. Like the Scarlet Woman wants to <i>watch </i>and wants to <i>act</i>, but more than anything else she wants to watch <i>someone else </i>do something they will regret. Where does impurity lie in the soul? What encourages it to emerge? A Cathar's questions, and the devilish Cathar whip in a sharpened tongue.<br /> <br /> When she shifts to look at <b>Solomon </b>the blue-skinned Osirian has a head wreathed in the pale grey clouds of regret, and beneath those clouds a storm of colour all directed at Satin. He is incandescent with the indigo of disgust, but it is not clear who it is directed at, though it is shot through with the pale amber glow of love faded over time. There is also the bright green bubble of resentment, simmering beneath the indigo, threatening to bubble to the surface, but even as Earth watches the indigo deepens and the amber glows more brightly, like a conscious effort to keep the resentment from boiling over. The uncomfortably cheerful yellow of discomfort, pale yellow, mustard yellow, the kind of yellow one would make a particularly appalling wallpaper, gleams about his hands, but even as the tension in Solomon's body rises the yellow is smothered by the earthen tones of resolve. He isn't going anywhere for now.<br /> <br /> Trying again to examine the enigmatic Golem in black, Earth sees clearly the colours of <b>Joshua's</b> Azothic Radiance, and there is the blue and gold of awe and inspiration. Blue and gold like a pharaoh's death mask, like the Ishtar Gate of Babylon (Earth has seen pictures of that, once upon a time. Ishtar was the Demiurge behind the Tammuz line). His attention is on Mark 5, battered and blackened by his own bile, but still powerful, still confident. Such power! Such skill! Within his hands, the ability to shake the foundations of the world. When Earth gazes for the black-clad Golem's Refinement there is a burst of blinding white light that is like trying to stare at the sun, like his Azoth is trying to burn through his skin, leaving him looking like little more than a ghost wrapped around a blazing white phosphorus core. Light-Bringer. Student of the ephemeral.<br /> <br /> When Earth turns their gaze elsewhere, they can see, simultaneously, the Created gathered under the Louis Riel bridge, and the interior of the Amalgama van. All the mercenaries without their helmets, looking so terribly human. The <b>Captain</b> marked so clearly by her scars. <b>Adonis</b>, <b>Tom Barebones</b>, <b>Isla</b>, and the <b>Frozen Pilgrim</b> chained a couple of seats down. She hears Adonis talk about some Pilgrim he used to know, a Muse named Elektra. That he'd failed her. The Frozen Pilgrim turns her head, and makes eye contact with the Earth-presence.<br /> <br /> She smiles.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> take a Beat from your Refinement Condition. This is a step for Earth, they're assessing and studying rather than acting, and that's an extremely Cuprum thing to do.</i><br /> <br /> <b>The Van</b><br /> <br /> While processing the concept of Alembics and Distillations in potions, <b>Isla</b> scrunches up her nose in disgust at the idea. Alchemy is a thing you just <i>do</i>, anything else seems just so horribly artificially. <b>Tom</b>, on the other hand, seems to jolt out of his reverie, trying to reach into his coat for his notepad and pencil, for his tape recorder. The words have to be <i>right </i>before he can say them, or why say anything at all? <b>The Frozen Pilgrim </b>considers Adonis' words carefully, placidly staring him in the eyes with an easy gaze, face shifted back to the relaxed mask of bemusement. The near-silent, intimate voice, so quiet it might as well be his own thoughts, drifts (emanates?) again.<br /> <br /> &quot;What is a sin?&quot;<br /> <br /> And then the Frozen Pilgrim turns and looks... not <i>at</i> the Captain, but <i>around </i>them, like they know something that the Captain doesn't. And then she does something strange. She <i>smiles</i>, warmly and reassuringly, the way Adonis has seen human mothers look at their children.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> I just realized enough time has elapsed that you can resolve Disquiet (Waitress) for a Beat, though, of course, you could trade it for Disquiet (The Captain) instead. You'd still get the Beat for resolving the previous one, but now you get a whole new complication that will quickly come up!</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T02:27:39-07:00","id":1122944,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Tilts: Arm Wreck<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (1), Charites (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0), Unfettered (0)<br /> Health:LLLLLLLLLBBBO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 3 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b></div> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000080\"><u><b>FLEE?!</b></u><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u><b>!</b></u></span>&quot; </span>Anger returned to Mark 5 in a flurry.<br /> Who did that guy think the Titan was? &quot;<span style=\"color:#000080\"><b>Run from adversity?! I am a Titan! </b>We don't run, we embrace!&quot;</span><br /> Exasperated, Mark 5 sighed. He looked into Joshua's eyes.<span style=\"color:#000080\"> &quot;You have betrayed us, if unwittingly. If you had not distracted me, all this might have gone differently.&quot;</span><br /> He looked down at his fist. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;I would have been able to hurt them more than I did, and they would have had to rely on their damned Flux much sooner.</span><span style=\"color:#000080\"> At the very least, they might have gone for me rather than Isla..</span><span style=\"color:#000080\">.&quot;</span> Looking back to Joshua, he wanted to say something along the lines of &quot;hope it was worth your step forward&quot; in an acidic tone, but if what Joshua said was true, he had only acted according to the whim of the Principle.<br /> Thinking that he might have done the same thing made Mark 5 angry with himself. Chaotic creation, that's what the principle was. And here, it had created pain and suffering.<br /> He brushed past Joshua with definetly more force than necessary, and stepped to the generator to heal.<br /> <br /> <i>Wow, Scout is in bad shape</i>, he noticed. <i>What did they DO to him?</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T10:00:45-07:00","id":1123053,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Patient, Watched<br /> Alembics: Verto (0), Stereo Humour (3), Arc (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 3/5 | Pyros: 5/12 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> It's amazing how much you notice when you step back instead of charging in and throwing lightning bolts left and right. Were those auras always there?<br /> <br /> Mark 5 is furious at onyx-eyes, but instead of jumping in, Earth waits and watches his bright red anger ground out into muddy guilt and exasperation. Scout is studying Earth like a specimen, discarding them, not focused on Satin's Torment but rather distracted by some beautifully complex scheme in his mind's eye. The operation of Saturninus backfires horribly. Two Radiances are now choked with Torment. Satin sinks deeper into vicious fury, ready to kill. The Scarlet Woman would be glad to see the wolf come out again. Earth knows that love is a sweet sickness of the spirit, a fairy-light that draws the afflicted into doing terrible things, so it makes perfect sense that the emotion would be mixed with disgust and resentment in Solomon's aura. Like Earth and Dead Girl, there is a heavy chain of history between Solomon and Satin.<br /> <br /> On a second look, Joshua's colors make sense. Another one of Ishtar's wayward children, stricken by a glimpse of the divine. Did the angels reward him with a vision for delaying Mark 5? If he's refining himself into burning Phosphorus, he won't want to calm things down. Might even make things worse. It's a volatile situation, and the only one here who's going to prevent an unstable reaction is Earth. <i>That's </i>new.<br /> <br /> The Pariah cuffs Scout on the shoulder and points him to the generator. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;You blew it, short stack. Go ride the lightning before a wolf eats your hand. <sub>(i swear you'd starve if we didn't feed you.)</sub>&quot;</span><br /> <br /> That's a start. At least it'll get him out of Satin's way before the Riven bites. Earth tries to give him some constructive direction: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;We want the same thing. If you're scheming, start by looking around. Something must've brought Mark's pal here. Can you still do that thing where we lick your blood and get smart ideas? This is a good time for inspiration.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Now to see how the theory of far-seeing works in practice. Claw dipped in the thawing blood, heterochromatic eyes blink. Earth's brown eye looks at the underpass, and mystic hazel looks at the owner of the blood.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> There she is. The Captain's face appears first, marked with burn scars, smelling of iron and sweat, and the vision blooms out from that central point.<br /> <br /> They're human under the armor. No horns or scales. Weak, pathetic humans. But how does this fit into a normal human life?<br /> <br /> Adonis is there, pouring his guts out. Feels like reading somebody else's diary. And Tom Barebones fumbling with his tape recorder, and that small clay golem Isla that Mark 5 likes, and a soft snowy woman...looking back?<br /> <br /> ???<br /> <br /> What's that expression? No one's ever looked at Earth quite that way before. A smile of...hunger? Mockery? Desire? Contempt? Maybe if they look a little deeper...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Attempting to use Hearing the Inner Voice on the Pilgrim. Wits+Composure+Azoth vs Composure+Azoth. 9 dice for me: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/536933\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes.</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T12:38:50-07:00","id":1123119,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Inspired (Alchemy), Informed (Amalgama LTD), Disquiet 2 (Amalgama), Steadfast, Tormented<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 8/13 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b></div> <br /> <br /> Scout glanced up to Earth as she cuffed him. His eyes seethed for a moment, squinting at her. She thought she could push him around just because she was bigger, stronger, more in tune with her power? Scout took heed of her words, though and relaxed a moment. Yes. His body was heavily damaged. What was that second part she'd said?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Assuming it's 8B source as Earth did, I will heal 1Ag, 3L, and 1 pyros on my first round, thanks to efficient conductor. 2nd round is 2L and 2 pyros thanks to efficient conductor. I'm assuming this takes care of the arm-wrack tilt, given there is 4B of extra electricity in that round.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Scout let the anger flood out of him as he restored his health and pyros. With that comes clarity. &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">You want to lick my blood to... ah. You mean you wish to Glimpse my journey. How is looking into my past going to help us now? I already have an idea on how to utterly destroy those pathetic worms for their assault. I just need the ingredients. Enough vitriol would do the trick. I could perhaps steal from the stores they have stolen from the dead, or formulate some from my own person, though that won't get as large of a firestorm. I can probably figure out how to put a timer on it so we wouldn't have to be near it for activation. We'll probably need to reduce our detectable azothic radiances for any sneaking in. And even then I'm sure their security would likely notice us. Especially since we'll be in a rush as they're likely to start processing their acquisitions soon. Which will limit the amount of time I have to create the bomb. I suppose I could create a normal bomb, that doesn't use pyros, but they might contain that. Oh, what if we did multiple bombs, but only one was a firestorm bomb? That could do. But we'd need ingredients. And even then, I'm not an experienced chemist *yet*, so unless one of you know how to make bombs,</span>&quot; he rubbed his chin, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">If they can detect Azoth, it'll mean I might have to create the bomb from within the facility. I don't know if a firestorm catalyst would radiate any sort of warning signal or energy before it's detonation.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Hmm... oh we could have the Mark 5 Weapon level the complex on one side as an alternative. If he can do that earthquake thing again, it would put him in considerable danger, but would create a large enough distraction for us to get in. And then all we need is for someone to short out the power in their facility. Easy enough for you Earth?</span>&quot; He glanced to each of them as he spoke, but didn't really pay any heed to their faces. He didn't have time to consider the implications of their emotions right now. That was Adonis's job. And Adonis... &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">If Adonis is smart, he'll be attempting to use that gold of his to turn them against themselves about now. I'm afraid I'm not able to manipulate disquiet in that manner, but I did suffuse that squad with a sufficient amount. I wonder if I could suffice the entire building with disquiet... and what exactly sort of an effect it would have. Oh, what if I intentionally generate a wasteland, spoiling the liquids in their facility? That would probably ruin a sufficient amount of their alchemical supplies, right?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Scout was rambling now. Guessing, taking shots in the dark. His mind was working overtime, but he couldn't nail down a single good idea.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Indulging in Introspective until someone stops him and forces him to get moving. Be warned, I'm good at rambling :P</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8122,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","user":"ArchonAres","date":". 07-31-2017, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T12:21:02-07:00","id":1123591,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Patient, Watched<br /> Alembics: Verto (0), Stereo Humour (3), Arc (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 3/5 | Pyros: 5/12 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 2/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> Earth closes their clairvoyant eye for a minute. It's a lot to take in. Mark 5 is rejuvenated, Scout is...monologuing. Even a brick-dumb Tammuz like Earth can tell you that endless words are a sign of Torment. Who knew that Osirans suffered the same way?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Yo, I know I'm not the brain genius of this throng, but calling down a firestorm is a <i>really </i>dumb idea. You gotta respect the vitriol. </span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998318-ic-promethean-the-created-2e-muddy-waters?p=1003708#post1003708\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Trust me.</span></a><span style=\"color:#DAA520\"> And I mean, it might be <i>easy</i> for me to short the power, but it'd be messy...wait, are you making fun of me?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Ugh. How are you supposed to motivate someone who's A) smarter than you, and B) unbalanced? Where's Adonis when you need him?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;You're just building sandcastles- you're not even building sandcastles right now, you're just spilling words. Mark, help me out here. We've got a lot of parts here, but no plan. Lashing out isn't gonna help when they've got all the guns and the potions and they know the territory. Scout: <i>do the work.</i>&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Both Earth's hands are on his shoulders. That line always worked for Heartsblood: <i>do the work. </i>Speaking of which, there's still Satin's Elpis to decode...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Wits+Empathy+Stereo Humour 2+Equipment (good relationship) 2 to infer Satin's Elpis, and a way out of their Torment. 6 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/537184\" target=\"_blank\">failure.</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> No good ideas. There's that Alienated nature bubbling up again. Despite tonight's conversation, Earth doesn't know Satin very well at all. But who does...?<br /> <br /> Solomon. Earth takes him aside for an awkward conversation. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Hey. Man to man. I guess you two know each other. Do you know how to balance Satin's humours? Can you two go off somewhere and...work on that? I'm just trying to keep any heads from getting ripped off.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'm gonna pitch this one as a Cuprum-related Milestone. Rather than taking personal responsibility for helping Satin without really knowing how, Earth is choosing to put aside their jealousy, step back, and humbly ask someone else with greater expertise (ie, Satin's ex) to soothe the Ulgan's Torment. And generally following the Hermit Role by distancing from a close confidant.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Earth opens their clairvoyant eye to focus on the van again. What does the Captain think about all this? Maybe the Frozen Pilgrim watching earlier was just a trick of the mind.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Attempting to listen in on the Captain's thoughts with Hearing the Inner Voice. Hopefully I'd like a sense of &quot;what does she expect to happen next, is this situation gonna resolve in the next few minutes or does the throng have an hour or two to prepare?&quot;<br /> <br /> Wits+Composure+Azoth, 9 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/537187\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes.</a> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 08-01-2017, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T14:37:04-07:00","id":1123639,"title":"","content":"<b>Louis Riel Bridge</b><br /> <br /> The Named Pariah tries to hear the <b>Frozen Pilgrim's</b> mind, but that calm, reassuring smile holds without faltering, facial expression unchanging. <b>Earth's</b> mind smoulders, filled not with thoughts, but instead with clarity, awareness, knowledge bordering on instinctual. Earth gets a flash of that alchemist from November (it seems so long ago) the one Adonis distracted to protect the Throng, and they see him arguing with Adonis, heatedly. It reminds Earth of the rows they used to have with Dead Girl. But watching Adonis argue with the alchemist... it doesn't fill them with anxiety, or concern, but instead with contentment, even joy. This argument is something that <i>must </i>happen.<br /> <br /> With <b>Scout </b>musing on the virtues of earthquakes and Firestorms, <b>Solomon </b>and the <b>Scarlet Woman </b>share a concerned glance. The blue-skinned Nepri's face brooks no reproach, she is not to antagonize him, and the slight flash of fear bordering on delighted disgust shows that she knows better than to mess with someone whose idea of a surefire plan is to unleash the truest expression of the Divine Fire's wrath. When Earth approaches Solomon, the elder Pilgrim simply nods while Satin stands to the side and broods, breathing hard and trying to avoid looking at Scout. Solomon walks over, whispers hard but not unkindly, and the two storm off. Talons flex and retract and Satin's flesh ripples, adopting a form with significantly more muscle tone than the one Earth is used to.<br /> <br /> Focusing back in on the van, Earth hears the echoes of the <b>Captain's </b>mind. She can hear the whispers of <i>several </i>voices at once, far more than she is ready to hear, and it borders on overwhelming. What Earth manages to process is the sense of general discomfort at the homunculi (that's an interesting word) talking to one another, making them seem sympathetic... approachable. None of them thought that this is where they would end up when their medical practice, or spiritual practice, or mystical experimentation, started to smoulder with something incredible, something miraculous. Raided houses, raided labs, raided churches, broken bones. Monsters in the night. The only way to make it stop was to become a leg-breaker and fire-starter yourself. They just want it to <i>end </i>but they'll be at the office in ten minutes and then the homunculi will go into processing and initial testing for the next several hours. But their part is done.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> replace Earth's Aspiration &quot;Gain a dot of Medicine&quot; with &quot;Push Adonis to confront Erwin&quot; and take the Shaken Condition from the overwhelming cloud of voices. Also take a Vitriol Beat from the minor Milestone. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> take a Beat from indulging the Introspective Condition.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T16:12:07-07:00","id":1123681,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Tilts: Arm Wreck<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (1), Charites (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0), Unfettered (0)<br /> Health:OOOOOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 3 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b></div> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Assuming 8 B source:<br /> Turn 1: 3 Bashing, 2 Lethal. +1 Pyros.<br /> Turn 2: 4 Lethal, 1 Pyros.<br /> Turn 3: 3 Lethal, 1 Pyros.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> It took some time for the Titan to restore himself. The damage to his body was extensive.<br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Mark, help me out here.&quot; </span><br /> Mark 5 turned to Earth. He'd missed something going on, apparently. Scout was spouting stuff non-stop. He held on to him.<br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Scout: <i>do the work.&quot;</i></span><span style=\"color:#000080\"><br /> &quot;Work, Scout!&quot;</span>Mark 5 chimed in. He also gently smacked Scout on the back of his head. Supposedly, that helped with thinking.<br /> <br /> Basically at the same time, he told his fellow Tammuz <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;We need to get moving, Earth. They got Isla, and...&quot; T</span>he Titan's voice got silent. He lifted his hands, and looked at them. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;These are strong hands, aren't they? And yet, I could not hold on to them. They got away. I failed, Earth. Again.<i> I failed</i>. I was helpless, weak. I could do nothing. They took away my Transmutation.</span><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;</span><br /> He looked to Earth, his eyes practically begging for help. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;How can I call myself a hero if I cannot help people?</span><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T16:20:09-07:00","id":1123685,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Patient, Watched, Shaken<br /> Alembics: Verto (0), Stereo Humour (3), Arc (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 3/5 | Pyros: 5/12 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 3/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> Following the commands of the Divine Fire and/or alluring ethereal women is nothing new for Earth. Whatever happens, Adonis needs to be set on a collision course with the alchemist. Of course!<br /> <br /> Listening to the Captain's mind leaves Earth dumbstruck. Many voices? Humans don't even think like they do? Is that how they fit in so easily with each other? The gulf between lead and gold seems wider than ever. Actually, the Pariah has never listened to other Created thoughts either. What if Earth is the only one who's alone in their own head? Is that why they're so broken? It would explain a lot...the thought is unsettling, and it doesn't fade.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;We need to get moving, Earth. They got Isla, and...&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Yeah. And Adonis, and Tom, too. I can still see 'em in one eye. We haven't lost the scent yet.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> But this is more than a tactics issue, huh? Mark looks...powerless. That's new and scary.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;These are strong hands, aren't they? And yet, I could not hold on to them. They got away. I failed, Earth. Again.<i> I failed</i>. I was helpless, weak. I could do nothing. They took away my Transmutation.</span><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Earth takes Mark 5's hands and feels the weight of them. Small calloused hand and fleshy claw feeling two hunks of stony ironflesh. This little moment is about as intimate as the two of them have ever been, even though it's framed more like admiring a tool than a body. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Strongest I've ever seen. I thought for sure you had 'em back there, man. You could move the world with these hands, if strength was all you needed. But it ain't. &quot;</span><br /> <br /> Took away...? <i>Oh.</i> Earth tries to comfort him, and comes off unusually soft. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Mark, that's not on you. What they did- that's Flux. They flared up the impurities in your own charged Alembic and made the whole mix burn out. Once you know what to look for, it's scary easy. You never saw a Freak with that trick before, huh? It's a nasty one. We called it <i>Solvent.</i> I dunno what kinda knockoff they used, but you're lucky it just grounded out your charge<i>. </i>I could do <i>way </i>worse back in the days, and being strong doesn't help a lick. Flux is anti-life. It turns your own imperfections against you until you can't see the perfect bits anymore.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;How can I call myself a hero if I cannot help people?</span><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Bringing up the past made things uncomfortable all of a sudden. This is too weird, too scary, too close. Earth pulls back their hands and scoffs at him. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Wait, wait,<i> you're</i> asking <i>me</i> how to be a hero now? We're really screwed this time.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Can't shove vulnerability back in somebody's face that easily, though. Not when Mark's worked so hard and so much to keep his fellow golem on the right path. Earth runs a claw through their hair and tries again. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I don't know. I don't call myself a hero, and I know I can't help anyone. Including you.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Torment simmers. But with effort, it subsides. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Well...that's a lie. If I really believed that, I would have turned and ran. But I rallied y'all here to the bridge. So I guess I believe we can help Adonis and the others. But I still know I'm weak in ways that make it hard to do right. I don't pretend to be something I'm not.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I'm gonna be really real with you. You made yourself strong as Iron, but Iron ain't perfect. And the more you make yourself like Iron, the more the big deep imperfections of Iron become part of you. When I lose a fight, it sucks, but I lose all the time and I don't expect better. But you've built up your whole self around being the strongest, so when <i>you </i>lost that fight tonight, it <i>broke </i>you. You put all your weight on your Vitality, and when they cracked that pillar with Flux, the whole temple crashed down. That doesn't mean you <i>embrace </i>Flux- that's where I went stupid. But you gotta start seeing those imperfections as part of what you are. Otherwise, something's gonna break again when we try to help.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> That's all the motivational juice Earth's got. There was barely any stuttering in that whole spiel. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Think on it, alright? We've got some time. I'm not riding out of here in a hurry just so you can prove you're strong enough. We're gonna make a plan and we're gonna do something on our terms, not the alchemists'.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 08-02-2017, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T17:34:12-07:00","id":1124091,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Tilts: Arm Wreck<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (1), Charites (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0), Unfettered (0)<br /> Health:OOOOOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 3 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Yeah. And Adonis, and Tom, too. I can still see 'em in one eye. We haven't lost the scent yet.&quot;</span><br /> Mark 5 near chocked. Pretty Boy was in trouble, too? He had failed not just one, but several Created? This burden came crushing down with force... wait, did Earth say she can see them?<br /> <br /> <br /> When Earth takes Mark 5's hands he feels strange, uncomfortable. Earth basically never touched him. Not even when they had fought - lightning and all that. That hug back when had been an extraordinary occurence. He wasn't being used to being touched softly, as Adonis had learned. And yet, this was oddly... comforting. Uncomfortable, but comforting. He wanted it to end. He wanted it to go on.<br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Strongest I've ever seen. I thought for sure you had 'em back there, man. You could move the world with these hands, if strength was all you needed. But it ain't. &quot;</span><br /> But strength was all he had... What else did he need? What was it he lacked?<br /> Earth seems distressed for a bit, pushes him away, then comes back.<br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I don't pretend to be something I'm not.&quot;</span><br /> <i><u>I</u> do, all the time</i>, the Titan thought. Maybe that was what was wrong with him? But how could he give up being - trying to be a hero? Again, it was all he had.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;I'm gonna be really real with you. You made yourself strong as Iron, but Iron ain't perfect. And the more you make yourself like Iron, the more the big deep imperfections of Iron become part of you. When I lose a fight, it sucks, but I lose all the time and I don't expect better. But you've built up your whole self around being the strongest, so when <i>you </i>lost that fight tonight, it <i>broke </i>you. You put all your weight on your Vitality, and when they cracked that pillar with Flux, the whole temple crashed down. That doesn't mean you <i>embrace </i>Flux- that's where I went stupid. But you gotta start seeing those imperfections as part of what you are. Otherwise, something's gonna break again when we try to help.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The words stung surprisingly deeply. <b>Leave </b>Ferrum? But they needed a Titan now more than ever, how could she say that? He was so close to mastering it all! And yet... Earth's words resonated with something inside the Tammuz, against his will. Ever since what happened before the Firestorm, he had felt... off, and the fight with the Pandoran made him feel even worse, in a way. That there were things he didn't know about himself was bad enough, but those things were... evil, weak. Things he had wanted to purge. What if Earth was right, though? Maybe he had been on Ferrum long enough. He'd heard of Pilgrims becoming stuck in a Role. Maybe he was in danger of becoming stuck in a Refinement? After all, he knew he'd have to try something else sometime, yet always pushed the thoughts away.<br /> It's just that Ferrum was so comfortable. He was comfortable with challenging himself. He KNEW Ferrum. He had been MADE for Ferrum. Mudbreaker had intended for him to <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000080\">..we are shaped by someone else, then shape ourselves.... was made to be a Titan, but it was <i>my</i> decision to <b>become</b> a Titan, to make myself hardy, to challenge myself... be <b>better </b>for it. I am thankful for challenges: they help me understand me. They help me learn new th...you will have <b>earned </b>it, on every step on the way you will have clawed your way up! You will..</span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> Of course. So simple. So obvious. Why are these things always so obvious looking back? A real Titan would not eschew the challenge. He had lost sight of what the goal was. It was not <i>being a Titan</i>, it was being <i>human</i>. It was time to move on. Time to learn more about humanity, humans, and himself.<br /> And by what Earth said, the smartest choice would be by learning more about that which he had tried to purge all this time.<br /> Wow. He really should ask Earth for advice more often.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Think on it, alright? We've got some time. I'm not riding out of here in a hurry just so you can prove you're strong enough. We're gonna make a plan and we're gonna do something on our terms, not the alchemists'.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Mark 5 closed his eyes, holding back bile, and nodded.<span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;I will.<br /> Oh, and... Earth?<br /> Thanks.<br /> Never knew you were this wise.&quot;</span><br /> His voice was perfectly honest, and there was nothing but thankfulness in his eyes when he opened them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 08-02-2017, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T15:50:21-07:00","id":1124985,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent; Katerina, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress, Stage 1), Callous, Beaten Down, Drugged<br /> Alembics: Eros (0), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: LLLLLOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 10/10<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 2</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis thinks the question over for a couple seconds. Sin's something he hears humans talk about, but even he doesn't really understand it. Sharon would read stories about men with strange names- Greek names, like his- who did bad things and came to bad ends because of bad choices they mad. He's heard some humans say that sins are bad things that humans do because the first man and woman ate a fruit that let them know what good and evil are. But that's too much for him to say. So he chooses an answer that another Created can understand pretty well. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">\u200b&quot;Sins are the things that humans and Created do that Cathars are interested in.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> Adonis follows the Frozen Pilgrim's eyes as she looks at the captain, but... not at the captain?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Going to have Adonis see if he can figure out what's going on with the Frozen Pilgrim. Wits 2 + Composure 2 = 4 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/538139\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes</a>. Might not be the best educated member of the ramble, but he's clearly got a clue that something's up.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T21:11:07-07:00","id":1125082,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Patient, Watched, Shaken<br /> Alembics: Verto (0), Stereo Humour (3), Arc (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 3/5 | Pyros: 5/12 | Beats: 3/5 | Vitriol Beats: 3/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">No energy for a long IC post so I'll just write up my next actions. I want to &quot;build&quot; a Plan based on Clairvoyance observations and brainstorming with the others, and also do some lucid dreaming for an hour or two to recover Pyros and force an Elpis vision.<br /> <br /> Build Equipment to make a +3 plan for sneaking into Amalgama. Wits 3+Composure 3-Difficulty 3+Pyros 2. 5 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/538221\" target=\"_blank\">1 success.</a><br /> <br /> Lucid dreaming in the frozen soil. Triggering Vivid Dreams to regain 2 WP from rest instead of 1. Replenish Pyros, Azoth 3+Composure 3+Vivid Dreams 3. 9 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/538223\" target=\"_blank\">1 success.</a> Harsh.<br /> <br /> Force an Elpis Vision, Composure+Azoth. 6 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/538226\" target=\"_blank\">5 successes!</a> I'll take the Inspired Condition, and I get +2 to interpret the vision.<br /> <br /> Interpret the Elpis Vision, Wits+Azoth+2+Willpower 3. 11 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/538230\" target=\"_blank\">4 successes.</a> Resolving Inspired for an x-success and +1 WP.<br /> Questions: What major or superlative Milestone will I face soon? Who will play a significant part in the next steps of my Pilgrimage?</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T08:16:11-07:00","id":1125230,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Inspired (Alchemy), Informed (Amalgama LTD), Disquiet 2 (Amalgama), Steadfast, Tormented<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 8/13 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b></div><br /> <br /> Scout eyed the pair as they attempted to physically interact with him, then went off to be all touchy-feely, snorting. &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">The Mark Five Weapon is correct, we should move now. We should at least try and get a visual on the facility. The longer we wait, the more likely it is that the others will die. And the less likely it is retrieving them will be an option. We at the very least need more ideas on what the facility can do.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> He got up and started walking, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I still like the idea of using one of you as a distraction, while we short out the power and go in. I'll be able to track the position of every azothic flame in the facility, but we'll need to be fast, quiet, and destroy as much of their facility as possible in the process. Or leave behind something that will. Again, I'll need more information for a proper plan. Until then, it's all theory and hope. Testing their response to a threat could be useful, but we'd need to do it without revealing ourselves. Perhaps if we set a fire on one corner of their compound... a really big one...</span>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T13:17:14-07:00","id":1126427,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Tilts: Arm Wreck<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (3), Charites (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0), Unfettered (0)<br /> Health:OOOOOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 3 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b></div> <br /> Mark 5 scoffed at being called a weapon, but agreed with the idea of distracting them. He'd be able to hold out the longest, so he was the logical choice.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;<b>No fire</b>. We will not risk killing Adonis, Isla, and the others, that would defeat the purpose of saving them! Think <i>harder</i>.<br /> Getting information is a good idea, though. If we want a plan, we need information. Sadly, the one who'd know most about Amagalma is Adonis.<br /> Also, I volunteer for distraction. In addition, we need a strike team. You and Earth, so you can track them down and Earth can take care of the threats. And someone else to help out.<br /> If you want a threat response threat, we could try going for an Earthquake.&quot;</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T06:10:31-07:00","id":1126671,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Inspired (Alchemy), Informed (Amalgama LTD), Disquiet 2 (Amalgama), Steadfast, Tormented<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 8/13 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b></div><br /> <br /> Scout frowned, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">An earthquake would give away our intent. We need a localized destructive force they can believe is a ongoing incident, but not easily contained. The fire suppression systems they likely maintain will be unlikely to allow it to damage their collection. It will, however, draw them out. The fire will draw first responders and evacuate others from it's reach,<br /> possibly the building. Then we can get in, get Adonis and your friends, steal their research and destroy the labs. If we short out the power along the way, it will be blamed on the fire, and increase the chaos of the scene. Leaves us more time to work.</span>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T08:41:35-07:00","id":1126728,"title":"","content":"<i>Louis Riel Bridge</i><br /> <br /> Several hours pass in the frozen dirt beneath the bridge. <b>Mark 5</b> and <b>Scout</b> discuss strategy. <b>Earth </b>dreams and meditates. Eventually, <b>Satin </b>and <b>Solomon </b>return from their walk, the elder Nepri visibly limping and nursing an injury, the Riven looking regretful but far more relaxed than before, the haze of Torment gone from them. They have settled back into the androgynous form that is most recognizable as them. Solomon takes hold of the generator again, breathing a sigh of relief as mummified flesh knits itself back together. This is not terribly relevant to Earth, however, who is dreaming their way into Azothic Memory, forcing an Elpis Vision to come upon them. And it does so <i>magnificently</i>.<br /> <br /> Earth dreams of endless fields of rolling banks of ash, a field of dark grey and stark white. There is a river of liquid mercury lapping at the ashen shore, and above the sky is a mandala of rolling flames, golden and white predominant, but shot through with cherry reds, royal indigos, verdant greens. Strange formations in the sky formed of smoky cloud and lightning whirl, the symbols for the alchemical metals. The symbols of the Refinements. The black-handed figure of white flame is waiting for Earth. They walk towards them, and where they step flowers and vines covered in thorns sprout forth from the ash. They point with their hand of black flame out into the middle distance, where Earth can see a stumbling porcelain figure, made so thin that you can see the blood that the hollow vessel has been filled with. Nearby, an ashen figure, looming and menacing, a coat of white ash and flickering white flames surrounding a solid black interior, charges towards them at a full sprint. Earth gathers lightning, but the manifestation of Azoth stays their hand, and the two figures freeze just before they collide.<br /> <br /> There are no words, there never are, but there is something there that the storm clouds and wild winds that always surrounded Earth kept them from hearing before. The sound of breathing, light and gentle, like someone in restful repose, and then that breathing began to harmonize with the rush of the wind, with the crackle of flame, with the flow of the river. The universe vibrated in anticipation of the Word, the thing before Creation, the thing before Earth was born. But it would not come.<br /> <br /> Earth can see a stout woman in the distance, starring at the swirling corona of flames in the heavens, as ashen beasts of silver and shadow looking vaguely like the creature Satin had transformed into circle her. They stand defiant, shot through with power, shot through with... Iron.<br /> <br /> <i>\u200bOOC: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> alright, so, here's the Elpis Vision. Your next Major Milestone is &quot;Not all battles are yours to fight&quot;. And I <b>think </b>I gave sufficient clues to indicate who will be important on the next step of Earth's Pilgrimage, but let me know if I am wrong.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Amalgama LTD</b><br /> <br /> It doesn't take long for the van to reach the Amalgama building. The doors stay closed for a while, but the Captain emerges, careful to keep herself between whoever was outside the van and the contents of its interior. Even through the sound-proofed doors, <b>Adonis </b>can hear the heated argument.<br /> <br /> &quot;What in the <i><b>fuck</b> </i>do you think you were doing? You are a goddamn biomedical corporation, not a paramilitary group! We were told you had finally gone to Oodena to retrieve that resource stockpile you keep saying you intended to get at, but the Government of Canada sure as shit didn't authorize the use of high explosives to retrieve it! You <i>do </i>know the Forks is one of the biggest tourist destinations in the city, right? People are already suggesting terrorism! The blast was big enough to simulate an earthquake and risk damages to the Canadian Museum for Human Rights. What in the hell did you use? Whatever this universal solvent you keep talking about is, I seriously doubt it warrants underground blasting at that magnitude.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Look, if you would like to take it up with my superiors, you can, but then you would have to eventually call up the chain of command to Project Magnet.&quot;<br /> <br /> The room suddenly goes dead quiet, even the machinery operating in the loading bay seems to be silent. The person behind the first voice sighs.<br /> <br /> &quot;This facility is intended, first and foremost, for the advancement of medical technology. Your universal catalyst and solvent you people keep talking about had <i>better </i>deliver, because letting you run free like this? Doing whatever the fuck you want? I'd say it definitely counts as breaking the Hippocratic Oath. Thin ice. Thin. Ice.&quot;<br /> <br /> The rest of the processing goes more or less without incident. <b>Tom</b> eventually panics, the stress of captivity and the lack of his anchoring object leading to him flaring with immense amounts of Pyros in an attempt to flee, but he very quickly runs out and his manacles still hold firm. Though a Wasteland <i>should </i>have formed from that, it didn't. The facility seems immune to it. <b>Isla </b>stays very quiet, aping what she thinks children should be in an effort to appear harmless, but the people in the hazmat suits appear unmoved. They are stripped of their clothing and belongings, which are stored in small crates marked &quot;Psychological Evaluation&quot; and given simple undyed jumpsuits to wear. The four Pilgrims are separated, put into different cells which each have just enough room for a mostly upright system of restraint and a technician or two to step in and take samples. Adonis is strapped down, hands and feet lashed with manacles, electrodes attached to his head, and two IVs inserted into his arm, except they more strongly resemble siphons to extract material than anything else.<br /> <br /> Eventually, a man in a lab coat marked with the Amalgama logo walks up and taps on the thick glass on the door to the Muse's tiny cell. The doctor is wearing a worn polo shirt under the lab coat, his dark curly hair cropped close to his head, small glasses sitting on a pronounced nose, smiling in a way carefully honed by years of practice in bedside manner to be reassuring.<br /> <br /> &quot;Do you know what you are?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T15:19:40-07:00","id":1128219,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Patient, Watched, Shaken, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Verto (0), Stereo Humour (0), Arc (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 4/12 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 3/5</b></div><br /> Earth awakens.<br /> <br /> &quot;So. We start a fire on their territory, we go in while they're runnin' around, we get the others, we break their expensive china and get out. I'm for it. Just as long as everything happens inside that's gotta happen. Without the spark, the Fire never starts.&quot;<br /> <br /> That felt like an echo of the vision, or the Frozen Pilgrim. Earth smacks their head.<br /> <br /> &quot;Think I got meltwater in my ear. Are we goin', or what?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T15:22:54-07:00","id":1128221,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent; Katerina, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress, Stage 1), Callous, Beaten Down, Drugged<br /> Alembics: Eros (1), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: LLLLLOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 6/10<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 2</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis stares at the doctor for a few seconds. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Yeah, I do. The question is, do you?&quot; </span>The drugs have slowed his mind, and his blood had chilled a little again. <i><span style=\"color:#00ff00\">If I can speak, I can control people. I can figure out a way out of this.</span></i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Spending a Pyros to charge Eros. Going to try to use Lure on this guy to get an inside man. Manipulation 3 + Persuasion 3 + Azoth 2 = 8 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/540207\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes</a>. If I'm reading the rules for Eros correctly, I get an Exceptional Success on all rolls using Persuasion at 3 successes.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T08:04:25-07:00","id":1129232,"title":"","content":"<b>Amalgama, LTD</b><br /> <br /> The doctor blinks, frowning, and narrows his eyes ever so slightly. They know something is wrong, but they <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=d370a0eb\" target=\"_blank\">cannot resist</a>. His face relaxes, with a touch of an upturned smile and the beginning of a blush. They adjust their name tag a little, pulling up a chair from the side just out of view. &quot;I do, actually. I'm a doctor. Doctor Roman. An admittedly <i>unusual </i>doctor, but a doctor nonetheless.&quot; He sits himself down, and clicks open a pen to start writing.<br /> <br /> &quot;I ended up stumbling across a chemical process that taps into what we here at the company labs call a 'universal catalyst'. A substance which can trigger any sort of complex chemical reaction you can imagine. What totipotent stem cells are to the human body, this universal solvent, what old alchemical texts calls Pyros or the Divine Fire, is to chemistry. It can accomplish incredible things, but its effects are... transitory at best. A stimulant incorporating the universal catalyst can elevate someone in a combat situation far above even the limits of humanity, but only for the span of an hour or two at most. Our competitors can produce permanent gains, and the results are stable instead of unpredictable. In order to produce permanent effects, we require a solvent derived from the universal catalyst that 'fixes' results. But it is extremely rare. The only place it is consistently found is in the flesh of homunculi, such as yourself.&quot;<br /> <br /> He adjust his glasses ever so slightly, and continues in a pleasant enough tone<br /> <br /> &quot;A homunculus is a replica human, most easily constructed from human tissue, but it is not a necessary requirement. Your biology, your thought process, <i>everything </i>is being sustained by the universal catalyst. You are, what, a couple years old at most? Ever wonder how you can speak? How you can walk? The catalyst has harnessed pre-existing neural pathways and then <i>continued </i>to grow them! Do you know how remarkable that is? Scans indicate you are developing new neural pathways daily, even though your host body's brain <i>should </i>be done producing new neurons. Using the catalyst in your veins is instinctual for you, chemical processes human researchers must spend months or years learning and developing the proper compounds for is just a matter of reflex and state of mind. Mixing the catalyst with the solvent produces even more exceptional effects, permanently affixing certain reactions as part of your peripheral nervous system, or producing wondrous objects that are difficult, or even impossible, to imitate. Regrettably, the only means we know of producing <i>more </i>of this solvent is by exposing homunculi to intense heat, retrieving the solvent from the ashes of the catalyst.&quot;<br /> <br /> The doctor does look upset at this, at which point you notice a surgically small blowtorch mounted near one of your arms. They will send you into Torment repeatedly and reap the rewards of the Vitriol that will slowly accumulate.<br /> <br /> &quot;Fortunately, we are aware of the horrible psychologically scarring side effects, but we know of how to alleviate them. Which is why I am here; to perform a full psychological profile of you.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T15:59:09-07:00","id":1130023,"title":"","content":"<b>Earth</b><br /> <br /> After recharging on the generator to top off their Pyros, Earth trudged with the others in the direction of Amalgama HQ. They huddled in an empty bus stop across the street from the medical building.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;So...now we start a fire? Or get in their house, first? We're gonna want the Cathars to mess with the guards' heads if we go inside.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T09:43:58-07:00","id":1131319,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Inspired (Alchemy), Informed (Amalgama LTD), Disquiet 2 (Amalgama), Steadfast, Tormented<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 13/13 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b></div><br /> Scout had recharged off and on through the night to fill his pyros, and worked at the plan, utilizing the blueprints he'd previously garnered and what he could divine from the information they had on the exact location of the Adonis and company, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Whoever starts the fire will do so on the opposite end of the compound to the entry point. I'll handle that part myself, as I think I'll be the most likely to be able to escape. I'll short out the compounds external electrical power ASAP after that, but you will need to fry any internal power sources they have. Get Adonis and the others. I'm guessing the biggest rooms in the blueprints will be the most likely to hold labs and the test subjects. Scarlet, I'd like to request you assist me on the diversion, in the event things go poorly. I'd rather not have to walk back from being dead this early in my pilgrimage. If you four need to split up, I'd like Solomon to stay with Mark 5, and Satin to stay with Earth. You'll be complimentary forces. I'll likely be invoking a lot of disquiet, so if you can make use of it, do it. Weakening any structural supports you find will be a boon. The less of this place is left standing, the more likely they'll be to abandon the facility.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">It *could* cause some issues with structural instability, but you'll probably be fine</span></i> Scout considered as he looked for the best spot to start his distraction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T11:07:50-07:00","id":1131359,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (0), Charites (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0), Unfettered (0)<br /> Health:OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 11/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 3 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b></div> <br /> Mark 5 recharged his Pyros before they left - he would need to be in top form, after all.<br /> <br /> When they arrived, he waited for Scout to repeat the plan, then nodded towards Solomon. He didn't know this Pilgrim, but Scout was smart - way smarter than the Tammuz. If he said this was a good idea, he was willing to trust him on that. Then he addressed the others, urgently and serious.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Alright. Let us try to stay together as long as possible. I will act as your shield. If there is a Pandoran or similar problem, and that is quite likely, and you have to hit me to get them, do not hesitate to do so.&quot; </span>He tried smiling at Earth.<span style=\"color:#000080\"> &quot;It's worked before, it will again.&quot;</span><br /> Truth be told, he was nervous. This was his chance to make up his mistake.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Let's move!&quot;</span><br /> With this, he started collecting Pyros in his body, to suffuse his flesh.<br /> <br /> OOC: Gathering 2 Pyros to charge Motus 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T13:57:21-07:00","id":1134935,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent; Katerina, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress, Stage 1), Callous, Beaten Down, Drugged<br /> Alembics: Eros (1), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: LLLLLOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 6/10<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 2</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis' eyes flit over to the blowtorch. He almost starts trying to escape as he realizes just what exactly Amalgama wants to do to him, but he fights it back. He turns his eyes back to Dr. Roman. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Doctor, I think you can afford to put off the procedure for a day or two, right? &quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis is going to try and make sure that he has a couple days' breathing-space before he starts getting burned for Vitriol. What with the exceptional success from the Lure roll, hopefully that's enough to make Dr. Roman put it off. Let me know if you think Adonis would actually need to make a roll.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T08:20:48-07:00","id":1137313,"title":"","content":"<b>Amalgama, LTD</b><br /> <br /> <i>Outside</i> the facility the alchemical corporation shares with Government of Canada researchers, seven Pilgrims huddle up against the frosty bricks of a university building. This is Lockhart Hall of the University of Winnipeg, and it is early in the morning after the last day of exams. The moon is starting to set, the wondrous silver glow fading into leaden darkness. The temperature drops as the shadows lengthen, the void that is a Winnipeg Night ready to swallow them whole. Joining <b>Earth, Scout, </b>and <b>Mark 5</b> is <b>Satin, Solomon, the Scarlet Woman </b>and curiously enough, <b>Joshua</b>. The black-clad Named hangs back, aware that he isn't terribly well-liked at the moment, but he is ready to leap into danger if it is strictly necessary. It isn't really proper to call the facility &quot;a&quot; building, since it is a small, tidy complex. Two buildings that seem rather modest compared to the rambling concrete and brick structure of the university. The one with less windows and direct access to the street is probably the lab. Beneath dim streetlights, the building glows with the not-quite-purple of the tinted glass that forms the buildings' exteriors. According to the blueprints, the labs are nearest to the loading docks, which have street access. The street is dead quiet, the occasional car passing up or down Ellice, the occasional shipping truck following after them, making its way towards the airport several miles down the road.<br /> <br /> <b>Joshua </b>eagerly steps forward to address <b>Scout </b>with an earnest grin &quot;I will set the fire, and lure anyone that comes after me. I have the alchemy to make it work.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Satin </b>breathes deeply and warps, changing shape into a silvery raven that alights on <b>Earth's </b>shoulder. The raven <i>quorks </i>a couple of times, clearing its throat, and then Satin's voice emerges, raspier than normal, with visible effort, each word spoken slowly for clarity's sake. &quot;I am quicker and less noticeable in this form. Can cover more ground. And ravens can still speak.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>Inside </i>the building, <b>Dr. Roman </b>raises an eyebrow at <b>Adonis'</b> courtesy and compliance &quot;You are not in any immediate distress, I must complete the psychological profile before the procedure begins. Took much undue psychological stress is dangerous to the subject and the researcher.&quot; He adjusts his glasses, clicks his pen a couple of times, and makes a few notes.<br /> <br /> &quot;I have a few customary questions to begin. First; who made you? Second; what do you remember of who you were made from? Third; what do you know about the Great Work, Magnum Opus, or New Dawn?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T10:53:43-07:00","id":1137362,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Inspired (Alchemy), Informed (Amalgama LTD), Disquiet 2 (Amalgama), Steadfast, Tormented<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 13/13 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b></div><br /> Scout eyed Joshua, but shrugged. Not having to light the fire was a bonus for him. &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Exceptionally convenient. But I accept your assistance. Remember, you need it large enough to really attract notice, but not so large it will endanger the entire facility before we can escape.</span>]&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T17:19:31-07:00","id":1137512,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (3), Charites (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0), Unfettered (0)<br /> Health:OOOOOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 9/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 3 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b></div> <br /> Mark 5 glowered at Joshua. He was obviously not happy with him being here OR handling the fire, but if Scout said it was alright... <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Just... don't try to pull anything. Again.&quot; </span>His eyes became small slits.<span style=\"color:#000080\"> &quot;You wouldn't like the consequences.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> With this, he released the stored Alchemical Fire to send his body into overcharge, his muscles in one pulsating movement growing in size. The Pyros ran through his being, making him lean, flexible and full of energy.<br /> <br /> This was not a threat.<br /> It was a promise.<br /> <br /> He turned to Scout, impatient: <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Go?&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T14:10:15-07:00","id":1138394,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Patient, Watched, Shaken, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Verto (0), Stereo Humour (0), Arc (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 10/12 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 3/5</b></div> <br /> A wolf <i>and</i> a raven? Aw man, Satin is so cool. Earth wants to be just like 'em when they grow up. They stroke the feathers on the silver bird's back, obviously impressed.<br /> <br /> To Mark 5: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;Yeah. Go.&quot;</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T19:05:11-07:00","id":1139329,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent; Katerina, Persistent) Disquiet (Waitress, Stage 1), Callous, Beaten Down, Drugged<br /> Alembics: Eros (1), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: LLLLLOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 6/10<br /> Beats: 0/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 2</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis can't help but blink at Dr. Roman's honesty. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;You know what we are? About the Pilgrimage, everything?&quot; </span>He lies there on the slab staring. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;So you really are Alchemists. We weren't sure how many of you knew the truth, and how many of you were in the dark.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Fine. If you want to play this way, I'm game. I was made by a woman named Sharon in Toronto. I'm sure you know that most Created are made by our own kind. But sometimes, humans touch the Divine Fire and use it to make one of us. Demiurges, we call them.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;I don't remember anything about the men I'm made from. Some of us get memories from their bodies. I know a Wretched who does. But I don't get those. Trust me, I wish I could. All I know is what Sharon- my demiurge- told me. Men she had crushes on. Most of them were dead, except my head. She tracked him down, killed him.<br /> <br /> &quot;The New Dawn's what we're all working towards. We aren't meant to exist. We're walking around with little sparks of Divine Fire inside us. We don't have souls. We burn the minds of humans we talk to. The world sickens and dies as we walk. We want to become human.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;And people like you look at us and think we're role-models or something. You want to do what we can, but you can't do it yourselves. So you steal from us. We spend months and years learning what you take for granted, asking questions you never need to think about. You burn us and destroy our progress because you don't realize how beautiful and perfect you are. You hate yourselves because you think you got cheated. You're all the same. You think you can make yourselves into gods or something. Well guess what? Godhood isn't what's waiting for you on the other side. This is.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> Adonis lets his Pyros flare up and his Azoth fades away. For a moment, he shows himself to Dr. Roman, scares and stitches and mismatched limbs.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;You're a moron playing with fire and you're gonna get burned. Now get out!&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Adonis spends a Pyros to manifest his Disfigurements. He's also trying to intimidate Dr. Roman. <br /> <br /> Presence 3 - Untrained Intimidate 1 + Willpower 3 = 5 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/549213\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes</a>. Actually, let's go ahead and make that a failure to resolve Callous. <br /> <br /> Azoth 2 = 2 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/549219\" target=\"_blank\">1 success.</a></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T16:35:58-07:00","id":1140350,"title":"","content":"<b>Amalgama LTD</b><br /> <br /> <b>Dr. Roman</b> looks on <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=dbaa1be8\" target=\"_blank\">impassively</a>, his face a tableau of disappointment. He makes a couple of notes on the paper, and writes for a good long couple of minutes, pausing every so often to flip pages, consult some charts. He leaves <b>Adonis </b>breathing hard, strapped upright to a metal slab, staring out with impotent fury through thick glass. He sighs, pushing his glasses up the bridge of his nose, and rubbing a hand down his face. From his reaction, it doesn't look like he's learned anything new. He stands up from the chair where he was sitting, and walks up to the thick glass, resting a hand on it, allowing his full weight to be taken by the glass.<br /> <br /> &quot;You know so little of alchemical theory. You can do things holy men go <i>lifetimes</i> trying to accomplish as a side effect of your occult biology; you cannot even see what a <i>wonder </i>you are. Your arms, legs, torso, head, they should all be rejecting each other, you never should have gotten up off the table you were stitched on, but you did. Your existence is miraculous, but not without... undesirable side effects, I'll grant you that.&quot; He shakes his head, lowering it a bit a chuckling &quot;The Great Work. Do you even begin to comprehend what the New Dawn actually <i>is</i><i>? </i>What your kind <i>does</i> when they grant themselves a soul? It is unison with the One, the guiding Principle of creation. In that moment you could do <i>anything</i>...&quot; The doctor's eyes are alight with possibility, with an awe approaching holy ecstasy. He is interrupted from his reverie by a knock on the heavy metal door at the end of the small hallway.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ah, that would be my new assistant. I requested someone be transferred earlier this evening when I received the news that so many new subjects had been acquired. Hopefully this isn't too much of a shock, we're a little understaffed in the, uh, specialist department, but I've been told he's a brilliant biochemist.&quot; He presses a button on a wall intercom and says, in a crisp, friendly tone, &quot;The door is open, come right on in.&quot; The thick steel door glides slowly open on greased hinges, and Dr. Roman's lab assistant stands in the doorway, frozen, eyes wide and lips parted ever so slightly in shock. It's a facial expression Adonis remembers fondly on the face looking with confusion at his battered state. <b>Erwin </b>stands slack-jawed at the end of what now feels like a much longer hallway.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> take a Beat from resolving <b>Calloused</b>, and a Beat from <b>Disquiet (Stage 1: Waitress)</b> because that one has Resolved by simple timeline.</i><br /> <br /> Outside the building, <b>Joshua </b>starts on his way towards the conventional entrance, balling up a newspaper in his bare hands, seemingly untouched by the cold. He knocks at the sealed glass doors, and armed security guards move to answer him. But there's something... off about the Named. There's more light around him than there should be. Like it's coming from within. The doors open as a guard steps out to confront him, at which point the paper sparks and bursts into flame. Joshua hurls it into a potted plant near the door, and his body glows with a soft, alluring phosphorescence, he flashes a smile back at the Pilgrims still on the sidewalk, ducks under a guard's grasp, and bolts, the guards following after him with manic determination. The door hangs open. <b>Solomon </b>stands with <b>Mark 5,</b> and <b>Satin </b>takes flight from their perch on <b>Earth's </b>shoulder to fly through the open door. The <b>Scarlet Woman </b>hangs back with <b>Scout</b>, waiting to see what they will do next, watching him with a fascinated gaze.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 09-14-2017, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T02:59:30-07:00","id":1140466,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Patient, Watched, Shaken, Inspired, Prepared (Amalgama)<br /> Alembics: Verto (0), Stereo Humour (0), Arc (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 10/12 | Beats: 0/5 | Vitriol Beats: 3/5</b></div> <br /> <br /> Go time. Earth reshapes their clay into something less distinctive, more generic, the embodiment of a service worker with whom eye contact is to be avoided. And most importantly, nothing like the monster from the Celebration Circle.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Putting 2 Pyros into Verto and 3 Pyros into Stereo Humour, flaring disfigurements while no one is watching. Activating Everyman, 5 dice: <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/550865\" target=\"_blank\">4 successes</a>. Earth becomes generic.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Pariah chases after the raven, through the sealed doors, not looking too closely at the fire in the pot. The Mission (ugh- Mark 5's rubbing off) is to get to where the captives are being held. And from what scrying on the Captain revealed of the floorplan, the first step should be going past the unattended security desk and down the first hallway to the left. There's supposed to be a service elevator on this floor that will lead down into the secure labs, but it's gonna take a keycard to access.<br /> <br /> Skulking through the dim hallway, Earth sez: <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">&quot;We gotta find the elevator, and we gotta find somebody with a key. Look for shiny stuff hanging from belts.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T13:57:34-07:00","id":1141198,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (3), Charites (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0), Unfettered (0)<br /> Health:OOOOOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 8/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 3 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b></div> <br /> Mark 5 followed, trying to stay out of sight as much as he could, following Earth like a shadow. Being really fast made this suprisingly <i>harder </i>than it should be, since stealth relied less on speed, and sudden movements tended to draw attention, but he managed, if barely.<br /> This whole approach rubbed him the wrong way - he wanted to <b><i>STORM </i></b>the place. Avoiding confrontation felt...un-Ferrum. Wrong. Which was something he would have to get used to, of course. Still. However, he was not going to argue with the others. They were doubtlessly smarter than him, after all.<br /> He told Solomon <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;Keep close&quot; </span>and looked around to see if he could find any of those two things.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=6b463a1c\" target=\"_blank\">1 Success on Dext+Stealth</a><br /> </div></div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T17:14:56-07:00","id":1141259,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Inspired (Alchemy), Informed (Amalgama LTD), Disquiet 2 (Amalgama), Steadfast, Tormented<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (0) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (0) Weaponize (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 13/13 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b></div><br /> Scout watched the others head in, and shook his head, looking back to the map &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Not what I had in mind, but I'll work with what I'm given. You answer to Scarlet? Good. What are your capabilities?</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> He didn't move to follow yet, merely watched and waited.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> 2017-09-17 18:13:08 Scout rolls 6 dice to Wits+Comp (8-again, 9-again) 3,4,2,3,8, 4,6 (1 success)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T15:36:52-07:00","id":1142320,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent; Katerina, Persistent), Beaten Down, Drugged<br /> Alembics: Eros (1), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: LLLLLOO I WP: 5/5 I Pyros 6/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 2</b><br /> <br /> </div> Even as Adonis' heart thaws, he sees Erwin standing there and suddenly wishes he could turn it to ice again. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>Erwin... oh, please tell me you didn't know. Please tell me they forced you. Please... </i></span>Tears begin to well in his eyes and he looks away from both of them. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Just my luck. You pick the one person in this entire company I was convinced wasn't a monster to help you.&quot; </span>He makes eye contact with Dr. Roman. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Doctor, I'll answer your questions. But it has to be from Erwin. I want a few minutes to speak to him. Alone.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Manipulation 3 + Persuasion 3 + Willpower 3 = 9 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/552204\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T16:54:21-07:00","id":1142751,"title":"","content":"<b>Amalgama LTD</b><br /> <br /> On the first floor of the building, <b>Earth</b> wanders around, mostly chasing after <b>Satin</b>, whose silvery raven form is keen-eyed and instinctually attracted to shiny baubles. The fire slowly starts to smoulder, but it's small enough that it hasn't triggered the fire alarm yet. Slowly, the flames start to lick their way up the potted plants, but living wood resists burning, sap and sugar and water holding back the flames. They have a few minutes before the alarms go off, and then a couple minutes more after that before the fire department gets there. <b>Satin</b> crows at <b>Earth</b>, flying in tight spirals by the button for the elevator. There's a card reader (Earth recognizes those from the stores they've bought things at. Humans use little plastic things as a promise of payment), but no keyhole. Need to find something like that.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Roll Wits + Composure to find <b>something </b>or Wits + Investigation to find something <b>immediately useful</b>. Alternatively, resolve the <b>Prepared Condition</b> for a Beat and to immediately find a keycard and a +2 piece of Equipment, like, say, a taser or other stun gun in a security guard's locker room or something.</i><br /> <br /> Following after them are <b>Mark 5</b> and <b>Solomon</b>, the unbelievably swift Titan finding it difficult to move without attracting attention, while the Cathar moves with easy confidence, keeping to the shadows as best he can. The blue-skinned Nepri pauses, as if about to say something, already rattled by tonight's events, but he breathes deeply and asks his question anyways. &quot;Did you ever figure out what you wanted to about intentions? Why people do things?&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Scarlet </b>smiles languidly at <b>Scout</b>, almost smirking in anticipation &quot;I can drive men mad with desire, or terror, or regret. I can cure sickness and worsen the impurities or mind, body, and soul. Everyone is impure, everyone has faults. But not everyone knows what they are or how far they'll go. I can help them find out.&quot;<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> Inside that suddenly dead quiet room, <b>Adonis' </b>voice rings out. <b>Erwin </b>is still frozen in the doorway, his hand still on the door, his arm visibly shaking, whether from constrained emotion that only emerges from his swiftly flickering eyes and twitching cheeks or from the sheer weight of the metal bearing down on him, trying to seal this awful tableau from his sight. <b>Dr. Roman </b>raises an eyebrow, slowly looking back and forth from his subject and his assistant. He steps slowly towards the door, those footsteps the only sound, and wordlessly pushes past Erwin. &quot;Excuse me- Erwin, is it? I need to make a call.&quot; The door swings shut quickly with no one the doorway, clanging shut with absolute finality. Erwin's face is exploding with emotion, hands resting on his head, pacing back and forth, air and curses emerging explosively in a staccato hiss between clenched teeth. He spins quickly on his heel, looking with terrified and confused eyes at the Muse's cell.<br /> <br /> &quot;What the fuck Mark. What the <i><b>fuck</b></i> is this?&quot; His fingers run through his close-cropped hair raking at his scalp. He paces back and forth, shaking his head, hands grabbing onto his own biceps with enough force that if his nails were a little longer he'd draw blood. As it is, you can see his fingernails go white from the pressure cutting off the blood flow. He lets out a frustrated scream that echoes in the narrow hallway and punches the wall, which turns quickly to pained yelps. He has no experience hitting things, and concrete is not forgiving. Erwin worked with chemicals, but if there is one thing you always remembered about those hands it's that they were soft and so terribly gentle. He could touch water without breaking the surface.<br /> <br /> &quot;Who are you? Who are you <i>really</i>? Shit, I told you <b><i>everything</i></b>. I told you about university, I told you about my sister, I told you about the debt these sons of bitches were drowning me in until I turned around and started working for them!&quot; It started as a hiss and ended in a thunderous shout. You've never heard his voice quite that loud before. &quot;Fuck. I was almost out. I was <i>this </i>close. <b><i>This. Close.</i></b> I was getting <i>out</i>, Mark! I enrolled at the U of M for the Winter Term starting in January! I was going to do my residency! I was going to tell you this weekend when we met up with my sister for dinner. She's in town just for a few days, wants to be home in time for Christmas with mom and dad.&quot; He realizes he's babbling and shakes his head, sliding slowly to the floor, his voice dropping to a hoarse whisper, the outrage bleeding out of him, leaving the hurt behind.<br /> <br /> &quot;Please just... be open with me. For once. Don't wait for me to tell you to tell me something about yourself.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T18:20:06-07:00","id":1142771,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Erwin, Persistent; Katerina, Persistent), Beaten Down, Drugged<br /> Alembics: Eros (1), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: LLLLLOO I WP: 4/5 I Pyros 6/10<br /> Beats: 2/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 2</b><br /> <br /> </div> Erwin's voice rises in volume, and through it all, Adonis becomes more and more shocked, more and more regretful. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>Erwin, I'm sorry. I've hurt you, haven't I? All this time I was using you, even when I didn't really mean to. Oh Principle damn me, I'm so sorry. </i></span><br /> <br /> When Erwin is finished, Adonis is still crying. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Erwin, I'm sorry. It's just... I was scared. I needed you more than you could ever understand. And I realized if I was honest, there was a good chance you would run away screaming. <br /> <br /> &quot;I'm not really called Mark. Well, I am. I was. Part of me. I...&quot; </span>He was fumbling for words. Sharon had made him bad at words. He was going to have to show Erwin, wasn't he? Taking a deep breath, he closed his eyes and allowed his Disfigurements to shine through again. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;I wasn't born. I was made. From several men, all of them actors. I was stitched together by a woman named Sharon, she wanted her crushes. My head belongs to Mark Austin. She killed him to get it. She named me Adonis, after Mark's big role. I just introduce myself to Mark to make things easier on me. People sometimes recognize me. She used me, Erwin. Like that movie. The one with the mad scientist who wears women's clothing and makes a husband. But...</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;When things like me are made, there's a little bit of something special in us. Pyros, the Divine Fire. It makes us walk, talk, think. But... it's not a soul. And people know that. Not really, but they can feel it. They get burned by the Fire. It breaks them, drives them crazy. That's what happened to Sharon. She spent too much time around me, tried to kill me so that I couldn't leave her or cheat on her. So I ran away. I spent months traveling to Winnipeg. To try and become human. Because if we learn from humans, learn everything we can about you... we can become real humans too. <br /> <br /> &quot;When I met you, some friends and I were looking in that van. I jumped out to distract you. And if I hadn't, Earth... well, she wasn't in a good place that night. Or for a while after that. But I met you and then I realized... you could help me. And I could keep you safe. Because Amalgama? It's terrible. Do you know what they do to us? They burn us alive, melt us down to our base parts and use it for the potions. And they had Pandorans in that van, Erwin. Monsters, worse than us, they just eat and eat and eat. If one of them had gotten out, they would've hurt people. So... they destroyed the van with them in it. I didn't know they were going to do it, but they had to. And afterwards, Earth wanted to kill you. To her, you're just another alchemist. But I could tell that wasn't you. You're not like the others. I told her I would ask you questions so that we could learn about Amalgama. Because the longer they operate, the more danger we are in.<br /> <br /> &quot;I haven't been honest with you, Erwin. But now I am. And I am telling you, we need to get out. Both of us. That alchemy stuff you were researching? It's real. And there's a different way to do it from Amalgama. Not as easy, but better, safer. I'm sure we could teach you. Just help me get out of here. Please. I love you.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Okay, here it is. Adonis laying it all on the line. Being completely honest with Erwin, not manipulating him, just presenting the truth. Erwin's free to react as he wishes. No Persuasion roll unless you think his plea to Erwin needs to be represented with a dice pool.<br /> <br /> Rolling for Disquiet. Dice don't fail me now. 2 Azoth = 2 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/552527\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>. Let's hope Erwin makes it on that resistance roll.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T07:08:37-07:00","id":1142885,"title":"","content":"<b>Amalgama LTD</b><br /> <br /> Huddled on the floor, knees held tight to his chest, <b>Erwin</b> looks over at <b>Adonis</b>, truly, for the first time. Disfigurements and all. It's a risk, a massive risk. You can feel the Fire spark and catch, too much sanguine humour, too much emotion roiling in a cloying incense-cloud in that tiny room. Erwin sits, mouth agape, and in that infuriating, miraculous way of his, simply starts shakily to his feet, his mind <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=35435bdf\" target=\"_blank\">incapable of burning</a>. He walks slowly towards the cell, his voice hissing and catching through clenched teeth and choked-back sobs. &quot;Now? You're saying that to me <i>now</i>, <i>here? </i>When there's the <b>huge</b> <i><b>fucking MESS </b></i>that we're in now?! Your... mother... Sharon. She went crazy. This Pyros, I guess that would be the Universal Catalyst, it burns out minds. Has it affected me? Am I only with you because there's a fucking mythical flame burning in my head that makes me crazy for you? Did you use alchemy on me to get me to fall for you?&quot;<br /> <br /> Erwin shook his head, turning his back on the thick glass and leaning against it. His voice drops to a quiet murmur &quot;I knew they were crossing lines. I knew it. Proper pharmaceutical corporations don't set up pyramid schemes. Shit.&quot; He sounds so tired. So worn down. So incredibly drained. &quot;This is a lot to process Mar-&quot; he trips on the name, catches his breath, and says the other name, the <i>real </i>name, with a hoarse whisper &quot;Adonis. I just... I can't do this right now.&quot; He walks to the door, and opens it without another word.<br /> <br /> Erwin is out of the room, and Adonis is alone with his thoughts.<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: Take a Beat from <b>Connected </b>for asking Erwin to do a favour for you.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 09-22-2017, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T07:30:25-07:00","id":1142896,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Earth resolves Prepared as suggested, finding a security station with an unattended keycard and +2 stun gun, then has Satin round up the others and heads to the elevator.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T11:00:34-07:00","id":1142978,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (0), Motus (3), Charites (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0), Unfettered (0)<br /> Health:OOOOOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 8/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 3 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Did you ever figure out what you wanted to about intentions? Why people do things?&quot;<br /> <br /> What a strange thing to ask, in the middle of their Mission, no less.<br /> Still, not answering it might leave the blue-skinned Nepri unfocused. Mark 5 started to shake his head, but instead shrugged. <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot; No. Not really. Not yet. I know that people usually do what they think is right, and sometimes they do things they know are wrong. Sometimes you mean well, but what you end up doing...&quot; </span>he looked down at his own hands. They looked clean, but they were covered in blood. That he knew.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;What you end up doing is not always what you wanted to do. All I know is, intentions are important. Because the same act can have a different meaning, and that is important.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The Tammuz would be hard-pressed to find the right words to explain <i>why </i>this was important, but he knew, deep inside, that it was.<span style=\"color:#000080\"> &quot;Did you? Figure it out, I mean.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=6dc2f873\" target=\"_blank\">2 Successes</a> on Wits+Investigation</div></div> </div> </div></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T12:12:33-07:00","id":1143000,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Katerina, Persistent), Beaten Down, Drugged<br /> Alembics: Eros (1), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: LLLLLOO I WP: 4/5 I Pyros 5/10<br /> Beats: 3/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 2</b><br /> <br /> </div> Erwin walks out, and Adonis is left alone. Well, all things considered, it could've gone better. But really, had he expected Erwin to say he loved him back? That was something that only happened in fairy tales. But Erwin had resisted the fire once again. And he knew he wasn't affected by Disquiet, otherwise he would've become more and more obsessed with him over time, just like Sharon had become. <br /> <br /> So now what? Was he just going to sit here on the slab waiting for Doctor Roman to come back and start burning him? Would the others come for him? He couldn't blame them if they didn't. But no, Earth probably wasn't going to let him rot away in here. And Mark 5 would probably come after her too out of loyalty. And Scout because he had nowhere else to go. So were the three of them going to try and take on Amalgama by themselves? After what had happened early that night, it was probably suicide.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T13:53:28-07:00","id":1143027,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama LTD), Disquiet 2 (Amalgama), Steadfast, Tormented<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (2) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (3) Weaponize (3)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 5/13 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b></div><br /> Scout looked over Scarlet as she responded, thinking that over, and finally walking towards the door, and pulling out the map of the facility from before, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Good. That will be of some use to us, I think. I can inflict them with disquiet, and have already done the previous night. I'm not sure if that will assist or hinder your efforts, however it will make even my small punches hurt very badly. Now, we're looking for structural beams we can weaken, and power generation points we can short out once we're inside. I'm thinking we might could cause a systematic power failure if we can find large enough points to overload. Or just drain. There are enough of us. Also, you should brace yourself for a moment.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> With that noted, he started charging up his alembics. The two that made him dangerous would be the first and most useful here so those he charged. Then he considered his options, and charged a second alembic set. There was a good chance that anyone who could detect him within the facility would already be able to. No reason to be shy about that.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Going to have scout try to detect, then pinpoint azothic Radiances in the facility in general. Finally, he'll use Controlled burn to bring his Azoth radiance up. I spent willpower on that one, and I'll resolve inspired (alchemy), to make that an exceptional success, as well as regain said willpower point, and create a False Trail of his new Azoth radiance to outside the building. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\" style=\"background-color: #15151A\"><td width=\"101\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\">2017-09-22 14:25:30</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"><span style=\"color:#99CCCC\">Scout</span> rolls 10 dice to <span style=\"color:#99CCCC\">Controlled Burn</span> (used willpower)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"><span style=\"color:grey\">1,3,<span style=\"color:lightgreen\">10</span>,<b><span style=\"color:lightgreen\">10</span></b>,<b>3</b>, 6,3,5,3,1, 1,<span style=\"color:lightgreen\">8</span></span><span style=\"color:white\"> (<a href=\"http://rpgroller.com/nwod/?show_roll=504401\" target=\"_blank\">3 successes</a>)</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\" style=\"background-color: #0C0C0F\"><td width=\"101\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\">2017-09-22 14:20:07</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"><span style=\"color:#99CCCC\">Scout</span> rolls 5 dice to <span style=\"color:#99CCCC\">Pinpoint Azothic Radiance</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"><span style=\"color:grey\"><span style=\"color:lightgreen\">8</span>,<span style=\"color:lightgreen\">9</span>,7,6,6</span><span style=\"color:white\"> (<a href=\"http://rpgroller.com/nwod/?show_roll=504400\" target=\"_blank\">2 successes</a>)</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\" style=\"background-color: #15151A\"><td width=\"101\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\">2017-09-22 14:19:19</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"><span style=\"color:#99CCCC\">Scout</span> rolls 6 dice to <span style=\"color:#99CCCC\">Detect Azothic Radiance</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"><span style=\"color:grey\">6,<span style=\"color:lightgreen\">10</span>,<b>2</b>,2,2, 2,3</span><span style=\"color:white\"> (<a href=\"http://rpgroller.com/nwod/?show_roll=504399\" target=\"_blank\">1 success</a>)</span></td> </tr> </table></div> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T10:27:52-07:00","id":1143836,"title":"","content":"<b>Amalgama LTD</b><br /> <br /> Down in his cell, <b>Adonis</b> can feel a sudden surge of Azoth, an aura that is familiar to him, but tainted now with Torment. <b>Scout</b>, outside the building, radiating with the heat of a blazing forest fire. Outside the heavy door, he can hear sensitive alchemists shouting, and a muffled alarm that is joined by a scratching, scrapping sound that echoes through the air ducts. There's something in this facility besides the Created, something reacting violently to the presence of powerful Azoth.<br /> <br /> Coming down the elevator, are <b>Earth, Scout, Mark 5, Satin, Solomon, </b>and <b>Scarlet</b>. Armed with a tazer, silvered raven perched on their shoulder, <b>Earth </b>is ready for action. As <b>Mark 5 </b>rejoins the group (having uncovered a list of security codes for numerous secured doors that should prove useful), <b>Solomon </b>frowns, thinking on the Titan's words. His response is just barely a whisper. &quot;No, not yet. But you are right, it <i>is </i>important.&quot; He starts muttering, mostly to himself, about intention and flaws, and whether intent matters when discussing the severity of a mistake or a flaw. Cathar problems, Cathar equations, Cathar alchemy. It's beyond the Titan, especially during a Mission. Needless noise, needless distraction. The elevator descends and pings open, the mismatched impromptu throng stepping out into a hallway with several surprised and confused employees wearing polo shirts emblazoned with the company logo.<br /> <br /> And then the fire alarm rang.<br /> <br /> The door to Adonis' cell opens again and <b>Dr. Roman </b>has returned &quot;You know, that was a very educational interaction. The boys studying homunculi are going to be <i>very </i>interested in those tapes. And in Erwin, of course.&quot; He sighs &quot;Poor boy. So bright, and now he'll be reduced to a cabinet curiosity.&quot; The alchemist steps closer, swiping a keycard on a read next to the cell, and the door swings open. He touches a panel on the wall and removes what looks like a bone marrow needle with a curiously thick glass vial attached to it. Several more sit inside the panel. &quot;Unfortunately,&quot; the doctor says, as the heavy metal door opens again &quot;you will <i>not </i>be continuing with us. A fire has broken out upstairs and that means that all kinds of people will want to check out specimen holding, which we cannot allow them to do. Others wouldn't... understand.&quot; Footsteps, nearly silent, padding along the floor. The doctor takes up all of Adonis' field of view, the silver gleam of the needle grabbing his attention as the doctor lines it up with Adonis' thigh &quot;So, I regret to inform you that we will be rushing the procedure. I truly am sorry, I was looking forwards to getting to know you.&quot; A shape, looming up behind the doctor, sleeves on a dark lab coat rolled up to the elbow, exposing familiar arms and soft hands covered in a chalky paste.<br /> <br /> The hands rub together, and a vaguely green viscous oil wells up between them, and they grab hold of the doctor's shoulders. The doctor looks perplexed for a moment as he is hauled backwards, but only for a moment. Soon he starts screaming as paper and fabric instantly chars, his skin turning red and peeling away. The figure knocks the disoriented doctor over and kicks him once to separate his shaking hands from his phone before wiping his hands off on the doctor's coat. <b>Erwin </b>is breathing hard, but manages a shaky smile.<br /> <br /> &quot;How about we get out of here?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T19:16:23-07:00","id":1143941,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Katerina, Persistent), Beaten Down, Drugged<br /> Alembics: Eros (1), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: LLLLLOO I WP: 4/5 I Pyros 5/10<br /> Beats: 3/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 2</b></div> <br /> Adonis feels the power of Scout's Azoth ripple through the building like a loud clap of lightning. For a moment, he can't help but feel his Azoth rise a little in happiness. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><i>They came for us, </i></span>he thinks. If Scout is here, Mark 5 and Earth have to have followed him, neither Named would let him come here on his own. But even as his happiness grows, he hears the horrible sound of Pandorans scratching and clawing. Somebody just rang the dinner bell. They are going to have to deal with that, and fast.<br /> <br /> But before he can think anything else, Dr. Roman talks back in. He prepares to start taking Adonis' vitriol forcibly, but then a figure uses a Distillation he does not recognize and attacks the doctor. It's Erwin. <br /> <br /> Adonis blinks and says, <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Hell yeah. Get me off this thing.&quot; </span>As soon as the restraints are loose, he rises up and kisses Erwin full on the cheeks. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;I'm sorry about everything. But we need to get out of here. Some of my friends have come to rescue us, we need to find them. But we need to do it fast, there's at least one Pandoran in here. Either a bunch of them or a really big one. We might need to burn down the building to get rid of it. Is there anything you want to bring with you? Research notes, alchemical texts? Anything related to... what did Roman call me? Homunculi? No, wait, first, get me to a power source. A breaker or something. The electricity is close enough to the Divine Fire to heal me.&quot;</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T14:57:54-07:00","id":1144205,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama LTD), Disquiet 2 (Amalgama), Steadfast, Tormented<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (2) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (3) Weaponize (3)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 5/13 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b></div> <br /> <br /> Scout could smell Adonis's Azothic Radiance among the others- a familiar scent he'd come to recognize, like a sweet white wine. The various other aromas assaulted his senses, and he recoiled slightly. So many alchemists... they tasted hollow, like their flavor would slip away after but a moment, like a stick of gum. The sour scent of the pandorans warred with it. There were other smells- those he didn't know as well. &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I can feel... a score of alchemists. Adonis... others... lots of pandorans that are probably wreaking havoc on the alchemists. And...</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> He paused as he discerned the final fragrance. Highwind had given him a chocolate once. A pure cocao creation, sweet and rich. He had received it from a friend in a far off country that Scout only wished he new. The genitor had made him take it slow with that, scenting it, tasting it, appreciating it. Scout sometimes wished he could recreate it with alchemy.That was what the pure azoth reminded him of.<br /> <br /> Scout looked up, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I... cannot be sure, but I think they have something else. It is an Azoth so pure... no torment, no flux. Just pure, refined Azoth. I... think it may be an Angel.</span>&quot; He stopped, and pointed towards where he could feel it all flowing from, &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">It is that way. They are all close together. If we are lucky, the Unborn and the Fire will keep the Alchemists busy.</span>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8122,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","user":"ArchonAres","date":". 09-26-2017, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T15:03:00-07:00","id":1144209,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (2), Motus (3), Charites (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0), Unfettered (0), Unbowed (0)<br /> Health:OOOOOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 6/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 3 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b></div> <br /> <br /> Scout's Azoth drew Mark 5's attention away for a split-second after handing the codes over to the blue-skinned Nepri.<span style=\"color:#000080\"> &quot;He will draw attention. They had Pandorans. They might have more. We need to be quick.&quot; </span><br /> Then he looked the Nepri straight in the eyes: <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;I need to learn about... impurity. Flaws. </span><span style=\"color:#000080\">But not now. We will have words later. </span><span style=\"color:#000080\">First: the Mission.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> As he stepped outside the elevator, the Titan started charding pyros again.<br /> The time for hiding would soon be over. It would be time to do battle. One last time, he would prove he was a Soldier, his Iron tested and true. He told the others without turning around <span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;The fighting will start soon. Get ready.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> OOC: Charging 2 Pyros to Hygeius, benefitting from Impossible Flesh and Human Flesh.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T15:22:06-07:00","id":1144216,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Earth<br /> Conditions: Patient, Watched, Shaken, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Verto (2), Stereo Humour (3), Arc (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 5/12 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 3/5</b></div><br /> <span style=\"color:blue\">&quot;I... cannot be sure, but I think they have something else. It is an Azoth so pure... no torment, no flux. Just pure, refined Azoth. I... think it may be an Angel.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Earth looks all dreamy. Happy, even. It's like crush+bliss+pilgrim's desire to see a sacred icon up close. &quot;It is. I saw her. She's still here?&quot;<br /> <br /> Mark sez: &quot;The fighting will start soon. Get ready.&quot;<br /> <br /> Earth ruminates: &quot;For you, yeah.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's weird.<br /> <br /> The Hermit brushes past the polo shirts and points down the hallway Scout indicated.<br /> <br /> &quot;Take a look, Satin.&quot;<br /> <br /> With the raven scouting the route and a taser close at hand, Earth trudges ahead with the others toward the Flames.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T19:16:07-07:00","id":1145059,"title":"","content":"<b>Amalgama LTD</b><br /> <br /> Still shaking from the violence of his sudden decision to rescue <b>Adonis</b>, <b>Erwin </b>jerks back unconsciously, keeping his hands still just slightly slick with acid as far away from his boyfriend as he can reasonably get and still maintain contact. He gestures back over his shoulder into the hallway as <b>Dr. Roman</b> coughs and lets out low moans of pain on the floor, trying to right himself. &quot;There's a, uh, breaker box down the hallway in the maintenance closet.&quot; He picks up a massive brown paper bag and passes it to Adonis. The bag smoulders just a little, but it seems like the acid flow has stopped for now. &quot;I got your things.&quot; It sounded like such an inane, domestic thing to say, that Erwin had to stifle back a laugh. &quot;Come on, let's go.&quot; He steps towards the door and takes a look as half a dozen employees in polo shirts, and a couple people in riot gear like at the Forks (possibly the same people) storming down the hall, followed by shuffling, misshapen, skittering things snarling, hissing, ragged, gasping for breath. Claws and... other things... raking at the doorway as a thing or two snuffles.<br /> <br /> The silver raven that is <b>Satin </b>flew forwards and down the hall, eyes scanning back and forth as <b>Earth</b>, looking every bit the generic employee, simply walked on through. The employees gawked at <b>Mark 5</b>, <b>Scout </b>and the others, however, pressing panic buttons on company wristbands and starting to make a run for the nearest intercom, but the staff <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=ab5295be\" target=\"_blank\">trip over each other</a> and collapse in a heap, stumbling back to their feet to either make a run to find actual help- if they can make it. <b>Satin </b>quorks with alarm at what she sees coming down the hall.<br /> <br /> &quot;Unborn!&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>OOC: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> any of you can roll a Down and Dirty combat roll to neutralize the employees and make sure they don't immediately alert someone more dangerous than them. As they've failed even a single success will handle it, but multiple people can roll if you want to have it as multiple characters working together.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T00:55:47-07:00","id":1145127,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (3), Motus (3), Charites (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (0), Unfettered (0), Unbowed (0)<br /> Health:OOOOOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 5/11 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 3 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b></div> <br /> Now that they no longer needed to stay hidden, Mark 5 could cut loose and move at full speed.<br /> It would have been easy to take these people out once and for all - the tools were at his hands. But he remembered the last time he fought human beings.<br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:10px\">He remembered the blood on his hands.</span></i><br /> These people were no threat, they posed no challenge. They were a speed bumper, at best.<br /> As Adonis once said, what felt like so long ago: <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">. I don't think he knows what was in those tubes and stuff. He thinks he's just working for a chemical company.</span><br /> This probably applied to these people, too. So he tried to be careful about sending them down. Deal just a blow with enough force to knock them out, no more, then go for the next one. Rinse and repeat.<br /> <br /> OOC: Charging 1 Pyros to Hygeius, benefitting from Resilient Flesh.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Wohooo! <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=e42c87f9\" target=\"_blank\">7 Successes!</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T14:37:55-07:00","id":1145892,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Adonis</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Conditions/Tilts: Masked (Refinement), Connected (Katerina, Persistent), Beaten Down, Drugged<br /> Alembics: Eros (1), Assimilate (0), Stalker (0), Eris (0)<br /> Health: LLLLLOO I WP: 4/5 I Pyros 5/10<br /> Beats: 3/5 I Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 2 I Vitriol Experiences 2</b><br /> <br /> </div> Adonis takes the bag and quickly dresses again. He peeks out the door, and then pulls his head back when he sees the Unborn. <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">&quot;Okay, those things following the humans. Those are Pandorans. Stay far, far away from them.&quot; </span>But then he furrows his brow. <span style=\"color:#00ff00\">&quot;Wait, they aren't trying to eat the humans. Amalgama must have some way of controlling them. Well, doesn't matter. They see us, we're toast. Here, give me your lab coat. If I don't draw attention to myself, humans have a hard time noticing me.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Adonis creeps out of the door and down the hallway to the maintenance, trying to be as silent as possible. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Dexterity 2 + Stealth 1 = 3 dice -&gt; <a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/554702\" target=\"_blank\">0 successes</a>. Let's just hope the -2 to the roll to notice him helps.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T17:56:17-07:00","id":1145927,"title":"","content":"<b><div align=\"center\">Earth<br /> Conditions: Patient, Watched, Shaken, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Verto (2), Stereo Humour (3), Arc (0)<br /> Health: OOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 5/5 | Pyros: 5/12 | Beats: 1/5 | Vitriol Beats: 3/5</div></b><br /> Fight's coming. Earth turns to the melee and gears up, ready to break faces. But...<br /> <br /> Why?<br /> <br /> These humans aren't a threat. Most humans aren't. Earth knows this.<br /> <br /> The ones in hard shells at the Circle were. These ones are with them. Maybe they hide sharp teeth, too.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they don't.<br /> <br /> It looks like Mark 5 can handle it himself. Earth hesitates, then turns back. It will be fine without them. The world passes the Hermit by.<br /> <br /> Unborn down the tunnel- er, hallway. Different fight. Will the others be okay again?<br /> <br /> Maybe.<br /> <br /> Earth goes further down the hallway incognito, looking for Adonis and Erwin. There's another Mission to attend to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T13:50:14-07:00","id":1146433,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Scout<br /> Conditions: Introspective, Informed (Amalgama LTD), Disquiet 2 (Amalgama), Steadfast, Tormented<br /> Alembics: Heed the Call (2) Plumb the Fathoms (0) Internalize (3) Weaponize (3)<br /> Health: OOOOOO | Willpower: 6/6 | Pyros: 5/13 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 4/5<br /> XP: 1 | VXP: 1</b></div><br /> <br /> Scout smelled the sour pandorans coming up and slipped into one of the offices as quietly as he could, tugging at Scarlet as he did so. Whether or not she followed was her problem, but he wasn't up for that fight. It hurt bad enough last time. This was a job for... someone else. If the others were fast enough, the pandorans would bypass them and go towards the false trail he'd laid.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Scout is going to slip off into a side room if he can.<br /> 2017-10-03 04:07:05 Scout rolls 6 dice to Dex+Stealth+Small frame 5,3,8,6,1, 2 (1 success)</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-10T07:25:15-07:00","id":1148574,"title":"","content":"<b>Amalgama LTD</b><br /> <br /> Sneaking down the hallway, walking briskly but confidently, is <b>Erwin</b> in his button-down shirt and <b>Adonis </b>holding a lab coat tight to himself as a form of camouflage. Somewhere further up ahead, a lone alchemist in a dishevelled suit pauses, looking around, a Pandoran at their heel, the skittering, many-limbed, glistening thing letting out a couple wheezing gasps. Its flowing, waxy flesh balloons with each sucking breath, causing it to bob in place. The alchemist scans the area and makes eye contact with the Muse as he glances backwards, eyes widening in shock and just barely suppressing a shudder. &quot;Hey! Wait!&quot; He starts running towards him, the Pandorn loping leisurely at his side &quot;Stop!&quot;<br /> <br /> Walking unhindered down the hall is <b>Earth</b>, whose flesh warps and ripples subtly every so often, a tremulous shudder like a shiver, adjusting ever so slightly as the nearby group shifts and changes, maintaining the illusion of normalcy based on the given population. The Unborn tilt their heads as they pass, but they are bound to the will of their masters, who are themselves fooled by the subtle alchemy. <b>Satin </b>flies overhead, close to the ceiling, certainly not where the alchemists expect to find a Created. <b>Scout </b>and <b>Scarlet </b>duck into an office, hearing rushing feet and skittering limbs slapping along tiles floors. Scarlet's face is enraptured, peering out of the window of the office door, waiting to see the mayhem unfold.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, <b>Mark 5 </b>cuts loose against the hopelessly outmatched employees, moving in a blur, one punch, one employee hits the floor, or flies back into the wall. The Titan's superhuman strength is overwhelming, iron mauls swung with the strength to shatter stone hurling human bodies aside with ease, leaving them in (still-breathing) heaps on the floor. Their breathing is laboured, but they <i>are </i>still alive. <b>Solomon </b>gives an appreciative nod, his gaze still ahead, studying the armoured humans and shambling Unborn racing towards them &quot;Well, let's give them a show, shall we?&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>\u200bOOC: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> gain a Beat from the Exceptional Success and roll for Initiative. There are three Amalgama mercenaries, and six Pandorans.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T07:41:19-07:00","id":1148816,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mark 5<br /> Conditions: Tenacious, Guilty, Inspired<br /> Alembics: Hygeius (3), Motus (3), Charites (0), Unbroken (0), Unconquered (1), Unfettered (0), Unbowed (0)<br /> Health:OOOOOOOOOOOOO | Willpower: 4/6 | Pyros: 4/11 | Beats: 2/5 | Vitriol Beats: 0/5<br /> Experiences: 3 I Vitriol Experiences 1</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type